"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/aispm-for-dummies.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/ai-security-posture-management-ai-spm-for-dummies?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY26Q1_INB_FORM_AI-SPM-for-Dummies-eBook&sfcid=701Py00000KWgAHIA1&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AI-SPMDummies)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Microsoft ends Authenticator password autofill, moves users to Edge\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft ends Authenticator password autofill, moves users to Edge\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * May 3, 2025\n  * 10:16 AM\n  * [6](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#comments)\n\n\n![Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/02\/10\/Microsoft_logo.jpg)\nMicrosoft has announced that it will discontinue the password storage and autofill feature in the Authenticator app starting in July and will complete the deprecation in August 2025.\nThe decision is to streamline autofill support and consolidate credentials management under a single platform, Microsoft Edge.\nThe move requires action from impacted users as they are given until August 1, 2025, to export their information from Authenticator, or risk losing it.\nMicrosoft Authenticator is a free mobile app ([iOS](https:\/\/apps.apple.com\/us\/app\/microsoft-authenticator\/id983156458) and [Android](https:\/\/play.google.com\/store\/apps\/details?id=com.azure.authenticator&hl=en)) that provides secure sign-in for mobile accounts using multi-factor authentication (MFA) methods like time-based one-time passwords (TOTPs), push notifications, or biometrics-based confirmations.\nThe app supports authentication for Microsoft services like Microsoft accounts, Azure AD, and GitHub, as well as non-Microsoft platforms.\nThe autofill feature was added to mobile Authenticator apps [in December 2020,](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-authenticator-brings-password-autofill-to-mobile-devices\/) allowing users to fill their credentials saved in the Authenticator on sign-in forms automatically.\nSupport for this feature is about to end, though, as Microsoft announced the phased deprecation of autofill in three steps:\n  * **June 2025** : You can no longer save new passwords in Authenticator.\n  * **July 2025** : Autofill will stop working in Authenticator; stored payment info will be deleted.\n  * **August 2025** : Saved passwords and unsaved generated passwords will no longer be accessible in Authenticator.\n\n\n## Users pushed to (the) Edge\nMicrosoft announced that autofill and the password manager are now moving to its browser, Edge.\nUsers who want to continue using the passwords saved in Microsoft Authenticator for autofill will need to install Microsoft Edge on their phone ([iOS](https:\/\/apps.apple.com\/us\/app\/microsoft-edge-ai-browser\/id1288723196), [Android](https:\/\/play.google.com\/store\/apps\/details?id=com.microsoft.emmx)).\n\"Your saved passwords (but not your generated password history) and addresses are securely synced to your Microsoft account, and you can continue to access them and enjoy seamless autofill functionality with Microsoft Edge,\" [reads the announcement](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-gb\/account-billing\/changes-to-microsoft-authenticator-autofill-09fd75df-dc04-4477-9619-811510805ab6).\nTo complete the migration of the autofill functionality to Microsoft's browser, users need to find 'Autofill\/Passwords' in their device settings and choose Edge as the preferred service.\nThen, launch Edge and sign in with your Microsoft account to allow the syncing of passwords to begin.\nIf everything is done correctly, all passwords should be accessible via Settings > Passwords on Edge.\nIf users don't want to use Edge, Microsoft allows exporting passwords so they can be moved to another password manager, but this must be done before August 1, 2025. For payment information, July 2025 is the deadline.\nTo [export passwords](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-gb\/account-billing\/export-passwords-from-microsoft-authenticator-10268a16-c0a4-4037-9bcb-b47c29409fe0) from Microsoft Authenticator, select menu > Settings > Autofill > Export Passwords > select an export location and tap 'Save.'\nThe importing process is only applicable to account passwords. Payment info will have to be manually re-inputted for security reasons.\nMicrosoft noted that Passkeys will continue to be supported in Authenticator, so users who actively use them to sign in to their Microsoft Accounts must ensure the app remains enabled as their Passkey Provider.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg)](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Coinbase fixes 2FA log error making people think they were hacked](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/coinbase-fixes-2fa-log-error-making-people-think-they-were-hacked\/)\n[Russian army targeted by new Android malware hidden in mapping app](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/russian-army-targeted-by-new-android-malware-hidden-in-mapping-app\/)\n[Microsoft says Edge browser is now 9% faster after optimizations](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-says-edge-browser-is-now-9-percent-faster-after-optimizations\/)\n[New Android malware steals your credit cards for NFC relay attacks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/supercard-x-android-malware-use-stolen-cards-in-nfc-relay-attacks\/)\n[7 Steps to Take After a Credential-Based cyberattack](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/7-steps-to-take-after-a-credential-based-cyberattack\/)\n  * [Autofill](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/autofill\/)\n  * [Deprecated](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/deprecated\/)\n  * [Deprecation](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/deprecation\/)\n  * [Microsoft Authenticator](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft-authenticator\/)\n  * [Microsoft Edge](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft-edge\/)\n  * [Mobile](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/mobile\/)\n  * [Password Management](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/password-management\/)\n  * [Passwords](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/passwords\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/going-refurbished-can-save-you-1-349-on-a-macbook-pro\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/google-notebooklm-is-now-using-gemini-25-flash\/)\n\n\n### Comments\n  * ![YZZCfubwAYcgKtRhitg Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/uploads\/profile\/photo-1341815.jpg?_r=1746283861)\n######  [YZZCfubwAYcgKtRhitg](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1341815\/yzzcfubwaycgktrhitg\/) - 1 day ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36100 \"Link\")\nThey are literally forcing users to use edge lol. many innocent people will just download edge browser because of this. \n  * ![leexgx Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n######  [leexgx](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/779146\/leexgx\/) - 1 day ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36101 \"Link\")\nI use edge automatically anyway (adblock Built in, I try using chrome mobile but websites are practically unusable on mobile with ads) But it extremely bugs me that it will NOT use the system set autofill (on including address passwords\/payments) so I have to open chrome copy the password and paste it into edge) if chrome had a built in adblocker I wouldn't even use edge at all\n  * ![ZeroYourHero Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n######  [ZeroYourHero](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1214717\/zeroyourhero\/) - 1 day ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36102 \"Link\")\nAntitrust violation?\n  * ![XSp Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n######  [XSp](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1275951\/xsp\/) - 1 day ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36106 \"Link\")\nAnother walled garden dictating how it's users should use their own computers... Makes it easier for bad actors to exploit vulnerabilities too, since everyone is obliged to do use the same stuff, do the same thing, etc.\n  * ![Princeps Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n######  [Princeps](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1344053\/princeps\/) - 1 day ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36109 \"Link\")\nLOL this is after they updated their setup flow to encourage you to set up a Passkey, which requires setting your password autofill provider on iOS to Authenticator\n  * ![JustinFlynn Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n######  [JustinFlynn](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1224783\/justinflynn\/) - 18 minutes ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/#cid36121 \"Link\")\nSo I must have read this differently. \"If you want to use their services, you need to use their product.\" I don't use Edge either.\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Sharp Rhino story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/sharp-rhino.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/sharprhino-an-old-new-threat\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trur-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Microsoft passwordless](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/) Microsoft makes all new accounts passwordless by default ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-makes-all-new-accounts-passwordless-by-default\/)\n  * [ ![ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/) OpenAI document explains when to use each ChatGPT model ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-document-explains-when-to-use-each-chatgpt-model\/)\n  * [ ![Co-op](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/) Co-op confirms data theft after DragonForce ransomware claims attack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/co-op-confirms-data-theft-after-dragonforce-ransomware-claims-attack\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/) View y