"title": "Co-op confirms data theft after DragonForce ransomware claims attack",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/co-op-confirms-data-theft-after-dragonforce-ransomware-claims-attack\/",,
"summary": "The UK retail giant Co-op confirmed a data theft incident following a ransomware attack by DragonForce. Hackers accessed and extracted data of numerous current and past customers, though financial details and passwords were not compromised. The attack involved social engineering, leading to the breach of the network by resetting an employee's password. Co-op's systems were compromised on April 22, allowing attackers to access files containing password hashes. Co-op is currently rebuilding its systems with support from Microsoft and KPMG. The ransomware group DragonForce, operating as a ransomware-as-a-service, is linked to the attack. Threat actors involved in this incident use tactics associated with the Scattered Spider or Octo Tempest collectives.",,
