"summary": "U.S. prosecutors have indicted a 36-year-old Yemeni man, Rami Khaled Ahmed, believed to be involved in the Black Kingdom ransomware operation that targeted about 1,500 computer systems in the U.S. and elsewhere. The indictment relates to attacks from March 2021 until at least June 2023, impacting sectors such as healthcare, education, and recreation. The malware encrypted data or claimed to steal it, demanding Bitcoin ransoms. Researchers consider the malware rudimentary but damaging, having targeted Microsoft Exchange servers.",,
