"summary": "A supply chain attack on Magento e-commerce platforms has compromised between 500 and 1,000 stores through the use of 21 backdoored extensions by vendors such as Tigren, Meetanshi, and MGS. The backdoors allowed attackers to take control of e-commerce servers through PHP files, enabling actions like data theft and skimmer injection. Sansec researchers found that some of these extensions had been backdoored as early as 2019, but were only activated recently in April 2025. Major multinational enterprises, including those valued at $40 billion, are affected. MGS reportedly has a backdoor in its free StoreLocator extension. Tigren was in denial of an extension breach, while Meetanshi acknowledged a server breach. Sansec warned users and provided indicators of compromise to detect these backdoor extensions.",,
