"title": "Commvault CVE-2025-34028 Added to CISA KEV After Active Exploitation Confirmed",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html",,
"summary": "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has added a critical flaw, CVE-2025-34028, to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog following its active exploitation. This vulnerability impacts Commvault Command Center versions 11.38.0 through 11.38.19, allowing a remote unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code via a path traversal bug. It has been resolved in versions 11.38.20 onwards. The cybersecurity firm watchTowr Labs identified this flaw, stating that the issue involves a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) induced by a malicious ZIP file, leading to remote code execution. Federal agencies are mandated to patch this vulnerability by May 23, 2025.",,
