"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AI Security Report](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiS3-N1dwbpW7jXMhyphenhyphen7_p0Q8s9OQpjbWqTZnBlYaqu9QuZ_QI95w6k63h9N3aySEjPfW-HRm2OF_sZXTaHFzoXUl0YRkOrNcN1ZJborZ4gVo_b_UycMQNROnrvtttC82SSaeuCqQPGbL2UH6rigwqJ2AVAgo-Ul8Gv58IK5OlxXTdWZT8HYPXB3aC-NX_a5\/s728-rw-e30\/f5e18cb2ed9e429ab490b482f9e990a8.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/threatlabz-ai-report-d)\n# [Commvault CVE-2025-34028 Added to CISA KEV After Active Exploitation Confirmed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html)\n_\ue802_ May 05, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Zero-Day\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiaPB2hvM7t0fKDqTHmLfXnPjYeGprAHSMkVmA66Wz51itW6sl_qZQLYzngCBcbwkjV0u8PAWdjaCiBk_YOWGwdsv9DSce9ho23QcpQoW-pcdGQ36RJ25tlmSEZ0tbSFEhWuM7dVNi9ELyDPN00Si_qNsRE4_A0DsPwd5BiBURTOBZiTwTe62Y_5dmKsQ2m\/s728-rw-e365\/comm.jpg)\nThe U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has [added](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/news-events\/alerts\/2025\/05\/02\/cisa-adds-two-known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog) a maximum-severity security flaw impacting Commvault Command Center to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog, a little over a week after it was publicly disclosed.\nThe vulnerability in question is CVE-2025-34028 (CVSS score: 10.0), a path traversal bug that affects 11.38 Innovation Release, from versions 11.38.0 through 11.38.19. It has been addressed in versions 11.38.20 and 11.38.25.\n\"Commvault Command Center contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code,\" CISA [said](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog).\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe flaw essentially permits an attacker to upload ZIP files that, when decompressed on the target server, could result in remote code execution.\nCybersecurity company watchTowr Labs, which was credited with discovering and reporting the bug, [said](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/critical-commvault-command-center-flaw.html) the problem resides in an endpoint called \"deployWebpackage.do\" that triggers a pre-authenticated Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF), ultimately resulting in code execution when using a ZIP archive file containing a malicious .JSP file.\nIt's currently not known in what context the vulnerability is being exploited, but the development makes it the second Commvault flaw to be weaponized in real-world attacks after [CVE-2025-3928](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-confirms-hackers-exploited.html) (CVSS score: 8.7), an unspecified issue in the Commvault Web Server that allows a remote, authenticated attacker to create and execute web shells.\nThe company revealed last week that the exploitation activity affected a small number of customers but noted that there has been no unauthorized access to customer backup data.\nIn light of active exploitation of CVE-2025-34028, Federal Civilian Executive Branch (FCEB) agencies are required to apply the necessary patches by May 23, 2025, to secure their networks.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_ Share on Linkedin](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf281_ Share on Reddit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf0e0_ Share on Email](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve-2025-34028-added-to-cisa.html#link_share) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/commvault-cve