"title": "Peru denies it was hit by ransomware attack following Rhysida claims",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/peru-rhysida-ransomware-claims-denied",,
"summary": "The Peruvian government has refuted claims made by the Rhysida ransomware gang regarding a takeover of its digital platform. While the central government maintained its operations were unaffected, they acknowledged a security breach in the tax administration website of Piura, a regional capital. The ransomware group demanded a ransom of 5 bitcoins, equivalent to roughly $472,000, alleging data theft. The Piura Tax Administration confirmed a cyberattack occurred on March 29, affecting their operations for 48 hours but denied any data loss. Peru's federal authorities are investigating and have urged other state entities to report cybersecurity incidents to the National Centre for Digital Security.",,
