"summary": "A new 'Bring Your Own Installer' technique is being used to bypass SentinelOne's tamper protection, allowing attackers to disable endpoint detection and response (EDR) agents and deploy Babuk ransomware. This attack exploits a gap in the SentinelOne installer during the agent upgrade process. The attack allows threat actors to terminate EDR agents, leaving devices vulnerable to ransomware attacks. SentinelOne recommends enabling 'Online Authorization' for mitigating this risk.",,
