"summary": "A critical security vulnerability designated as CVE-2025-3248 has been identified in the Langflow platform, affecting the \/api\/v1\/validate\/code endpoint due to missing authentication. This flaw allows remote, unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code on the server. The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has added this vulnerability to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog after evidence of active exploitation surfaced. The vulnerability has a CVSS score of 9.8, making it extremely severe. Langflow's vulnerability has been addressed in version 1.3.0. Horizon3.ai discovered and reported the issue, and a proof-of-concept exploit was made available in April 2025. The flaw potentially impacts 466 internet-exposed Langflow instances concentrated in countries like the U.S., Germany, Singapore, India, and China.",,
