"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AI Security Report](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiS3-N1dwbpW7jXMhyphenhyphen7_p0Q8s9OQpjbWqTZnBlYaqu9QuZ_QI95w6k63h9N3aySEjPfW-HRm2OF_sZXTaHFzoXUl0YRkOrNcN1ZJborZ4gVo_b_UycMQNROnrvtttC82SSaeuCqQPGbL2UH6rigwqJ2AVAgo-Ul8Gv58IK5OlxXTdWZT8HYPXB3aC-NX_a5\/s728-rw-e30\/f5e18cb2ed9e429ab490b482f9e990a8.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/threatlabz-ai-report-d)\n# [Critical Langflow Flaw Added to CISA KEV List Amid Ongoing Exploitation Evidence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html)\n_\ue802_ May 06, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCybersecurity \/ Vulnerability\n[![Critical Langflow Flaw](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhw6sLlizbyssgoIYMOEX4lqWt_3mEDPsaarzYSyeiNQTZKoNGTa_DtPhOqZnGkt-4ThjqSIj1aXjP_Ok6z0bu255_1ZbZNLSS8HrzZ_8K9ZY83bSWFQ_uW79mv7YpgZy-OSIHJPI-np-zeYk1fjLTHdC2FZI10C0OGeqCgCbU42DLnprh6Apua4hSEyZEC\/s728-rw-e365\/langflow.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhw6sLlizbyssgoIYMOEX4lqWt_3mEDPsaarzYSyeiNQTZKoNGTa_DtPhOqZnGkt-4ThjqSIj1aXjP_Ok6z0bu255_1ZbZNLSS8HrzZ_8K9ZY83bSWFQ_uW79mv7YpgZy-OSIHJPI-np-zeYk1fjLTHdC2FZI10C0OGeqCgCbU42DLnprh6Apua4hSEyZEC\/s728-rw-e365\/langflow.jpg)\nA [recently disclosed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/weekly-recap-critical-sap-exploit-ai.html) critical security flaw impacting the open-source Langflow platform has been [added](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/news-events\/alerts\/2025\/05\/05\/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog) to the Known Exploited Vulnerabilities ([KEV](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog)) catalog by the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), citing evidence of active exploitation.\nThe vulnerability, tracked as **CVE-2025-3248** , carries a CVSS score of 9.8 out of a maximum of 10.0.\n\"Langflow contains a missing authentication vulnerability in the \/api\/v1\/validate\/code endpoint that allows a remote, unauthenticated attacker to execute arbitrary code via crafted HTTP requests,\" CISA said.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-3 \"Cybersecurity\")\nSpecifically, the endpoint has been found to improperly invoke Python's built-in exec() function on user-supplied code without adequate authentication or sandboxing, thereby allowing attackers to execute arbitrary commands on the server.\nThe shortcoming, which affects most versions of the popular tool, has been addressed in [version 1.3.0](https:\/\/github.com\/langflow-ai\/langflow\/releases\/tag\/1.3.0) released on March 31, 2025. Horizon3.ai has been credited with discovering and reporting the flaw in February.\n[![Critical Langflow Flaw](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi7EnIcqjdp3sDmVX3JEFpFJybDpyXh3f9_z3bTPyBiDxZ6gOIwA46kLRBaaZzTxuCyysRh02_oa-jlHBDVDsej6EjOuxz8IDTmymX6-1upqM_IWXdl8-d9mJY4h8tEVb14p2zgJkA96JkHhgZ0tEzs2VhqC8krWNrwS-KKq5OxTQbtec7Eb0kCZ-0SenO-\/s728-rw-e365\/poc.jpg)\nAccording to the company, the vulnerability is \"[easily exploitable](https:\/\/horizon3.ai\/attack-research\/disclosures\/unsafe-at-any-speed-abusing-python-exec-for-unauth-rce-in-langflow-ai\/)\" and allows unauthenticated remote attackers to take control of Langflow servers. A proof-of-concept (PoC) exploit has since been made as of April 9, 2025, by other researchers.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-saas-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nData from attack surface management platform Censys [shows](https:\/\/search.censys.io\/search?resource=hosts&sort=RELEVANCE&per_page=25&virtual_hosts=EXCLUDE&q=services.http.response.body%3Alangflow) that there are 466 internet-exposed Langflow instances, with a majority of them concentrated in the United States, Germany, Singapore, India, and China.\nIt's currently not known how the vulnerability is being abused in real-world attacks, by whom, and for what purpose. Federal Civilian Executive Branch (FCEB) agencies have time until May 26, 2025, to apply the fixes.\n\"CVE-2025-3248 highlights the risks of executing dynamic code without secure authentication and sandboxing measures,\" Zscaler [noted](https:\/\/www.zscaler.com\/blogs\/security-research\/cve-2025-3248-rce-vulnerability-langflow) last month. \"This vulnerability serves as a critical reminder for organizations to approach code-validation features with caution, particularly in applications exposed to the internet.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fcritical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html&t=Critical%20Langflow%20Flaw%20Added%20to%20CISA%20KEV%20List%20Amid%20Ongoing%20Exploitation%20Evidence) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Critical%20Langflow%20Flaw%20Added%20to%20CISA%20KEV%20List%20Amid%20Ongoing%20Exploitation%20Evidence \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fcritical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fcritical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fcritical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html&text=Critical%20Langflow%20Flaw%20Added%20to%20CISA%20KEV%20List%20Amid%20Ongoing%20Exploitation%20Evidence)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[CISA](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/CISA)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Langflow](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Langflow)[Open Source](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Open%20Source)[Patch Management](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Patch%20Management)[remote code execution](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/remote%20code%20execution)[server security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/server%20security)[Vulnerability](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Vulnerability)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj5q7racGwMr5emA21v4uOtTjSF4X1U2UIB1VXdECJy_UlSerg-4nUz1sWoQPECXE52nExclTrzA8PSWUvGhM_NOY6KlHcLZHn61pnpthgtEfcAqeRnCVYq1timp_hDOibhzVIVe88exkuUO-W29dSFiS96BH2j2HD-_-aPf7X73C3l2V5FKCuy8t04tiTI\/s728-rw-e365\/cis-side-2.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/cis-controls-rsrcs)\nTrending News\n[ ![The Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\