"summary": "A supply-chain attack on Linux servers was detected, involving disk-wiping malware hidden in malicious Golang modules published on GitHub. The malware appears in three obfuscated Go modules that execute a destructive Bash script designed specifically to operate on Linux environments, wiping entire disks leading to data and system collapse. This threat underlines the vulnerabilities within the decentralized Go ecosystem where malicious packages can mimic legitimate ones, thereby facilitating undetected integration of harmful codes in developer projects.",,
