"summary": "The National Security Agency (NSA) is set to cut up to 2,000 civilian roles as part of a broader downsizing initiative by the Trump administration aimed at reducing the size of the U.S. federal government. The NSA's reduction is part of an 8% budget cut over the next five years for combat support agencies. The initiative also impacts other intelligence agencies like the CIA. The NSA plans to focus on offering early retirement and buyout options rather than mass layoffs. This restructuring follows recent leadership changes at the NSA and U.S. Cyber Command, with potential political motivations influencing decisions.",,
