"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/aispm-for-dummies.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/ai-security-posture-management-ai-spm-for-dummies?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY26Q1_INB_FORM_AI-SPM-for-Dummies-eBook&sfcid=701Py00000KWgAHIA1&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AI-SPMDummies)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * New Microsoft 365 outage impacts Teams and other services\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/)\n\n\n# New Microsoft 365 outage impacts Teams and other services\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 6, 2025\n  * 11:31 AM\n  * [1](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/#comments)\n\n\n![Microsoft 365](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/05\/06\/Microsoft-365.jpg)\nMicrosoft is investigating a new Microsoft 365 outage affecting multiple services across North America, including the company's Teams collaboration platform.\nSince the incident started over two hours ago, outage monitoring service Downdetector has [received thousands of user reports](https:\/\/downdetector.com\/status\/microsoft-365\/), with most affected users saying they're experiencing server connection and website problems when trying to access Microsoft 365 services and features.\n\"We're investigating an issue impacting multiple Microsoft 365 services and features in the North America region,\" Microsoft confirmed via its official Microsoft 365 Status Twitter account.\nIn a service alert (MO1068615) in the Microsoft 365 admin center, the company says impacted services include but are not limited to Microsoft Teams, adding that the most likely cause could be a faulty routing configuration for its Azure Front Door (AFD) cloud content delivery network.\n\"We're reviewing Azure Front Door (AFD) routing configurations and networking telemetry to isolate the source of the issue,\" Microsoft added.\n\"We've identified a section of AFD infrastructure is performing below acceptable thresholds. We're rerouting traffic to alternate infrastructure to mitigate impact. Meanwhile, we're also taking mitigation actions to expedite recovery of the Microsoft Teams service.\"\nWhile the company has yet to share more information on the outage's root cause and how widespread it is, Microsoft tagged this as a critical service issue in the admin center, which typically involves noticeable user impact.\n\u200bIn March, Redmond [mitigated another outage](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-causes-call-failures\/) that affected Teams customers, causing call failures and impacting other services such as Outlook, OneDrive, and Exchange Online, preventing users from checking email messages.\nThe same month, it [addressed an issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-exchange-online-outage-affects-outlook-web-users\/) that prevented Outlook on the web users from accessing Exchange Online mailboxes and a [week-long Exchange Online outage](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/week-long-exchange-online-outage-causes-email-failures-delays\/) that caused delays and failures when sending or receiving email messages.\nMore recently, in April, Microsoft [fixed an issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-investigates-global-exchange-admin-center-outage\/) blocking IT admins worldwide from accessing the Exchange Admin Center (EAC).\n_Update May 06, 11:31 EDT:_ Microsoft says the outage has been mitigated and that it also affected SharePoint Online and OneDrive for Business customers.\nA final admin center update added that the root cause was higher than normal CPU usage across systems part of Microsoft's AFD infrastructure.\n\"A small section of AFD infrastructure started to perform below acceptable thresholds. We have identified high Central Processing Unit (CPU) utilization as a potential contributing factor that resulted in impact. Further investigations are ongoing and more detail will be provided within the Post-Incident Report,\" it said.\n\"We're isolating the source of the high CPU utilization so that action items can be identified to prevent impact reoccurring.\"\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg)](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft: Licensing issue blocks Microsoft 365 Family for some users](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-licensing-issue-blocks-microsoft-365-family-for-some-users\/)\n[Microsoft investigates global Exchange Admin Center outage](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-investigates-global-exchange-admin-center-outage\/)\n[Microsoft Exchange Online outage affects Outlook web users](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-exchange-online-outage-affects-outlook-web-users\/)\n[Week-long Exchange Online outage causes email failures, delays](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/week-long-exchange-online-outage-causes-email-failures-delays\/)\n[Microsoft fixes Outlook paste, blank calendar rendering issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-outlook-paste-blank-calendar-rendering-issues\/)\n  * [Microsoft 365](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft-365\/)\n  * [Microsoft Teams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft-teams\/)\n  * [Outage](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/outage\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/why-easm-is-vital-to-modern-digital-risk-protection\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/critical-langflow-rce-flaw-exploited-to-hack-ai-app-servers\/)\n\n\n### Comments\n  * ![Seeprime Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/)\n######  [Seeprime](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1320594\/seeprime\/) - 44 minutes ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/#cid36137 \"Link\")\nThe persistent instability of Azure essentially locks Microsoft behind Amazon Web Services. Microsoft will spend marketing money, but continue to cut costs with imperfect AI. They may never improve enough.\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Sharp Rhino story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/sharp-rhino.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/sharprhino-an-old-new-threat\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trur-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) OpenAI document explains when to use each ChatGPT model ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-document-explains-when-to-use-each-chatgpt-model\/)\n  * [ ![Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) Microsoft ends Authenticator password autofill, moves users to Edge ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n  * [ ![Hacker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) New \"Bring Your Own Installer\" EDR bypass used in ransomware attack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-bring-your-own-installer-edr-bypass-used-in-ransomware-attack\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything ](https:\/\/www.picussecurity.com\/resource\/blog\/rethinking-automated-penetration-testing?utm_campaign=7149959-Red%20Report%202025&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=blog)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n  * [ ![View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/) View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition ](https:\/\/www.ctm360.com\/free-access?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=sidebar&utm_campaign=ctm360_bleepingcomputer)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[