"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers discovered a malicious package on the Python Package Index (PyPI) repository named 'discordpydebug' which masquerades as a Discord-related utility but is actually a remote access trojan (RAT). The package has been downloaded over 11,500 times. The trojan is capable of reading and writing arbitrary files, running shell commands, and exfiltrating data. The use of outbound HTTP polling helps bypass firewalls. Additionally, over 45 malicious npm packages were found imitating legitimate libraries, which suggest the involvement of a single threat actor.",,
