"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AI Security Report](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiS3-N1dwbpW7jXMhyphenhyphen7_p0Q8s9OQpjbWqTZnBlYaqu9QuZ_QI95w6k63h9N3aySEjPfW-HRm2OF_sZXTaHFzoXUl0YRkOrNcN1ZJborZ4gVo_b_UycMQNROnrvtttC82SSaeuCqQPGbL2UH6rigwqJ2AVAgo-Ul8Gv58IK5OlxXTdWZT8HYPXB3aC-NX_a5\/s728-rw-e30\/f5e18cb2ed9e429ab490b482f9e990a8.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/threatlabz-ai-report-d)\n# [NSO Group Fined $168M for Targeting 1,400 WhatsApp Users With Pegasus Spyware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html)\n_\ue802_ May 07, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Spyware\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhZGCwEHTeWpcmH7pcho4nVCj3nqvnjVzlDQ9rZRfKgwi3zLkb71An1vp0OBAUTsqQ8CaAh2ifs8wZ9MXNrAEqagfMeTQ_oLcy5SsDq8c1c8OEpmVfTBcHOtwxREXr670K3U0Ams6WIKQmpcDQA92vwpG3aBasaxUYOUyyFi5KiXHR3tgAW3LY0rQZNS4JV\/s728-rw-e365\/nso-whatsapp.png)\nA federal jury on Tuesday decided that NSO Group must pay Meta-owned WhatsApp WhatsApp [approximately $168 million](https:\/\/storage.courtlistener.com\/recap\/gov.uscourts.cand.350613\/gov.uscourts.cand.350613.736.0.pdf) in monetary damages, more than four months after a federal judge ruled that the Israeli company violated U.S. laws by exploiting WhatsApp servers to deploy Pegasus spyware, targeting over 1,400 individuals globally.\nWhatsApp originally filed the [lawsuit](https:\/\/www.courtlistener.com\/docket\/16395340\/whatsapp-inc-v-nso-group-technologies-limited\/?filed_after=&filed_before=&entry_gte=&entry_lte=&order_by=desc) against NSO Group in 2019, accusing the latter of using Pegasus to target journalists, human rights activists, and political dissidents.\nCourt documents released as part of the trial have [revealed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/thn-weekly-recap-ios-zero-days-4chan.html) that 456 Mexicans were targeted during the campaign, followed by 100 victims in India, 82 in Bahrain, 69 in Morocco, and 58 in Pakistan. In total, individuals across 51 different countries were targeted.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe attacks leveraged a then zero-day vulnerability in WhatsApp's voice calling feature ([CVE-2019-3568](https:\/\/nvd.nist.gov\/vuln\/detail\/CVE-2019-3568), CVSS score: 9.8) to trigger the deployment of the spyware. \nIn a ruling issued in December 2024, United States District Judge Phyllis J. Hamilton [noted](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/12\/us-judge-rules-against-nso-group-in.html) that Pegasus was sent through WhatsApp's California-based servers 43 times during the relevant time period in May 2019.\n\"Our case against spyware developer NSO made history when the court found that they broke both federal and state laws in the United States in December,\" Will Cathcart, head of WhatsApp at Meta, in a statement on X.\n\"And the jury's verdict today to punish NSO is a critical deterrent to the spyware industry against their illegal acts aimed at American companies and our users worldwide.\"\nCathcart added the company's next step is to secure a court order to prevent NSO from ever targeting WhatsApp again, adding it will be making a donation to digital rights organizations that are working to defend people against such attacks across the world.\nIn addition to the $167,254,000 in punitive damages, the jury determined that NSO Group must pay WhatsApp $444,719 in compensatory damages for the significant efforts WhatsApp engineers made to block the attack vectors.\nThe development is a major victory for privacy advocates and human rights organizations, who have repeatedly called out NSO Group for licensing its potent surveillance software to customers for keeping tabs on members of civil society.\nWhile NSO Group tried to evade liability by claiming that it does not have visibility into what its clients do with Pegasus, Judge Hamilton pointed out it cannot claim that \"its intent is to help its clients fight terrorism and child exploitation, and on the other hand say that it has nothing to do with what its client does with the technology, other than advice and support.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-GenAI-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"NSO was forced to admit that it spends tens of millions of dollars annually to develop malware installation methods including through instant messaging, browsers, and operating systems and that its spyware is capable of compromising iOS or Android devices to this day,\" Meta [said](https:\/\/about.fb.com\/news\/2025\/05\/winning-the-fight-against-spyware-merchant-nso\/).\nIn a statement shared with [Courthouse News](https:\/\/www.courthousenews.com\/meta-wins-168-million-in-damages-from-israeli-cyberintel-firm-in-whatsapp-spyware-scandal\/) and [POLITICO](https:\/\/www.politico.com\/news\/2025\/05\/06\/nso-group-pegasus-whatsapp-hack-170-million-damages-00332155), NSO Group said its technology plays a crucial role in preventing serious crime and terrorism, and that it intends to pursue appropriate legal remedies. The company was [sanctioned](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2021\/11\/us-sanctions-pegasus-maker-nso-group.html) by the U.S. government in 2021 for engaging in \"malicious cyber activities.\"\nApple, which filed a similar lawsuit against NSO Group, [dropped](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/09\/apple-drops-spyware-case-against-nso.html) it in September 2024, saying that continuing it could reveal sensitive details of its security program.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_ Share on Linkedin](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf281_ Share on Reddit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf0e0_ Share on Email](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html#link_share) [_\uf232_ Share on Wh