"summary": "The article discusses multiple security vulnerabilities in the on-premise version of SysAid IT support software. The vulnerabilities identified, CVE-2025-2775, CVE-2025-2776, CVE-2025-2777, and CVE-2025-2778, include XML External Entity (XXE) injections and an operating system command injection. These flaws can be exploited for pre-authenticated remote code execution, enabling attackers to obtain sensitive information and potentially gain full administrative access. SysAid has patched these vulnerabilities with version 24.4.60 b16. A proof-of-concept exploit is available, emphasizing the need for users to update to avoid potential exploitation.",,
