"summary": "Polish authorities, in collaboration with law enforcement agencies from Germany, the Netherlands, and the United States, have dismantled six DDoS-for-hire services and arrested four individuals suspected of operating these platforms. The services, known as Cfxapi, Cfxsecurity, neostress, jetstress, quickdown, and zapcut, were used to launch DDoS attacks targeting various sectors worldwide since 2022. These platforms were marketed as legitimate tools but were mainly used for illegal activities, allowing users to disrupt online services with ease. The operation, part of the ongoing Operation PowerOFF, also involved the seizure of nine domains and intelligence sharing by Dutch and German authorities.",,
