"summary": "The report focuses on the evolving ransomware landscape in 2025, highlighting the dominance of Ransomware-as-a-Service (RaaS) models, the rise in cross-platform attacks, and shifts in attack strategies such as prioritizing data exfiltration over encryption. Noteworthy disruptions include operations against LockBit and ALPHV\/BlackCat, although many groups quickly rebound. Sectors impacted include finance, education, technology, and government. Emerging group FunkSec utilizes AI tools in ransomware development. The article discusses the state of ransomware in 2025, highlighting new strategies used by ransomware groups, such as exploiting unconventional vulnerabilities and targeting less-secure entry points like IoT devices and misconfigured hardware. The Akira gang and others are innovating tactics to evade traditional defenses. The piece also warns of increasing ransomware threats in sectors like manufacturing, agriculture, and education, with regions like Europe being targeted despite strong cybersecurity defenses. Ransomware-as-a-Service continues to support less-skilled attackers. Organizations are urged to adopt a multi-layered defense strategy, secure IoT ecosystems, and prioritize employee training to combat ransomware threats.",,
