"title": "Ransomware Attackers Leveraged Privilege Escalation Zero-day",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.security.com\/threat-intelligence\/play-ransomware-zero-day",,
"summary": "Attackers associated with the Play ransomware deployed a zero-day privilege escalation exploit targeting the Common Log File System (CLFS) on Windows (CVE-2025-29824). The Balloonfly group, linked to Play ransomware, conducted the attack which involved deploying the Grixba infostealer and leveraging the zero-day to escalate privileges in U.S. company systems. The exploit involved manipulating kernel memory to gain control over the system, and although no ransomware payload was deployed, the attack showcased the serious threat posed by zero-days. The malicious activity was detected before the vulnerability was patched, extending the impact of this cyber incident.",,
