"title": "Microsoft: April updates cause Windows Server auth issues",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft's April 2025 security updates have caused authentication issues on some Windows Server domain controllers, affecting platforms including Windows Server 2016, 2019, 2022, and 2025. These issues are due to security measures linked to CVE-2025-26647, which mitigates a vulnerability allowing privilege escalation through Kerberos. The updates impact Active Directory Domain Controllers relying on certificate-based credentials using Kerberos. Home users are unlikely affected as domain controllers are primarily used for enterprise environments.",,
