"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/aispm-for-dummies.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/ai-security-posture-management-ai-spm-for-dummies?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY26Q1_INB_FORM_AI-SPM-for-Dummies-eBook&sfcid=701Py00000KWgAHIA1&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AI-SPMDummies)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft: April updates cause Windows Server auth issues\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft: April updates cause Windows Server auth issues\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 7, 2025\n  * 05:55 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/05\/16\/Windows-Server.jpg)\nMicrosoft says the April 2025 security updates are causing authentication issues on some Windows Server 2025 domain controllers.\nThe list of impacted platforms includes Windows Server 2016, Windows Server 2019, Windows Server 2022, and the latest version, Windows Server 2025.\nHowever, as the company further explained, home users are unlikely to be affected by this known issue since domain controllers are typically used for business and enterprise authentication.\n\"After installing the April Windows monthly security update released April 8, 2025 (KB5055523) or later, Active Directory Domain Controllers (DC) might experience issues when processing Kerberos logons or delegations using certificate-based credentials that rely on key trust via the Active Directory msds-KeyCredentialLink field,\" Microsoft said in a Windows release health update.\n\"This can result in authentication issues in Windows Hello for Business (WHfB) Key Trust environments or environments that have deployed Device Public Key Authentication (also known as Machine PKINIT).\"\nThese problems could also impact software relying on these two features for authentication, including but not limited to third-party single sign-on (SSO) solutions, identity management systems, and smart card authentication products.\nAffected auth protocols include Kerberos Public Key Cryptography for Initial Authentication (Kerberos PKINIT) and Certificate-based Service-for-User Delegation (S4U) via Kerberos Resource-Based Constrained Delegation (RBKCD or A2DF Delegation) or Kerberos Constrained Delegation (KCD or A2D2 Delegation).\n## Auth issues linked to CVE-2025-26647 security patches\nAccording to Microsoft, these issues are [linked to security measures](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/protections-for-cve-2025-26647-kerberos-authentication-5f5d753b-4023-4dd3-b7b7-c8b104933d53) designed to mitigate a high-severity vulnerability tracked as [CVE-2025-26647](https:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/vulnerability\/CVE-2025-26647) that can let authenticated attackers escalate privileges remotely by exploiting an improper input validation weakness in Windows Kerberos, which [superseded NTLM](https:\/\/answers.microsoft.com\/en-us\/msoffice\/forum\/all\/ntlm-vs-kerberos\/d8b139bf-6b5a-4a53-9a00-bb75d4e219eb) as the new default auth protocol for domain-connected devices on all Windows versions released since Windows 2000.\n\"An attacker who successfully exploited this vulnerability could be assigned much greater rights by the Key Distribution Center to the certificate than intended,\" Redmond explains.\n\"An authenticated attacker could exploit this vulnerability by obtaining a certificate containing the target Subject Key Identifier (SKI) value from a Certificate Authority (CA). The attacker could then use this certificate to get a Ticket Granting Ticket (TGT) for the target user from the Key Distribution Center (KDC).\"\nAs a workaround, affected customers are advised to switch the AllowNtAuthPolicyBypass registry value in HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Kdc from \"2\" to \"1\" as detailed in[ this support document](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/protections-for-cve-2025-26647-kerberos-authentication-5f5d753b-4023-4dd3-b7b7-c8b104933d53#bkmk_registry_settings).\nLast month, Microsoft [mitigated another known issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-auth-issues-on-windows-server-windows-11-24h2\/) causing authentication problems on Windows 11 and Windows Server 2025 devices using the Kerberos PKINIT security protocol when Credential Guard is enabled.\nRedmond also released emergency out-of-band (OOB) updates in November 2022 to [fix a bug causing Kerberos sign-in failures](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-kerberos-auth-issues-in-emergency-updates\/) and other auth problems on domain controllers.\nOne year earlier, it [addressed authentication failures](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-emergency-updates-fix-windows-server-auth-issues\/) related to Kerberos delegation scenarios on Windows Server and [similar Kerberos auth problems](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-kerberos-authentication-issues-in-oob-update\/) impacting domain-connected devices running Windows 2000 and later.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft fixes auth issues on Windows Server, Windows 11 24H2](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-auth-issues-on-windows-server-windows-11-24h2\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows Server 2025 restarts break connectivity on some DCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-server-2025-restarts-break-services-on-domain-controllers\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows Server hotpatching to require subscription](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-server-hotpatching-to-require-subscription\/)\n[Microsoft: April 2025 updates break Windows Hello on some PCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-2025-updates-break-windows-hello-on-some-pcs\/)\n[Microsoft fixes Windows Server 2025 blue screen, install issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-2025-blue-screen-and-install-issues\/)\n  * [Active Directory](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/active-directory\/)\n  * [Authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/authentication\/)\n  * [Domain Controller](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/domain-controller\/)\n  * [Kerberos](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kerberos\/)\n  * [Windows Hello](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-hello\/)\n  * [Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server\/)\n  * [Windows Server 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server-2025\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/apache-parquet-exploit-tool-detect-servers-vulnerable-to-critical-flaw\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/block-ads-forever-with-a-adguard-lifetime-access-now-just-16\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Sharp Rhino story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/sharp-rhino.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/sharprhino-an-old-new-threat\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trur-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) OpenAI document explains when to use each ChatGPT model ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-document-explains-when-to-use-each-chatgpt-model\/)\n  * [ ![Hacker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) New \"Bring Your Own Installer\" EDR bypass used in ransomware attack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-bring-your-own-installer-edr-bypass-used-in-ransomware-attack\/)\n  * [ ![Microsoft 365](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) New Microsoft 365 outage impacts Teams and other services ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-microsoft-365-outage-impacts-teams-and-other-services\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition ](https:\/\/www.ctm360.com\/free-access?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=sidebar&utm_campaign=ctm360_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/) Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything ](https:\/\/www.picussecurity.com\/resource\/blog\/rethinking-automated-penetration-testing?utm_campaign=7149959-Red%20Report%202025&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=blog)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.8219918564966242)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n",,
