"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AI Security Report](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiS3-N1dwbpW7jXMhyphenhyphen7_p0Q8s9OQpjbWqTZnBlYaqu9QuZ_QI95w6k63h9N3aySEjPfW-HRm2OF_sZXTaHFzoXUl0YRkOrNcN1ZJborZ4gVo_b_UycMQNROnrvtttC82SSaeuCqQPGbL2UH6rigwqJ2AVAgo-Ul8Gv58IK5OlxXTdWZT8HYPXB3aC-NX_a5\/s728-rw-e30\/f5e18cb2ed9e429ab490b482f9e990a8.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/threatlabz-ai-report-d)\n# [Europol Shuts Down Six DDoS-for-Hire Services Used in Global Attacks](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html)\n_\ue802_ May 07, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananDark Web \/ Cybercrime\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiNf4frc_NepXcz7P0Eqk9AspgP92si36VWa3A-uxmXQ7HMNmrLsMW8mEdN-07QFkcHLIji7U7gdVHtrJ7uj-z4kwkkkqoXodkd9EyHXFoUa8l9nSheFClYICW7PgCHwI85D6u9kanbhCV4RBCbOBK1M2gQWopqzjHVIA4SYaGsNaYIbRElxtREhtD3Fu9k\/s728-rw-e365\/ddos.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiNf4frc_NepXcz7P0Eqk9AspgP92si36VWa3A-uxmXQ7HMNmrLsMW8mEdN-07QFkcHLIji7U7gdVHtrJ7uj-z4kwkkkqoXodkd9EyHXFoUa8l9nSheFClYICW7PgCHwI85D6u9kanbhCV4RBCbOBK1M2gQWopqzjHVIA4SYaGsNaYIbRElxtREhtD3Fu9k\/s728-rw-e365\/ddos.jpg)\nEuropol has announced the takedown of distributed denial of service (DDoS)-for-hire services that were used to launch thousands of cyber-attacks across the world.\nIn connection with the operation, Polish authorities have arrested four individuals and the United States has seized nine domains that are associated with the now-defunct platforms.\n\"The suspects are believed to be behind six separate stresser\/booter services that enabled paying customers to flood websites and servers with malicious traffic \u2014 knocking them offline for as little as EUR 10,\" Europol [said](https:\/\/www.europol.europa.eu\/media-press\/newsroom\/news\/ddos-for-hire-empire-brought-down-poland-arrests-4-administrators-us-seizes-9-domains) in a statement.\nThe services, named cfxapi, cfxsecurity, neostress, jetstress, quickdown and zapcut, are said to have been instrumental in launching widespread attacks on schools, government services, businesses, and gaming platforms between 2022 and 2025. \n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nEuropol said the platforms offered \"slick user interfaces,\" enabling malicious actors with little to no technical expertise to orchestrate DDoS attacks by simply entering a target IP address, choosing the type of attack, and paying a fee.\nStresser services, typically advertised on underground forums, are often disguised as legitimate stress-testing tools but are designed to disrupt access to web resources by letting their customers unleash a flood of fake traffic against a target site, making them inaccessible to real users.\n\"Unlike traditional botnets, which require the control of large numbers of infected devices, stresser\/booter services industrialise DDoS attacks through centralised, rented infrastructure,\" Europol noted.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEh3ESWnuTmf9FRAeoZEhkJ2rmHmc3EBi8UMb8iFhmjPua6Lt32iFOvNT_WiK4gTJYLWVk6vwEFKNgfowqxN9q1xoot_2ushs2Y9QCHvKT8Fj48XpupQFkjzdnBljWCfOLAehcDxW2GGQDZJOeLR6bIfguiRO70fptIaMIEanEWte_fannu9nllnuY6tCPiz\/s728-rw-e365\/QuickDown.jpg)  \n---  \nQuickDown Pricing Plans as of July 15, 2024  \nAccording to snapshots captured on the Internet Archive, [cfxsecurity](https:\/\/web.archive.org\/web\/20240517155349\/https:\/\/cfxsecurity.cc\/), hosted on the domains cfxsecurity[.]bet and \"cfxsecurity.cc,\" marketed itself as the \"#1 stress testing service\" and that it provided \"comprehensive stress test, ensuring your website and services are ready to weather any storm.\"\nThe service offered three plans, Starter for $20\/month, Premium for $50\/month, and Enterprise for $130\/month. [QuickDown](https:\/\/circleid.com\/posts\/20240607-profiling-a-popular-ddos-booter-services-ecosystem) (\"quickdown[.]pro\"), likewise, [priced](https:\/\/web.archive.org\/web\/20240715085514\/https:\/\/quickdown.pro\/) its kit for anywhere between $20\/month to $379\/month.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-eliminate-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nCloud security company Radware, in a [report](https:\/\/www.radware.com\/security\/threat-advisories-and-attack-reports\/common-trends-in-the-latest-generation-of-ddos-as-a-service\/) published in August 2024, revealed that QuickDown is among a new crop of stresser services that have adopted a hybrid architecture combining both botnets and dedicated servers. QuickDown is said to have introduced a \"Botnet addon and new plans related to the Botnet network\" in September 2023.\nThe latest action, conducted in collaboration with Dutch and German authorities, is part of an ongoing effort called Operation PowerOFF that aims to dismantle infrastructure facilitating DDoS-for-hire activity.\nIn December 2024, a set of 27 stresser services were [taken offline](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/12\/europol-dismantles-27-ddos-attack.html), alongside announcing charges against six different individuals in the Netherlands and the U.S.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Feuropol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html&t=Europol%20Shuts%20Down%20Six%20DDoS-for-Hire%20Services%20Used%20in%20Global%20Attacks) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Europol%20Shuts%20Down%20Six%20DDoS-for-Hire%20Services%20Used%20in%20Global%20Attacks \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Feuropol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/europol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Feuropol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Feuropol-shuts-down-six-ddos-for-hire.html&text=Europol%20Shuts%20Down%20Six%20DDoS-for-Hire%20Services%20Used%20in%20Global%20Attacks)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[botnet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/botnet)[Cloud security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cloud%20security)[Cybercrime](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cybercrime)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[dark web](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/dark%20web)[ddos attack](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/ddos%20attack)[Europol](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Europol)[law enforcement](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/law%20enforcement)[Online Services](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Online%20Services)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search