"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/ottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AI Security Report](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiS3-N1dwbpW7jXMhyphenhyphen7_p0Q8s9OQpjbWqTZnBlYaqu9QuZ_QI95w6k63h9N3aySEjPfW-HRm2OF_sZXTaHFzoXUl0YRkOrNcN1ZJborZ4gVo_b_UycMQNROnrvtttC82SSaeuCqQPGbL2UH6rigwqJ2AVAgo-Ul8Gv58IK5OlxXTdWZT8HYPXB3aC-NX_a5\/s728-rw-e30\/f5e18cb2ed9e429ab490b482f9e990a8.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/threatlabz-ai-report-d)\n# [OttoKit WordPress Plugin with 100K+ Installs Hit by Exploits Targeting Multiple Flaws](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/ottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html)\n_\ue802_ May 07, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Web Security\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhXPyVtflZRlV-ihA94_FHChQqbUOg7HxqdPBHAave1hCikscpzZD5NPaGiRNUuEaZgBRJpkCDWCHWwbUFPPlbn9XOgbPMUD_nCF_O1CyrNSG0eanjg88CFbOj7pwZ5AHBKsUpIGbbac-1_DijQ3fb6GvKZxVvmjjZ3ncx5av_6luFu79Zf-5Bq21ggrX7F\/s728-rw-e365\/wordpress.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhXPyVtflZRlV-ihA94_FHChQqbUOg7HxqdPBHAave1hCikscpzZD5NPaGiRNUuEaZgBRJpkCDWCHWwbUFPPlbn9XOgbPMUD_nCF_O1CyrNSG0eanjg88CFbOj7pwZ5AHBKsUpIGbbac-1_DijQ3fb6GvKZxVvmjjZ3ncx5av_6luFu79Zf-5Bq21ggrX7F\/s728-rw-e365\/wordpress.jpg)\nA second security flaw impacting the [OttoKit](https:\/\/wordpress.org\/plugins\/suretriggers\/) (formerly **SureTriggers**) WordPress plugin has come under active exploitation in the wild.\nThe vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2025-27007 (CVSS score: 9.8), is a privilege escalation bug impacting all versions of the plugin prior to and including version 1.0.82. \n\"This is due to the create_wp_connection() function missing a capability check and insufficiently verifying a user's authentication credentials,\" Wordfence [said](https:\/\/www.wordfence.com\/blog\/2025\/05\/recently-disclosed-suretriggers-critical-privilege-escalation-vulnerability-under-active-exploitation\/). \"This makes it possible for unauthenticated attackers to establish a connection, which ultimately can make privilege escalation possible.\"\nThat said, the vulnerability is exploitable only in two possible scenarios -\n  * When a site has never enabled or used an application password, and OttoKit has never been connected to the website using an application password before\n  * When an attacker has authenticated access to a site and can generate a valid application password\n\n\nWordfence revealed that it observed the threat actors attempting to exploit the initial connection vulnerability to establish a connection with the site, followed by using it to create an administrative user account via the automation\/action endpoint.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/ottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nFurthermore, the attack attempts simultaneously aim for [CVE-2025-3102](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/ottokit-wordpress-plugin-admin-creation.html) (CVSS score: 8.1), another flaw in the same plugin that has also been exploited in the wild since last month.\nThis has raised the possibility that the threat actors are opportunistically scanning WordPress installations to see if they are susceptible to either of the two flaws. The IP addresses that have been observed targeting the vulnerabilities are listed below - \n  * 2a0b:4141:820:1f4::2\n  * 41.216.188.205\n  * 144.91.119.115\n  * 194.87.29.57\n  * 196.251.69.118\n  * 107.189.29.12\n  * 205.185.123.102\n  * 198.98.51.24\n  * 198.98.52.226\n  * 199.195.248.147\n\n\nGiven that the plugin has over 100,000 active installations, it's essential that users move quickly to apply the latest patches (version 1.0.83).\n\"Attackers may have started actively targeting this vulnerability as early as May 2, 2025 with mass exploitation starting on May 4, 2025,\" Wordfence said.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html&t=OttoKit%20WordPress%20Plugin%20with%20100K%2B%20Installs%20Hit%20by%20Exploits%20Targeting%20Multiple%20Flaws) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=OttoKit%20WordPress%20Plugin%20with%20100K%2B%20Installs%20Hit%20by%20Exploits%20Targeting%20Multiple%20Flaws \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/ottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fottokit-wordpress-plugin-with-100k.html&text=OttoKit%20WordPress%20Plugin%20with%20100K%2B%20Installs%20Hit%20by%20Exploits%20Targeting%20Multiple%20Flaws)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Patch Management](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Patch%20Management)[Plugin Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.c