"summary": "Ahead of the Victory Day parade, Russian authorities imposed mobile internet restrictions in Moscow and surrounding regions due to security concerns. Kremlin spokesperson attributed this to potential drone threats from Ukraine, affecting multiple services like mobile banking and ride-sharing apps. These restrictions, not new to Russia, indicate a pattern of controlling internet access during significant events.",,
