"markdown": "![South African Airways](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_South_African_Airways_2f53fe4ef3.jpg)\nCredit: Aero Icarus \/ Flickr\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 7th, 2025\n# South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems \nSouth Africa\u2019s state-owned airline said a cyberattack on Saturday temporarily disrupted its website and several internal operational systems. \nSouth African Airways (SAA) said the attack also affected its mobile application but noted the IT team was able to contain the incident and \u201cminimize disruption to core flight operations.\u201d \n\u201cThey also ensured the continued functionality of essential customer service channels, such as the airline's contact centers and sales offices,\u201d the airline said in a statement published on Tuesday. \u201cNormal system functionality across all affected platforms was restored later the same day.\u201d \nThe airline did not respond to requests for comment about whether the incident involved ransomware. \nCEO John Lamola [said](https:\/\/www.flysaa.com\/about-us\/leading-carrier\/media-center\/media-releases\/newsroom) they are currently investigating the incident to \u201cdetermine the root cause\u201d and are looking into the potential leak of sensitive information. \nThe company reported the incident to the State Security Agency, the South African Police Service (SAPS) and the Information Regulator of South Africa \u201cas a precautionary measure.\u201d \nSAA said it plans to notify anyone who may have had information stolen during the attack. The company reported more than $300 million in revenue last year and services flights to 16 locations. \nAs of Wednesday afternoon, no hacking group had taken credit for the incident. \nSouth Africa continues to face an unprecedented assault on its major institutions by cybercriminal gangs. \nIn 2023, a ransomware gang [leaked the personal phone number and email](https:\/\/mybroadband.co.za\/news\/security\/505562-russian-group-hacks-south-african-department-of-defence-allegedly-leaks-ramaphosas-number.html) of the country\u2019s president alongside a portion of the [1.6 terabytes of data](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cna-confirms-data-incident) stolen from the country\u2019s defense department. \nSince then, cybercriminals have caused havoc with incidents involving a [state-owned bank](https:\/\/therecord.media\/development-bank-of-southern-africa-akira-ransomware-attack), an [energy giant](https:\/\/therecord.media\/southern-africa-utility-targeted-cyberattack), the [government workers pension fund](https:\/\/therecord.media\/lockbit-ransomware-takes-credit-for-south-african-pension-fund-attack) and the country\u2019s [national lab service](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-africa-national-health-laboratory-service-ransomware-recovery). \nIn the first four months of this year, threat actors have already breached South Africa\u2019s [government weather service](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-weather-service-cyberattack), the [largest chicken producer](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyberattack-delays-south-african-chicken-producer) and [one of the largest telecommunications companies](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-telecom-provider-discloses-data-breach-ransomware). \nLast week, South African telecom MTN Group [said it suffered a cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/largest-african-telecom-warns-of-data-exposure) that exposed the personal information of an unknown number of customers. The company is the largest provider in Africa. \nThe string of attacks prompted South Africa\u2019s government to enact a new law in April that [forces](https:\/\/inforegulator.org.za\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/04\/MEDIA-STATEMENT-INVITATION-TO-REPORT-SECURITY-COMPROMISES-THROUGH-THE-eSERVICES-PORTAL-.pdf) all organizations to report cyberattacks to the country\u2019s information regulator, an effort to facilitate the \u201cmonitoring of security incidents affecting personal information,\u201d regulators said. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems )\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [South Africa](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/south-africa)\n  * [Africa](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/africa)\n  * [airline](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/airline)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems May 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-airways-cyberattack-disrupted)\n  * [Trump picks private sector veteran for Pentagon CIOMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/trump-picks-private-sector-veteran-for-dod-cio-position)\n  * [Poland arrests four in global DDoS-for-hire takedownMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-arrests-four-ddos-hire)\n  * [Poland accuses Russia of \u2018unprecedented\u2019 interference ahead of presidential electionMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-elections-russia-hybrid-threats-disinformation)\n  * [California fines clothing retailer, orders changes in privacy business practicesMay 6th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/california-fines-clothing-retailer-privacy)\n  * [NSA to cut up to 2,000 civilian roles as part of intel community downsizingMay 6th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nsa-to-cut-up-to-2000-roles-downsizing)\n  * [Multiple iHeartRadio stations breached in DecemberMay 6th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/iheart-radio-stations-breached-december)\n  * [Peru denies it was hit by ransomware attack following Rhysida claimsMay 5th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/peru-rhysida-ransomware-claims-denied)\n  * [Ukraine detains alleged FSB agent recruited via TikTok for spying on militaryMay 5th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukraine-arrests-fsb-agent-spying-recruited-tiktok)\n\n\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n## [Stimmen aus Moskau: Russian Influence Operations Target German Elections![Stimmen aus Moskau: Russian Influence Operations Target German Elections](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/Main_Feature_65c13c676d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/stimmen-aus-moskau-russian-influence-operations-target-german-elections)\n",,
