"title": "PowerSchool hacker now extorting individual school districts",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/powerschool-hacker-now-extorting-individual-school-districts\/",,
"summary": "The article discusses a significant cybersecurity incident involving PowerSchool, where a hacker group is extorting individual school districts by threatening to release previously stolen student and teacher data unless a ransom is paid. This comes after a breach in December 2024 where the hackers accessed and downloaded databases containing sensitive information using compromised credentials. Despite PowerSchool paying a ransom in hopes of securing the data, the hackers did not delete the data as promised and are now continuing their extortion activities. Affected products include PowerSchool's customer support portal and database systems. The education sector, particularly K-12 school districts in the U.S., Canada, and other countries, is directly impacted.",,
