"summary": "Cisco has issued patches for a critical vulnerability in its IOS XE Wireless Controller, tracked as CVE-2025-20188, with a CVSS score of 10.0. This vulnerability allows unauthenticated remote attackers to upload arbitrary files due to a hard-coded JSON Web Token (JWT). The exploit allows execution of arbitrary commands with root privileges if the Out-of-Band AP Image Download feature is enabled. Affected products include various Catalyst Wireless Controllers. Users are advised to disable the feature or update to the latest version to mitigate the risk. There is no evidence of active exploitation in the wild.",,
