"summary": "Researchers at Google have identified new malware named 'Lostkeys' used by the Russian government-backed hacking group Coldriver in a cyber espionage campaign. This malware is capable of stealing files and system information. Traditionally, the group targets high-profile individuals through phishing. Lostkeys is delivered via a fake CAPTCHA page that releases malicious PowerShell code to the victim. Previous campaigns have included targets like diplomats, military advisers, journalists, and think tanks in NATO countries. Coldriver is associated with Russia\u2019s intelligence services and is known for stealing credentials and emails.",,
