"summary": "SonicWall has released patches for three security vulnerabilities in its SMA 100 Secure Mobile Access appliances. These flaws, identified as CVE-2025-32819, CVE-2025-32820, and CVE-2025-32821, could allow authenticated attackers to bypass security checks, manipulate file system permissions, and eventually achieve remote code execution with root privileges. Rapid7 reported these vulnerabilities could be chained together for a complete exploit. The vulnerabilities have affected products such as SMA 200, 210, 400, 410, and 500v, now addressed in version 10.2.1.15-81sv. Despite indications of potential exploitation in the wild, SonicWall has not confirmed real-world attacks.",,
