"title": "Cisco fixes max severity IOS XE flaw letting attackers hijack devices",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/cisco-fixes-max-severity-ios-xe-flaw-letting-attackers-hijack-devices\/",,
"summary": "Cisco announced a fix for a maximum severity flaw in its IOS XE Software for Wireless LAN Controllers. The vulnerability, identified as CVE-2025-20188, is due to a hard-coded JSON Web Token that could allow unauthenticated remote attackers to compromise devices. This vulnerability affects systems where the 'Out-of-Band AP Image Download' feature is enabled, allowing attackers to upload files, perform path traversal, and execute arbitrary commands with root privileges. Affected devices include certain Catalyst Wireless Controllers and Embedded Wireless Controllers within the Catalyst product lines. Cisco has released security updates to address this issue, although no active exploitations have been reported.",,
