"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers have identified a campaign targeting Portuguese-speaking users in Brazil. It abuses free trial periods of commercial remote monitoring and management (RMM) software to gain access to target systems. This campaign uses spam emails leveraging Brazil's electronic invoice system (NF-e) to trick users into clicking links leading to malicious content hosted in Dropbox. The attackers deploy RMM tools like N-able RMM Remote Access and PDQ Connect to access systems and can install additional tools post-initial compromise. Notable targets include C-level executives in various industries. The campaign is linked to an Initial Access Broker (IAB).",,
