"markdown": "![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_hero_tiny\/public\/2025-05\/toru-wa-r_tezel9XC8-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=5a187b4b&itok=Dh8xA-9J)\n![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_author_avatar_small\/public\/blog-author-pictures\/315909675_10166679624225114_40949048126495061_n.jpg.webp?h=050dc016&itok=61Uif09r)\nAlisha SmithHead of Product Marketing, Enterprise Security Group at Broadcom\nSHARE\n  * **With threats ramping up, an EDR solution that can\u2019t see the full picture is already a step behind.**\n  * **Before investing, asking the right questions can save you from getting stuck with an EDR that can\u2019t keep up.**\n  * **Certain endpoint security tools are built to make your life easier\u2014let us show you how.**\n\n\nRansomware hasn\u2019t just stuck around in headlines, [ _it\u2019s evolved_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/threat-intelligence\/ransomware-trends-2025). With [ _35 years in the making_](https:\/\/www.cnbc.com\/2024\/12\/30\/ransomware-35-years-on-history-behind-hacking-method-and-whats-next.html), it\u2019s gotten bigger and bolder. [ _Ransomware-as-a-service (RaaS)_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/feature-stories\/ransomware-gang) operators like [ _Medusa_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/threat-intelligence\/medusa-ransomware-attacks) are more organized than ever\u2014and they\u2019re lowering the barrier for entry. As if all this weren\u2019t bad enough, threat actors are now leveraging [ _AI and machine learning (ML)_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/ai-field) to power their efforts, making it easier than ever for inexperienced bogeys to launch enterprise-level attacks, often targeting endpoints as their first way in. \nThese new productions are slicing through ill-prepared organizations\u2019 first-line defenses like a hot knife across butter. Nearly six out of 10 (59%) IT and security professionals report an [ _increase in the volume and severity of malware attacks_](https:\/\/docs.broadcom.com\/doc\/how-to-feel-more-secure-about-edr-ebook). And small to medium-sized businesses (SMBs) with fewer resources and leaner security budgets are [ _feeling the heat_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/expert-perspectives\/help-wanted-bad-actors-apply-within) the most.\nTo protect millions of users across organizations from evolving threats, [ _compliance regulations are evolving too_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/blogs\/expert-perspectives\/identity-solutions), making reliable endpoint monitoring and fast response table stakes for avoiding fines and reputational fallout. \nBut an endpoint detection and response (EDR) solution is more than a layer of defense\u2014it's the foundation your security stack needs in times of uncertainty. And when it comes to such an important player, you need an EDR built on proven fundamentals, not just hype. \n## The right questions lead to the right protection\nChoosing the right security partner can be as stressful as vetting a new hire for that hard-fought headcount\u2014because in a sense, you\u2019re hiring an EDR solution to protect you. At the evaluation stage, everyone promises superior detection, speed and coverage, but how can you be sure they\u2019ll deliver?\nHere are four questions to ask that go beyond what looks good on paper: \n### What level of visibility are we talking about?\nThreat intel is a great place to start, but if it's only firing off alerts and not providing context, you\u2019ll waste time piecing things together yourself. The right EDR should give you a full view across all your endpoints with rich insight into attacker behavior, so you\u2019re ready to respond smarter and faster. \n### Does it play well with the rest of my security stack? \nFor your EDR to really shine as the MVP, it needs to integrate smoothly with the rest of your stack. A robust, reliable EDR comes with solid APIs to ensure interoperability with other tools. You want something that consolidates data and simplifies workflows all from one same place. Trust us, your security team will thank you for it. \n### How far does the protection actually reach? \nIf your workloads live in containers or on cloud platforms (and many probably do), your EDR needs to extend coverage beyond on-prem systems. Containers often get overlooked, but that\u2019s exactly why bad actors use them as hiding spots. Make sure your EDR can extend protection to all your containers while still integrating with your existing endpoints, giving cybercriminals no room to slink about. \n### How much heavy lifting is involved?\nLet\u2019s be real, security teams are often working with limited resources, time and bandwidth. That\u2019s why a truly user-first EDR solution should be effortless to deploy, simple to manage and flexible enough to adapt to your needs. You especially want to look out for ongoing vendor support\u2014that cherry on top that keeps things running smoothly and lets your team focus on staying proactive.\nWhen you ask the right questions, the best partner stands out. And you might just be looking at \u201cthe one\u201d. \n## The EDR with the right answers \nAs a trusted leader in cybersecurity and EDR, Carbon Black (one of two legendary portfolios offered by Broadcom\u2019s Enterprise Security Group) is sought after for reliability, transparency and long-term value. Organizations of all sizes have placed their hard-earned trust in us\u2014avoiding costly downtime from data breaches, driving significant cost savings and improving the efficiency of their security operations, [ _according to Forrester\u2019s Total Economic Impact\u2122 (TEI) report_](https:\/\/tei.forrester.com\/go\/carbonblack\/cloud\/index.html?lang=en-us). \nWith [ _award-winning solutions_](https:\/\/cybersecurity-excellence-awards.com\/2023-cybersecurity-product-service-awards-winners\/) like Carbon Black EDR, we delivered a composite organization a whopping 427% return on investment (ROI). If that\u2019s not enough to make your knees buckle, Broadcom\u2019s Symantec portfolio pushes endpoint protection even further with new, groundbreaking capabilities like [ _Symantec Incident Prediction_](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/using-ai-predict-stop-and-recover-next-ransomware-incident), which now leverages AI and threat intelligence to predict an attacker\u2019s next four or five moves with up to 100% confidence.\nOur industry-defining portfolio was built to grow with you\u2014today, tomorrow and beyond. \n### Do more than check boxes \nStay one step ahead of threats wherever they come from. With Symantec and Carbon Black, you\u2019re backed by two legendary forces in cybersecurity. We\u2019re here to strengthen your defenses and simplify your security with seamless integrations, comprehensive protections and scalable solutions that grow with your needs. \nBacked by one of tech\u2019s biggest R&D engines, our portfolio outpaces the usual \u201cgood enough\u201d offerings from all-in-one vendors. We don\u2019t want to just check your boxes. We want a partnership that\u2019s built on trust and innovation with gold-award defenses that meet you where you are. We\u2019re here to level up your protection\u2014without slowing you down. \n**More questions to consider.** Get your copy of the eBook [ _How to Feel More Secure About EDR_](https:\/\/docs.broadcom.com\/doc\/how-to-feel-more-secure-about-edr-ebook)for thefull list of questions to ask\u2014and the  _right_ answers to look for. \n![Symantec](https:\/\/www.security.com\/assets\/logo--white.20230425.svg)Symantec Enterprise Blogs\nYou might also enjoy \n[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_bundle_small\/public\/2024-08\/120341818_l.jpg.webp?h=51a72048&itok=wZnqfty4)](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/5-signs-you-are-ready-edr)\n4 Min Read\n## [5 Signs That You\u2019re Ready for EDR](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/5-signs-you-are-ready-edr)\n### How to tell you need a second line of defense \n![Symantec](https:\/\/www.security.com\/assets\/logo--white.20230425.svg)Symantec Enterprise Blogs\nYou might also enjoy \n[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_bundle_small\/public\/2025-01\/joshua-newton-Igct8iZucFI-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=9dd951d5&itok=uHpb2Yci)](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/edr-legend)\n5 Min Read\n## [The EDR That Became Legend](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/edr-legend)\n### From humble beginnings to unparalleled hits, Carbon Black helped create a chart-topping category \n![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_author_bio_small\/public\/blog-author-pictures\/315909675_10166679624225114_40949048126495061_n.jpg.webp?h=050dc016&itok=wM7BNDuj)\nAlisha Smith is the head of product marketing for Broadcom\u2019s Enterprise Security Group, which offers cybersecurity solutions from Symantec and Carbon Black.\nWe encourage you to share your thoughts on your favorite social platform.\n[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_hero_related_small\/public\/2025-04\/pawel-czerwinski-4vkaa4OvyCM-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=bd2e85f6&itok=HBdnQ3ye)Posted: 15 Apr, 20254 Min ReadUsing AI to Predict, Stop and Recover from the Next Ransomware Incident](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/using-ai-predict-stop-and-recover-next-ransomware-incident)[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_hero_related_small\/public\/2025-04\/florian-cordier-E6R0Kn8TKQg-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=790be497&itok=3IKdU7Lm)Posted: 10 Apr, 20254 Min ReadAnalysts Are Touting the Power of Symantec DLP](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/analysts-are-touting-power-symantec-dlp)[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_hero_related_small\/public\/2025-04\/henry-be-lc7xcWebECc-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=d627821a&itok=6owqHeg-)Posted: 4 Apr, 20256 Min ReadOptimize Data Classification at Rest With These Easy Steps](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/optimize-data-classification-rest-these-easy-steps)[![](https:\/\/www.security.com\/sites\/default\/files\/styles\/blogs_hero_related_small\/public\/2025-03\/mauricio-artieda-On6lAWkijIA-unsplash.jpg.webp?h=2f7726b9&itok=6fiBA9Tw)Posted: 3 Apr, 20254 Min ReadThe Evolution of App Control, A Carbon Black Legend](https:\/\/www.security.com\/product-insights\/evolution-app-control-carbon-black-legend)\n![Explore upcoming events](https:\/\/www.security.com\/assets\/images\/bolts.svg)\n## Explore Upcoming Events\nFind experts in the wild\n[See what's next](https:\/\/www.security.com\/broadcom-at-rsa-2025)\n## Get Broadcom Software and Symantec Enterprise Latest Blog Posts _In Your Inbox_\nClose\n",,
