"title": "Police dismantles botnet selling hacked routers as residential proxies",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/police-dismantles-botnet-selling-hacked-routers-as-residential-proxies\/",,
"summary": "Law enforcement authorities dismantled a botnet built over 20 years that infected thousands of routers to create proxy networks called Anyproxy and 5socks. Four individuals were indicted for operating these services, which sold access to compromised routers for a monthly fee. The networks were used to conduct illicit activities such as ad fraud, DDoS attacks, and data exploitation. The malware affected various router models, and the FBI has warned these are used for cybercrime activities.",,
