"title": "US surveillance watchdog says expanded use of facial recognition at airports should be voluntary",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-surveillance-watchdog-pclob-airport-facial-recognition-tech",,
"summary": "The U.S. Privacy and Civil Liberties Oversight Board (PCLOB) released a report expressing concerns about the use of facial recognition technology (FRT) at airport checkpoints. The report highlights issues of privacy, data retention, and demographic accuracy in FRT usage. It recommends improvements in transparency, accuracy across racial demographics, and limits on data retention. The report stresses that participation in FRT programs should remain voluntary. The TSA plans to expand FRT use across U.S. airports, but there is pushback from civil liberties advocates.",,
