"summary": "German law enforcement agencies have dismantled the cryptocurrency mixing platform eXch and seized its assets, including more than $30 million in digital currencies. This action was linked to the laundering of funds stolen in the $1.46 billion Bybit hack. eXch, known for preserving financial anonymity, was implicated in laundering over $200 million of the stolen cryptocurrency. The site's servers, data, and digital assets were confiscated. It operated on both clearnet and darknet since 2014, managing approximately $1.9 billion in cryptocurrency transactions. The operation aims to aid investigations into other cybercrimes.",,
