"markdown": "![eXch takedown, seizure](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_exch_takedown_splash_page_may2025_a99335b5ed.jpg)\nThe German law enforcement splash page on eXch.\n[James Reddick](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/james-reddick)May 9th, 2025\n# German operation shuts down crypto mixer eXch, seizes millions in assets\nGerman police have seized infrastructure belonging to the cryptocurrency platform eXch and confiscated more than $30 million worth of digital currency. \nOn April 30, the internet crime branch of Frankfurt\u2019s Public Prosecutor\u2019s Office, along with Germany\u2019s Federal Criminal Police Office (BKA), shut down the platform, which is believed to have been used to launder much of the funds stolen in the [$1.46 billion hack of Bybit](https:\/\/therecord.media\/north-koreans-initial-laundering-bybit-hack) in February. \nAccording to a BKA [release](https:\/\/www.bka.de\/DE\/Presse\/Listenseite_Pressemitteilungen\/2025\/Presse2025\/250509_exch_abgeschaltet.html), police seized the exchange\u2019s German server infrastructure, more than 8 terabytes of data and crypto assets worth about $38.2 million. \nThe sting was hastened by eXch\u2019s [proclamation](https:\/\/bitcointalk.org\/index.php?topic=577207.msg65286839#msg65286839) that it would be shutting down its operations on May 1 because of what an administrator called \u201can active transatlantic operation aimed at forcibly shutting our project down and prosecuting us for \u2018money laundering and terrorism.\u2019\u201d \n\u201cThe operators had initially announced at short notice that they would cease their service on May 1, 2025,\u201d the BKA said. \u201cThe authorities anticipated this and secured numerous pieces of evidence and leads. Despite a short preparation time, the platform's database and the associated crypto assets were seized. \neXch professes to be a privacy-minded exchange intent on preserving financial anonymity \u2014 a position that law enforcement and researchers say makes it ripe for money laundering. \nImmediately following the hack of Bybit, the platform accused eXch of serving as a conduit for hackers to launder the funds and requested that it freeze the funds, which was rebuffed. \nSubsequent investigations by threat researchers charted the flow of funds through eXch after the [exploit by North Korea\u2019s Lazarus Group](https:\/\/therecord.media\/lazarus-hackers-behind-bybit-crypto-heist). The blockchain research firm Elliptic [estimated](https:\/\/www.elliptic.co\/blog\/the-rise-and-fall-of-exch-the-dark-service-used-by-north-korea-to-launder-200-million-stolen-from-bybit#:~:text=Around%20%24200%20million%20of%20the,this%20service%20in%20the%20past.) that more than $200 million worth of Bybit\u2019s stolen cryptocurrency went through eXch, which said it had received an \u201cinsignificant\u201d amount of the stolen funds. \nAn eXch administrator did not immediately respond to a request for comment. \nGerman investigators estimate that since the service launched in 2014, cryptocurrency worth about $1.9 billion has been transferred through the exchange. Its services have been accessible on both the clearnet and the darknet. \nThey said they expect the findings in this operation to \u201calso contribute to the investigation of numerous other cybercrimes.\u201d \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=German operation shuts down crypto mixer eXch, seizes millions in assets)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=German operation shuts down crypto mixer eXch, seizes millions in assets )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [takedown](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/takedown)\n  * [seizure](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/seizure)\n  * [cryptocurrency](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cryptocurrency)\n  * [cryptocurrency mixers](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cryptocurrency-mixers)\n  * [mixer](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/mixer)\n  * [bybit](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Germany](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/germany)\n  * [server](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/server)\n  * [Law enforcement](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/law-enforcement)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![James Reddick](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/Headshot_9468680de9.JPG)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/james-reddick)\n[James Reddick](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/james-reddick)\nhas worked as a journalist around the world, including in Lebanon and in Cambodia, where he was Deputy Managing Editor of The Phnom Penh Post. He is also a radio and podcast producer for outlets like Snap Judgment.\n## Briefs\n  * [German operation shuts down crypto mixer eXch, seizes millions in assetsMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/exch-cryptocurrency-mixer-germany-takedown)\n  * [Hackers hijack Japanese financial accounts to conduct nearly $2 billion in tradesMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/hackers-hijack-japan-finance-accounts)\n  * [Captain of ship that damaged Baltic Sea cable arrested and jailed in Hong KongMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ship-captain-baltics-gas-pipeline-damage-arrested-hong-kong)\n  * [Russian state-linked Coldriver spies add new malware to operationMay 8th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/coldriver-russia-cyber-espionage-lostkeys-malware)\n  * [Despite ransom payment, PowerSchool hacker now extorting individual school districtsMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/despite-ransom-payment-powerschool-extorting)\n  * [South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems May 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-airways-cyberattack-disrupted)\n  * [Trump picks private sector veteran for Pentagon CIOMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/trump-picks-private-sector-veteran-for-dod-cio-position)\n  * [Poland arrests four in global DDoS-for-hire takedownMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-arrests-four-ddos-hire)\n  * [Poland accuses Russia of \u2018unprecedented\u2019 interference ahead of presidential electionMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-elections-russia-hybrid-threats-disinformation)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
