"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Google Pays $1.375 Billion to Texas Over Unauthorized Tracking and Biometric Data Collection](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html)\n_\ue802_ May 10, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananBiometric Data \/ Privacy\n[![Google](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhr7bUscIi13dXg3GTZyVBGGDAu0SqelQdrFZRi7iPas43DFi0K1IQ9s8v8kuM3ZLdyEtceULw0LbWFxTyZhIkDl7Bbp-WNjYI6gjQwrY9Rkx_OyCkRVE9k4XqSLIxvoMSw33qe26goX9GrSwfoZRmnnmkutNbLSAmrNai91RNTXVgpXYeEXu-T1VWyxOVC\/s728-rw-e365\/google.jpg)\nGoogle has agreed to pay the U.S. state of Texas nearly $1.4 billion to settle two lawsuits that accused the company of tracking users' personal location and maintaining their facial recognition data without consent.\nThe $1.375 billion payment dwarfs the fines the tech giant has paid to settle similar lawsuits brought by other U.S. states. In November 2022, it paid [$391 million](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2022\/11\/google-to-pays-391-million-privacy-fine.html) to a group of 40 states. In January 2023, it paid [$29.5 million](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/01\/google-to-pay-295-million-to-settle.html) to Indiana and Washington. Later that September, it forked out another [$93 million](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/09\/google-agrees-to-93-million-settlement.html) to settle with California.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe case, originally filed in 2022, related to unlawful tracking and collection of user data, regarding [geolocation](https:\/\/www.texasattorneygeneral.gov\/news\/releases\/ag-paxton-sues-google-deceptively-tracking-users-location-without-consent), [incognito searches](https:\/\/www.texasattorneygeneral.gov\/news\/releases\/ag-paxton-amends-google-lawsuit-include-incognito-mode-another-deceptive-trade-practices-act), and [biometric data](https:\/\/www.texasattorneygeneral.gov\/news\/releases\/paxton-sues-google-its-unauthorized-capture-and-use-biometric-data-and-violation-texans-privacy), tracking users' whereabouts even when the Location History setting was disabled and collecting the biometric data without informed consent.\n\"For years, Google secretly tracked people's movements, private searches, and even their voiceprints and facial geometry through their products and services,\" Texas Attorney General Ken Paxton [said](https:\/\/www.texasattorneygeneral.gov\/news\/releases\/attorney-general-ken-paxton-secures-historic-1375-billion-settlement-google-related-texans-data) in a statement.\n\"This $1.375 billion settlement is a major win for Texans' privacy and tells companies that they will pay for abusing our trust.\"\nLast year, Google [announced](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/06\/google-maps-timeline-data-to-be-stored.html) plans to store Maps Timeline data locally on users' devices instead of their Google accounts. The company has also rolled out other privacy controls that allow users to auto-delete location information when the Location History setting is enabled.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-GenAI-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe payment also rivals a [$1.4 billion fine](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/07\/meta-settles-for-14-billion-with-texas.html) that Meta paid Texas to settle a lawsuit over allegations that it illegally collected the biometric data of millions of users without their permission.\nThe development comes at a time when Google is the [subject](https:\/\/www.reuters.com\/sustainability\/boards-policy-regulation\/italys-moltiply-sues-google-3-billion-euro-lawsuit-over-market-dominance-2025-05-09\/) of intense regulatory scrutiny on both sides of the Atlantic, facing calls to break up parts of its business to satisfy antitrust concerns.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/google-pays-1375-billion-to-texas-over.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehac