"markdown": "[![The Independent Singapore](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5)](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/ \"Singapore News\")\n  * [The Independent Singapore](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-news\/)\n    * [Featured News](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/features\/)\n    * [International](https:\/\/theindependent.co\/)\n    * [SG Economy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/business\/sg-economy\/)\n    * [Singapore Politics](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-politics\/)\n    * [In the Hood](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-news\/in-the-hood\/)\n    * [Lifestyle](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/)\n    * [Celebrity](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/celebrity\/)\n    * [Entertainment](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/)\n    * [Lifestyle](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/)\n  * [About Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/about-us\/)\n    * [Our Philosophy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/our-philosophy\/)\n    * [Contact Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/contact-us\/)\n    * [Join Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/join-us\/)\n    * [T&Cs](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/tcs\/)\n    * [Privacy Policy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/privacy-policy\/)\n\n\n[![Logo](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5)](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/)\nSunday, May 11, 2025\n30 C\nSingapore\n  * [Home](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/home\/)\n\n\n[](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5)\n[Youtube](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/TheIndependentSingapore \"Youtube\")\n  * [The Independent Singapore](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-news\/)\n    * [Featured News](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/features\/)\n    * [International](https:\/\/theindependent.co\/)\n    * [SG Economy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/business\/sg-economy\/)\n    * [Singapore Politics](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-politics\/)\n    * [In the Hood](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/singapore-news\/in-the-hood\/)\n    * [Lifestyle](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/)\n    * [Celebrity](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/celebrity\/)\n    * [Entertainment](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/)\n      * [Gaming](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/gaming\/)\n      * [Movie](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/movie\/)\n      * [Music](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/entertainment\/music\/)\n      * [Sports](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/sports\/)\n    * [Lifestyle](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/)\n      * [Fashion](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/fashion\/)\n      * [Food](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/food\/)\n      * [Travel](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/lifestyle\/travel\/)\n  * [About Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/about-us\/)\n    * [Our Philosophy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/our-philosophy\/)\n    * [Contact Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/contact-us\/)\n    * [Join Us](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/join-us\/)\n    * [T&Cs](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/tcs\/)\n    * [Privacy Policy](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/privacy-policy\/)\n\n\n[Subscribe](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5 \"Subscribe\")\n![StarHub Building](https:\/\/media.theindependent.sg\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/StarHub-Building-Facade-2-1068x601.jpg) Photo: StarHub\n[Business](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/business\/)\n1 min.Read\n# StarHub reports 18.4% drop in net profit to S$31.8M in Q1 2025 amid lower mobile, entertainment, and cybersecurity revenue\n[![Mary Alavanza](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5)](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/author\/mary\/ \"Mary Alavanza\")\nBy [Mary Alavanza](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/author\/mary\/)\nMay 11, 2025\n[WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=StarHub+reports+18.4%25+drop+in+net+profit+to+S%2431.8M+in+Q1+2025+amid+lower+mobile%2C+entertainment%2C+and+cybersecurity+revenue %0A%0A https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/starhub-reports-18-4-drop-in-net-profit-to-s31-8m-in-q1-2025-amid-lower-mobile-entertainment-and-cybersecurity-revenue\/ \"WhatsApp\")\n[ ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\?oc=5 \"More\")\n- Advertisement -\nSINGAPORE: Singapore-based telco company StarHub reported a net profit after tax of S$31.8 million for the first quarter of 2025, down 18.4% year-on-year (YoY) from S$38.9 million.\nThe company\u2019s earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortisation (EBITDA) also fell 5.2% YoY to S$100.2 million, from S$105.6 million, in tandem with higher depreciation and amortisation expenses. This was partly offset by a higher share of profits from joint ventures and lower tax expense, according to the telco\u2019s performance update released on Friday (May 9).\nTotal revenue fell 2.4% to S$540.5 million, from S$553.9 million in the same period last year.\nStarHub\u2019s regional enterprise segment rose 10% YoY, supported by a 20.2% increase in managed services and a strong order book. The group\u2019s broadband segment also grew 5% YoY, driven by sustained momentum in the migration towards higher bandwidth plans and the strength of its Infinity Play and bundling offers.\n- Advertisement -\nOffset by lower revenue contributions from mobile, entertainment, and cybersecurity, the group\u2019s services revenue slipped 0.7% YoY to S$464 million, from S$467.4 million.\nStill, the company\u2019s balance sheet showed a free cash flow of S$32.0 million and a low net debt to EBITDA ratio of 1.26x as of March 31, 2025.\n\u201cThe company remains focused on delivering long-term value, not only for shareholders, but also for customers, partners and the broader community,\u201d it stated in a press release on Friday.\n\u201cStarHub is taking steps to strengthen its consumer market presence, scale up its Enterprise business and Modern Digital Infrastructure platform and services across the region, and drive greater operational efficiency by leveraging on platforms it has invested in over the last few years. The Group will concurrently explore synergistic acquisitions that support its strategic growth and competitive positioning,\u201d it added. \/[TISG](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/)\n- Advertisement -\nRead also:[FLCT posts 13.8% YoY drop in 1HFY2025 DPU to 3 cents](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/flct-posts-13-8-yoy-drop-in-1hfy2025-dpu-to-3-cents\/)\n- Advertisement -\n  * Tags\n  * [Earnings Report](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/breaking-news\/earnings-report\/)\n  * [Starhub](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/breaking-news\/starhub\/)\n  * [StarHub Q1 2025](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/breaking-news\/starhub-q1-2025\/)\n\n\nHot this week\n[](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/dont-borrow-cash-to-the-limit-32-y-o-woman-faces-hk60k-month-housing-loans-after-real-estate-gamble-backfires\/ \"Don\u2019t borrow cash to the limit: 32 y\/o woman faces HK$60K\/month housing loans after real estate gamble backfires\")\n[Personal Finance](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/news\/business\/personal-finance\/)\n### [Don\u2019t borrow cash to the limit: 32 y\/o woman faces HK$60K\/month housing loans after real estate gamble backfires](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/dont-borrow-cash-to-the-limit-32-y-o-woman-faces-hk60k-month-housing-loans-after-real-estate-gamble-backfires\/ \"Don\u2019t borrow cash to the limit: 32 y\/o woman faces HK$60K\/month housing loans after real estate gamble backfires\")\nMay 11, 2025 [0](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/dont-borrow-cash-to-the-limit-32-y-o-woman-faces-hk60k-month-housing-loans-after-real-estate-gamble-backfires\/#respond)\nHONG KONG: A 32-year-old woman investor from Hong Kong...\n[](https:\/\/theindependent.sg\/ukrainian-marta-kostyuk-shakes-hands-with-russian-daria-kasatkina-at-the-italian-open-applauds-her-anti-war-views\/ \"Ukrainian Marta Kostyuk shakes hands with Russian Daria Kasatkina at the Italian Open, applauds her anti-war views\")\n[Sports