"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Bluetooth 6.1 enhances privacy with randomized RPA timing\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/)\n\n\n# Bluetooth 6.1 enhances privacy with randomized RPA timing\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * May 11, 2025\n  * 11:21 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Bluetooth](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/05\/09\/bluetooth.jpg)\nThe Bluetooth Special Interest Group (SIG) has announced Bluetooth Core Specification 6.1, bringing important improvements to the popular wireless communication protocol.\nOne new feature highlighted in the latest release is the increased device privacy via randomized Resolvable Private Addresses (RPA) updates.\n\"Randomizing the timing of address changes makes it much more difficult for third parties to track or correlate device activity over time,\" [reads SIG's announcement](https:\/\/www.bluetooth.com\/blog\/delivering-on-the-bi-annual-release-schedule-bluetooth-core-6-1-is-here\/).\nA Resolvable Private Address (RPA) is a Bluetooth address created to look random and is used in place of a device's fixed MAC address to protect user privacy. It allows trusted devices to securely reconnect without revealing their true identity.\nCurrently, RPAs are updated at fixed intervals, usually every 15 minutes, which introduces a level of predictability. This predictability can be exploited in correlation attacks, making long-term tracking possible.\nBluetooth 6.1 improves privacy by randomizing the RPA updates between 8 and 15 minutes (default), while also allowing custom values between the range of 1 second to 1 hour.\nThe Controller picks a random value in the defined range using a NIST-approved random number generator, and updates the RPA. This makes tracking significantly harder, as there is no pattern in the value selection.\nMore details about how the new privacy feature works can be found in the [specification document](https:\/\/files.bluetooth.com\/download\/core_v6-1\/) published along with the announcement.\nAnother feature highlighted in the announcement is better power efficiency starting from Bluetooth 6.1, which stems from allowing the chip (Controller) to autonomously handle the randomized RPA updates.\nSpecifically, the Bluetooth chip will choose the randomized timing intervals and generate and update the RPA internally without waking the host device.\nThis saves CPU cycles and memory operations, so much power is saved when conditions are met. For smaller devices like fitness bands, earbuds, and IoT sensors, this could make a big difference in battery life.\nWhile Bluetooth 6.1 has made exciting steps forward, it's important to underline that actual support in hardware and firmware may take years to arrive.\nThe first wave of chips with Bluetooth 6.1 should not be realistically expected before 2026, and even then, early implementations may not immediately expose all the newly available features, as testing and validation may be required.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Brave's Cookiecrumbler tool taps community to help block cookie notices](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/braves-cookiecrumbler-tool-taps-community-to-help-block-cookie-notices\/)\n[Microsoft Teams will soon block screen capture during meetings](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-teams-will-soon-block-screen-capture-during-meetings\/)\n[Google fixes actively exploited FreeType flaw on Android](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/google-fixes-actively-exploited-freetype-flaw-on-android\/)\n[Microsoft ends Authenticator password autofill, moves users to Edge](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-ends-authenticator-password-autofill-moves-users-to-edge\/)\n[TikTok fined \u20ac530 million for sending European user data to China](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/tiktok-fined-530-million-for-sending-european-user-data-to-china\/)\n  * [Bluetooth](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/bluetooth\/)\n  * [Mobile](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/mobile\/)\n  * [Privacy](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/privacy\/)\n  * [Tracking](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/tracking\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/chatgpt-is-finally-adding-download-as-pdf-for-deep-research\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Microsoft Teams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Microsoft Teams will soon block screen capture during meetings ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-teams-will-soon-block-screen-capture-during-meetings\/)\n  * [ ![Pearson](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Education giant Pearson hit by cyberattack exposing customer data ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/education-giant-pearson-hit-by-cyberattack-exposing-customer-data\/)\n  * [ ![NPM supply chain](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Supply chain attack hits npm package with 45,000 weekly downloads ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/supply-chain-attack-hits-npm-package-with-45-000-weekly-downloads\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n  * [ ![View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) View your organization's attack surface & digital frauds - at no cost. Register now for CTM360's Community Edition ](https:\/\/www.ctm360.com\/free-access?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=sidebar&utm_campaign=ctm360_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/) Rethinking Automated Penetration Testing: Why Validation Changes Everything ](https:\/\/www.picussecurity.com\/resource\/blog\/rethinking-automated-penetration-testing?utm_campaign=7149959-Red%20Report%202025&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=blog)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.31935369297156124)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n",,
