"markdown": "X\n[News](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/news)\n[Telecom & Internet](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/telecom-internet)\nStaff Reporter \n, [ Singapore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/market\/singapore)\nPublished: \n_ 4 minutes ago _\n![](https:\/\/news.google.com\/s3\/files\/styles\/article_details_tablet_image\/public\/2025-05\/starhub-building-logo-side-in-portrait-1.jpg.webp?itok=xw9Cx9DS)\nPhoto from press release.\n#  StarHub\u2019s net earnings down 18.4% in Q1 \n**Regional enterprise and broadband gains were offset by lower sales from other segments.**\n[StarHub](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-nokia-dell-complete-southeast-asias-first-5g-cloud-ran-trial) has reported a net profit after tax (NPAT) attributable to shareholders of $31.8m in the first quarter (Q1) of 2025, down 18.4% from last year.\nIn a bourse filing, the company said the lower net earnings were recorded following a 0.7% decline in service revenue, which settled to $464.0m. \nBroken down, StarHub logged 10% and 5% gains in its regional enterprise and broadband segments in Q1. However, these were offset by lower revenue contributions from mobile, entertainment, and cybersecurity due to the timing of project recognition.\nThe lower NPAT was also coupled with a 5.2% decline in earnings before interest, taxes, depreciation, and amortisation to settle at $100.2m. The company said this was due to lower gross profit from certain segment revenue declines, alongside higher operating expenditure from outsourcing costs and operating lease, offset by lower staff costs and R&M.\n## Follow the link for more news on \n[ Starhub ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/company\/starhub)\n[ Financial Statements ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/topics\/financial-statements)\n## Also Read\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-nokia-dell-complete-southeast-asias-first-5g-cloud-ran-trial)\n###  [ StarHub, Nokia, Dell complete Southeast Asia's first 5G Cloud RAN trial ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-nokia-dell-complete-southeast-asias-first-5g-cloud-ran-trial)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/telecom-internet\/news\/mobile-services-hit-2b-in-2029-5g-driving-revenue-stability)\n###  [ Mobile services to hit $2b in 2029 with 5G driving revenue stability ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/telecom-internet\/news\/mobile-services-hit-2b-in-2029-5g-driving-revenue-stability)\nJoin Singapore Business Review community \nSince you're here...\n...there are many ways you can work with us to advertise your company and connect to your customers. Our team can help you dight and create an advertising campaign, in print and digital, on this website and in print magazine. \nWe can also organize a real life or digital event for you and find thought leader speakers as well as industry leaders, who could be your potential partners, to join the event. We also run some awards programmes which give you an opportunity to be recognized for your achievements during the year and you can join this as a participant or a sponsor. \nLet us help you drive your business forward with a good partnership! \nYes, contact me \n[ I want to download the media kit  ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/digital-events)\n##  Most Read \n[ 1. Global trade war may spur prime property deals ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/commercial-property\/exclusive\/global-trade-war-may-spur-prime-property-deals) [ 2. Gates Foundation expands into Singapore with EDB support ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets\/news\/gates-foundation-expands-singapore-edb-support) [ 3. UOL, Hilton to open Asia Pacific\u2019s first NoMad Hotel in Singapore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/residential-property\/news\/uol-hilton-open-asia-pacifics-first-nomad-hotel-in-singapore) [ 4. HDB resale price growth slows to 1.6% as buyer caution rises: report ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/residential-property\/news\/hdb-resale-price-growth-slows-16-buyer-caution-rises-report) [ 5. President Shanmugaratnam urges \u2018new green revolution\u2019 to secure food future ](h