"summary": "Threat actors are leveraging fake AI tools as lures to spread the Noodlophile malware. These tools are advertised on platforms like Facebook to attract users seeking AI-based video and image editing applications. Victims are tricked into downloading malicious files purporting to be AI content, which actually contain information-stealing malware. The campaign primarily targets individuals interested in AI tools, as well as Vietnamese cyber-crime operators. The malware is distributed through a fake CapCut AI video editor site, ultimately leading to data theft including browser credentials and cryptocurrency wallet details. Some instances also include a remote access trojan.",,
