"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [Fake AI Tools Used to Spread Noodlophile Malware, Targeting 62,000+ via Facebook Lures](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html)\n_\ue802_ May 12, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananMalware \/ Artificial Intelligence\n[![Fake AI Tools Used to Spread Malware](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhZoVp2dX-q0ZHqxjc46BSTr-DolE_tHEmfCHVh2h57nLK5aKMZuq4GWTHspg5h556PqE_UN5ZCuUhj7BEKpxT6EK70zua7u_AxXGMwdPXXVKKyww8DmdS1_0lKzXsSGg9H-fDnxc5NpQtysIDV4J8OP67-3DlaekGgJuX741gz8ErIZdo98tYF9Q6tAQrZ\/s728-rw-e365\/ai-tools-malware.png)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhZoVp2dX-q0ZHqxjc46BSTr-DolE_tHEmfCHVh2h57nLK5aKMZuq4GWTHspg5h556PqE_UN5ZCuUhj7BEKpxT6EK70zua7u_AxXGMwdPXXVKKyww8DmdS1_0lKzXsSGg9H-fDnxc5NpQtysIDV4J8OP67-3DlaekGgJuX741gz8ErIZdo98tYF9Q6tAQrZ\/s728-rw-e365\/ai-tools-malware.png)\nThreat actors have been observed leveraging fake artificial intelligence (AI)-powered tools as a lure to entice users into downloading an information stealer malware dubbed **Noodlophile**.\n\"Instead of relying on traditional phishing or cracked software sites, they build convincing AI-themed platforms \u2013 often advertised via legitimate-looking Facebook groups and viral social media campaigns,\" Morphisec researcher Shmuel Uzan [said](https:\/\/www.morphisec.com\/blog\/new-noodlophile-stealer-fake-ai-video-generation-platforms\/) in a report published last week.\nPosts shared on these pages have been found to attract over 62,000 views on a single post, indicating that users looking for AI tools for video and image editing are the target of this campaign. Some of the fake social media pages identified include Luma Dreammachine Al, Luma Dreammachine, and gratistuslibros.\nUsers who land on the social media posts are urged to click on links that advertise AI-powered content creation services, including videos, logos, images, and even websites. One of the bogus websites masquerades as CapCut AI, offering users an \"all-in-one video editor with new AI features.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nOnce unsuspecting users upload their image or video prompts on these sites, they are then asked to download the supposed AI-generated content, at which point a malicious ZIP archive (\"VideoDreamAI.zip\") is downloaded instead.\nPresent within the file is a deceptive file named \"Video Dream MachineAI.mp4.exe\" that kick-starts the infection chain by launching a legitimate binary associated with ByteDance's video editor (\"CapCut.exe\"). This C++-based executable is used to run a .NET-based loader named CapCutLoader that, in turn, ultimately loads a Python payload (\"srchost.exe\") from a remote server.\nThe Python binary paves the way for the deployment of Noodlophile Stealer, which comes with capabilities to harvest browser credentials, cryptocurrency wallet information, and other sensitive data. Select instances have also bundled the stealer with a remote access trojan like [XWorm](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/05\/xworm-malware-exploits-follina.html) for entrenched access to the infected hosts.\n[![Fake AI Tools Used to Spread Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi1EpYii2DPp5eRAUVcN5V2Q_jmAWm1yUzAJJQFsCVYtVVvG2qNFqi1qi_RfB8FO9P4FlHNNV6P4T9Ooq7jXIL15tYo2gY6liyqnD3dnJcQC0kr0PinoCAh5rcVnbEnSuQOq4z8-ZiRvx4d0BIUmPAEabbnyXQMMdLhvhRm93S9i6dLZnOUjsGuL-CI-whb\/s728-rw-e365\/VideoDream_AI_Diagram_5.png)\nThe developer of Noodlophile is assessed to be of Vietnamese origin, who, on their GitHub profile, [claims](https:\/\/github.com\/luci205) to be a \"passionate Malware Developer from Vietnam.\" The account was created on March 16, 2025. It's worth pointing out that the Southeast Asian nation is home to a [thriving cybercrime ecosystem](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/04\/vietnam-based-hackers-steal-financial.html) that has a history of distributing various stealer malware families targeting Facebook.\nBad actors weaponizing public interest in AI technologies to their advantage is not a new phenomenon. In 2023, Meta said it [took down](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/05\/meta-takes-down-malware-campaign-that.html) more than 1,000 malicious URLs from being shared across its services that were found to leverage OpenAI's ChatGPT as a lure to propagate about 10 malware families since March 2023.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-eliminate-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe disclosure comes as CYFIRMA detailed another new .NET-based stealer malware family codenamed PupkinStealer that can steal a wide range of data from compromised Windows systems and exfiltrate it to an attacker-controlled Telegram bot.\n\"With no specific anti-analysis defenses or persistence mechanisms, PupkinStealer depends on straightforward execution and low-profile behavior to avoid detection during its operation,\" the cybersecurity company [said](https:\/\/www.cyfirma.com\/research\/pupkinstealer-a-net-based-info-stealer\/). \"PupkinStealer exemplifies a simple yet effective form of data-stealing malware that leverages common system behaviors and widely used platforms to exfiltrate sensitive information.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Ffake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html&t=Fake%20AI%20Tools%20Used%20to%20Spread%20Noodlophile%20Malware%2C%20Targeting%2062%2C000%2B%20via%20Facebook%20Lures) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Fake%20AI%20Tools%20Used%20to%20Spread%20Noodlophile%20Malware%2C%20Targeting%2062%2C000%2B%20via%20Facebook%20Lures \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Ffake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Ffake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Ffake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html&text=Fake%20AI%20Tools%20Used%20to%20Spread%20Noodlophile%20Malware%2C%20Targeting%2062%2C000%2B%20via%20Facebook%20Lures)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[artificial intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/artificial%20intelligence)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Facebook)[Information Stealer](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Information%20Stealer)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Python](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Python)[Remote Access Trojan](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Remote%20Access%20Trojan)[social engineering](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/social%20engineering)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj5q7racGwMr5emA21v4uOtTjSF4X1U2UIB1VXdECJy_UlSerg-4nUz1sWoQPECXE52nExclTrzA8PSWUvGhM_NOY6KlHcLZHn61pnpthgtEfcAqeRnCVYq1timp_hDOibhzVIVe88exkuUO-W29dSFiS96BH2j2HD-_-aPf7X73C3l2V5FKCuy8t04tiTI\/s728-rw-e365\/cis-side-2.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/cis-controls-rsrcs)\nTrending News\n[ ![The Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html) Linux io_uring PoC Rootkit Bypasses System Call-Based Threat Detection Tools ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/linux-iouring-poc-rootkit-bypasses.html)\n[ ![The Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html) Wormable AirPlay Flaws Enable Zero-Click RCE on Apple Devices via Public Wi-Fi ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/wormable-airplay-flaws-enable-zero.html)\n[ ![The Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html) Why top SOC teams are shifting to Network Detection and Response ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/why-top-soc-teams-are-shifting-to.html)\n[ ![The Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fake-ai-tools-used-to-spread.html) \u26a1 Weekly Recap: Nation-State Hacks, Spyware Alerts, Deepfake Malware, Supply Chain