"markdown": "![airplane](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_airplane_airbus_8e0ebd4dc1.png)\nImage: Kevin Wang via Unsplash\/Photomosh\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 12th, 2025\n# Airline carrying out deportation flights confirms cyberattack to SEC\nAn airline involved in [deportation flights](https:\/\/www.propublica.org\/article\/inside-ice-air-deportation-flights?ref=404media.co) on behalf of the Trump administration confirmed reports of a cybersecurity incident with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) on Friday. \nGlobal Crossing Airlines Group [said](https:\/\/www.sec.gov\/Archives\/edgar\/data\/1846084\/000095017025068004\/jetmf-20250505.htm) a cyberattack on May 5 gave hackers access to \u201csystems supporting portions of its business applications.\u201d The filing with the SEC confirms [reporting](https:\/\/www.404media.co\/globalx-airline-for-trumps-deportations-hacked\/) this week from the news outlet 404 Media, which was contacted by a hacker with information allegedly stolen from the company about ICE deportation flights. \nThe company, which has [facilitated](https:\/\/www.pogo.org\/investigations\/meet-the-ice-contractor-running-deportation-flights?ref=404media.co) hundreds of ICE deportation flights through a subcontractor since last year, offered few details about the incident. \nLaw enforcement has been contacted and a cybersecurity firm was hired but the company did not respond to several inquires about what data was taken and whether the hacker identified themselves. \nThe FBI and DHS declined to comment. \nGlobal Crossing Airlines Group noted that none of its operations were disrupted and that it does not believe the incident will have a \u201cmaterial effect on the company\u2019s financial condition.\u201d \nThe alleged hacker behind the incident, who called themselves Anonymous, told 404 Media that they [defaced](https:\/\/web.archive.org\/web\/20250505140730\/https:\/\/foqa.globalxair.com\/) the company\u2019s website before stealing flight records and manifests. The data provided to 404 Media was verified against public reports and incidents of deportations \u2014 and includes evidence of the company's involvement in [two notable flights in March](https:\/\/www.supremecourt.gov\/opinions\/24pdf\/24a931_2c83.pdf?ref=404media.co). \nThe company, which also refers to itself as GlobalX, is a Miami-based airline offering passenger and cargo flights in the U.S., Latin America, Europe and the Caribbean. \nIt reported a 2023 revenue of $160 million and makes about [$65 million annually](https:\/\/www.investing.com\/news\/stock-market-news\/earnings-call-global-crossing-airlines-reports-robust-q2-growth-93CH-3572766?ref=404media.co) from its work with ICE. \nThe Department of Homeland Security and ICE did not respond to requests for comment about the data stolen or the incident. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Airline carrying out deportation flights confirms cyberattack to SEC)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Airline carrying out deportation flights confirms cyberattack to SEC )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [airline](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/airline)\n  * [Trump administration](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/trump-administration)\n  * [Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/sec)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Airline carrying out deportation flights confirms cyberattack to SECMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/airline-carrying-out-deportation-flights-confirms-cyberattack-sec)\n  * [Moldova arrests suspect in ransomware attacks targeting Dutch firmsMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/moldova-arrest-suspect-ransomware-attacks-netherlands)\n  * [German operation shuts down crypto mixer eXch, seizes millions in assetsMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/exch-cryptocurrency-mixer-germany-takedown)\n  * [Hackers hijack Japanese financial accounts to conduct nearly $2 billion in tradesMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/hackers-hijack-japan-finance-accounts)\n  * [Captain of ship that damaged Baltic Sea cable arrested and jailed in Hong KongMay 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ship-captain-baltics-gas-pipeline-damage-arrested-hong-kong)\n  * [Russian state-linked Coldriver spies add new malware to operationMay 8th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/coldriver-russia-cyber-espionage-lostkeys-malware)\n  * [Despite ransom payment, PowerSchool hacker now extorting individual school districtsMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/despite-ransom-payment-powerschool-extorting)\n  * [South African Airways says cyberattack disrupted operational systems May 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-airways-cyberattack-disrupted)\n  * [Trump picks private sector veteran for Pentagon CIOMay 7th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/trump-picks-private-sector-veteran-for-dod-cio-position)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
