"title": "Weekly Recap: Zero-Day Exploits, Developer Malware, IoT Botnets, and AI-Powered Scams",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/weekly-recap-zero-day-exploits.html",,
"summary": "The article discusses the rise in zero-day exploits, developer malware, IoT botnets, and AI-powered scams. Key highlights are mechanisms through which fake security plugins on WordPress can enable remote admin access for attackers, impacting website security. Additionally, the report touches on AI-powered scams becoming more sophisticated, leveraging emerging technologies to bypass traditional defenses. The content discusses various cybersecurity threats and incidents. It includes zero-day exploits, malware distribution, and botnet dismantling operations. A key threat is the 5Socks proxy network using IoT devices, which was dismantled by law enforcement. The Play ransomware group exploited CVE-2025-29824. Russian actor COLDRIVER distributed LOSTKEYS malware, targeting Western advisors, journalists, and NGOs. Other threats involve malicious npm packages, SysAid vulnerabilities, Mirai botnet exploitation using devices with unpatched flaws, and financial damages awarded against NSO Group for their misuse of Pegasus spyware. This weekly cybersecurity recap discusses a variety of significant cyber threats and vulnerabilities, including vendor-specific zero-day exploits allowing access to sensitive files and malware campaigns. Key issues include zero-day vulnerabilities impacting major phone vendors, attacks using malicious IIS modules, enforcement of email rules by Microsoft, and financial account hijacking in Japan. Additionally, cryptocurrency scams and new malware discoveries are highlighted, along with geopolitical tensions between India and Pakistan leading to cyberattacks. Guidance for mitigating operational technology threats and a hack on the LockBit ransomware admin panel are also covered.",,
