"summary": "A T\u00fcrkiye-backed cyberespionage group exploited a zero-day vulnerability (CVE-2025-27920) in the Output Messenger app, allowing attackers to access sensitive files and deploy malicious payloads. The vulnerability was discovered in a LAN messaging application and patched in December. The cyber attackers, known as Marbled Dust, used this flaw to target Output Messenger users linked to the Kurdish military in Iraq. After gaining access, they could steal sensitive data and cause operational disruptions. Techniques like DNS hijacking were potentially used to gain authentication.",,
