"summary": "Six Bulgarian nationals were sentenced to a total of over 50 years in the UK for espionage activities under the direction of the Russian government. The group's activities included surveillance of Kremlin critics and other targets selected by Russian intelligence. The operation was managed by Jan Marsalek, a fugitive connected to Russian intelligence. The incident highlights the trend of outsourcing espionage activities and the challenges faced by host nations.",,
