"summary": "The article discusses the impact of Encrypted Client Hello (ECH), a new IETF standard, on internet privacy and security. While ECH enhances user privacy by encrypting TLS metadata, it limits network visibility, affecting threat detection and compliance. Major CDNs like Cloudflare and Akamai are adopting ECH, which poses challenges for enterprises in monitoring and ensuring security. This shift might accelerate the move from infrastructure-based security to an application-layer approach. Enterprises are advised to disable ECH on managed endpoints and evaluate its impact on their networks.",,
