"title": "Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft lifted an upgrade block that affected Safe Exam Browser users, preventing them from updating to Windows 11 24H2 due to compatibility issues. Safe Exam Browser, used to secure online exams, had a known issue in version 3.7 or lower, which was resolved with version 3.8 or later. The compatibility hold was added in September but was removed after developers fixed this problem. Affected users must update to the latest version before upgrading to Windows 11 24H2. Microsoft mentioned various safeguards and compatibility holds for other issues with Windows 11 updates, affecting specific hardware, software, and sectors.",,
