"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj_qMszEYVjwFa9p_Krb5PlKHZJ_qBguBZqxrUfXlqHzxZp2oUt8yjE6vjlrLVTK0Y1GtUlNL0C05SY-iq5GFsNkYrpPSTbPj30XarU3aO5dCJ-JkolvzdnxuynVOr9iXHx-dxJxuf-Ie7jyStTAnUzs8echAPUUsWcrutKu-pumRQLp2UIDfddyBqzblfx\/s728-e300\/training-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/training-d)\n# [Moldovan Police Arrest Suspect in \u20ac4.5M Ransomware Attack on Dutch Research Agency](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html)\n_\ue802_ May 13, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCybercrime \/ Ransomware\n[![Ransomware Attack](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEik1fgTx_HyseLqB9OE8HWyASnch91wHnw8zh_mHnNGsO4ysR-ghAHXgXhZjlLEdpJpzO_VwVIK6FgjjgoGBjf33cna3laddh0wykyg_CqZX8Rf9oi35-a9vx4BQUvxipuKKdQckfK0ckNox5cuEPHH1FKgh3Wp7luBHpAQfc3vHw1yCQkRRl8_qmzL9h_d\/s728-rw-e365\/policee.png)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEik1fgTx_HyseLqB9OE8HWyASnch91wHnw8zh_mHnNGsO4ysR-ghAHXgXhZjlLEdpJpzO_VwVIK6FgjjgoGBjf33cna3laddh0wykyg_CqZX8Rf9oi35-a9vx4BQUvxipuKKdQckfK0ckNox5cuEPHH1FKgh3Wp7luBHpAQfc3vHw1yCQkRRl8_qmzL9h_d\/s728-rw-e365\/policee.png)\nMoldovan law enforcement authorities have arrested a 45-year-old foreign man suspected of involvement in a series of ransomware attacks targeting Dutch companies in 2021.\n\"He is wanted internationally for committing several cybercrimes (ransomware attacks, blackmail, and money laundering) against companies based in the Netherlands,\" officials [said](https:\/\/politia.md\/ro\/content\/cetatean-strain-aflat-cautare-internationala-pentru-comiterea-infractiunilor-cibernetice) in a statement Monday.\nIn conjunction with the arrest, police seized over \u20ac84,000 ($93,000) in cash, an electronic wallet, two laptops, a mobile phone, a tablet, six bank cards, two data storage devices, and six memory cards.\nThe suspect's name was not disclosed. But he is said to have been detained after a search of his residence in Moldova. In at least one instance, the individual conducted a [ransomware attack](https:\/\/www.nwo-i.nl\/en\/artikel\/a-nightmare\/) on the Netherlands Organization for Scientific Research (NWO), causing material damage worth approximately \u20ac4.5 million.\nThe attack took place in February 2021, resulting in the leak of internal documents after the organization refused to pay up. It was attributed to a ransomware crew known as DoppelPaymer.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-eliminate-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"The attacker blocked network drives, rendered documents inaccessible, and stole some of our files,\" NWO [disclosed](https:\/\/www.nwo.nl\/en\/double-lockdown) at the time. \"Following a demand for a ransom, which NWO cannot and will not accept on principle, the organization published some of the stolen files.\"\n[DoppelPaymer](https:\/\/www.trendmicro.com\/en_us\/research\/21\/a\/an-overview-of-the-doppelpaymer-ransomware.html), a ransomware family that first appeared in June 2019, is believed to be based on the BitPaymer ransomware, due to similarities in their source code, ransom notes, and payment portals.\nIn March 2023, law enforcement authorities from Germany and Ukraine [targeted](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/03\/core-members-of-doppelpaymer-ransomware.html) suspected core members of a cybercrime group that has been behind large-scale attacks using DoppelPaymer ransomware.\nGermany also issued arrest warrants against three alleged DoppelPaymer operatives \u2013 lgor Olegovich Turashev, Igor Garshin (aka Igor Garschin), and Irina Zemlianikina \u2013 who are said to be the \"masterminds of the criminal group.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_ Share on Linkedin](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf281_ Share on Reddit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf0e0_ Share on Email](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/moldovan-police-arrest-suspect-in-45m.html#link_share) [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp]