"summary": "Microsoft has decided to continue providing security updates for Office apps on Windows 10 until 2028, extending support by three years after initially planning to end it in 2025. This move is intended to maintain security while users transition to Windows 11. The company also reminded users of the end of support schedules for Office 2016 and 2019 products, urging upgrades to Microsoft 365 Apps. Despite Windows 10 reaching its end of support, a large percentage of systems still run on this platform. No direct mention of vulnerabilities, malware, or threat groups related to this announcement.",,
