"title": "Fortinet fixes critical zero-day exploited in FortiVoice attacks",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fortinet-fixes-critical-zero-day-exploited-in-fortivoice-attacks\/",,
"summary": "Fortinet has released security updates to address a critical remote code execution vulnerability, CVE-2025-32756, in FortiVoice enterprise phone systems. The vulnerability, which is a stack-based overflow, was exploited as a zero-day and also affects FortiMail, FortiNDR, FortiRecorder, and FortiCamera. Attackers used this flaw to execute arbitrary code or commands via specifically crafted HTTP requests. Indicators of Compromise (IOCs) include unusual network scans and the enabling of 'fcgi debugging', which is not toggled by default. Fortinet suggests disabling the HTTP\/HTTPS administrative interface as a mitigation for those who cannot apply the updates immediately.",,
