"title": "South Korean researchers uncover another cyber-espionage campaign from the North",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/apt37-scarcruft-cyber-espionage-campaign-south-korea",,
"summary": "South Korean researchers have identified a new cyber-espionage campaign by the North Korean state-sponsored hacker group APT37, also known as ScarCruft, targeting organizations in South Korea with interests in national security. The group used phishing emails impersonating a North Korea-focused expert and a think tank to trick victims into opening malicious links. The emails contained Dropbox links aimed at deploying the RoKRAT malware, which can gather detailed system information and capture real-time screenshots. There is also evidence of Russian Yandex email accounts linked to the campaign. The group's operations are a significant part of North Korea's cyber warfare strategy, often involving social engineering tactics.",,
