"title": "New Intel CPU flaws leak sensitive data from privileged memory",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-intel-cpu-flaws-leak-sensitive-data-from-privileged-memory\/",,
"summary": "A recently discovered flaw in modern Intel CPUs, named 'Branch Privilege Injection' and tracked as CVE-2024-45332, allows attackers to leak sensitive data from privileged memory regions. The vulnerability impacts Intel CPUs from the ninth generation onward, including Coffee Lake, Comet Lake, Rocket Lake, Alder Lake, and Raptor Lake. This exploit can lead to sensitive data leakage like passwords and cryptographic keys by breaching user and kernel isolation. Although demonstrated on Linux, it is theoretically exploitable on Windows as well. Intel has released microcode updates to mitigate this flaw, though users may experience performance overheads.",,
