"summary": "A critical security flaw in SAP NetWeaver, identified as CVE-2025-31324, allows remote code execution and has been exploited by China-linked nation-state actors. The intrusions have impacted critical infrastructure in several sectors, including natural gas networks in the UK, water utilities in the US, and government ministries in Saudi Arabia. The attack is attributed to threat groups UNC5221, UNC5174, and CL-STA-0048, with malware like KrustyLoader, VShell, and SuperShell deployed. Active exploitation has been observed, and patches are available from SAP. The attack highlights strategic targeting of enterprise applications to maintain persistence in critical infrastructure networks.",,
