"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [China-Linked APTs Exploit SAP CVE-2025-31324 to Breach 581 Critical Systems Worldwide](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html)\n_\ue802_ May 13, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Threat Intelligence\n[![China-Linked APTs](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgSEkrKUhagfatMO2rFk0BkOn3IuanFsxGaa-ad1U3Yuy52MUkaRuIxMsrBGdSdYsSi_QlCFHxONnvQzayrGoSMMHcGFuIrEoY5AoKL6et9XTy45geq2DjsUtMAx52PCIXe0eiwRcl43S_aTUrtlD0nVmzyvdnOmLjtvsHz7tG4fkeekxBTztbP3LnuZeuY\/s728-rw-e365\/SAP-chinese-hackers.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgSEkrKUhagfatMO2rFk0BkOn3IuanFsxGaa-ad1U3Yuy52MUkaRuIxMsrBGdSdYsSi_QlCFHxONnvQzayrGoSMMHcGFuIrEoY5AoKL6et9XTy45geq2DjsUtMAx52PCIXe0eiwRcl43S_aTUrtlD0nVmzyvdnOmLjtvsHz7tG4fkeekxBTztbP3LnuZeuY\/s728-rw-e365\/SAP-chinese-hackers.jpg)\nA recently disclosed critical security flaw impacting SAP NetWeaver is being exploited by multiple China-nexus nation-state actors to target critical infrastructure networks.\n\"Actors leveraged [CVE-2025-31324](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/sap-confirms-critical-netweaver-flaw.html), an unauthenticated file upload vulnerability that enables remote code execution (RCE),\" EclecticIQ researcher Arda B\u00fcy\u00fckkaya [said](https:\/\/blog.eclecticiq.com\/china-nexus-nation-state-actors-exploit-sap-netweaver-cve-2025-31324-to-target-critical-infrastructures) in an analysis published today.\nTargets of the campaign include natural gas distribution networks, water and integrated waste management utilities in the United Kingdom, medical device manufacturing plants oil and gas exploration and production companies in the United States, and government ministries in Saudi Arabia that are responsible for investment strategy and financial regulation.\nThe findings are based on a publicly exposed directory uncovered on attacker-controlled infrastructure (\"15.204.56[.]106\") that contained event logs capturing the activities across multiple compromised systems.\nThe Dutch cybersecurity company has attributed the intrusions to Chinese threat activity clusters tracked as [UNC5221](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/01\/ivanti-flaw-cve-2025-0282-actively.html), [UNC5174](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/chinese-hackers-target-linux-systems.html), and [CL-STA-0048](https:\/\/unit42.paloaltonetworks.com\/espionage-campaign-targets-south-asian-entities\/), the last of which was linked to attacks targeting high-value targets in South Asia by exploiting known vulnerabilities in public-facing IIS, Apache Tomcat, and MS-SQL servers to drop web shells, reverse shells, and the PlugX backdoor.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nIt also noted that an uncategorized China-nexus threat actor is conducting a widespread internet scanning and exploitation campaign against SAP NetWeaver systems. The server hosted at the IP address \"15.204.56[.]106\" has been found to contain multiple files, including -\n  * \"CVE-2025-31324-results.txt,\" which has recorded 581 SAP NetWeaver instances compromised and backdoored with a web shell\n  * \"\u670d\u52a1\u6570\u636e_20250427_212229.txt,\" which lists 800 domains running SAP NetWeaver likely for future targeting\n\n\n\"The exposed open-dir infrastructure reveals confirmed breaches and highlights the group's planned targets, offering clear insight into both past and future operations,\" B\u00fcy\u00fckkaya noted.\nThe exploitation of CVE-2025-31324 is followed by the threat actor deploying two web shells that are designed to maintain persistent remote access to the infected systems and execute arbitrary commands.\nIn addition, three different Chinese hacking groups have been observed exploiting the SAP NetWeaver vulnerability as part of efforts to maintain remote access, conduct reconnaissance, and drop malicious programs -\n  * CL-STA-0048, which has attempted to establish an interactive reverse shell to \"43.247.135[.]53,\" an IP address previously identified as used by the threat actor\n  * UNC5221, which has leveraged a web shell to deploy [KrustyLoader](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/01\/chinese-hackers-exploiting-critical-vpn.html), a Rust-based malware that can used to serve second-stage payloads like Sliver, set up persistence, and execute shell commands\n  * UNC5174, which has leveraged a web shell to download SNOWLIGHT, a loader that initiates a connection with a hard-coded server to fetch a Go-based remote access trojan named VShell and a backdoor known as GOREVERSE\n\n\n\"China-linked APTs are highly likely to continue targeting internet-exposed enterprise applications and edge devices to establish long-term strategic and persistence access to critical infrastructure networks globally,\" B\u00fcy\u00fckkaya said.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEh3mEIu7goyAj8CeOZzutE9Hzr9dIEXnigMN7DoVAmTvYMgDPKc0i8GP1zoGqSq1-mRFaqpMf-sDEEkX8Sh4bdiV8iGKBlPQChA9MfXF6AjbhnxhX2LiIyN0o3XqXLETC_TZQ7vSQ6fNHZGFwKmZzqG2rUbzoWnwCxSOo9R5ALz3Zrf9YSI_ULki5exioUw\/s728-rw-e365\/SAPNetweaver005.png)\n\"Their focus on widely used platforms like SAP NetWeaver is a strategic move, as these systems are deeply integrated into enterprise environments and often host unpatched vulnerabilities.\"\n### SAP Patches New NetWeaver Flaw in May 2025 Patch[#](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html#sap-patches-new-netweaver-flaw-in-may-2025-patch)\nThe disclosure comes days after another China-linked unnamed threat actor dubbed Chaya_004 has also been [attributed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/chinese-hackers-exploit-sap-rce-flaw.html) to the exploitation of CVE-2025-31324 to deploy a Go-based reverse shell called SuperShell.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-eliminate-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nSAP security firm Onapsis [said](https:\/\/onapsis.com\/blog\/sap-security-patch-day-may-2025\/) it is \"seeing significant activity from attackers who are using public information to trigger exploitation and abuse web shells placed by the original attackers, who have currently gone dark.\"\nFurther analysis of these attacks has led to the discovery of another critical defect in NetWeaver's Visual Composer Metadata Uploader component. Tracked as [CVE-2025-42999](https:\/\/www.cve.org\/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-42999) (CVSS score: 9.1), it has been described as a deserialization vulnerability that could be exploited by a privileged user to upload untrusted or malicious content.\nIn light of ongoing active exploitation, customers of SAP NetWeaver are recommended to update their instances to the [latest version](https:\/\/support.sap.com\/en\/my-support\/knowledge-base\/security-notes-news\/may-2025.html) as soon as possible.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fchina-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html&t=China-Linked%20APTs%20Exploit%20SAP%20CVE-2025-31324%20to%20Breach%20581%20Critical%20Systems%20Worldwide) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=China-Linked%20APTs%20Exploit%20SAP%20CVE-2025-31324%20to%20Breach%20581%20Critical%20Systems%20Worldwide \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fchina-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/china-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fchina-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fchina-linked-apts-exploit-sap-cve-2025.html&text=China-Linked%20APTs%20Exploit%20SAP%20CVE-2025-31324%20to%20Breach%20581%20Critical%20Systems%20Worldwide)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Chinese Hackers](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Chinese%20Hackers)[critical infrastructure](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/critical%20infrastructure)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[remote code execution](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/remote%20code%20execution)[SAP NetWeaver](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/SAP%20NetWeaver)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)[Vulnera