"markdown": "![vulnerability](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_digital_danger_vulnerability_1661a0104c.jpg)\nImage: Getty via Unsplash+\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)May 13th, 2025\n# EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threats\nThe European Union launched on Tuesday its new vulnerability database to provide aggregated information regarding cybersecurity issues affecting various products and services. \nDespite being known as the [European Vulnerability Database](https:\/\/www.enisa.europa.eu\/news\/consult-the-european-vulnerability-database-to-enhance-your-digital-security), the service is more of a notification platform than a repository for vulnerability reports, resembling MITRE and the U.S. Department of Homeland Security\u2019s Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) Program. \nSpeaking to Recorded Future News last year, Hans de Vries, the head of the EU\u2019s cybersecurity agency ENISA, [said](https:\/\/therecord.media\/enisa-will-not-create-vulnerability-database-cyber-resilience-act) the agency did not want to create \u201ca huge database that can very much be hacked and have all the exploits in.\u201d \nThe CVE program is a critical utility within the cybersecurity sector, used by countless vendors, governments and critical infrastructure entities to identify and prioritise their response to new vulnerabilities that could expose their organisations to risk. \nENISA stated on Tuesday it was currently \u201cin contact with MITRE to understand the impact and next steps\u201d over questions regarding how that program is funded. \nLast month, the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) said that the MITRE Corporation will [continue operating](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cisa-extends-cve-program-contract-with-mitre) the CVE program for at least another 11 months after federal cybersecurity officials confirmed that they temporarily extended their contract with the organization to keep the platform running. \nAt the time, many in the cybersecurity community[ expressed alarm](https:\/\/therecord.media\/mitre-warns-of-cve-program-lapse-contract-expires) following a letter from MITRE\u2019s vice president which warned that funding for the CVE program was expiring and the federal government appeared to have no intention to renew the contract. \nA MITRE spokesperson told Recorded Future News that were the contract to lapse, no new CVEs would be added to the program and the CVE program website online would eventually cease. MITRE said historical CVE records will be available on [GitHub](https:\/\/github.com\/CVEProject). \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threats)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threats )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/technology)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [ENISA](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/enisa)\n  * [Vulnerability](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/vulnerability)\n  * [Database](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/database)\n  * [Department of Homeland Security (DHS)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/department-of-homeland-security)\n  * [MITRE](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/mitre)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Alexander Martin](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/headshot_79eb085f87.jpeg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\nis the UK Editor for Recorded Future News. He was previously a technology reporter for Sky News and is also a fellow at the European Cyber Conflict Research Initiative.\n## Briefs\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n  * [EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threatsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-launches-vulnerability-database)\n  * [Alabama says \u2018cybersecurity event\u2019 could disrupt state government servicesMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions)\n  * [States push WeChat for answers over money laundering allegationsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/states-push-wechat-for-money-laundering-answers)\n  * [Microsoft spots zero-day use in spy campaign against Kurdish military in IraqMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/microsoft-zero-day-spy-campaign)\n  * [South African influencers-for-hire target Ukraine\u2019s president in influence campaign, researchers sayMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-influencers-anti-zelensky-campaign)\n  * [Google to pay Texas nearly $1.4 billion over alleged data privacy violationsMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/google-texas-privacy-violations-billions)\n  * [Airline carrying out deportation flights confirms cyberattack to SECMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/airline-carrying-out-deportation-flights-confirms-cyberattack-sec)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
