"summary": "Twilio has denied being breached following claims by a threat actor known as Machine1337 who advertised to sell a large amount of Steam user records containing one-time access codes. The leaked data analysis suggested potential involvement of Twilio's backend systems, hinting at a possible compromise through a supply-chain attack, although Twilio stated no evidence of breach within its systems. The leaked data may have originated from an intermediary SMS provider. Steam users are advised to use additional security measures and monitor account activities.",,
