"summary": "Fortinet has patched a critical zero-day vulnerability, CVE-2025-32756, affecting FortiVoice among other products. This vulnerability, a stack-based overflow, allows remote unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code via crafted HTTP requests. Observed exploits have targeted FortiVoice systems. The affected products include FortiVoice, FortiMail, FortiNDR, FortiRecorder, and FortiCamera with specific vulnerable versions listed. No specific threat actors were mentioned, but IP addresses used by attackers were identified. Patching is recommended to protect against active exploitation.",,
