"summary": "Ivanti has addressed two security vulnerabilities in its Endpoint Manager Mobile (EPMM) software, one allowing authentication bypass (CVE-2025-4427) and the other facilitating remote code execution (CVE-2025-4428). These flaws have been exploited in limited attacks. Affected versions include 11.12.0.4 and prior, 12.3.0.1 and prior, and others detailed in the patch notes. Ivanti says that filtering API access can reduce risk, and that vulnerabilities in open-source libraries used in EPMM are under investigation. They have also addressed an authentication bypass flaw in Neurons for ITSM (CVE-2025-22462).",,
