"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Horabot Malware Targets 6 Latin American Nations Using Invoice-Themed Phishing Emails](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html)\n_\ue802_ May 14, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananWindows Security \/ Threat Intelligence\n[![Horabot Malware](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi2SzPScfH5aQVNeVYaqK2B2M-19lO1Rr9zK2zhn7DqPbnQ92GmIfBDRr37gq9jtVEFTiR45fWPcKQg-RYnIlodJnxDy2qR_ZBPmDDF_1n-BLzx_DRj48OcMxvWFHrAp0YGsrqyrV-om0jt0qdr9oEEX-G9Gj8eDPQRLI7yTvmrydugxOAl-qLUHssRZzXn\/s728-rw-e365\/invoice.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi2SzPScfH5aQVNeVYaqK2B2M-19lO1Rr9zK2zhn7DqPbnQ92GmIfBDRr37gq9jtVEFTiR45fWPcKQg-RYnIlodJnxDy2qR_ZBPmDDF_1n-BLzx_DRj48OcMxvWFHrAp0YGsrqyrV-om0jt0qdr9oEEX-G9Gj8eDPQRLI7yTvmrydugxOAl-qLUHssRZzXn\/s728-rw-e365\/invoice.jpg)\nCybersecurity researchers have discovered a new phishing campaign that's being used to distribute malware called **Horabot** targeting Windows users in Latin American countries like Mexico, Guatemala, Colombia, Peru, Chile, and Argentina.\nThe campaign is \"using crafted emails that impersonate invoices or financial documents to trick victims into opening malicious attachments and can steal email credentials, harvest contact lists, and install banking trojans,\" Fortinet FortiGuard Labs researcher Cara Lin [said](https:\/\/www.fortinet.com\/blog\/threat-research\/horabot-unleashed-a-stealthy-phishing-threat).\nThe activity, observed by the network security company in April 2025, has primarily singled out Spanish-speaking users. The attacks have also been found to send phishing messages from victims' mailboxes using Outlook COM automation, effectively propagating the malware laterally within corporate or personal networks.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nIn addition, the threat actors behind the campaign execute various VBScript, AutoIt, and PowerShell scripts to conduct system reconnaissance, steal credentials, and drop additional payloads.\nHorabot was [first documented](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/06\/new-botnet-malware-horabot-targets.html) by Cisco Talos in June 2023 as targeting Spanish-speaking users in Latin America since at least November 2020. It's assessed that the attacks are the work of a threat actor from Brazil.\nThen last year, Trustwave SpiderLabs [revealed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/04\/cybercriminals-targeting-latin-america.html) details of another phishing campaign targeting the same region with malicious payloads which it said exhibits similarities with that of Horabot malware.\n[![Horabot Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi-MwDKXD3_0rLNLPQwoyFbf5mEjmzD-gvvhZI3rtvBsj2yiuRmIKNzYH3ccV5cgj-MtPRdgCXsoM1pHXt6RQ9GpLg_v5idS0F5cDwh84hyphenhyphenbsPAkmNPm6T1kGnppGteyAr1MY581OXsWrj-CWn48a1R03cW7E4BsGv-DLCsezBYWGRE3sRB5KoJfsuvTNNc\/s728-rw-e365\/autoit.jpg)\nThe latest set of attacks starts with a phishing email that employs invoice-themed lures to entice users into opening a ZIP archive containing a PDF document. However, in reality, the attached ZIP file contains a malicious HTML file with Base64-encoded HTML data that's designed to reach out to a remote server and download the next-stage payload.\nThe payload is another ZIP archive that contains an HTML Application (HTA) file, which is responsible for loading a script hosted on a remote server. The script then injects an external Visual Basic Script (VBScript) that performs a series of checks that cause it to terminate if Avast antivirus is installed or it's running in a virtual environment.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-GenAI-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe VBScript proceeds to collect basic system information, exfiltrate it to a remote server, and retrieves additional payloads, including an AutoIt script that unleashes the banking trojan by means of a malicious DLL and a PowerShell script that's tasked with spreading the phishing emails after building a list of target email addresses by scanning contact data within Outlook.\n\"The malware then proceeds to steal browser-related data from a range of targeted web browsers, including Brave, Yandex, Epic Privacy Browser, Comodo Dragon, Cent Browser, Opera, Microsoft Edge, and Google Chrome,\" Lin said. \"In addition to data theft, Horabot monitors the victim's behavior and injects fake pop-up windows designed to capture sensitive user login credentials.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fhorabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html&t=Horabot%20Malware%20Targets%206%20Latin%20American%20Nations%20Using%20Invoice-Themed%20Phishing%20Emails) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Horabot%20Malware%20Targets%206%20Latin%20American%20Nations%20Using%20Invoice-Themed%20Phishing%20Emails \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fhorabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/horabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fhorabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fhorabot-malware-targets-6-latin.html&text=Horabot%20Malware%20Targets%206%20Latin%20American%20Nations%20Using%20Invoice-Themed%20Phishing%20Emails)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[banking Trojan](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/banking%20Trojan)[browser security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/browser%20security)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[email security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/email%20security)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Phishing](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Phishing)[powershell](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/powershell)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)[windows security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/windows%20security)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\