"title": "Microsoft fixes Linux boot issues on dual-boot Windows systems",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft resolved a Secure Boot issue preventing Linux from booting on dual-boot systems after August 2024 Windows updates. This issue, causing SBAT verification errors, impacted systems with Secure Boot enabled, including Windows 10, 11, and Windows Server. The problem was linked to a CVE-2022-2601-related SBAT update that affected UEFI shim bootloaders. Although Microsoft intended to exclude dual-boot systems, flawed detection led to the issue for several Linux distributions like Ubuntu and Linux Mint. The problem was fixed in May 2025's Patch Tuesday.",,
