"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/gen-ai-best-practices.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/genai-security-best-practices-cheat-sheet?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q3_INB_FORM_GenAI-Security-Best-Practices-Cheat-Sheet&sfcid=701Py00000ENEjlIAH&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=GenAIBestPractices)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft fixes Linux boot issues on dual-boot Windows systems\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft fixes Linux boot issues on dual-boot Windows systems\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 14, 2025\n  * 10:50 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Linux](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/05\/14\/Linux.jpg)\nMicrosoft has fixed a known issue preventing Linux from booting on dual-boot systems with Secure Boot enabled after installing the August 2024 Windows security updates.\nThe list of affected systems includes those running client (Windows 10 and Windows 11) and server (Windows Server 2012 and later) OS versions.\nThis issue is triggered by a Secure Boot Advanced Targeting (SBAT) update that blocks [UEFI shim bootloaders](https:\/\/github.com\/rhboot\/shim\/blob\/main\/SBAT.md) vulnerable to exploits targeting the [CVE-2022-2601](https:\/\/bugzilla.redhat.com\/show_bug.cgi?id=2112975#c0) GRUB2 Secure Boot bypass.\nWhile Microsoft said in the CVE-2022-2601 advisory that this SBAT update would not be delivered to devices where dual booting is detected, it also acknowledged that the dual-boot detection failed to detect some customized methods of dual-booting and applied the update anyway.\nAs revealed by [many](https:\/\/community.frame.work\/t\/sbat-verification-error-booting-linux-after-windows-update\/56354) [Linux](https:\/\/github.com\/ventoy\/Ventoy\/issues\/2947) [users](https:\/\/askubuntu.com\/questions\/1523353\/windows-aug-13-update-broke-my-ubuntu-system) (running a wide range of distros, including but not limited to Ubuntu, Zorin OS, Linux Mint, and Puppy Linux), [their](https:\/\/forum.zorin.com\/t\/verifying-shim-sbat-data-failed-security-policy-violation\/40257\/2) systems [stopped](http:\/\/forums.linuxmint.com\/viewtopic.php?t=427297) [booting](http:\/\/forum.puppylinux.com\/viewtopic.php?t=12452) after installing the August 2024 Windows updates, and the SBAT update was incorrectly applied.\nMicrosoft [confirmed the known issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-august-updates-break-linux-boot-in-dual-boot-systems\/) following widespread reports, saying that affected users saw \"Something has gone seriously wrong: SBAT self-check failed: Security Policy Violation\" errors on systems rendered unbootable.\n![Linux boot broken after Windows security update](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2024\/Windows%20updates%20break%20Linux%20dual-boot.jpeg)_Linux boot broken after Windows security update ()_\n## Fixed after nine months\nThis week, nine months after confirming the issue, Microsoft announced that the May 2025 Patch Tuesday security updates should fix the boot problems for all affected users.\n\"This issue was resolved by Windows updates released May 13, 2025 [..], and later,\" [Redmond noted](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/status-windows-server-2022#3377msgdesc) in a Windows release health update. \"We recommend you install the latest update for your device as it contains important improvements and issue resolutions, including this one.\"\nThe fix comes after the company [shared a temporary workaround](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-shares-temp-fix-for-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-systems\/) in late August, weeks after the first user reports surfaced, to help revive impacted dual-boot systems, requiring them to delete the SBAT update and ensuring that future SBAT updates would no longer be installed. \nOn September 19, it also [stopped applying the problematic SBAT update](https:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2022-2601#exploitability) to the firmware automatically, advising those who want to prevent future SBAT updates in Windows to run the following command:\n```\nreg add HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecureBoot\\SBAT \/v OptOut \/d 1 \/t REG_DWORD\n```\n\n\"This known issue only occurs with the installation of the August 2024 security and preview updates. The September 2024 security update and later updates do not contain the settings that caused this issue,\" Microsoft added. \n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Windows 10 KB5058379 update fixes SgrmBroker errors in Event Viewer](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5058379-update-fixes-sgrmbroker-errors-in-event-viewer\/)\n[Microsoft May 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes 5 exploited zero-days, 72 flaws](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-may-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-5-exploited-zero-days-72-flaws\/)\n[Microsoft will update Office apps on Windows 10 until 2028](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-will-update-office-apps-on-windows-10-until-2028\/)\n[Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/)\n[Windows 11 24H2 blocked on PCs with code-obfuscation driver BSODs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/windows-11-24h2-blocked-on-pcs-with-code-obfuscation-driver-bsods\/)\n  * [Boot Issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/boot-issues\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Linux](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/linux\/)\n  * [Secure Boot](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/secure-boot\/)\n  * [Security Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/security-update\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/steel-giant-nucor-corporation-facing-disruptions-after-cyberattack\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/skuld-stealer.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/tmpn-skuld-stealer-the-dark-side-of-open-source\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trus-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![iClicker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) iClicker site hack targeted students with malware via fake CAPTCHA ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/iclicker-hack-targeted-students-with-malware-via-fake-captcha\/)\n  * [ ![Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Microsoft May 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes 5 exploited zero-days, 72 flaws ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-may-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-5-exploited-zero-days-72-flaws\/)\n  * [ ![Linux](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Hackers now testing ClickFix attacks against Linux targets ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-now-testing-clickfix-attacks-against-linux-targets\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03m1Jw30 )\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.43232639030755393)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campai