"title": "Focused Phishing: Attack Targets Victims With Trusted Sites and Live Validation",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/focused-phishing-attack-targets-victims-with-trusted-sites-and-live-validation\/",,
"summary": "The content describes a sophisticated phishing attack where attackers leverage trusted domains and a technique called 'Precision-Validated Phishing' to target victims. The attack uses real-time email validation to ensure only targeted victims are presented with tailored phishing pages, often mimicking Microsoft login forms. The phishing infrastructure includes mechanisms to dynamically pre-populate email addresses to minimize user friction and employs CAPTCHA challenges to evade detection. Attacks are executed in browser environments where trusted sites are manipulated to host malicious content, indicating the need for real-time, browser-based phishing protection.",,
