"markdown": "![hands keyboard](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_hands_keyboard_27d16135ea.jpg)\nImage: Soumil Kumar \/ Pexels\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)May 14th, 2025\n# Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agent\nA cadet from the Russian military space academy in St. Petersburg has reportedly been arrested for allegedly developing and attempting to sell a hacking tool capable of breaching a classified security system used by law enforcement and military personnel. \nThe system, known as Secret Net Studio, is designed to secure workstations and servers at the data, application, network, operating system and hardware levels. \nAccording to a [report](https:\/\/t.me\/voenpravoru\/12260) from a Telegram channel that provides updates on legal regulations and official documents related to the Russian military, the cadet developed an algorithm that could bypass the protective infrastructure of the software and gain access to restricted data. \nHe reportedly listed the tool for sale on Avito, a popular Russian online marketplace, for 8,000 rubles (approximately $100). He ended up attempting to sell it to an undercover agent with the Federal Security Service (FSB), which led to the cadet's detention. \nThe suspected hacker now faces charges of unlawful access to legally protected computer information and could potentially be prosecuted for treason. \nNo announcement of the charges have been made on official Russian channels, and the report could not be independently verified. But it would not be the first time students from the academy have faced legal issues. Earlier this week, local media [reported](https:\/\/mr-7.ru\/articles\/2025\/05\/12\/peterburgskomu-kursantu-dali-desiat-let-kolonii-za-ubiistvo-zhenshchiny-kotoruiu-on-prinial-za-shpionku-news) that another cadet was sentenced to 10 years in prison for killing a woman he believed to be a spy. According to reports, the suspect mistook the victim's hearing aid for espionage equipment. \nIn a separate case this week, a Russian court [sentenced](https:\/\/t.me\/sudpress70\/217) a university student to six years in a penal colony for allegedly aiding hacker groups linked to Ukrainian security services. The student, [arrested](https:\/\/therecord.media\/detained-russian-hacked-for-ukrainian) in October 2023, was accused of participating in cyberattacks on behalf of the pro-Ukrainian hacking collective Cyber Anarchy Squad. While the group denied directly tasking him, it publicly endorsed his actions, adding that the mentioned student \u201cis doing more\u201d than the majority of Russians. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agent)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agent )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [arrests](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/arrests)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [FSB](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/fsb)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n  * [EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threatsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-launches-vulnerability-database)\n  * [Alabama says \u2018cybersecurity event\u2019 could disrupt state government servicesMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions)\n  * [States push WeChat for answers over money laundering allegationsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/states-push-wechat-for-money-laundering-answers)\n  * [Microsoft spots zero-day use in spy campaign against Kurdish military in IraqMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/microsoft-zero-day-spy-campaign)\n  * [South African influencers-for-hire target Ukraine\u2019s president in influence campaign, researchers sayMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-influencers-anti-zelensky-campaign)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
