"summary": "The Alabama state government is dealing with a cybersecurity event discovered on May 9, which has not caused major disruptions but has led to a continuous response effort. The incident, involving compromised employee passwords, has involved two third-party incident response teams working continuously. Although no major disruptions or exfiltration of personal data have been confirmed, all state agencies were asked to reset passwords, and caution is advised with emails. The investigation is ongoing, with more updates to follow when possible.",,
