"markdown": "![Montgomery Alabama](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_Montgomery_dc56c0f2a4.jpg)\nImage: Michael Barera \/ Wikimedia Commons\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 14th, 2025\n# Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continues\nAlabama\u2019s technology office says a \u201ccybersecurity event\u201d first discovered May 9 has not caused major disruptions to state services, but incident responders are still working around the clock to contain its effects. \nIn an update [posted](https:\/\/oit.alabama.gov\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/05\/May-2025-Cybersecurity-Event-UPDATE.pdf) Tuesday, the Office of Information Technology (OIT) said it has called in two incident response teams from third-party firms, \u201cmaintaining 24 hours-a-day, 7 days-a-week mitigation activities as technical specialists work extended shifts to ensure a continuous, uninterrupted response to this event.\u201d \nOIT has not described the nature of the incident, but a statement Monday from Gov. Kay Ivey [said](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions) that state employees had been reminded to be careful with suspicious emails, and that it appeared some employee passwords had been compromised. \nTuesday\u2019s update said all state agencies had been asked to reset employee passwords. \n\u201cAt this time, no major disruptions to State services have been traced to the event and there is no evidence of exfiltration of the personally identifiable information of Alabama citizens,\u201d the OIT update said. \nPublic information about the incident has been limited. \n\u201cAs this is an active, ongoing investigation, updates will be provided as new information becomes available and security protocol allows,\u201d the agency said. \u201cOIT is working diligently to balance transparency and security interests as this situation progresses.\u201d \nThe state government has about 29,000 employees across two dozen agencies, according to the most recent [report](https:\/\/personnel.alabama.gov\/LegalNotices\/2023AnnualReport.pdf) from its personnel office. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continues)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continues )\n\n\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [Alabama](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/alabama)\n  * [incident response](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/incident-response)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n  * [EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threatsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-launches-vulnerability-database)\n  * [Alabama says \u2018cybersecurity event\u2019 could disrupt state government servicesMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions)\n  * [States push WeChat for answers over money laundering allegationsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/states-push-wechat-for-money-laundering-answers)\n  * [Microsoft spots zero-day use in spy campaign against Kurdish military in IraqMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/microsoft-zero-day-spy-campaign)\n  * [South African influencers-for-hire target Ukraine\u2019s president in influence campaign, researchers sayMay 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/south-african-influencers-anti-zelensky-campaign)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
