"title": "CTM360 Identifies Surge in Phishing Attacks Targeting Meta Business Users",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/ctm360-identifies-surge-in-phishing.html",,
"summary": "CTM360 has identified a new global phishing campaign named 'Meta Mirage' targeting users of Meta's Business Suite. The campaign impersonates official Meta communications to steal credentials and cookies, affecting businesses' advertising and brand management accounts. The phishing attempts are using cloud-hosted fake pages on platforms like GitHub, Firebase, and Vercel. The attackers send fake alerts about policy violations and account suspensions in an attempt to trick victims into divulging sensitive information. Over 14,000 malicious URLs have been detected, with nearly 78% not blocked by browsers. The report highlights the use of techniques such as credential theft and cookie theft. No specific threat actors or CVEs are named, and no mention of patches. The campaign is indicative of increased phishing activities leveraging trusted cloud platforms.",,
