"summary": "The article discusses the expanded focus of nation-state attackers, which now includes small and mid-sized businesses (SMBs) as their targets. Historically, Advanced Persistent Threats (APTs) were focused on governmental and large enterprises, but this has changed, with attackers like China, Russia, North Korea, and Iran targeting smaller firms for economic espionage, supply chain infiltration, and ransomware attacks. This shift necessitates SMBs to adopt enterprise-grade, AI-powered security solutions to defend against sophisticated threats. The article outlines emerging trends where Chinese groups employ diverse tactics, Russian groups persistently use phishing, North Korean groups target financial gain, and Iranian groups execute destructive espionage. The discussion emphasizes a strategic defense approach to reduce vulnerabilities, leveraging technologies like AI for predictive security, incident prediction, and deploying advanced detection systems.",,
