"summary": "Google has identified that a hacking group, suspected of conducting cyberattacks on UK retailers, has expanded its operations to target similar companies in the US. This group, known as Scattered Spider, is associated with ransomware and extortion operations, and has previously launched high-profile attacks against US casino giants and various tech companies. The group is known for using strategies like social engineering to infiltrate mature security systems. It has been linked to the DragonForce ransomware, and their activities suggest a focused targeting of the retail sector.",,
