"title": "Xinbi Telegram Market Tied to $8.4B in Crypto Crime, Romance Scams, North Korea Laundering",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/xinbi-telegram-market-tied-to-84b-in.html",,
"summary": "The Xinbi Guarantee, a Chinese-language Telegram-based marketplace, has been linked to $8.4 billion in transactions since 2022. Facilitating cybercrime activities, it offers services ranging from money laundering to scams, with USDT as its primary payment method. Notably, some transactions are tied to funds stolen by North Korea. Xinbi has targeted Southeast Asia, utilizing romance baiting schemes among others. The marketplace operates completely on Telegram and involves over 233,000 users. It also falsely claims to be a U.S. registered investment company, yet is marked 'delinquent' for not filing reports. In total, both Xinbi and HuiOne have laundered over $35 billion in cryptocurrencies, leading to Telegram shutting down associated channels.",,
