"markdown": "![nucor](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_nucor_1_95776b3ed7.jpg)\nImage: Nucor\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 14th, 2025\n# Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offline\nNorth Carolina-based steel company Nucor said it temporarily halted production operations at some locations because of a recent cybersecurity incident and is working to restart them. \nIn an [8-K filing with federal regulators](https:\/\/www.sec.gov\/Archives\/edgar\/data\/73309\/000119312525119311\/d795264d8k.htm), Nucor said the incident involved \u201cunauthorized third party access to certain information technology systems\u201d but did not explain further. \nThe company \u201cbegan promptly taking steps to contain and respond to the incident, including activating its incident response plan, proactively taking potentially affected systems offline and implementing other containment, remediation, or recovery measures,\u201d the filing said. \nNucor did not specify which facilities were affected. The company said it only halted some operations \u201cin an abundance of caution.\u201d From recycling centers to large plants, the company operates at about 300 locations overall. \nHeadquartered in Charlotte, Nucor [reported](https:\/\/nucor.com\/news-release\/nucor-reports-results-for-the-first-quarter-of-2025-122971) sales of $7.83 billion in the first quarter of 2025 and calls itself \u201cNorth America\u2019s largest steel manufacturer and recycler,\u201d with about 25,000 employees. Industry analysts list it as [one of the top 20](https:\/\/worldsteel.org\/data\/top-producers\/) in the world. \nOne of its largest projects is a $3 billion facility [under construction](https:\/\/wvpublic.org\/nucor-plant-construction-brings-unprecedented-growth-challenges\/) in West Virginia. \nLarge manufacturers are under constant pressure from malicious hackers, whether the interest is financial cybercrime, intellectual property theft or even nation-state espionage. \nRecent cybersecurity-related 8-K filings by U.S. manufacturers include medical technology company [Masimo](https:\/\/therecord.media\/masimo-medical-device-company-cyberattack), industrial sensor maker [Sensata](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sensata-technologies-ransomware-attack), home appliance company [National Presto Industries](https:\/\/therecord.media\/presto-home-appliances-manufacturer-cyberattack) and semiconductor firm [Microchip Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/microchip-technology-data-breach-sec-filing). \nThe trend applies globally, with industrial firms in the [United Kingdom](https:\/\/therecord.media\/imi-uk-engineering-company-reports-cyber-incident) and [Switzerland](https:\/\/therecord.media\/swiss-manufacturer-investigating-ransomware-incident) among those reporting cybersecurity incidents over the past year. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offline)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offline )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [steel industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/steel-industry)\n  * [manufacturing](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/manufacturing)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [disruption](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/disruption)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n  * [Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offlineMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyber-incident-forces-nucor-steel-to-take-systems-offline)\n  * [Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groupsMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-internet-shutdown-condemned-by-rights-groups)\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n  * [EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threatsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-launches-vulnerability-database)\n  * [Alabama says \u2018cybersecurity event\u2019 could disrupt state government servicesMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
