"title": "British retailer M&S reportedly set to claim \u00a3100 million from insurers after cyberattack",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/british-retailer-marks-spencer-insurance",,
"summary": "Marks & Spencer (M&S) is speculated to claim \u00a3100 million from insurers after a cyberattack disrupted the retailer's systems. The attack affected M&S's app and online shopping platform, which remained unavailable, while store shelves experienced stock shortages. The incident potentially cost over \u00a360 million due to loss of online sales, with cybersecurity firm Sto\u00efk's Craig Dunn highlighting the role of cyber insurance in covering loss of gross profit. The attack was reportedly claimed by the DragonForce ransomware group, though confirmation is pending. The National Cyber Security Centre has yet to determine if this attack is linked to similar incidents at other UK retailers.",,
