"markdown": "![victory day](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_victory_day_parade_54d810ea18.jpg)\nThe shutdowns were implemented ahead of Russia's Victory Day celebrations. Image: Kremlin\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)May 14th, 2025\n# Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groups\nDigital rights organizations condemned Russia\u2019s decision to implement a sweeping [internet shutdown](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-internet-restrictions-victory-day) during the 80th anniversary of Victory Day celebrations last week. \nRussian authorities restricted mobile internet access from May 5 to May 9, citing security concerns related to the preparation and celebration of the Victory Day parade in Moscow. During this period, residents across more than 30 regions experienced disrupted or completely absent cellular networks. \nSuch blackouts, imposed without public oversight or legal justification, violate fundamental human rights, according to a [statement](https:\/\/www.accessnow.org\/press-release\/kremlin-must-end-internet-shutdowns-national-events\/) this week by digital rights nonprofit Access Now and 29 other organizations. \nKremlin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov [acknowledged](https:\/\/t.me\/tass_agency\/313818) the shutdown and urged the public to accept it for the sake of security. A deputy in the State Duma also referred to the restrictions as a \u201cpreventive defense\u201d against potential drone attacks from Ukraine. \nHowever, the rights groups argue that such measures were disproportionate, as there were no reports of drone-related incidents in the affected areas. The shutdown was also arbitrary and unclear, lacking transparency and legal basis, which goes against international standards, according to Access Now. \nA report by Russian digital rights nonprofit Roskomsvoboda [said](https:\/\/roskomsvoboda.org\/ru\/post\/nationwide-internet-shutdown-russia-may-holidays-2025\/) that the latest internet restrictions disrupted essential services in Russia, such as banking, online shopping and government websites. Small businesses that rely on mobile internet for daily operations were hit hardest, while online marketplaces like Wildberries and Yandex Market reported significant drops in mobile app orders. Delivery services were forced to manage operations manually. \nA member of the Russian parliament\u2019s committee on information policy, Anton Nemkin, [defended](https:\/\/www.iphones.ru\/iNotes\/v-gosdume-obyasnili-pochemu-nuzhno-otklyuchat-mobilnyy-internet-na-vremya-meropriyatiy) the restrictions, describing them as a necessary measure in the context of hybrid warfare. \u201cIn these conditions, where communication tools can also be used for control in combat operations, such restrictions are unavoidable,\u201d he said, emphasizing that the safety of people and event participants outweighed the inconvenience caused by the shutdown. \nHowever, digital rights advocates argue that this shutdown made the ongoing issues with Russia's heavy internet censorship even worse. The move, they said, severely limited the public\u2019s ability to access crucial information during a significant national event. \n\u201cWe urge the Russian authorities to refrain from restricting internet access in the future and ensure the internet and all communication channels remain free, accessible, and secure,\u201d the statement said. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groups)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groups )\n\n\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [Internet](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/internet)\n  * [shutdown](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/shutdown)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [Access Now](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/access-now)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n  * [Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offlineMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyber-incident-forces-nucor-steel-to-take-systems-offline)\n  * [Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groupsMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-internet-shutdown-condemned-by-rights-groups)\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n  * [EU launches vulnerability database to tackle cybersecurity threatsMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-launches-vulnerability-database)\n  * [Alabama says \u2018cybersecurity event\u2019 could disrupt state government servicesMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-says-cyber-event-could-cause-disruptions)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
