"title": "Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackers",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice",,
"summary": "Nova Scotia Power, the largest electric utility in Nova Scotia, experienced a cyberattack resulting in the theft of sensitive customer information, including contact details, account history, driver\u2019s license details, Social Insurance numbers, and possibly bank account numbers. The breach was discovered on April 25, although unauthorized access occurred on March 19. No ransomware or specific threat group has been identified, and physical operations were not affected. There has been an increase in impersonation scams post-breach.",,
