"title": "Samsung Patches CVE-2025-4632 Used to Deploy Mirai Botnet via MagicINFO 9 Exploit",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html",,
"summary": "Samsung has released updates to fix a critical security flaw in MagicINFO 9 Server, known as CVE-2025-4632, which has been exploited to deploy the Mirai botnet. The vulnerability is a path traversal flaw allowing attackers to write arbitrary files with system authority. CVE-2025-4632 is a bypass for CVE-2024-7399 and has been exploited in the wild, with incidents involving downloads of malicious payloads such as 'srvany.exe' and 'services.exe'. Users are advised to upgrade to version 21.1052.0 to mitigate this vulnerability.",,
