"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [Samsung Patches CVE-2025-4632 Used to Deploy Mirai Botnet via MagicINFO 9 Exploit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html)\n_\ue802_ May 14, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Malware\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi9Y473_f8HQTyAdKAUz_UnUOsL-Z925rXBPVq5oWm6zKljOP2dPhWSIal4kPTtZr3hXyLGS9_MKSVQIZlDg35iKCDoI_wH4zFBq2twZENAghHtiRuUh-0g9y3EYC8oxBiDRSibXQWtut9IKsrRtM7R8sobRyDVzr7AsutGBHpCmsSe8K4p3gF7FJFqtI_B\/s728-rw-e365\/malwaree.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi9Y473_f8HQTyAdKAUz_UnUOsL-Z925rXBPVq5oWm6zKljOP2dPhWSIal4kPTtZr3hXyLGS9_MKSVQIZlDg35iKCDoI_wH4zFBq2twZENAghHtiRuUh-0g9y3EYC8oxBiDRSibXQWtut9IKsrRtM7R8sobRyDVzr7AsutGBHpCmsSe8K4p3gF7FJFqtI_B\/s728-rw-e365\/malwaree.jpg)\nSamsung has released software updates to address a critical security flaw in MagicINFO 9 Server that has been actively exploited in the wild.\nThe vulnerability, tracked as [CVE-2025-4632](https:\/\/security.samsungtv.com\/securityUpdates#SVP-MAY-2025) (CVSS score: 9.8), has been described as a path traversal flaw.\n\"Improper limitation of a pathname to a restricted directory vulnerability in Samsung MagicINFO 9 Server version before 21.1052 allows attackers to write arbitrary files as system authority,\" according to an [advisory](https:\/\/www.cve.org\/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-4632) for the flaw.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nIt's worth noting that CVE-2025-4632 is a patch bypass for CVE-2024-7399, another path traversal flaw in the same product that was patched by Samsung in August 2024.\nCVE-2025-4632 has since been [exploited](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/hackers-exploit-samsung-magicinfo.html) in the wild shortly after the release of a proof-of-concept (PoC) by SSD Disclosure on April 30, 2025, in some instances to even deploy the Mirai botnet.\nWhile it was initially assumed that the attacks were targeting CVE-2024-7399, cybersecurity company Huntress first revealed the existence of an unpatched vulnerability last week after finding signs of exploitation even on MagicINFO 9 Server instances running the latest version (21.1050).\nIn a follow-up report published on May 9, Huntress [revealed](https:\/\/www.huntress.com\/blog\/post-exploitation-activities-observed-from-samsung-magicinfo-9-server-flaw) that three separate incidents that involved the exploitation of CVE-2025-4632, with unidentified actors running an identical set of commands to download additional payloads like \"srvany.exe\" and \"services.exe\" on two hosts and executing reconnaissance commands on the third.\nUsers of the Samsung MagicINFO 9 Server are recommended to apply the latest fixes as soon as possible to safeguard against potential threats.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/nudge-GenAI-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"We have verified that [MagicINFO 9 21.1052.0](https:\/\/eu.community.samsung.com\/t5\/samsung-solutions\/update-magicinfo-server-v9-21-1052-0-setup-file\/ta-p\/11374265) does mitigate the original issue raised in CVE-2025-4632,\" Jamie Levy, director of adversary tactics at Huntress, told The Hacker News.\n\"Any machine that has versions v8 - v9 21.1050.0 will still be affected by this vulnerability. We've also discovered that upgrading from MagicINFO v8 to v9 21.1052.0 is not as straightforward since you have to first upgrade to 21.1050.0 before applying the final patch.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsamsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html&t=Samsung%20Patches%20CVE-2025-4632%20Used%20to%20Deploy%20Mirai%20Botnet%20via%20MagicINFO%209%20Exploit) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Samsung%20Patches%20CVE-2025-4632%20Used%20to%20Deploy%20Mirai%20Botnet%20via%20MagicINFO%209%20Exploit \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsamsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/samsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsamsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsamsung-patches-cve-2025-4632-used-to.html&text=Samsung%20Patches%20CVE-2025-4632%20Used%20to%20Deploy%20Mirai%20Botnet%20via%20MagicINFO%209%20Exploit)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[botnet](https:\/\/theh