"summary": "The article reveals that two cybercrime groups, BianLian and RansomExx, have exploited a vulnerability in SAP NetWeaver to deploy the PipeMagic Trojan. The exploitation involved the BianLian data extortion group and the RansomExx ransomware family, known as Storm-2460 by Microsoft. The vulnerability is linked to CVE-2025-31324 and CVE-2025-42999, with evidence of active exploitation using the Windows Common Log File System zero-day bug (CVE-2025-29824). Victims targeted include entities in the U.S., Venezuela, Spain, and Saudi Arabia. There is active exploitation observed in the wild.",,
