"markdown": "This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. [Learn more](https:\/\/www.cookiesandyou.com)\nGot it!\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/news\/)\n  * [Cloud](https:\/\/news.google.com\/cloud\/)\n\n\n# StarHub and Nokia partner on network APIs to drive 5G and 4G application development in enterprise verticals\nStarHub and Nokia have teamed up to enhance application development for enterprise sectors using their 5G and 4G networks. This collaboration aims to simplify access to network APIs for \nFebruary 06, 2025 \n\nBy\n     [ StringerAI\u2122 ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/profile\/stringer-ai\/) [Comment](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMi2AFBVV95cUxPUHRDeHJIVXZuNEdTOElmNGI3c3FQYUJua01uckNBcDg4VFo0TGkxTlViYWxtaklwNWZQeXBQekI0Ny1UUjRrazVPS1Robnd0SHh2Z0l1b0FRbzBDS0RMQVJ6X3lndnFqWEo0d0U4d1lwRk5yRE94dWFnUVdFUTN3V05ZZVdIZ1pSRVc5RDRSbXpjWE9Hd2lSU0FkS1ZzWUhocXJXamlkeV9VNWJ1aGhMMkNVX3UyZzVQMnA5RmdULXRpWjc4R1cyb1UyY2djRVZFa25WZHE0TEc?oc=5#disqus_thread)\n[](https:\/\/www.addtoany.com\/share)\n[StarHub](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/directory\/starhub-inc\/ \"StarHub\") and Nokia are collaborating to enhance application development for enterprise sectors utilizing 5G and 4G technologies. This partnership aims to facilitate developers in creating applications tailored for industries such as banking, finance, online streaming, and the public sector.\nThe companies will integrate StarHub's 5G and 4G networks with [Nokia](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/directory\/nokia\/ \"Nokia\")'s Network as Code platform, providing developers with streamlined access to network capabilities through a comprehensive developer portal. This initiative is expected to simplify the process of creating applications that leverage network functionalities.\nAyush Sharma, CTO at StarHub, commented, \u201cWe are pleased to deepen our partnership with Nokia to deliver a simplified and improved developer experience. Giving developers access to a wider selection of attractive network APIs is critical to unlocking the full value of [5G](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/5g\/definitions\/what-is-5g\/ \"What Is 5G? Everything You Need to Know \u2014 Definition\") and 4G networks in Singapore and the wider region.\u201d\nStarHub has been active in industry initiatives through [GSMA](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/directory\/gsma\/ \"GSMA\") Open Gateway and Linux Foundation CAMARA, supporting the development of technical standards for network APIs. Nokia participates in both efforts, contributing to the ongoing development of new use cases for developers.\nNokia has an extensive ecosystem featuring over 45 partners, including major telecommunications providers such as BT, Orange, and Telefonica, as well as cloud platform providers like Google. This approach is designed to connect API ecosystems through its Network as Code platform, enhancing accessibility while ensuring robust operational security.\nShkumbin Hamiti, Head of Network Monetization Platform at Nokia, stated, \u201cNokia\u2019s approach to network APIs reflects a strategic focus of driving new business models and unlocking the potential that [5G and 4G](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/5g\/definitions\/top-5g-business-case\/how-is-5g-different-from-4g-lte\/4g-to-5g-transition\/ \"How Carriers Are Transitioning From 4G to 5G\") networks can deliver from the perspective of innovation, sustainability, collaboration, and productivity. With this relationship, StarHub will have more choice and flexibility to create new value for its customers.\u201d\n[](https:\/\/www.addtoany.com\/share)\n### Tags\n  * [Cloud](https:\/\/news.google.com\/tags\/cloud_1\/)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/news.google.com\/tags\/industry\/)\n  * [Networking](https:\/\/news.google.com\/tags\/networking_1\/)\n  * [Enterprise](https:\/\/news.google.com\/tags\/enterprise_1\/)\n\n\n## Resources [ More](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/)\n  * ![pg 1 AI-Data-Centers-Scaling-Up-and-Scaling-Out-White-Paper \\(2\\) \\(2\\) - Tim Hazlehurst_page-0001](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/pg_1_AI-Data-Centers-Scaling-Up-and-Scaling-O.height-150.jpg)\n#  [AI Data Centers: Scaling Up and Scaling Out](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/ai-data-centers-scaling-up-and-scaling-out\/)\n13 Mar 2025\n  * #  [Advanced Networks for Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Computing](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/advanced-networks-for-articial-intelligence-and-machine-learning-computing\/)\n21 Feb 2025\n  * #  [DCD>Survey: Data center networking trends](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/dcdsurvey-data-center-networking-trends\/)\n09 Jan 2025\n  * #  [Future-proof your datacenter with DDC S-Series](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/futureproof-your-datacenter-with-ddc-s-series\/)\n08 Jan 2025\n  * [More](https:\/\/www.sdxcentral.com\/resources\/)\n\n\n![SDx X DCD SITE PLAY THUMBNAILV2](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/SDx_X_DCD_SITE_PLAY_THUMBNAILV2.2e16d0ba.fill-280x185.png)\n#  Episode [Software and hardware co-design: Optimizing next-gen compute](https:\/\/news.google.com\/broadcasts\/dcdcompute-storage-networking\/2025\/software-and-hardware-co-design-optimizing-next-gen-compute\/)\n",,
