"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers have identified a malicious npm package named \"os-info-checker-es6\" masquerading as an OS utility tool. It employs Unicode-based steganography for hiding its malicious code and a Google Calendar event short link as a C2 dropper. Once installed, it parses Unicode \"Private Use Access\" characters to extract and deploy subsequent malware. The use of Google Calendar allows evasion of detection by leveraging a trusted service. This campaign seems dormant or incomplete currently, with no additional payloads being distributed. The same user also uploaded a related package named \"skip-tot\". No CVEs are directly mentioned in relation to this package. The advisories do not specify affected sectors or countries such as Singapore or ASEAN members.",,
