"markdown": "![email](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_email_de941d199e.jpg)\nImage: Unsplash+\/Getty\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)May 15th, 2025\n# Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agencies\nThe Russia-linked hacking group APT28 was recently observed exploiting cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities to target webmail servers used by state entities and defense companies in Eastern Europe, according to a new report. \nThe group, also tracked as Fancy Bear and BlueDelta, mainly targeted entities in Ukraine, Bulgaria and Romania, but governments in Africa, South America and other parts of Europe were also affected, Slovak-based cybersecurity firm ESET said in a [report](https:\/\/www.welivesecurity.com\/en\/eset-research\/operation-roundpress\/) published Thursday. \nThe campaign typically involved a phishing email that contained news excerpts or links to articles \u2014 in one case, a Ukrainian target received an email referencing the Kyiv Post, a well-known newspaper in the country. Malicious code triggering an XSS vulnerability was hidden inside the message\u2019s body, and was not directly visible to the user, the researchers said. \nThe payloads loaded by the XSS vulnerabilities allowed attackers to steal login credentials, exfiltrate contacts and access email communications from the victim's inbox. Some of the defense companies targeted produce Soviet-era weapons for Ukraine amid its ongoing conflict with Russia. APT28 has been operating since at least 2004 and is believed to be tied to Russia\u2019s military intelligence agency (GRU). \nOver the past two years, webmail services like Roundcube and Zimbra have been heavily targeted by multiple espionage groups, including APT28, GreenCube and Winter Vivern. \nIn 2023, Winter Vivern \u2014 a state-sponsored hacker group previously implicated in cyberattacks on the governments of Poland, Ukraine and India \u2014 [exploited](https:\/\/therecord.media\/winter-vivern-hackers-roundcube-webmail-zero-day) a zero-day vulnerability in Roundcube webmail software used by governments across Europe. \nThat same year, APT28 [targeted](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-fancy-bear-hackers-targeted-ukraine) the Ukrainian government and a company involved in military aviation through three different vulnerabilities in Roundcube\u2019s service. The campaign used news about Russia\u2019s invasion of Ukraine to entice victims into opening malicious emails. \n\u201cBecause many organizations don\u2019t keep their webmail servers up to date and because the vulnerabilities can be triggered remotely by sending an email message, it is very convenient for attackers to target such servers for email theft,\u201d ESET researchers said. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agencies)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agencies )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [APT28](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/apt28)\n  * [GRU](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/gru)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [Ukraine](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ukraine)\n  * [Romania](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/romania)\n  * [Bulgaria](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/bulgaria)\n  * [webmail](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/webmail)\n  * [XSS](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/xss)\n  * [espionage](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/espionage)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agenciesMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kremlin-linked-hackers-target-webmail-eastern-europe-governments)\n  * [Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackersMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice)\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n  * [Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offlineMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyber-incident-forces-nucor-steel-to-take-systems-offline)\n  * [Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groupsMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-internet-shutdown-condemned-by-rights-groups)\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
