"markdown": "![Coinbase](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_51203948014_9d714ca3e0_o_38748eddfd.jpg)\nImage: Ivan Radic via Flickr \/ CC BY 2.0\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 15th, 2025\n# Coinbase offers $20 million bounty after extortion attempt with stolen data\nCryptocurrency trading platform Coinbase said it was the victim of an extortion attempt involving stolen data and is offering $20 million for information leading to the arrest and conviction of the perpetrator. \nThe industry giant said in a [regulatory filing](https:\/\/www.sec.gov\/ix?doc=\/Archives\/edgar\/data\/1679788\/000167978825000094\/coin-20250514.htm) with the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) that an \u201cunknown threat actor\u201d emailed a demand on May 11 for $20 million, threatening to publish stolen data about Coinbase customers and other company information. \u201cWe said no,\u201d Coinbase said Thursday in a [blog post](https:\/\/www.coinbase.com\/blog\/protecting-our-customers-standing-up-to-extortionists) explaining the incident. \n\u201cCriminals targeted our customer support agents overseas. They used cash offers to convince a small group of insiders to copy data in our customer support tools for less than 1% of Coinbase monthly transacting users,\u201d the blog post said. \u201cTheir aim was to gather a customer list they could contact while pretending to be Coinbase\u2014tricking people into handing over their crypto.\u201d \nA company executive [told](https:\/\/fortune.com\/crypto\/2025\/05\/15\/coinbase-puts-20-million-bounty-on-crooks-who-tried-to-extort-firm-over-stolen-customer-data\/) Fortune that the compromised agents worked in India and have all been fired. Data [published](https:\/\/www.theblock.co\/data\/crypto-markets\/public-companies\/coinbase-monthly-transacting-users) by cryptocurrency news site The Block says Coinbase had about 9.7 million monthly transacting users during the first quarter of this year, meaning that fewer than 100,000 were likely affected in the incident. \nThe 8-K filing said Coinbase estimates it will spend $180 million to $400 million on remediation and response costs, but those numbers could change as it continues to assess the situation. \nThe company said the stolen data included names, addresses, phone numbers and email addresses; \u201cmasked\u201d versions of the last four digits of customer Social Security numbers and similarly encoded bank-account numbers; images of government IDs such as driver\u2019s licenses; account data such as transaction histories; and \u201climited corporate data.\u201d \nThe scheme did not capture login credentials or two-factor authentication codes, private keys, \u201cthe ability to move or access customer funds,\u201d access to Coinbase Prime accounts or access to cryptocurrency wallets, the company said. \n\u201cExpect imposters,\u201d the blog post said. \u201cScammers\u2014related to this breach or not\u2014may pose as Coinbase employees and try to pressure you into moving your funds. Remember, Coinbase will never ask for your password, 2FA codes, or for you to transfer assets to a specific or new address, account, vault or wallet.\u201d \nCoinbase said it will reimburse anyone tricked into sending funds to the attacker and is \u201ccooperating closely with law enforcement to pursue the harshest penalties possible.\u201d It did not specify how many people already might have fallen for related scams. \nCoinbase is one of the world\u2019s largest crypto exchanges and had a market capitalization of about $67 billion as of Thursday morning. Its stock, traded on the Nasdaq, was [added to the S&P 500](https:\/\/www.cnbc.com\/2025\/05\/13\/coinbase-jumps-sp-500-inclusion.html) index earlier this week. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Coinbase offers $20 million bounty after extortion attempt with stolen data)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Coinbase offers $20 million bounty after extortion attempt with stolen data )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [social engineering](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/social-engineering)\n  * [Coinbase](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/coinbase)\n  * [cryptocurrency](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cryptocurrency)\n  * [data breach](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-breach)\n  * [financial](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/financial)\n  * [extortion](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/extortion)\n  * [reward](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/reward)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agenciesMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kremlin-linked-hackers-target-webmail-eastern-europe-governments)\n  * [Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackersMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice)\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n  * [Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offlineMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyber-incident-forces-nucor-steel-to-take-systems-offline)\n  * [Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groupsMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-internet-shutdown-condemned-by-rights-groups)\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n  * [US extradites Kosovo national charged in operating illegal online marketplaceMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-extradites-kosovo-national-online-marketplace)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers disrupt drone supply chains in Taiwan, researchers sayMay 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-hackers-target-taiwan-military-sector)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
