"summary": "A cyberattack conducted by the pro-Ukraine hacking group BO Team on Russia's national case management and electronic court filing system, Pravosudiye, resulted in the deletion of about a third of its case archives, affecting nearly 89 million court files. This attack exploited vulnerabilities in the outdated system, which had not been fully updated since its implementation and had not undergone an external security check since 2015. The breach highlights significant weaknesses in the system's security infrastructure, including outdated foreign software and data storage in a single data center.",,
