"title": "New Tor Oniux tool anonymizes any Linux app's network traffic",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-tor-oniux-tool-anonymizes-any-linux-apps-network-traffic\/",,
"summary": "The Tor Project has introduced Oniux, a new command-line tool for anonymizing network traffic of any Linux application by routing it securely through the Tor network. Unlike the older torsocks method, Oniux utilizes Linux namespaces to provide a fully isolated network environment that ensures no data leaks even if an application is malicious or misconfigured.",,
