"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Nova Scotia Power confirms hackers stole customer data in cyberattack\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/)\n\n\n# Nova Scotia Power confirms hackers stole customer data in cyberattack\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * May 15, 2025\n  * 12:38 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Nova Scotia Power](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/05\/15\/nova-scotia-power-header.jpg)\nNova Scotia Power confirms it suffered a data breach after threat actors stole sensitive customer data in a cybersecurity incident discovered last month.\nNova Scotia Power, a subsidiary of Emera Inc., is a significant utility in Canada. It serves over 500,000 residential, commercial, and industrial customers in Nova Scotia, holding 95% of the market share.\nIt generates over 10,000 GWh of energy annually, distributed through an extensive network of power lines extending for 32,000 kilometers (20,000 miles).\nOn April 28, 2025, the company announced that it had discovered unauthorized access into certain parts of its network and servers supporting its business.\nAlthough there was no impact on the company's electricity production and distribution, the incident response efforts disrupted internal operations.\nFurther investigations revealed on May 1, 2025, that customer information might have been stolen. An update published yesterday confirmed this previous finding, specifying the following data was exposed:\n  * Full name\n  * Phone number\n  * Email address\n  * Mailing and service addresses\n  * Nova Scotia Power program participation information\n  * Date of birth\n  * Customer account history (power consumption, service requests, customer payment, billing, credit history, and customer correspondence)\n  * Driver's license number\n  * Social Insurance Number\n  * Bank account numbers (for some customers)\n\n\nAlso, the company found that the actual breach occurred earlier than initially anticipated, on March 19, 2025, which means that nearly two months had passed by the time affected customers were informed via notices mailed to their addresses.\nNova Scotia Power says there are no signs the stolen data has been misused, but it will provide two years of credit monitoring service coverage to letter recipients to mitigate the risks.\n\"Notifications are in the process of being mailed to impacted account holders, which includes detailed information about resources and support,\" [reads the incident status update](https:\/\/www.nspower.ca\/).\n\"While we have no evidence of misuse of your personal information, as a precaution, arrangements have been made with the consumer reporting agency, TransUnion, to provide impacted individuals with a two-year subscription to a comprehensive credit monitoring service at no cost.\"\nCustomers of Nova Scotia Power are advised to remain vigilant for phishing attempts, including cases of threat actors impersonating the utility to trick people into giving away sensitive data.\nAt the time of writing, no ransomware gangs have assumed responsibility for the attack at Nova Scotia Power.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Fashion giant Dior discloses cyberattack, warns of data breach](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fashion-giant-dior-discloses-cyberattack-warns-of-data-breach\/)\n[M&S says customer data stolen in cyberattack, forces password resets](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/mands-says-customer-data-stolen-in-cyberattack-forces-password-resets\/)\n[VC giant Insight Partners confirms investor data stolen in breach](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vc-giant-insight-partners-confirms-investor-data-stolen-in-breach\/)\n[VeriSource now says February data breach impacts 4 million people](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/verisource-now-says-february-data-breach-impacts-4-million-people\/)\n[Interlock ransomware claims DaVita attack, leaks stolen data](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/interlock-ransomware-claims-davita-attack-leaks-stolen-data\/)\n  * [Canada](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/canada\/)\n  * [Critical Infrastructure](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/critical-infrastructure\/)\n  * [Customer Data](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/customer-data\/)\n  * [Data Breach](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/data-breach\/)\n  * [Electricity](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/electricity\/)\n  * [Nova Scotia](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/nova-scotia\/)\n  * [Utility](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/utility\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/windows-11-and-red-hat-linux-virtualbox-hacked-on-first-day-of-pwn2own\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/skuld-stealer.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/tmpn-skuld-stealer-the-dark-side-of-open-source\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trus-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Steam](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Twilio denies breach following leak of alleged Steam 2FA codes ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/twilio-denies-breach-following-leak-of-alleged-steam-2fa-codes\/)\n  * [ ![Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Microsoft May 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes 5 exploited zero-days, 72 flaws ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-may-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-5-exploited-zero-days-72-flaws\/)\n  * [ ![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Windows 11 KB5058411 and KB5058405 cumulative updates released ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-kb5058411-and-kb5058405-cumulative-updates-released\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03m1Jw30 )\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/nova-scotia-power-confirms-hackers-stole-customer-data-in-cyberattack\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.6107851348472383)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n![](https:\/\/sync.intentiq.com\/profiles_engine\/ProfilesEngineServlet?at=20&mi=10&secure=1&dpi=456059511&iiqidtype=2&iiqpcid=bb5acec5-ef24-4741-9227-389069feb773&iiqpciddate=1747328410715&tsrnd=237_1747328410715&vrref=&jsver=5.082)\n",,
