"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [Meta to Train AI on E.U. User Data From May 27 Without Consent; Noyb Threatens Lawsuit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html)\n_\ue802_ May 15, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananAI Training \/ Data Protection\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjNDV7RaVWy7oIolFm4g_uLVp282bNtK1a2q0K3pBerDV-6vvGffgbodDS7o_ZH_Tw7T-LyX5YbhW2RMyG1y640NM7AOhqLXgY9fStAkBanZxS1j1_uaPLm4BJ3um69JfCU4eOx6U7WvUWYCbtBCt2DfOPOZBzNAkp4QFdobvjaZ_N-bSWfdH3R0JU02QpV\/s728-rw-e365\/meta-ai.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjNDV7RaVWy7oIolFm4g_uLVp282bNtK1a2q0K3pBerDV-6vvGffgbodDS7o_ZH_Tw7T-LyX5YbhW2RMyG1y640NM7AOhqLXgY9fStAkBanZxS1j1_uaPLm4BJ3um69JfCU4eOx6U7WvUWYCbtBCt2DfOPOZBzNAkp4QFdobvjaZ_N-bSWfdH3R0JU02QpV\/s728-rw-e365\/meta-ai.jpg)\nAustrian privacy non-profit noyb (none of your business) has sent Meta's Irish headquarters a cease-and-desist letter, threatening the company with a class action lawsuit if it proceeds with its plans to train users' data for training its artificial intelligence (AI) models without an explicit opt-in.\nThe move comes weeks after the social media behemoth [announced](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/meta-resumes-eu-ai-training-using.html) its plans to train its AI models using public data shared by adults across Facebook and Instagram in the European Union (E.U.) starting May 27, 2025, after it paused the efforts in June 2024 following concerns raised by Irish data protection authorities.\n\"Instead of asking consumers for opt-in consent, Meta relies on an alleged 'legitimate interest' to just suck up all user data,\" noyb [said](https:\/\/noyb.eu\/en\/noyb-sends-meta-cease-and-desist-letter-over-ai-training-european-class-action-potential-next-step) in a statement. \"Meta may face massive legal risks \u2013 just because it relies on an 'opt-out' instead of an 'opt-in' system for AI training.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe advocacy group further noted that Meta AI is not compliant with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) in the region, and that, besides claiming that it has a \"[legitimate interest](https:\/\/www.gdpreu.org\/the-regulation\/key-concepts\/legitimate-interest\/)\" in taking user data for AI training, the company is also limiting the right to opt-out before the training has started.\nNoyb also pointed out that even if 10% of Meta's users expressly agree to hand over the data for this purpose, it would amount to enough data points for the company to learn E.U. languages.\nIt's worth pointing out that Meta previously [claimed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/06\/meta-halts-ai-training-on-eu-user-data.html) that it needed to collect this information to capture the diverse languages, geography, and cultural references of the region.\n\"Meta starts a huge fight just to have an opt-out system instead of an opt-in system,\" noyb's Max Schrems said. \"Instead, they rely on an alleged 'legitimate interest' to just take the data and run with it. This is neither legal nor necessary.\"\n\"Meta's absurd claims that stealing everyone's personal data is necessary for AI training is laughable. Other AI providers do not use social network data \u2013 and generate even better models than Meta.\"\nThe privacy group also accused the company of moving ahead with its plans by putting the onus on users and pointed out that national data protection authorities have largely stayed silent on the legality of AI training without consent.\n\"It therefore seems that Meta simply moved ahead anyways \u2013 taking another huge legal risk in the E.U. and trampling over users' rights,\" noyb added.\nIn a statement shared with Reuters, Meta has [rejected](https:\/\/www.reuters.com\/sustainability\/boards-policy-regulation\/advocacy-group-threatens-meta-with-injunction-over-use-eu-data-ai-training-2025-05-14\/) noyb's arguments, stating they are wrong on the facts and the law, and that it has provided E.U. users with a \"clear\" option to object to their data being processed for AI training.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThis is not the first time Meta's reliance on GDPR's \"legitimate interest\" to collect data without explicit opt-in consent has come under scrutiny. In August 2023, the company [agreed](https:\/\/about.fb.com\/news\/2023\/01\/how-meta-uses-legal-bases-for-processing-ads-in-the-eu\/) to change the legal basis from \"legitimate interest\" to a consent-based approach to process user data for serving targeted ads for people in the region.\nThe disclosure comes as the Belgian Court of Appeal [ruled](https:\/\/www.dataprotectionauthority.be\/citizen\/the-market-court-rules-in-the-iab-europe-case) the [Transparency and Consent Framework](https:\/\/www.iccl.ie\/digital-data\/eu-ruling-tracking-based-advertising-by-google-microsoft-amazon-x-across-europe-has-no-legal-basis\/), used by Google, Microsoft, Amazon, and other companies to obtain consent for data processing for personalized advertising purposes, is [illegal](https:\/\/iabeurope.eu\/belgian-market-court-confirms-limited-role-of-iab-europe-in-tcf\/) across Europe, citing violation of several principles of GDPR laws.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmeta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html&t=Meta%20to%20Train%20AI%20on%20E.U.%20User%20Data%20From%20May%2027%20Without%20Consent%3B%20Noyb%20Threatens%20Lawsuit) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Meta%20to%20Train%20AI%20on%20E.U.%20User%20Data%20From%20May%2027%20Without%20Consent%3B%20Noyb%20Threatens%20Lawsuit \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmeta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmeta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmeta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html&text=Meta%20to%20Train%20AI%20on%20E.U.%20User%20Data%20From%20May%2027%20Without%20Consent%3B%20Noyb%20Threatens%20Lawsuit)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[AI Training](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/AI%20Training)[data collection](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/data%20collection)[data protection](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/data%20protection)[European Union](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/European%20Union)[GDPR](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/GDPR)[Meta](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Meta)[Privacy](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Privacy)[Social media](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Social%20media)[User Consent](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/User%20Consent)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj5q7racGwMr5emA21v4uOtTjSF4X1U2UIB1VXdECJy_UlSerg-4nUz1sWoQPECXE52nExclTrzA8PSWUvGhM_NOY6KlHcLZHn61pnpthgtEfcAqeRnCVYq1timp_hDOibhzVIVe88exkuUO-W29dSFiS96BH2j2HD-_-aPf7X73C3l2V5FKCuy8t04tiTI\/s728-rw-e365\/cis-side-2.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/cis-controls-rsrcs)\nTrending News\n[ ![Security Tools Alone Don't Protect You \u2014 Control Effectiveness Does](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html) Security Tools Alone Don't Protect You \u2014 Control Effectiveness Does ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/security-tools-alone-dont-protect-you.html)\n[ ![NSO Group Fined $168M for Targeting 1,400 WhatsApp Users With Pegasus Spyware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html) NSO Group Fined $168M for Targeting 1,400 WhatsApp Users With Pegasus Spyware ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/nso-group-fined-168m-for-targeting-1400.html)\n[ ![Third Parties and Machine Credentials: The Silent Drivers Behind 2025's Worst Breaches](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/meta-to-train-ai-on-eu-user-data-from.html) Third Parti