"markdown": "![tp link](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_tp_link_1_2072891ccf.jpg)\nImage: Joetimetodo via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA4.0)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 15th, 2025\n# Ban sales of gear from China\u2019s TP-Link, Republican lawmakers tell Trump administration\nSales of networking products from Chinese manufacturer TP-Link should be prohibited in the U.S., more than a dozen congressional Republicans said in a letter to the Trump administration, echoing previous claims that the company presents a national security risk and engages in predatory pricing. \nSenate Intelligence Committee Chairman Tom Cotton and 16 other GOP lawmakers [wrote](https:\/\/www.cotton.senate.gov\/imo\/media\/doc\/tplinkfinal.pdf) this week to Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick, saying his department should block future sales of TP-Link\u2019s popular small office\/home office (SOHO) internet routers. \n\u201cTP-Link\u2019s deep ties to the Chinese Communist Party (CCP), use of predatory pricing to eliminate trusted U.S. alternatives, and role in embedding foreign surveillance and destructive capabilities into our networks render it a clear and present danger,\u201d the senators wrote. \nSOHO routers from various manufacturers have been [vulnerable to botnets](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ballista-botnet-tp-link-archer-routers) used for cybercrime and nation-state cyberthreats. In 2024 the FBI touted [takedowns](https:\/\/therecord.media\/fbi-dismantles-flax-typhoon-china-linked-botnet-wray-aspen) of at least two botnets attributed to Chinese state-backed hackers. Lawmakers [asked](https:\/\/therecord.media\/routers-from-tp-link-security-commerce-department) the Commerce Department last year to investigate security risks presented by TP-Link routers. \nIn an emailed statement, TP-Link said the latest letter was \u201cunfortunately based on unfounded press rumors.\u201d The company said it is not state-sponsored and has no ties to the ruling Chinese Communist Party, adding that \u201cTP-Link has been the victim of a smear campaign, driven by the goal of removing a competitor from the marketplace.\u201d \nTP-Link said it has received no inquiries from U.S. antitrust investigators, and it maintains that the Commerce Department \u201cdoes not have legal authority to immediately prohibit sales of TP-Link products.\u201d The company has a U.S. office in Irvine, California, but is based in Shenzen, China. \nIn requesting the ban on TP-Link router sales, the lawmakers cited [Executive Order 13873](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/eo-13873), signed by President Donald Trump in his first term, which allows the Commerce Department to prohibit foreign-made products deemed to present threats to national security. \nIn a detailed [blog post](https:\/\/www.tp-link.com\/us\/press\/news\/21656\/) in March, TP-Link disputed [testimony](https:\/\/selectcommitteeontheccp.house.gov\/committee-activity\/hearings\/hearing-end-typhoons-how-deter-beijings-cyber-actions-and-enhance) in a House panel about the company\u2019s links to the CCP and its American market share. TP-Link said the [Volt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/volt-typhoon), [Salt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/salt-typhoon), and [Flax Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/flax-typhoon) hacking campaigns attributed to China \u201chave no discernible preference for using TP-Link routers as a vector.\u201d \nIn late April the company [praised](https:\/\/www.tp-link.com\/us\/press\/news\/21761\/) the House passage of the [ROUTERS Act](https:\/\/www.congress.gov\/bill\/119th-congress\/house-bill\/866), legislation that would direct the Commerce Department to study \u201cthe national security risks posed by consumer routers and modems.\u201d \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Ban sales of gear from China\u2019s TP-Link, Republican lawmakers tell Trump administration)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Ban sales of gear from China\u2019s TP-Link, Republican lawmakers tell Trump administration )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/technology)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [TP-Link](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/tp-link)\n  * [Congress](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/congress)\n  * [Trump administration](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/trump-administration)\n  * [China](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/china)\n  * [Salt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/salt-typhoon)\n  * [Volt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/volt-typhoon)\n  * [router](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/router)\n  * [hardware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/hardware)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [Proofpoint to acquire European cloud security firm Hornetsecurity for over $1 billionMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/proofpoint-hornetsecurity-acquisition)\n  * [Attack claimed by pro-Ukraine hackers reportedly erases a third of Russian court case archiveMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-court-system-hack-third-of-case-files-deleted)\n  * [Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agenciesMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kremlin-linked-hackers-target-webmail-eastern-europe-governments)\n  * [Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackersMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice)\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n  * [Cybersecurity incident forces largest US steelmaker to take some operations offlineMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cyber-incident-forces-nucor-steel-to-take-systems-offline)\n  * [Russian internet shutdown that disrupted essential services condemned by rights groupsMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-internet-shutdown-condemned-by-rights-groups)\n  * [Russian military cadet reportedly arrested for selling hacking tool to FSB agentMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-military-cadet-reportedly-arrested-for-selling-hacking-tool)\n  * [Alabama state government says cyber incident\u2019s effects are limited, but response continuesMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-state-government-cyber-incident)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
