"summary": "The article discusses a cyberespionage campaign named 'RoundPress' attributed to Russian state-sponsored hackers, APT28. The campaign targeted government and military organizations using XSS vulnerabilities in webmail software to steal sensitive information. The affected webmail products include Roundcube, Horde, MDaemon, and Zimbra. Vulnerabilities like CVE-2020-35730, CVE-2023-43770, CVE-2024-11182, and CVE-2024-27443 were exploited. The campaign impacted organizations in Europe, Ukraine, and Ecuador across sectors like government, military, and critical infrastructure. The attacks involved spear-phishing emails with malicious JavaScript payloads.",,
