"summary": "The Windows 10 KB5058379 cumulative update, released by Microsoft as part of the May 2025 Patch Tuesday, is causing some devices to trigger unexpected BitLocker recovery prompts after installation and restart. This issue affects some devices, with reports mainly from users of Lenovo, Dell, and HP hardware. The root cause seems connected to a conflict involving Trusted Execution Technology (TXT) and Secure Boot settings. Microsoft has provided a workaround involving disabling Secure Boot and virtualization technologies, though these solutions may compromise security. Microsoft is reportedly aware of the issue and investigating a fix.",,
