"summary": "A high-severity vulnerability in the Chrome web browser, identified as CVE-2025-4664, was discovered by Solidlab security researcher Vsevolod Kokorin. The flaw involves insufficient policy enforcement in Chrome's Loader component, allowing remote attackers to leak cross-origin data via malicious HTML. The vulnerability has a public exploit, indicating active exploitation, and has been added to CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. U.S. federal agencies are required to patch their Chrome installations by May 7th. This is the second actively exploited Chrome zero-day patched by Google this year.",,
