"markdown": "[ Branded ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/category\/branded)\n# I\u2019m a Liverpool fan & I\u2019m bringing my Man United-supporting friends to the Football for All Carnival on May 25\nBecause you\u2019ll never celebrate alone. \n[ ![author profile](https:\/\/news.google.com\/assets\/images\/global\/author-logo.png) ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNY3lFUlF6TWdxcDBDckJfODZicWRDNkJ6WDlXMnhHSEF3T2U1Zy1icUxTdEZ1akJ5RzFRZS13V1lfMGw0T0MyTlZFYlNOTUt4cUhtUG9mUGJldHZadU5aanpZWW1pdzhoZ2M3c1U5UFUzckd6NzNwMGMyR0lMSDNKRA?oc=5#author) [Tristan Koay](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNY3lFUlF6TWdxcDBDckJfODZicWRDNkJ6WDlXMnhHSEF3T2U1Zy1icUxTdEZ1akJ5RzFRZS13V1lfMGw0T0MyTlZFYlNOTUt4cUhtUG9mUGJldHZadU5aanpZWW1pdzhoZ2M3c1U5UFUzckd6NzNwMGMyR0lMSDNKRA?oc=5#author)\n[ ![author profile](https:\/\/news.google.com\/assets\/images\/global\/author-logo.png) ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNY3lFUlF6TWdxcDBDckJfODZicWRDNkJ6WDlXMnhHSEF3T2U1Zy1icUxTdEZ1akJ5RzFRZS13V1lfMGw0T0MyTlZFYlNOTUt4cUhtUG9mUGJldHZadU5aanpZWW1pdzhoZ2M3c1U5UFUzckd6NzNwMGMyR0lMSDNKRA?oc=5#author) [Branded](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMigAFBVV95cUxNY3lFUlF6TWdxcDBDckJfODZicWRDNkJ6WDlXMnhHSEF3T2U1Zy1icUxTdEZ1akJ5RzFRZS13V1lfMGw0T0MyTlZFYlNOTUt4cUhtUG9mUGJldHZadU5aanpZWW1pdzhoZ2M3c1U5UFUzckd6NzNwMGMyR0lMSDNKRA?oc=5#sponsored)\n![clock](https:\/\/news.google.com\/assets\/images\/global\/time.png)\n### May 16, 2025, 06:00 PM\n![image](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/starhub-football-for-all-carnival.png)\nLiverpool have clinched their 20th league title, finally equalling Manchester United\u2019s record. \nAs a Liverpool Fan, I couldn\u2019t be happier. Some of my friends, for obvious reasons, are not as pleased. \nBut before I rub my hands with glee, the football gods whispered in my ear: \u201cFootball is supposed to unite, not divide.\u201d \nThat\u2019s why I\u2019ve decided to bring my Manchester United-supporting friends to StarHub\u2019s \u201cFootball for All\u201d Carnival. \nStarHub, together with official venue partner Resorts World Sentosa, will be screening all 10 final-day matches live at the Resorts World Convention Centre. \nHere, they\u2019ll be able to celebrate all things football, as well as Liverpool\u2019s title win, of course. \nBut I\u2019m not there to just gloat (it\u2019s hardly in my nature, I swear) as there is plenty of football left. \nThe title-race may be wrapped up, but fans still have plenty to look forward to with the race for European places still ongoing. Newcastle, Manchester City, Chelsea, Aston Villa and Nottingham Forest are all vying it out for the remaining Champions League places. \nWhat\u2019s more, attendees can expect a special appearance from Premier League legends Joe Hart (formerly of Manchester City) and John Barnes (formerly of Liverpool). \n![](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/starhub-ffa-stars.jpg) Photo from StarHub. \nFestivities will kick off from 7pm, with football-themed games, family-friendly activities and exciting giveaways, so even your non-football-loving friends have reasons to tag along. \nThere will also be one lucky winner who will win a pair of hospitality tickets to a Premier League 2025\/26 match. \n![](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/starhub-ffa-activities.png) Photo from StarHub. \nThere will also be exclusive goodie bags up for grabs, available on a first-come, first-served basis. \nAs part of StarHub\u2019s 25th birthday celebrations, the event is free for all to attend. \nAll you need to do is sign up at the link [here](https:\/\/www.starhub.com\/personal\/bundles\/football-carnival.html). Fastest fingers only, as space is limited. \nAttendees can also sign up for an exclusive Broadband offer with a 50-inch Samsung UHD TV, alongside two free seasons of the Premier League. \nThere will be free shuttle services from Resorts World Sentosa to Harbourfront available from 11:30pm till 2:30am. \nPerfect. You\u2019ll never celebrate alone. \n## StarHub\u2019s \u201cFootball for All\u201d Carnival\n![](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/starhub-football-for-all.jpg) Photo from StarHub. \n**Date:** May 25, 2025 (Sunday) \n**Time:** From 7pm onwards (11pm kick-off time for all matches) \n**Venue:** Resorts World Convention Centre, 8 Sentosa Gateway, S098269 \n_**This branded article by StarHub has elevated the friendship between this writer and his Man United-supporting friends.**_\n_Cover photo from Mothership._\nEvents\nFollow us on and [ Telegram ](https:\/\/t.me\/mothershipsg)to get the latest updates.\n  * [![image](https:\/\/news.google.com\/assets\/images\/global\/telegram.png)](https:\/\/t.me\/mothershipsg)\n\n\nMORE STORIES\n[![image](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/starhub-football-for-all-carnival.png)](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/liverpool-manchester-united-starhub-football\/)\n####  [Branded](https:\/\/news.google.com\/category\/branded) May 16, 2025, 06:00 PM\n##  [I\u2019m a Liverpool fan & I\u2019m bringing my Man United-supporting friends to the Football for All Carnival on May 25](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/liverpool-manchester-united-starhub-football\/)\n[![image](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/Article-cover-photo-2-2025-05-16T164932.134.jpg)](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/hit-and-run-serangoon-man-visually-impaired\/)\n####  [News](https:\/\/news.google.com\/category\/news) May 16, 2025, 05:08 PM\n##  [Hit-&-run in Serangoon: Man, 60, who is visually impaired, found bleeding on road](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/hit-and-run-serangoon-man-visually-impaired\/)\n[![image](https:\/\/static.mothership.sg\/1\/2025\/05\/teo-heng.png)](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/teo-heng-terminal-3\/)\n####  [Nova](https:\/\/news.google.com\/category\/nova) May 16, 2025, 04:37 PM\n##  [Karaoke chain Teo Heng opens outlet at Changi Airport Terminal 3](https:\/\/mothership.sg\/2025\/05\/t