"summary": "Ransomware gangs are increasingly utilizing a malware named Skitnet ('Bossnet') for stealthy post-exploitation activities. Skitnet has been gaining traction among ransomware operations since early 2025. It is commonly deployed in Microsoft Teams phishing attacks and other real-world scenarios by ransomware groups like BlackBasta and Cactus. The malware is distinguished by its Rust-based loader, its DNS-based reverse shell communications, and its capabilities for persistence, remote access, and execution of PowerShell scripts. This commercially available malware presents a cost-effective and less attributable option for threat actors.",,
