"summary": "The Lecardo Clinic in Chuvashia, Russia, experienced a multi-day shutdown due to a cyberattack claimed by the pro-Ukraine hacker group 4B1D. The attack targeted the clinic's software for managing patient records, accessing the system through the compromised account of the clinic's director. The hackers wiped servers, deleted backups, encrypted and exported patient data, affecting the operations of over 100 computers. Personal data of 52,000 individuals was compromised, with some records sold on the dark web. Local prosecutors are investigating staff compliance with information security regulations.",,
