"title": "Key lawmaker says pause in offensive cyber operations against Russia lasted one day",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-pause-offensive-cyber-operations-russia-lasted-one-day-rep-bacon-says",,
"summary": "The article details the U.S. Defense Department's temporary halt of offensive cyber operations against Russia, which lasted only one day. This pause was confirmed by Rep. Don Bacon, who leads the House Armed Services Cyber Subcommittee and occurred amidst negotiations during the Trump administration's effort to end Russia\u2019s war on Ukraine. No officials from the Trump administration have publicly acknowledged the halt, and a Department of Defense (DOD) rapid response account denied such an order. The halt and other administrative decisions, such as the firing of Cyber Command and NSA chief Timothy Haugh, draw bipartisan criticism, indicating potential impacts on national security. This is a cyber-related geopolitical event with no specific vulnerabilities, malware, or directly affected products detailed.",,
