"summary": "Procolored, a printing solutions provider, inadvertently included malware in the official software for their printers, specifically a remote access trojan (RAT) and a cryptocurrency stealer. This issue persisted for at least six months, impacting multiple printer models primarily distributed through the Mega file-sharing platform. The malware, identified as XRedRAT and SnipVex, posed a significant threat by enabling remote control capabilities and manipulation of cryptocurrency transactions. Following the discovery, Procolored removed the software from its website for thorough malware scanning.",,
