"title": "OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hack",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner",,
"summary": "Senator Mark Warner has advised the Office of Personnel Management (OPM) to maintain its identity protection services, introduced after the extensive data breach in 2015. This breach affected 21.5 million individuals, compromising sensitive information such as Social Security numbers and birthdates. The Senator highlighted that the Department of Government Efficiency's budget-cutting initiative should not affect these critical services, which protect federal employees from further victimization. He emphasized the potential long-term risks associated with the stolen data, including fingerprints and medical records.",,
