"title": "Ransomware Is Changing Financial Services\u2014Are You Ready?",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.security.com\/expert-perspectives\/ransomware-changing-financial-services",,
"summary": "Ransomware is a significant threat to financial services, with evolving regulations defining data security standards. The financial sector has seen a doubling of reported ransomware attacks from 2021 to 2024, causing insurance premiums to rise. Notable regulations like NYDFS, GLBA, and European laws mandate enhanced cybersecurity measures. The article describes Ally Bank's breach as an example of the risks and discusses various compliance-driven security strategies.",,
