"title": "Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft has confirmed that some Windows 10 and Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2021 systems boot into BitLocker recovery after installing the May 2025 security updates (KB5058379). BitLocker is a Windows security feature that encrypts drives to protect data. Affected systems may display BitLocker recovery screens after installing the update, requiring recovery keys to start. Users have reported seeing these issues across a variety of system configurations, including devices from Lenovo, Dell, and HP. There are no mentions of specific vulnerabilities, malware, or threat groups in the article. Microsoft is investigating the issue to determine the root cause and will provide updates. Some recommendations include disabling Intel Trusted Execution Technology or Secure Boot to bypass recovery prompts. There is no mention of specific motivations or active exploitation.",,
