"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Firefox Patches 2 Zero-Days Exploited at Pwn2Own Berlin with $100K in Rewards](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html)\n_\ue802_ May 19, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananBrowser Security \/ Vulnerability\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiIcxpAWOa6Hr8B2dRjoacBO5J2kmFI5MSZnAegbkVXakygRaT7seCDpCIE3AGkeLFrSNQuEx3DDDCQ961olReVHLX78m6tVdEGBFx4vOJXLfYbLAbDhKybuyakpH6f3GmZ3pXGo2zciVnl1AYqEiPx04m33YTaSIL8w9ycL4UJQivJm3gl5O1cMyopPsOY\/s728-rw-e365\/forefox.jpg)\nMozilla has released security updates to address two critical security flaws in its Firefox browser that could be potentially exploited to access sensitive data or achieve code execution.\nThe vulnerabilities, both of which were exploited as a zero-day at Pwn2Own Berlin, are listed below -\n  * CVE-2025-4918 - An out-of-bounds access vulnerability when resolving Promise objects that could allow an attacker to perform read or write on a JavaScript Promise object\n  * CVE-2025-4919 - An out-of-bounds access vulnerability when optimizing linear sums that could allow an attacker to perform read or write on a JavaScript object by confusing array index sizes\n\n\nIn other words, successful exploitation of either of the flaws could permit an adversary to achieve [out-of-bounds read](https:\/\/cwe.mitre.org\/data\/definitions\/125.html) or [write](https:\/\/cwe.mitre.org\/data\/definitions\/787.html), which could then be abused to access otherwise sensitive information or result in memory corruption that could pave the way for code execution.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-3 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe vulnerabilities affect the following versions of the Firefox browser -\n  * All versions of [Firefox before 138.0.4](https:\/\/www.mozilla.org\/en-US\/security\/advisories\/mfsa2025-36\/)\n  * All versions of [Firefox Extended Support Release (ESR) before 128.10.1](https:\/\/www.mozilla.org\/en-US\/security\/advisories\/mfsa2025-37\/)\n  * All versions of [Firefox ESR before 115.23.1](https:\/\/www.mozilla.org\/en-US\/security\/advisories\/mfsa2025-38\/)\n\n\nEdouard Bochin and Tao Yan from Palo Alto Networks have been credited with finding and reporting CVE-2025-4918. The discovery of CVE-2025-4919 has been credited to Manfred Paul.\nIt's worth noting that both shortcomings were [demonstrated](https:\/\/www.zerodayinitiative.com\/blog\/2025\/5\/16\/pwn2own-berlin-2025-day-two-results) at the [Pwn2Own Berlin](https:\/\/www.zerodayinitiative.com\/blog\/2025\/5\/17\/pwn2own-berlin-2025-day-three-results) hacking contest last week for which they were awarded $50,000 each.\nWith web browsers continuing to be an attractive vector for malware delivery, users are advised to update their instances to the latest version to safeguard against potential threats.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_ Share on Linkedin](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf281_ Share on Reddit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf0e0_ Share on Email](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploited.html#link_share) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/firefox-patches-2-zero-days-exploit