"title": "UK government confirms massive data breach following hack of Legal Aid Agency",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-legal-aid-agency-data-breach",,
"summary": "The UK Ministry of Justice has confirmed a significant data breach following a cyberattack on the Legal Aid Agency's online platform. Hackers accessed extensive personal information of applicants for legal aid, including potentially sensitive data such as criminal histories, affecting individuals who have used the service since 2010. The attackers claim to have data on over 2 million people and threaten to release the information online. The UK government has secured a legal injunction to prevent data distribution, and law enforcement, including the National Crime Agency, is investigating. The breach has impacted public services and raised concerns about security measures in place to protect vulnerable individuals.",,
