"title": "SolarWinds security chief on the risks and rewards of being a CISO",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/solarwinds-security-chief-tim-brown-interview",,
"summary": "The article discusses an interview with Tim Brown, the chief information security officer of SolarWinds, focusing on the challenges he faced during the 2020 Sunburst incident where Russian operatives inserted malware into SolarWinds' Orion IT monitoring application, affecting major U.S. government departments and high-value targets. Brown talks about lessons learned in transparency and communication during cyber incidents, the role of the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC) and other agencies in cybersecurity, and gives his perspective on nation-state threats, particularly from Russia and China. The content focuses on various cybersecurity incidents and threats involving hackers erasing a third of Russian court case archives, targeting webmail servers of Eastern European government agencies, and potential data breaches at Nova Scotia Power. It highlights the threats posed by malware such as TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger and discusses broader geopolitical and cyber implications involving threat actors.",,
