"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [RVTools Official Site Hacked to Deliver Bumblebee Malware via Trojanized Installer](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html)\n_\ue802_ May 19, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananMalware \/ Supply Chain Attack\n[![Bumblebee Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiqwSRRvndYEfYUh806L-fRrWP18sXtzw10WRKFvK_ZTyLCiM7pj8L5fAv-i8HrImfoGVl1z4vi1I6rDoJkiawJ_MZudJfjENhv7TbxjBMvknHhafsUzg1MVbxuO51im4BkIIGA0ETFxhyphenhyphenwzr7oK2wgBnD9P3SN_f_eRsRfzTWrBOZSoIlGB4-YPGjq36Xc\/s728-rw-e365\/malware-software.jpg)\nThe official site for RVTools has been hacked to serve a compromised installer for the popular VMware environment reporting utility.\n\"Robware.net and RVTools.com are currently offline. We are working expeditiously to restore service and appreciate your patience,\" the company [said](https:\/\/www.robware.net\/home) in a statement posted on its website.\n\"Robware.net and RVTools.com are the only authorized and supported websites for RVTools software. Do not search for or download purported RVTools software from any other websites or sources.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe development comes after security researcher Aidan Leon [revealed](https:\/\/zerodaylabs.net\/rvtools-bumblebee-malware\/) that an infected version of the installer downloaded from the website was being used to sideload a [malicious DLL](https:\/\/www.virustotal.com\/gui\/file\/27282e66e73fb247ba92a91f500b52d641549a8388e35155938b0d2da3abd537) that turned out to be a known malware loader called [Bumblebee](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/02\/bumblebee-malware-returns-with-new.html).\nIt's currently not known how long the trojanized version of RVTools had been available for download and how many had installed it before the site was taken offline.\nIn the interim, users are recommended to verify the installer's hash and review any execution of version.dll from user directories.\nThe disclosure comes as it has come to light that the official software supplied with Procolored printers included a Delphi-based backdoor called XRed and a clipper malware dubbed SnipVex that's capable of substituting wallet addresses in the clipboard with that of a hard-coded address.\nDetails of the malicious activity were [first discovered](https:\/\/www.hackster.io\/news\/the-maker-s-toolbox-procolored-v11-pro-dto-uv-printer-review-680d491e17e3) by Cameron Coward, who is behind the YouTube channel Serial Hobbyism.\n[XRed](https:\/\/www.esentire.com\/blog\/xred-backdoor-the-hidden-threat-in-trojanized-programs), believed to be active since at least 2019, comes with features to collect system information, log keystrokes, propagate via connected USB drives, and execute commands sent from an attacker-controlled server to capture screenshots, enumerate file systems and directories, download files, and delete files from the system.\n\"[SnipVex] searches the clipboard for content that resembles a BTC address and replaces it with the attacker's address, such that cryptocurrency transactions will be diverted to the attacker,\" G DATA researcher Karsten Hahn, who further investigated the incident, [said](https:\/\/www.gdatasoftware.com\/blog\/2025\/05\/38200-printer-infected-software-downloads).\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nBut in an interesting twist, the malware infects .EXE files with the clipper functionality and makes use of an infection marker sequence \u2013 0x0A 0x0B 0x0C \u2013 at the end to avoid re-infecting the files a second time. The [wallet address](https:\/\/www.blockchain.com\/explorer\/addresses\/btc\/1BQZKqdp2CV3QV5nUEsqSg1ygegLmqRygj) in question has received 9.30857859 BTC (about $974,000) to date.\nProcolored has since acknowledged that the software packages were uploaded to the Mega file hosting service in October 2024 via USB drives and that the malware may have been introduced during this process. Software downloads are currently only available for F13 Pro, VF13 Pro, and V11 Pro products.\n\"The malware's command-and-control server has been offline since February 2024,\" Hahn noted. \"So it is not possible that XRed established a successful remote connection after that date. The accompanying clipbanker virus SnipVex is still a serious threat. Although transactions to the BTC address stopped on March 3, 2024, the file infection itself damages systems.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf09a_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf099_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[_\uf099_ Tweet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share)\n[_\uf0e1_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share)\n[_\uf09a_ Share](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share)\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf09a_ Share on Facebook](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf099_ Share on Twitter](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf0e1_ Share on Linkedin](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf281_ Share on Reddit](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf0e0_ Share on Email](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/rvtools-official-site-hacked-to-deliver.html#link_share)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[cryptocurrency](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cryptocurrency)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[data bre