"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/ai-security-risk-ebook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-ai-security-ai-risks-how-to-prevent-them-and-ai-for-defender?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q3_INB_FORM_Getting-Started-with-AI-Security-AI-Risks-How-to-Prevent-Them&sfcid=701Py00000DP3ZaIAL&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AISecurityeBook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft unveils Windows AI Foundry for AI-powered PC apps\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft unveils Windows AI Foundry for AI-powered PC apps\nBy \n###### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n  * May 19, 2025\n  * 12:18 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/02\/07\/Windows-11.jpg)\nMicrosoft is replacing 'Copilot Runtime' with Windows AI Foundry to help developers build, experiment, and reach users with AI experiences in their apps.\nWindows AI Foundry will not only include Microsoft's model but other open-source models as well, including those from Nvidia, such as NVIDIA NIM.\nWith these models, developers can integrate new AI experiences and models in their applications.\n\"In addition, Windows AI Foundry offers ready-to-use AI APIs that are powered by Windows inbox models on Copilot+ PCs for key language and vision tasks, like text intelligence, image description, text recognition, custom prompt and object erase,\" Microsoft announced in a [blog post](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windowsdeveloper\/2025\/05\/19\/advancing-windows-for-ai-development-new-platform-capabilities-and-tools-introduced-at-build-2025\/).\n\"We are announcing new capabilities like LoRA (low-rank-adaption) for finetuning our inbox SLM, Phi Silica, with custom data. We are also announcing new APIs for semantic search and knowledge retrieval so developers can build natural language search and RAG (retrieval-augmented generation) scenarios in their apps with their custom data.\"\n## AI Foundry helps dev build new AI models for their PCs\nAI Foundry in Windows also makes it easier for developers to use powerful AI models on their PCs without needing a lot of setup or optimization. It checks what kind of hardware your computer has and then shows which AI models will work best.\n![Windows Foundry AI](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1097497\/Windows%2011\/AI-Foundry.jpg)\nFor example, AI Foundry automatically matches models to your device's hardware, so if you're a developer, you don't have to figure it out.\nHere is the complete list of features:\n  * **Ready-to-use models:** It gives developers access to pre-trained open-source AI models (like those from Ollama, NVIDIA, and others) that are already optimized to run smoothly on different computer hardware, whether that's a CPU, GPU, or NPU (Neural Processing Unit).\n  * **Foundry Local: T** his helps find and use the right models for your PC. You can install it using a simple command (winget install Microsoft.FoundryLocal).\n  * **Developer tools:** Developers also get a command-line tool (CLI) and an SDK (software kit) to easily test and add these models to their apps.\n\n\nAll of these features will soon be built directly into Windows 11 and the Windows App SDK.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Windows 11 KB5055627 update released with 30 new changes, fixes](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-kb5055627-update-released-with-30-new-changes-fixes\/)\n[Windows 11's Recall AI is now rolling out on Copilot+ PCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11s-recall-ai-is-now-rolling-out-on-copilot-plus-pcs\/)\n[Microsoft: Some devices offered Windows 11 upgrades despite Intune blocks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-some-devices-offered-windows-11-upgrades-despite-intune-blocks\/)\n[Microsoft: New Windows updates fix Active Directory policy issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-new-emergency-windows-updates-fix-ad-policy-issues\/)\n[Windows 11 tests sharing apps screen and files with Copilot AI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-tests-sharing-apps-screen-and-files-with-copilot-ai\/)\n  * [Artificial Intelligence](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/artificial-intelligence\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft\/)\n  * [Model](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/model\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows AI Foundry](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-ai-foundry\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n##### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\nMayank Parmar is an technology entrepreneur who is currently pursuing an MBA. At BleepingComputer, he covers technology news with a strong focus on Microsoft and Windows-related stories. He is always poking under the hood of Windows, looking for the latest secrets to reveal. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Astaroth Unleashed story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/Astaroth-unleashed.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/astaroth-unleashed\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trua-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows BitLocker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/)\n  * [ ![Microsoft Defender](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) New 'Defendnot' tool tricks Windows into disabling Microsoft Defender ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-defendnot-tool-tricks-windows-into-disabling-microsoft-defender\/)\n  * [ ![Pwn2Own Berlin](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Hackers exploit VMware ESXi, Microsoft SharePoint zero-days at Pwn2Own ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-exploit-vmware-esxi-microsoft-sharepoint-zero-days-at-pwn2own\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03m1Jw30 )\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.19061274823759233)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n",,
