"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft confirms new \"Advanced\" Settings for Windows 11\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft confirms new \"Advanced\" Settings for Windows 11\nBy \n###### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n  * May 19, 2025\n  * 12:06 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/04\/02\/Windows-11.jpg)\nAt the Build 2025 developer conference, Microsoft announced a new 'Advanced Settings' feature to help users and developers personalize the OS experience.\nWith 'Advanced' settings, you can customize several features of Windows 11, such as File Explorer and Virtual Machines.\nThe new 'Advanced' Settings page can be accessed from Settings > System > Advanced. It replaces the 'For developers' tab in the Settings and retains all of the features.\n![Advanced Settings](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1097497\/Windows%2011\/Advanced-Settings.jpg)\nUnlike the old For Developers page, it gives users more control over how files and folders are shown and how version control works. At the top, you can see options like:\n  * Show file extensions: When turned on, you can see file types like .txt, .jpg, etc. after the file name.\n  * Show hidden and system files: This shows files that are normally hidden by Windows, like system files.\n  * Show full path in title bar: This displays the full folder path at the top of File Explorer.\n  * Show option to run as different user in Start: If turned on, you can choose to run apps as another user.\n  * Show empty drives: This shows USB or other drives even when they have nothing in them.\n\n\nAt the bottom, there\u2019s a new section called File Explorer + version control. It lets you link folders that are Git repositories. For example, the user has connected folders like:\n  * D:\\GitHub\\WSL\n  * D:\\GitHub\\terminal\n  * D:\\GitHub\\PowerToys\n\n\nThis is useful for developers who use Git, as it helps manage code versions directly from File Explorer. There's also a \"Choose folder\" button to add more Git folders.\nMicrosoft says the Advanced Settings page has been open-sourced on GitHub, and it will be maintained via the Windows Store.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Hackers earn $1,078,750 for 28 zero-days at Pwn2Own Berlin](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-earn-1-078-750-for-28-zero-days-at-pwn2own-berlin\/)\n[Windows 11 and Red Hat Linux hacked on first day of Pwn2Own](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/windows-11-and-red-hat-linux-virtualbox-hacked-on-first-day-of-pwn2own\/)\n[Windows 11 KB5058411 and KB5058405 cumulative updates released](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-kb5058411-and-kb5058405-cumulative-updates-released\/)\n[Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows 11 24H2 now ready to rollout to everyone](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-24h2-now-ready-to-rollout-to-everyone\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n##### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\nMayank Parmar is an technology entrepreneur who is currently pursuing an MBA. At BleepingComputer, he covers technology news with a strong focus on Microsoft and Windows-related stories. He is always poking under the hood of Windows, looking for the latest secrets to reveal. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-open-sources-windows-subsystem-for-linux-at-build-2025\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-unveils-windows-ai-foundry-for-ai-powered-pc-apps\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows BitLocker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/)\n  * [ ![Microsoft Defender](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) New 'Defendnot' tool tricks Windows into disabling Microsoft Defender ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-defendnot-tool-tricks-windows-into-disabling-microsoft-defender\/)\n  * [ ![Pwn2Own Berlin](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Hackers exploit VMware ESXi, Microsoft SharePoint zero-days at Pwn2Own ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-exploit-vmware-esxi-microsoft-sharepoint-zero-days-at-pwn2own\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Learn why identity attacks were the #1 threat facing organizations in 2024 ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/resources\/2024-identity-attacks?utm_campaign=12100141-FY25Q2_Bleeping-Computer-Article&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored&utm_content=external-article)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03m1Jw30 )\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.6880982209561646)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n",,
