"markdown": "![Romania election](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_Romania_elections_ac6b3f777a.jpg)\nImage: Bucharest Mayor Nicu\u0219or Dan (left) and George Simion, candidate from the Alliance for the Union of Romanians, met for a presidential debate on May 8, 2025. Credit: Alliance for the Union of Romanians\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)May 19th, 2025\n# Russia-linked disinformation floods Poland, Romania as voters cast ballots\nRomania and Poland each reported increased Russian disinformation activity ahead of their presidential elections, with authorities warning the Kremlin-backed network [Doppelg\u00e4nger](https:\/\/therecord.media\/search-results?term=Doppleganger) is actively attempting to influence voters. \nRomania\u2019s Interior Ministry [said](https:\/\/www.mai.gov.ro\/precizare-45\/) on Friday that the group, which has been operating in Europe since at least 2022, launched a new disinformation campaign targeting the second round of the Romanian presidential election held on Sunday. Last year, the country [annulled](https:\/\/therecord.media\/romania-annuls-presidential-election-over-interference) its presidential election results following revelations of Russian interference. \nAuthorities said Doppelg\u00e4nger used its typical technique of impersonating the official websites of public institutions, television stations, and press agencies. However, this time their actions were more overt, making them easier to detect, officials added. \nThe predominant narratives [pushed](https:\/\/www.euronews.com\/my-europe\/2025\/05\/15\/romania-grapples-with-disinformation-ahead-of-tense-presidential-run-off) by Russia-linked actors ahead of Sunday\u2019s vote included accusations of crimes committed by the Romanian government against its citizens, unfounded allegations of \u201cmassive electoral fraud,\u201d and claims that Sunday\u2019s vote had already been canceled. \n\u201cThe group has shown a high level of adaptability, syncing messages with key domestic and international events, and utilizing political microtargeting in sponsored campaigns,\u201d Romania's Interior Ministry said in a statement. \nRomania previously issued [warnings](https:\/\/www.ancom.ro\/avertizare-privind-prezenta-in-spatiul-autohton-online-a-unei-retele-de-site-uri-de-tip-doppelganger_7542) ahead of the first round of the election in May, which was also marked by Russian disinformation campaigns. \nRomania\u2019s pro-European Union presidential candidate Nicu\u0219or Dan won the runoff election on Sunday, defeating his far-right rival George Simion. \n**Read more:**[France rejects Telegram CEO's accusations of Romanian election interference](https:\/\/therecord.media\/france-rejects-durov-telegram-accusations-romania-election)\nIn Poland, where citizens went to the polls on Sunday in a first round of voting, authorities have discovering paid disinformation campaigns on Facebook, which appear to have been financed from outside the country. Though authorities did not elaborate on the sources, they expressed concern over the scale of the operation. \nUkraine\u2019s military intelligence (HUR) has also raised alarms, [reporting](https:\/\/t.me\/DIUkraine\/5890) that Doppelg\u00e4nger has intensified its influence efforts in Poland in the run-up to the country\u2019s presidential elections. \nAccording to HUR, Russian intelligence services are disseminating false and manipulative messages, particularly on the social media platform X. The group is utilizing bot farms and fake accounts to impersonate real voters, the agency said. \nThe narratives promoted by Doppelg\u00e4nger focus on criticizing Poland\u2019s support for Ukraine, advocating for the country\u2019s withdrawal from the European Union, and discrediting the policies of the current government. \nPoland\u2019s cybersecurity officials have previously [warned](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-elections-russia-hybrid-threats-disinformation) of an \"unprecedented\" Russian effort to disrupt the nation\u2019s elections through disinformation and hybrid cyberattacks. Poland has also accused Moscow of recruiting Polish citizens to spread disinformation. \nIn the days leading up to Sunday\u2019s election, Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk Russian hackers targeted the websites of the ruling Civic Platform party. \nFollowing the election on Sunday, Poland\u2019s pro-EU candidate and a right-wing nationalist are set to compete in the second round of voting in June. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Russia-linked disinformation floods Poland, Romania as voters cast ballots)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Russia-linked disinformation floods Poland, Romania as voters cast ballots )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Elections](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/elections)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [Doppelg\u00e4nger](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/doppelganger)\n  * [Romania](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/romania)\n  * [Poland](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/poland)\n  * [disinformation](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/disinformation)\n  * [influence operations](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/influence-operations)\n  * [Election Security](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/election-security)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n  * [OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hackMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner)\n  * [EU court rules that tracking-based online ads are illegalMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-court-rules-tracking-based-ads-illegal)\n  * [UK National Health Service suppliers asked to tackle \u2018endemic\u2019 ransomware attacksMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-nhs-suppliers-ransomware-letter)\n  * [Proofpoint to acquire European cloud security firm Hornetsecurity for over $1 billionMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/proofpoint-hornetsecurity-acquisition)\n  * [Attack claimed by pro-Ukraine hackers reportedly erases a third of Russian court case archiveMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-court-system-hack-third-of-case-files-deleted)\n  * [Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agenciesMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kremlin-linked-hackers-target-webmail-eastern-europe-governments)\n  * [Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackersMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice)\n  * [Google says hackers behind UK retail cyber campaign now also targeting USMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
