"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/aispm-for-dummies.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/ai-security-posture-management-ai-spm-for-dummies?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY26Q1_INB_FORM_AI-SPM-for-Dummies-eBook&sfcid=701Py00000KWgAHIA1&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AI-SPMDummies)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Windows 10 emergency updates fix BitLocker recovery issues\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/)\n\n\n# Windows 10 emergency updates fix BitLocker recovery issues\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 19, 2025\n  * 01:59 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/06\/12\/windows-blue-background.jpg)\nMicrosoft has released out-of-band updates to fix a known issue causing Windows 10 systems to boot into BitLocker recovery after installing the May 2025 security updates.\nTo fix systems stuck at a BitLocker recovery prompt, install today's KB5061768 emergency update, available exclusively through the [Microsoft Update Catalog](https:\/\/www.catalog.update.microsoft.com\/Search.aspx?q=KB5061768). This is also a cumulative update, meaning you won't have to install any previous updates before deploying the fix for the BitLocker recovery issue affecting your device.\nMicrosoft says that this known issue affects systems running Windows 10 22H2, Windows 10 Enterprise LTSC 2021, and Windows 10 IoT Enterprise LTSC 2021 with Intel vPro processors (10th gen or later) with Intel Trusted Execution Technology (TXT) enabled.\nConsumer devices running Home and Pro editions of Windows 10 are also unlikely to be impacted because home users don't typically use Intel vPro processors.\n\"On these systems, installing the May 13, 2025, Windows security update (KB5058379) might cause the Local Security Authority Subsystem Service (LSASS) process to terminate unexpectedly, triggering an Automatic Repair prompting for the BitLocker recovery key to continue,\" the company [said](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/may-19-2025-kb5061768-os-builds-19044-5856-and-19045-5856-out-of-band-75b27cbd-072e-4c5a-b40e-87e00aaa42dd#id0elbj=windows_10%2C_version_21h2) in an advisory issued today.\nIf you can't immediately install the KB5061768 update to revive impacted devices, you can also try disabling the Intel Trusted Execution Technology (TXT) from the BIOS.\n![BitLocker recovery screen](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2024\/BitLocker%20recovery%20screen.png)_BitLocker recovery screen (Microsoft)_\n\u200bThe company [acknowledged](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/) the issue after a [wave of reports](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5058379-update-triggering-bitlocker-recovery-after-install\/) from Windows users and admins seeing devices unexpectedly displaying a BitLocker recovery screen after entering the Windows Recovery Environment (WinRE) and after installing the [KB5058379 cumulative update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5058379-update-fixes-sgrmbroker-errors-in-event-viewer\/) released as part of the [May 2025 Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-may-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-5-exploited-zero-days-72-flaws\/).\nAccording to Redmond, impacted users who check the Windows Event Viewer can see LSASS errors and installation failure events with 0x800F0845 errors in the System event log.\n\"On affected devices, upon installing the update, Windows might fail to start enough times to trigger an Automatic Repair,\" [the company said](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/status-windows-10-22h2#windows-10-might-repeatedly-display-the-bitlocker-recovery-screen-at-startup) in a Windows release health update. \"On devices with BitLocker enabled, BitLocker requires the input of your BitLocker recovery key to initiate an Automatic Repair.\"\nIn August 2022, Windows devices were hit by a similar issue, which caused devices to after installing the KB5012170 security update.\nLast year, in August, Microsoft [fixed another known issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-issue-that-sent-pcs-into-bitlocker-recovery\/) triggering BitLocker recovery prompts on Windows 10, Windows 11, and Windows Server systems after [installing the July 2024 Windows security updates](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-july-security-updates-send-pcs-into-bitlocker-recovery\/).\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/)\n[Windows 10 KB5058379 update triggers BitLocker recovery on some devices](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5058379-update-triggering-bitlocker-recovery-after-install\/)\n[Microsoft silently fixes Start menu bug affecting Windows 10 PCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-silently-fixes-start-menu-bug-affecting-windows-10-pcs\/)\n[Microsoft fixes bug causing incorrect Windows Recovery errors](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-bug-causing-incorrect-windows-recovery-errors\/)\n[Microsoft: New Windows updates fix Active Directory policy issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-new-emergency-windows-updates-fix-ad-policy-issues\/)\n  * [BitLocker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/bitlocker\/)\n  * [BitLocker Recovery](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/bitlocker-recovery\/)\n  * [KB5058379](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kb5058379\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Recovery](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/recovery\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 10](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-10\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/arla-foods-confirms-cyberattack-disrupts-production-causes-delays\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/skuld-stealer.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/tmpn-skuld-stealer-the-dark-side-of-open-source\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trus-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows BitLocker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/)\n  * [ ![Microsoft Defender](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) New 'Defendnot' tool tricks Windows into disabling Microsoft Defender ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-defendnot-tool-tricks-windows-into-disabling-microsoft-defender\/)\n  * [ ![Pwn2Own Berlin](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) Hackers exploit VMware ESXi, Microsoft SharePoint zero-days at Pwn2Own ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-exploit-vmware-esxi-microsoft-sharepoint-zero-days-at-pwn2own\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](h