"summary": "Two significant data breaches have exposed sensitive healthcare information of over 500,000 individuals. Serviceaide's database hosting details of 483,126 people for Catholic Health was accessed by hackers between September and November 2024. Although no copying activity was confirmed, data including Social Security numbers and medical records were at risk. Simultaneously, Nationwide Recovery Services, a medical debt collection firm, was breached in July 2024, affecting clients such as Harbin Clinic, Erlanger, and Hamilton Health Care System, resulting in potential exposure of financial and medical data.",,
