"markdown": "X\n[News](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/news)\n[Information Technology](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology)\nStaff Reporter \n, [ Singapore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/market\/singapore)\nPublished: \n_ 41 minutes ago _\n![](https:\/\/news.google.com\/s3\/files\/styles\/article_details_tablet_image\/public\/2025-05\/starhubtrendsmou2.jpg.webp?itok=Ebo5GL5n)\nPress photo\n#  StarHub expands regional footprint in new Philippine tech partnership \n**It aims to help businesses in the Philippines accelerate their adoption of digital technologies.**\n[StarHub](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/telecom-internet\/news\/starhubs-net-earnings-down-184-in-q1) has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with Philippine-based ICT firm Trends and Technologies, Inc. (Trends), expanding its presence in the region.\nThe agreement aims to help businesses in the Philippines accelerate their adoption of digital technologies.\nUnder the partnership, Starhub will deliver integrated solutions built on its modern digital infrastructure platform, powered by Cloud Infinity, and its managed services capabilities.\nMoreover, the collaboration will offer businesses in the region secure and scalable tech solutions, backed by local support.\n## Follow the link for more news on \n[ Starhub ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/company\/starhub)\n## Also Read\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/singapore-lags-asean-peers-in-cybersecurity-readiness)\n###  [ Singapore lags ASEAN peers in cybersecurity readiness ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/singapore-lags-asean-peers-in-cybersecurity-readiness)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/singapore-firms-report-660000-in-losses-software-issues-report)\n###  [ Singapore firms report $660,000 in losses from software issues: report ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/singapore-firms-report-660000-in-losses-software-issues-report)\nJoin Singapore Business Review community \nSince you're here...\n...there are many ways you can work with us to advertise your company and connect to your customers. Our team can help you dight and create an advertising campaign, in print and digital, on this website and in print magazine. \nWe can also organize a real life or digital event for you and find thought leader speakers as well as industry leaders, who could be your potential partners, to join the event. We also run some awards programmes which give you an opportunity to be recognized for your achievements during the year and you can join this as a participant or a sponsor. \nLet us help you drive your business forward with a good partnership! \nYes, contact me \n[ I want to download the media kit  ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/digital-events)\n##  Most Read \n[ 1. Oliver opens new manufacturing facility in Johor ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/healthcare\/news\/oliver-opens-new-manufacturing-facility-in-johor) [ 2. SGX RegCo proposes shift to disclosure-based market rules ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/news\/sgx-regco-proposes-shift-disclosure-based-market-rules) [ 3. Franklin Templeton gets approval to launch first retail tokenised fund in Singapore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/news\/franklin-templeton-gets-approval-launch-first-retail-tokenised-fund-in-singapore) [ 4. Frasers Property, Frasers Hospitality Trust announced a trading halt ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets-investing\/news\/frasers-property-frasers-hospitality-trust-announced-trading-halt) [ 5. Cariflex inaugurates new $461m latex plant in Singapore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/manufacturing\/news\/cariflex-inaugurates-new-461m-latex-plant-in-singapore)\n##  [Top News](https:\/\/news.google.com\/news)\n[ DFI Retail Group reports underlying profit drop of 18% in Q1 2025 ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/retail\/news\/dfi-retail-group-reports-underlying-profit-drop-18-in-q1-2025)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/retail\/news\/dfi-retail-group-reports-underlying-profit-drop-18-in-q1-2025)\n[ DFI Retail Group reports underlying profit drop of 18% in Q1 2025 ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/retail\/news\/dfi-retail-group-reports-underlying-profit-drop-18-in-q1-2025)\nThe group still maintains its full-year profit guidance of $297.88m to $349.68m \n[ Retail ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/retail)\n17 minutes ago \n[ VFlowTech raises $26.5m to scale energy storage, boost AI energy ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/manufacturing\/news\/vflowtech-raises-265m-scale-energy-storage-boost-ai-energy)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/manufacturing\/news\/vflowtech-raises-265m-scale-energy-storage-boost-ai-energy)\n[ VFlowTech raises $26.5m to scale energy storage, boost AI energy ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/manufacturing\/news\/vflowtech-raises-265m-scale-energy-storage-boost-ai-energy)\nThis will also fund VFlowTech's global expansion. \n[ Manufacturing ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/manufacturing)\n17 minutes ago \n[ StarHub expands regional footprint in new Philippine tech partnership ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-expands-regional-footprint-in-new-philippine-tech-partnership)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-expands-regional-footprint-in-new-philippine-tech-partnership)\n[ StarHub expands regional footprint in new Philippine tech partnership ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology\/news\/starhub-expands-regional-footprint-in-new-philippine-tech-partnership)\nIt aims to help businesses in the Philippines accelerate their adoption of digital technologies. \n[ Information Technology ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/information-technology)\n41 minutes ago \n[ Economists warn April export surge may fade post-tariff pause ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/economy\/news\/economists-warn-april-export-surge-may-fade-post-tariff-pause)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/economy\/news\/economists-warn-april-export-surge-may-fade-post-tariff-pause)\n[ Economists warn April export surge may fade post-tariff pause ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/economy\/news\/economists-warn-april-export-surge-may-fade-post-tariff-pause)\nElectronics exports led the charge, soaring 23.5% YoY, driven by explosive gains in integrated circuits and personal computers. \n[ Economy ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/economy)\n2 hours ago \n##  [Exclusives](https:\/\/news.google.com\/exclusives)\n[ Singapore pushes virtual power plants to hit 2035 RE goal ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/exclusive\/singapore-pushes-virtual-power-plants-hit-2035-re-goal-0)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/exclusive\/singapore-pushes-virtual-power-plants-hit-2035-re-goal-0)\n[ Singapore pushes virtual power plants to hit 2035 RE goal ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/exclusive\/singapore-pushes-virtual-power-plants-hit-2035-re-goal-0)\nIt also wants power companies to build hydrogen-ready plants. \n21 hours ago \n[ US levies on Chinese vessels may cause shipping delays ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/shipping-marine\/exclusive\/us-levies-chinese-vessels-may-cause-shipping-delays)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/shipping-marine\/exclusive\/us-levies-chinese-vessels-may-cause-shipping-delays)\n[ US levies on Chinese vessels may cause shipping delays ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/shipping-marine\/exclusive\/us-levies-chinese-vessels-may-cause-shipping-delays)\nRedeploying vessels to US trade routes based on shipbuilding origin would be inefficient. \n[ Shipping & Marine ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/shipping-marine)\n6 days ago \n[ Johor-Singapore ecozone needs stable marketplace for energy credits ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/energy-offshore\/exclusive\/johor-singapore-ecozone-needs-stable-marketplace-energy-credits)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/energy-offshore\/exclusive\/johor-singapore-ecozone-needs-stable-marketplace-energy-credits)\n[ Johor-Singapore ecozone needs stable marketplace for energy credits ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/energy-offshore\/exclusive\/johor-singapore-ecozone-needs-stable-marketplace-energy-credits)\nThis is expected to drive investment in cross-border electricity trade. \n[ Energy & Offshore ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/energy-offshore)\n[ Thryve Earth eyes more carbon projects for \u2018planetary scale\u2019 impact ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets-investing\/exclusive\/thryve-earth-eyes-more-carbon-projects-planetary-scale-impact)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets-investing\/exclusive\/thryve-earth-eyes-more-carbon-projects-planetary-scale-impact)\n[ Thryve Earth eyes more carbon projects for \u2018planetary scale\u2019 impact ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets-investing\/exclusive\/thryve-earth-eyes-more-carbon-projects-planetary-scale-impact)\nThe startup\u2019s first three projects could yield up to 15 million carbon credits over time. \n[ Markets & Investing ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/markets-investing)\n##  [Event News](https:\/\/news.google.com\/event-news)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-dr-navin-bhatnager-y3-technologies-pte-ltd) [](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-dr-navin-bhatnager-y3-technologies-pte-ltd)\n[SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Dr Navin Bhatnager of Y3 Technologies Pte Ltd](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-dr-navin-bhatnager-y3-technologies-pte-ltd)\nDr Navin Bhatnager, Chief Executive Officer of Y3 Technologies Pte Ltd, shares how its RFID solution improves warehouse efficiency, accuracy, and customer satisfaction. \n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-brian-chow-fairprice-group-supply-chain) [](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-brian-chow-fairprice-group-supply-chain)\n[ SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Brian Chow of FairPrice Group Supply Chain](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-brian-chow-fairprice-group-supply-chain)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/co-written-partner\/event-news\/singapore-pools-brings-home-sbr-technology-excellence-awards-2025-data-centre-modernisation)\n[Co-Written \/ Partner](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/co-written-partner) [ Singapore Pools brings home SBR Technology Excellence Awards 2025 for data centre modernisation](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/co-written-partner\/event-news\/singapore-pools-brings-home-sbr-technology-excellence-awards-2025-data-centre-modernisation)\n[ ](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-international-business-awards-2025-winner-wee-tee-hsien-fujifilm-business-innovation-singapore) [](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-international-business-awards-2025-winner-wee-tee-hsien-fujifilm-business-innovation-singapore)\n[ SBR International Business Awards 2025 Winner: Wee Tee Hsien, FUJIFILM Business Innovation Singapore](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-international-business-awards-2025-winner-wee-tee-hsien-fujifilm-business-innovation-singapore)\n##  Videos \n![SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Dr Navin Bhatnager of Y3 Technologies Pte Ltd](https:\/\/www.cmgassets.com\/s3fs-public\/styles\/video_thumbnail\/public\/2025-05\/sbr-nba-2025-y3-technologies-pte-ltd.png.webp?itok=oxuSitT0)\n###  [ SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Dr Navin Bhatnager of Y3 Technologies Pte Ltd](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-dr-navin-bhatnager-y3-technologies-pte-ltd)\n![SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Brian Chow of FairPrice Group Supply Chain](https:\/\/www.cmgassets.com\/s3fs-public\/styles\/video_thumbnail\/public\/2025-05\/sbr-nba-2025-fairprice-group-supply-chain.png.webp?itok=9RfYyx_n)\n###  [ SBR National Business Awards 2025 Winner: Brian Chow of FairPrice Group Supply Chain](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/sbr-national-business-awards-2025-winner-brian-chow-fairprice-group-supply-chain)\n![Singapore businesses urged to act as inflation views split](https:\/\/www.cmgassets.com\/s3fs-public\/styles\/video_thumbnail\/public\/2025-05\/video-capture-t0031.00seg-9261.png.webp?itok=OPaQlLLj)\n###  [ Singapore businesses urged to act as inflation views split](https:\/\/sbr.com.sg\/videos\/singapore-businesses-urged-act-inflation-views-split)\n![Singapore firms deploy AI to counter s