"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers identified malicious packages in the PyPI repository designed to verify stolen email addresses against TikTok and Instagram APIs. These packages, including checker-SaGaF, steinlurks, and sinnercore, have been removed but are known for validating user accounts for nefarious purposes such as doxing, spamming, or launching credential stuffing attacks. Additional malicious packages like dbgpkg, linked to backdoor installations, were discovered, possibly connected to the Phoenix Hyena hacktivist group.",,
