"title": "Go-Based Malware Deploys XMRig Miner on Linux Hosts via Redis Configuration Abuse",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/go-based-malware-deploys-xmrig-miner-on.html",,
"summary": "A new Linux cryptojacking campaign named 'RedisRaider' has been detected, targeting publicly accessible Redis servers. This campaign uses legitimate Redis configuration commands to execute malicious cron jobs on vulnerable systems, ultimately deploying a Go-based payload responsible for unleashing an XMRig miner on compromised systems. This malware abuses Redis's commands to change configurations and schedule tasks that download the RedisRaider binary, serving as a dropper for a bespoke version of XMRig, and expanding to other Redis instances. Minimizing detection, the campaign implements anti-forensics measures. Additionally, a related campaign exploits legacy authentication protocols in Microsoft Entra ID for brute-force attacks, emphasizing vulnerabilities in outdated security architectures.",,
