"summary": "The logistics company Peter Green Chilled was hit by a ransomware attack disrupting supplies of refrigerated goods to major British supermarkets. The attack did not impact transport activities but affected the IT systems used for processing orders. This incident follows similar past attacks in the UK retail sector. There have been calls for the British government to enhance its approach to ransomware. No CVEs were mentioned, and no specific threat actors or malware were identified. The incident highlights vulnerabilities in the cybersecurity measures of logistics and distribution firms serving critical sectors like food supply chains.",,
