"markdown": "![Peter Green Chilled lorry](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_487062444_650775081245138_5285124135153519300_n_24e8f03470.jpg)\nImage: Peter Green Chilled via Facebook\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)May 20th, 2025\n# Ransomware attack hits supplier of refrigerated groceries to British supermarkets\nThe logistics company Peter Green Chilled has announced being hit by a ransomware attack that is disrupting supplies of refrigerated goods to some of the country\u2019s largest supermarkets, according to reports. \nCustomers \u2014 mostly smaller producers who provide food to regional supermarkets in Somerset, including Aldi, Tesco and Sainsbury\u2019s \u2014 were sent an email last Thursday in which the company said it would not be able to process some of their orders due to the cyber incident, as [reported](https:\/\/www.bbc.co.uk\/news\/articles\/czr88myp570o) by BBC News. \nPeter Green Chilled told the BBC the attack took place last Wednesday and that it had not impacted the company\u2019s transport activities, but declined to explain what impact the incident had on the IT systems orders are placed through. \nIt follows an attack several years ago on the cold storage and refrigerated transport firm Reed Boardall, which is responsible for moving a significant amount of the country\u2019s frozen food. \nAlthough Peter Green Chilled is a much smaller supplier than Reed Boardall, some of its customers have warned that if they were unable to get their products delivered to retailers in time then they would be spoiled. \nThe attack is the latest to impact the British retail sector following incidents impacting [Marks & Spencer](https:\/\/therecord.media\/british-retailer-marks-spencer-insurance), the [Co-op](https:\/\/therecord.media\/co-op-cyberattack-uk-company-fears-hackers-still-in-system) and the luxury store [Harrods](https:\/\/therecord.media\/harrods-cyberattack-uk-retailer) in London. \nThe slew of recent attacks, including another confirmed this week which may potentially [expose the personal details of domestic violence victims ](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-legal-aid-agency-data-breach)to their abusers, has led to renewed calls for the British government to take a more aggressive approach toward the ransomware menace. \n**Read more:** [UK government urged to get on \u2018forward foot\u2019 with ransomware instead of \u2018absorbing the punches\u2019](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-urged-to-get-on-forward-foot-with-ransomware)\nThe \u201cideal response\u201d to ransomware gang\u2019s data extortion attempts \u2014 when the gangs steal data and threaten to release it unless a sum of money is paid in cryptocurrency \u2014 is for law enforcement agencies to hack the criminals\u2019 systems and take that down, said Gareth Mott, a research fellow at the Royal United Services Institute think tank. \nMott acknowledged that doing so wasn\u2019t easy. While the National Crime Agency and its partners have had successes tackling ransomware groups like [LockBit](https:\/\/therecord.media\/lockbit-ransomware-disrupted-international-operation), Mott said he wasn\u2019t sure that it had the capability currently to selectively take down the most risky data breaches. \nRansomware attacks in the U.K. have risen year-on-year for the past five years, according to the [best dataset available](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-ico-ransomware-investigations-data), but authorities have [warned](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-increasingly-concerned-of-ransomware-victims-keeping-quiet-ncsc) they are \u201cincreasingly concerned\u201d victims are keeping incidents secret, meaning even that data provides only a partial view of the true scale of the problem. \nBack in December 2023, a parliamentary committee on national security warned that the British government\u2019s [failures to tackle ransomware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-government-risking-catastrophic-ransomware) meant there was a \u201chigh risk\u201d the country faces a \u201ccatastrophic ransomware attack at any moment.\u201d \nAlthough the Labour Party has entered government since that inquiry report was published, there has been no substantial new funding for law enforcement disruption operations. \nEarlier this year the government [proposed](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-proposes-banning-ransoms-hospitals) a major overhaul of how the country responds to ransomware attacks, including by banning public sector bodies from making extortion payments and requiring all victims to report incidents to the government \u2014 although the proposals are identical to ones formulated under the previous government, as first [reported](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-proposal-mandatory-reporting-ransomware-attacks) by Recorded Future News. \nPeter Green Chilled could not be reached for comment. An automated reply from its postmaster account declaring the company was currently only accepting messages from an allowed senders list. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Ransomware attack hits supplier of refrigerated groceries to British supermarkets)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Ransomware attack hits supplier of refrigerated groceries to British supermarkets )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [Logistics](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/industry)\n  * [Food and beverage](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [food](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/food)\n  * [retail](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/retail)\n  * [Ransomware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ransomware)\n  * [Shipping](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/shipping)\n  * [grocery](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/grocery)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Alexander Martin](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/headshot_79eb085f87.jpeg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\nis the UK Editor for Recorded Future News. He was previously a technology reporter for Sky News and is also a fellow at the European Cyber Conflict Research Initiative.\n## Briefs\n  * [Dutch government passes law to criminalize cyber-espionageMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/netherlands-law-criminalizes-cyber-espionage)\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n  * [OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hackMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner)\n  * [EU court rules that tracking-based online ads are illegalMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-court-rules-tracking-based-ads-illegal)\n  * [UK National Health Service suppliers asked to tackle \u2018endemic\u2019 ransomware attacksMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-nhs-suppliers-ransomware-letter)\n  * [Proofpoint to acquire European cloud security firm Hornetsecurity for over $1 billionMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/proofpoint-hornetsecurity-acquisition)\n  * [Attack claimed by pro-Ukraine hackers reportedly erases a third of Russian court case archiveMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-court-system-hack-third-of-case-files-deleted)\n  * [Kremlin-linked hackers target webmail servers of Eastern European government agenciesMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kremlin-linked-hackers-target-webmail-eastern-europe-governments)\n  * [Nova Scotia Power says customer banking details may have been stolen by hackersMay 14th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nova-scotia-power-data-breach-notice)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
