"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [South Asian Ministries Hit by SideWinder APT Using Old Office Flaws and Custom Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html)\n_\ue802_ May 20, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananMalware \/ Cyber Espionage\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgO6d1Ta82xBvexs6YgMM0BzcQS1ZohcRy5lcYEj3PdNVEQgS3aQa7nwtnPQBjFegJlglUYFuZ15-taL6YRD-zIFQCFBqBUkYPTcBKC2UPE97Ev-mO2IgApC9M_d6fNWA9QNJlEQDUdUjMqf2rLYW0yfdO_oXz4tqACqdSXHRQ5ONT8aaBsDKlJZlTTyHbS\/s728-rw-e365\/cyberattack.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgO6d1Ta82xBvexs6YgMM0BzcQS1ZohcRy5lcYEj3PdNVEQgS3aQa7nwtnPQBjFegJlglUYFuZ15-taL6YRD-zIFQCFBqBUkYPTcBKC2UPE97Ev-mO2IgApC9M_d6fNWA9QNJlEQDUdUjMqf2rLYW0yfdO_oXz4tqACqdSXHRQ5ONT8aaBsDKlJZlTTyHbS\/s728-rw-e365\/cyberattack.jpg)\nHigh-level government institutions in Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, and Pakistan have emerged as the target of a new campaign orchestrated by a threat actor known as SideWinder.\n\"The attackers used spear phishing emails paired with geofenced payloads to ensure that only victims in specific countries received the malicious content,\" Acronis researchers Santiago Pontiroli, Jozsef Gegeny, and Prakas Thevendaran [said](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/from-banks-to-battalions-sidewinders-attacks-on-south-asias-public-sector\/) in a report shared with The Hacker News.\nThe attack chains leverage spear-phishing lures as a starting point to activate the infection process and deploy a known malware referred to as StealerBot. It's worth pointing out that the modus operandi is consistent with recent SideWinder attacks [documented](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/03\/sidewinder-apt-targets-maritime-nuclear.html) by Kaspersky in March 2025.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nSome of the targets of the campaign, per Acronis, include Bangladesh's Telecommunication Regulatory Commission, Ministry of Defence, and Ministry of Finance; Pakistan's Directorate of Indigenous Technical Development; and Sri Lanka's Department of External Resources, Department of Treasury Operations, Ministry of Defence, and Central Bank.\nThe attacks are characterized by the use of years-old remote code execution flaws in Microsoft Office ([CVE-2017-0199 and CVE-2017-11882](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/06\/china-linked-valleyrat-malware.html)) as initial vectors to deploy malware capable of maintaining persistent access in government environments across South Asia.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiwxU2YwvD4iJofwmD8U77A66lDmo7Z1H-dWVuVCnTU8OFdsafQgcnQle831NwuMCnkvXjCHDW1ffBTmFywoB5fITOQofLwS0kV1vdYz6x3DADTQnx3OEcij66wPCs_R73YNVqqftLSSvvkJUMpsdeetkgGN2CaH15JzmeXPsLX9-aJWUMtvC0P3ZSWkEey\/s728-rw-e365\/code.jpg)\nThe malicious documents, when opened, trigger an exploit for CVE-2017-0199 to deliver next-stage payloads that are responsible for installing StealerBot by means of DLL side-loading techniques.\nOne noteworthy tactic adopted by SideWinder is that the spear-phishing emails are coupled with geofenced payloads to ensure that only victims meeting the targeting criteria are served the malicious content. In the event the victim's IP address does not match, an empty RTF file is sent instead as a decoy.\nThe malicious payload is an RTF file that weaponizes CVE-2017-11882, a memory corruption vulnerability in the Equation Editor, to launch a shellcode-based loader that runs the StealerBot malware.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nStealerBot, according to Kaspersky, is a [.NET implant](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/10\/sidewinder-apt-strikes-middle-east-and.html) that's engineered to drop additional malware, launch a reverse shell, and collect a wide range of data from compromised hosts, including screenshots, keystrokes, passwords, and files.\n\"SideWinder has demonstrated consistent activity over time, maintaining a steady pace of operations without prolonged inactivity \u2014 a pattern that reflects organizational continuity and sustained intent,\" the researchers said.\n\"A closer analysis of their tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs) reveals a high degree of control and precision, ensuring that malicious payloads are delivered only to carefully selected targets, and often only for a limited time.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsouth-asian-ministries-hit-by.html&t=South%20Asian%20Ministries%20Hit%20by%20SideWinder%20APT%20Using%20Old%20Office%20Flaws%20and%20Custom%20Malware) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=South%20Asian%20Ministries%20Hit%20by%20SideWinder%20APT%20Using%20Old%20Office%20Flaws%20and%20Custom%20Malware \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsouth-asian-ministries-hit-by.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/south-asian-ministries-hit-by.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsouth-asian-ministries-hit-by.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fsouth-asian-ministries-hit-by.html&text=South%20Asian%20Ministries%20Hit%20by%20SideWinder%20APT%20Using%20Old%20Office%20Flaws%20and%20Custom%20Malware)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[cyber espionage](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cyber%20espionage)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Microsoft office](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Microsoft%20office)[South Asia](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/South%20Asia)[Spear Phishing](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Spear%20Phishing)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj5q7racGwMr5emA21v4uOtTjSF4X1U2UIB1VXdECJy_UlSerg-4nUz1sWoQPECXE52nExclTrzA8PSWUvGhM_NOY6KlHcLZHn61pnpthgtEfcA