"title": "AWS Default IAM Roles Found to Enable Lateral Movement and Cross-Service Exploitation",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/aws-default-iam-roles-found-to-enable.html",,
"summary": "A cybersecurity report reveals vulnerabilities in default IAM roles in Amazon Web Services (AWS), which could lead to privilege escalation, cross-service exploitation, and possible account compromises. The affected AWS services include SageMaker, Glue, EMR, and Lightsail, which create roles with overly broad permissions like AmazonS3FullAccess. The article also outlines a security flaw in an open-source framework called Ray. Following the disclosure, AWS has modified the AmazonS3FullAccess policy for default roles.",,
