"title": "100+ Fake Chrome Extensions Found Hijacking Sessions, Stealing Credentials, Injecting Ads",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/100-fake-chrome-extensions-found.html",,
"summary": "An unknown threat actor has developed over 100 fake Chrome extensions designed to hijack user sessions, steal credentials, and inject ads. These malicious extensions masquerade as legitimate utilities and are distributed through the Google Chrome Web Store and fake websites mimicking well-known services. The extensions grant themselves excessive permissions and execute arbitrary code, compromising browser security through various methods, including credential theft and session hijacking. Google has removed these extensions, but users are advised to exercise caution and verify extensions before installation.",,
