"summary": "The threat actor known as 'Hazy Hawk' is exploiting misconfigured DNS CNAME records pointing to abandoned cloud services to hijack trusted domains of governments, universities, and Fortune 500 companies. By registering new cloud resources with the same names as the abandoned ones, Hazy Hawk can redirect the subdomains to sites under their control. This technique has been used to distribute scams, fake applications, and malicious advertisements. Impacted entities include US CDC, Honeywell, University of California Berkeley, Michelin Tires UK, the 'Big Four' consulting firms, TED, Australian Department of Health, UNICEF, New York University, Unilever, and the California State Government.",,
