"summary": "The Kettering Health system in Ohio experienced a significant cyberattack, resulting in widespread outages across its hospitals and medical facilities. This incident was a cybersecurity breach due to unauthorized access, impacting the network's ability to access patient care systems. Elective procedures were canceled, and the call center was affected. Emergency rooms and clinics remain operational. The attack has been linked to the Interlock ransomware gang. The cyberattack has affected the healthcare industry's critical systems.",,
