"markdown": "![Kettering Health](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_Kettering_Health_Emergency_ef5c9e76cd.jpg)\nThe Kettering Health emergency entrance in Franklin, Ohio. Image: ketteringhealth.org\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 20th, 2025\n# Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattack\nA cyberattack has disrupted hospitals and medical facilities in Ohio that are run by Kettering Health. \nA spokesperson told Recorded Future News that the nonprofit hospital network is \u201ccurrently experiencing a cybersecurity incident resulting from unauthorized access.\u201d \nIn a message on its [website](https:\/\/ketteringhealth.org\/kettering-health-earns-a-hospital-safety-grades-from-the-leapfrog-group\/) and on , the network said the incident began on Tuesday morning and caused a system-wide technology outage that limited workers\u2019 ability to access certain patient care systems. \n\u201cWe have taken steps to contain and mitigate this activity and are actively investigating and monitoring the situation. We will continue to provide updates as appropriate,\u201d the spokesperson added. \nElective inpatient and outpatient procedures at Kettering Health facilities have been canceled for Tuesday and will be rescheduled. The hospital network\u2019s call center is also down as a result of the attack. \nKettering Health said it has procedures in place to handle these types of situations. All emergency rooms and clinics are still open and seeing patients. \nThe spokesperson did not respond to questions about whether the hospital network is dealing with a ransomware attack. \nCNN [reported](https:\/\/www.cnn.com\/2025\/05\/20\/politics\/ransomware-attack-medical-centers) that a ransom note found by the hospital network\u2019s IT workers allegedly came from the Interlock ransomware gang \u2014 which caused alarm last month after [shutting down the network](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dialysis-davita-reviewing-data-leak) of dialysis treatment company DaVita. The group also previously attacked the [Texas Tech University Health Sciences Center](https:\/\/therecord.media\/texas-county-disaster-declaration-cyberattack) and its El Paso counterpart. \nKettering Health, which bills itself as a \u201cfaith based\u201d Seventh Day Adventist system, runs 14 medical centers and dozens of clinics primarily in the Dayton area \u2014 managing nearly 400,000 emergency room visits in 2023 alone. \nPrevious attacks on healthcare networks have caused significant issues for nurses and doctors, limiting access to critical systems that track medications, medical history and more. \nA similar cyberattack took down [a large Maryland healthcare network](https:\/\/therecord.media\/maryland-healthcare-ransomware-frederick-health) in January and Microsoft [warned in March](https:\/\/therecord.media\/rural-hospitals-need-millions-cyber) that hospitals will need to spend millions more to better protect critical systems necessary for patient care. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattack)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattack )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [healthcare](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/healthcare)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [hospital](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/hospital)\n  * [Ohio](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ohio)\n  * [Ransomware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ransomware)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kettering-health-system-ohio-cyberattack)\n  * [Cyberthreat to Alabama state government \u2018neutralized\u2019May 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-cyberattack-neutralized)\n  * [Major Russian state services disrupted, reportedly due to cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/major-russian-state-services-disrupted-ddos)\n  * [Dutch government passes law to criminalize cyber-espionageMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/netherlands-law-criminalizes-cyber-espionage)\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n  * [OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hackMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner)\n  * [EU court rules that tracking-based online ads are illegalMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-court-rules-tracking-based-ads-illegal)\n  * [UK National Health Service suppliers asked to tackle \u2018endemic\u2019 ransomware attacksMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-nhs-suppliers-ransomware-letter)\n  * [Proofpoint to acquire European cloud security firm Hornetsecurity for over $1 billionMay 15th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\