"summary": "SK Telecom experienced a cybersecurity incident lasting nearly three years, during which malware went undetected. The breach, identified in April 2025, exposed sensitive data of 27 million subscribers, including USIM data, IMSI numbers, and potentially facilitating SIM-swapping attacks. A joint investigation revealed infections on 23 servers, compromising 25 distinct malware types. SK Telecom is offering SIM replacements and has intensified its security measures to mitigate risks.",,
