"summary": "Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem faced questions from U.S. senators about a proposed $491 million budget cut to the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) under the Trump administration. Noem did not provide specific details during the Senate Committee hearing, focusing instead on efforts to remove parts of CISA dealing with disinformation. The budget note indicates a desire to eliminate 'duplicative' offices and programs, suggesting that CISA was too focused on censorship rather than cybersecurity.",,
