"title": "Premium WordPress 'Motors' theme vulnerable to admin takeover attacks",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/premium-wordpress-motors-theme-vulnerable-to-admin-takeover-attacks\/",,
"summary": "A critical privilege escalation vulnerability (CVE-2025-4322) was discovered in the premium WordPress theme Motors, developed by StylemixThemes. This vulnerability allows unauthenticated attackers to hijack administrator accounts and gain complete control of websites. It affects all versions of the Motors theme up to and including 5.6.67. The vulnerability arises from improper validation of user identity before updating passwords, enabling attackers to change user passwords and access accounts. Malicious activities could include implanting malware, exfiltrating data, or redirecting users to harmful sites. StylemixThemes released version 5.6.68 to patch this issue on May 14, 2025.",,
