"summary": "The VanHelsing ransomware-as-a-service group published the source code for its affiliate panel, data leak blog, and Windows encryptor builder after an incident involving a former developer. The source code for the affiliate panel and data leak site was posted on the RAMP forum, although it doesn't contain the complete Linux builder or databases, limiting use by law enforcement and researchers. This leak includes the source code of Windows encryptor, decryptor, and a loader, along with an attempted MBR locker. Previous similar leaks, such as the Babuk, Conti, and LockBit ransomware builders, have led to widespread use by other threat actors.",,
