"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/gen-ai-best-practices.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/genai-security-best-practices-cheat-sheet?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q3_INB_FORM_GenAI-Security-Best-Practices-Cheat-Sheet&sfcid=701Py00000ENEjlIAH&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=GenAIBestPractices)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * VanHelsing ransomware builder leaked on hacking forum\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)\n\n\n# VanHelsing ransomware builder leaked on hacking forum\nBy \n###### [Lawrence Abrams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/lawrence-abrams\/)\n  * May 20, 2025\n  * 03:06 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![VanHelsing](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/03\/24\/vanhelsing.jpg)\nThe VanHelsing ransomware-as-a-service operation published the source code for its affiliate panel, data leak blog, and Windows encryptor builder after an old developer tried to sell it on the RAMP cybercrime forum.\nVanHelsing is a RaaS operation [launched in March 2025, ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-vanhelsing-ransomware-targets-windows-arm-esxi-systems\/)promoting the ability to target Windows, Linux, BSD, ARM, and ESXi systems.\nSince then, the operation has shown some success, with [Ransomware.live](https:\/\/www.ransomware.live\/group\/VanHelsing) stating that there are eight known victims for the ransomware gang.\n## VanHelsing source code leaked on cybercrime forum\nEarly this morning, a person using the alias 'th30c0der' attempted to sell the source code for the VanHelsing affiliate panel and data leak Tor sites, as well as the builders for the Windows and Linux encryptors, for $10,000.\n\"vanhelsing ransomware source code for sell: include TOR keys + web panel for admin + chat + file server + blog include database everything,\" th30c0der posted to the RAMP forum.\n![th30c0der attempting to sell the VanHelsing source code](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/ransomware\/v\/vanhelsing\/leaked-code\/builder-for-sale.jpg)**th30c0der attempting to sell the VanHelsing source code**\nAs first reported by , the VanHelsing operators decided to beat the seller to punch, releasing the source code themselves and stating that the th30c0der is one of their old developers trying to scam people.\n\"Today we are announcing that we are publishing the old sources codes and will soon come back with the new and improved version of the locker(VanHelsing 2.0),\" the VanHelsing operator posted to RAMP.\n![VanHelsin RaaS releases the source code on RAMP\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/ransomware\/v\/vanhelsing\/leaked-code\/vanhelsing-leaking-source-code.jpg)**VanHelsin RaaS releases the source code on RAMP** \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\nHowever, this leaked data is incomplete compared to what the 30c0der says they have, as it does not include the Linux builder or any databases, which would be much more helpful for law enforcement and cybersecurity researchers.\nBleepingComputer has obtained the leaked source code and has confirmed that it contains the legitimate builder for the Windows encryptor and the source code for the affiliate panel and data leak site.\n![Leaked source code](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)**Leaked source code** _Source: BleepingComputer_\nThe builder's source code is somewhat of a mess, with the Visual Studio project files found in the \"Release\" folder, which is typically used to hold compiled binaries and build artifacts.\nWhile complete, using the VanHelsing builder will require some work, as it connects back to the affiliate panel, which was running 31.222.238[.]208, to receive data used for the build process.\n![common.h header file used by the builder](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)**common.h header file used by the builder** _Source: BleepingComputer_\nHowever, the leak also includes the source code for the affiliate panel, which hosts the api.php endpoint, so threat actors could modify the code or run their own version of this panel to get the builder to work.\nThe archive also contains the source code for the Windows encryptor, which can be used to create a standalone build, the decryptor, and a loader.\n![](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)**VanHelsing encryptor source code** _Source: BleepingComputer_\nThe leaked source code also revealed that the threat actors were attempting to build an MBR locker that would replace the master boot record with a custom bootloader that displays a lock message.\n![VanHelsing MBRLocker source code](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)**VanHelsing MBRLocker source code** _Source: BleepingComputer_\nThis leak is not the first time a ransomware builder or encryptor source code has been leaked online, which allowed new ransomware groups or individual threat actors to quickly conduct attacks. \nIn June 2021, the [Babuk ransomware builder was leaked](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/leaked-babuk-locker-ransomware-builder-used-in-new-attacks\/), allowing anyone to create encryptors and decryptors for Windows and VMware ESXi. The Babuk leak has become one of the [most widely used builders](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/babuk-code-used-by-9-ransomware-gangs-to-encrypt-vmware-esxi-servers\/) to conduct attacks on VMware ESXi servers.\nIn March 2022, when the [Conti ransomware operation suffered a data breach](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/conti-ransomwares-internal-chats-leaked-after-siding-with-russia\/), its [source code was also leaked online](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/conti-ransomware-source-code-leaked-by-ukrainian-researcher\/). Other threat actors quickly used this source code in their own attacks.\nIn September 2022, the [LockBit ransomware operation suffered a breach](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/lockbit-ransomware-builder-leaked-online-by-angry-developer\/) when an allegedly disgruntled developer leaked the gang's builder. This too has become widely used by other threat actors to this day.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/)](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Texas State Bar warns of data breach after INC ransomware claims attack](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/texas-state-bar-warns-of-data-breach-after-inc-ransomware-claims-attack\/)\n[New VanHelsing ransomware targets Windows, ARM, ESXi systems](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-vanhelsing-ransomware-targets-windows-arm-esxi-systems\/)\n[Service desks are under attack: What can you do about it?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/service-desks-are-under-attack-what-can-you-do-about-it\/)\n[Fake KeePass password manager leads to ESXi ransomware attack](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fake-keepass-password-manager-leads-to-esxi-ransomware-attack\/)\n[Ransomware gangs increasingly use Skitnet post-exploitation malware](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/ransomware-gangs-increasingly-use-skitnet-post-exploitation-malware\/)\n  * [Data Leak](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/data-leak\/)\n  * [Encryptor](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/encryptor\/)\n  * [Ransomware](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/ransomware\/)\n  * [Ransomware Builder](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/ransomware-builder\/)\n  * [Source Code](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/source-code\/)\n  * [VanHelsing](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/vanhelsing\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/lawrence-abrams\/)\n##### [Lawrence Abrams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/lawrence-abrams\/)\nLawrence Abrams is the owner and Editor in Chief of BleepingComputer.com. Lawrence's area of expertise includes Windows, malware removal, and computer forensics. Lawrence Abrams is a co-author of the Winternals Defragmentation, Recovery, and Administration Field Guide and the technical editor for Rootkits for Dummies. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/***REMOVED***\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/premium-wordpress-motors-theme-vulnerable-to-admin-takeover-attacks\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Microsoft Defender](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) New 'Defendnot' tool tricks Windows into disabling Microsoft Defender ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-defendnot-tool-tricks-windows-into-disabling-microsoft-defender\/)\n  * [ ![Keepass Hacker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Fake KeePass password manager leads to ESXi ransomware attack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fake-keepass-password-manager-leads-to-esxi-ransomware-attack\/)\n  * [ ![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Microsoft confirms new \"Advanced\" Settings for Windows 11 ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03m1Jw30 )\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![Cybersecurity Lock World](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/) How to tell if your organization\u2019s credentials have been involved in a breach? ](https:\/\/outpost24.com\/blog\/find-credentials-involved-breach\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=referral_content)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/vanhelsing-ransomware-builder-leaked-on-hacking-forum\/ \"Submit\")\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.