"title": "Dero miner zombies biting through Docker APIs to build a cryptojacking horde",,
"url": "https:\/\/securelist.com\/dero-miner-infects-containers-through-docker-api\/116546\/",,
"summary": "The article discusses how a Dero cryptocurrency miner is exploiting Docker API misconfigurations to create a cryptojacking network. It highlights vulnerabilities related to Docker, the spread of malware named 'nginx' and 'cloud', and compromised containers. The content emphasizes the importance of securing container environments against such attacks. The article discusses a new cryptojacking campaign that exploits insecurely published Docker APIs to infect containerized infrastructures. The attack is automated using two malware samples: 'nginx' which facilitates propagation and 'cloud,' a Dero crypto miner. Both malware samples are written in Go and packed with UPX. The threat exploits open Docker API ports (2375) identified through masscan scanning. The campaign does not rely on command-and-control servers, making it persistent and hard to disrupt.",,
