"markdown": "![Russian flag](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_russia_flag_2023_Victory_Day_Parade_4c93737dcc.jpg)\nImage: Wikimedia Commons\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)May 21st, 2025\n# Western intelligence agencies unite to expose Russian hacking campaign against logistics and tech firms\nA notorious Russian hacking unit was blamed on Wednesday for conducting a widespread campaign that officials say \u201cpresents a serious risk\u201d to the targeted organizations and sectors in more than a dozen countries. \nIn a [joint cybersecurity advisory](https:\/\/media.defense.gov\/2025\/May\/21\/2003719846\/-1\/-1\/0\/CSA_RUSSIAN_GRU_TARGET_LOGISTICS.PDF) co-sealed by what appears to be a record number of allied countries (11) and intelligence agencies (21), the hacking group widely known as Fancy Bear or APT28 was accused of being behind attempted digital break-ins at multiple Western logistics providers and technology firms. \n\u201cDozens of entities, including government organizations and private\/commercial entities across virtually all transportation modes: air, sea, and rail\u201d have been targeted in the campaign within NATO member states, within Ukraine, and at international organisations, according to the advisory. \nAlongside the \u201cespionage-oriented campaign\u201d the hackers are also believed to have accessed legitimate municipal traffic cams as well as \u201cprivate cameras at key locations, such as near border crossings, military installations, and rail stations, to track the movement of materials into Ukraine.\u201d \nThe hackers also \u201cconducted reconnaissance on at least one entity involved in the production of industrial control system components for railway management, though a successful compromise was not confirmed,\u201d warned the advisory. \nThe intelligence agencies formally attributed the attacks to the \u201c85th Main Special Service Center (85th GTsSS), military unit 26165\u201d of Russia\u2019s military intelligence agency, the GRU, and acknowledged the hacking unit\u2019s campaigns were tracked under a number of names, including Fancy Bear and APT 24. \nAlthough the campaign did not utilize any novel techniques \u2014 with the hackers described as gaining initial access to their victims\u2019 networks by \u201cusing a mix of previously disclosed techniques, including credential guessing, spear-phishing and exploitation of Microsoft Exchange mailbox permissions\u201d \u2014 the widespread nature of the campaign has prompted the advisory encouraging potential victims to shore up their defenses. \nPaul Chichester, the director of operations at Britain\u2019s National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC) said: \u201cThis malicious campaign by Russia\u2019s military intelligence service presents a serious risk to targeted organisations, including those involved in the delivery of assistance to Ukraine. \n\u201cThe UK and partners are committed to raising awareness of the tactics being deployed. We strongly encourage organisations to familiarise themselves with the threat and mitigation advice included in the advisory to help defend their networks,\u201d added Chichester. \nThe NCSC said that both executives at technology and logistics companies, as well as network defenders, needed to recognise the elevated threat of targeting \u201cand take immediate action to protect themselves.\u201d \nAgencies from the U.K., U.S., Germany, France, Canada, Czechia, Poland, Australia, Estonia, Denmark and the Netherlands co-signed the advisory. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Western intelligence agencies unite to expose Russian hacking campaign against logistics and tech firms)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Western intelligence agencies unite to expose Russian hacking campaign against logistics and tech firms )\n\n\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Nation-state](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/nation-state)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [espionage](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/espionage)\n  * [GRU](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/gru)\n  * [Fancy Bear](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/fancy-bear)\n  * [APT28](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/apt28)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [intelligence agency](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/intelligence-agency)\n  * [United Kingdom](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/united-kingdom)\n  * [Germany](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/germany)\n  * [France](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/france)\n  * [United States](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/united-states)\n  * [Australia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/australia)\n  * [Canada](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/canada)\n  * [Estonia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/estonia)\n  * [Denmark](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/denmark)\n  * [Poland](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/poland)\n  * [Czech Republic](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/czech-republic)\n  * [Netherlands](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/netherlands)\n  * [Logistics](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Shipping](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/shipping)\n  * [transportation](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/transportation)\n  * [Ukraine](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ukraine)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Alexander Martin](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/headshot_79eb085f87.jpeg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\n[Alexander Martin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/alexander-martin)\nis the UK Editor for Recorded Future News. He was previously a technology reporter for Sky News and is also a fellow at the European Cyber Conflict Research Initiative.\n## Briefs\n  * [Senators question Noem about CISA cuts, but get few detailsMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/noem-cisa-cuts-senate-hearing)\n  * [Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kettering-health-system-ohio-cyberattack)\n  * [Cyberthreat to Alabama state government \u2018neutralized\u2019May 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-cyberattack-neutralized)\n  * [Major Russian state services disrupted, reportedly due to cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/major-russian-state-services-disrupted-ddos)\n  * [Dutch government passes law to criminalize cyber-espionageMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/netherlands-law-criminalizes-cyber-espionage)\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n  * [OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hackMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner)\n  * [EU court rules that tracking-based online ads are illegalMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-court-rules-tracking-based-ads-illegal)\n  * [UK National Health Service suppliers asked to tackle \u2018endemic\u2019 ransomware attacksMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-nhs-suppliers-ransomware-letter)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
