"title": "Data-stealing Chrome extensions impersonate Fortinet, YouTube, VPNs",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/data-stealing-chrome-extensions-impersonate-fortinet-youtube-vpns\/",,
"summary": "A malicious campaign involving over 100 Google Chrome browser extensions impersonates legitimate tools, such as VPNs and AI assistants, to steal user information and execute remote scripts. These extensions mimic brands like Fortinet and YouTube, connecting to threat actor infrastructure to steal data or execute commands. The campaign can modify network traffic to display ads or redirect traffic. Identified by DomainTools, this campaign includes numerous fake domains, some of which still have extensions available on the Chrome Web Store. The extensions request permissions to steal cookies, perform phishing, and inject scripts. Risks include account hijacking and data theft. The malicious extensions can proxy traffic through malicious servers.",,
