"title": "Lumma infostealer malware operation disrupted, 2,300 domains seized",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/lumma-infostealer-malware-operation-disrupted-2-300-domains-seized\/",,
"summary": "The Lumma infostealer malware operation was disrupted by a coordinated effort involving tech companies and law enforcement, resulting in the seizure of 2,300 domains which were part of its infrastructure. This operation saw the collaboration of entities like Microsoft, Europol, and law enforcement authorities from Japan, among others. Microsoft seized these domains after a legal interception of Lumma's infrastructure, which was facilitating data theft through malware-as-a-service targeting Windows and macOS systems. The malware was distributed using various methods and targeted sensitive data, including credentials and financial information. Key technology services like Cloudflare were used by the attackers, which required additional security measures to prevent data exfiltration.",,
