"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/)\n  * Russia to enforce location tracking app on all foreigners in Moscow\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/)\n\n\n# Russia to enforce location tracking app on all foreigners in Moscow\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * May 21, 2025\n  * 02:24 PM\n  * [1](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/#comments)\n\n\n![Russia](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2021\/10\/08\/Russia-flag.jpg)\nThe Russian government has introduced a new law that makes installing a tracking app mandatory for all foreign nationals in the Moscow region.\nThe new proposal was announced by the chairman of the State Duma, Vyacheslav Volodin, who presented it as a measure to tackle migrant crimes.\n\"The adopted mechanism will allow, using modern technologies, to strengthen control in the field of migration and will also contribute to reducing the number of violations and crimes in this area,\" [stated Volodin](http:\/\/duma.gov.ru\/news\/61435\/).\nUsing a mobile application that all foreigners will have to install on their smartphones, the Russian state will receive the following information:\n  * Residence location\n  * Fingerprint\n  * Face photograph\n  * Real-time geo-location monitoring\n\n\n\"If migrants change their actual place of residence, they will be required to inform the Ministry of Internal Affairs (MVD) within three working days,\" the high-ranking politician explained.\nThe measures will not apply to diplomats of foreign countries or citizens of Belarus.\nForeigners attempting to avoid their obligation in relation to the new law will be added to a registry of monitored individuals and deported from Russia.\nRussian internet freedom observatory [Roskomsvoboda's reactions](https:\/\/roskomsvoboda.org\/en\/post\/spying-on-foreigners-via-smartphone\/) to this proposal reflect skepticism and concern.\nLawyer Anna Minushkina noted that the proposal violates Articles 23 and 24 of the Russian Constitution, guaranteeing the right to privacy.\nPresident of the Uzbek Community in Moscow, Viktor Teplyankov, characterized the initiative as \"ill-conceived and difficult to implement,\" expressing doubts about its feasibility.\nFinally, PSP Foundation's Andrey Yakimov warned that such aggressive measures are bound to deter potential labor migrants, creating a different problem in the country.\nThe proposal hasn't reached its final form yet, and specifics like what happens in the case of device theft\/loss or similar technical or practical obstacles are to be addressed in the upcoming period during meetings between the Ministry and regional authorities.\nThe mass-surveillance experiment will run until September 2029, and if deemed successful, the mechanism will extend to cover more parts of the country.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Government webmail hacked via XSS bugs in global spy campaign](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/government-webmail-hacked-via-xss-bugs-in-global-spy-campaign\/)\n[Bluetooth 6.1 enhances privacy with randomized RPA timing](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/bluetooth-61-enhances-privacy-with-randomized-rpa-timing\/)\n[Pro-Russia hacktivists bombard Dutch public orgs with DDoS attacks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/pro-russia-hacktivists-bombard-dutch-public-orgs-with-ddos-attacks\/)\n[France ties Russian APT28 hackers to 12 cyberattacks on French orgs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/france-ties-russian-apt28-hackers-to-12-cyberattacks-on-french-orgs\/)\n[Russian army targeted by new Android malware hidden in mapping app](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/russian-army-targeted-by-new-android-malware-hidden-in-mapping-app\/)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/government\/)\n  * [Mobile](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/mobile\/)\n  * [Moscow](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/moscow\/)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/russia\/)\n  * [Tracking](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/tracking\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/worried-about-your-webcam-privacy-this-deal-may-be-for-you\/)\n\n\n### Comments\n  * ![ThomasMann Photo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/public\/style_images\/master\/profile\/default_large.png)\n######  [ThomasMann](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/u\/1162586\/thomasmann\/) - 1 hour ago\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/ \"Report\")\n    * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/#cid36229 \"Link\")\nOn the other hand.... Given the record of f.e. the European Union, I would fear abuse of my data from Them much more than from Russia. What could they do with it, that might have a negative impact on me?\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/) Microsoft confirms new \"Advanced\" Settings for Windows 11 ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-new-advanced-settings-for-windows-11\/)\n  * [ ![Keepass Hacker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/) Fake KeePass password manager leads to ESXi ransomware attack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fake-keepass-password-manager-leads-to-esxi-ransomware-attack\/)\n  * [ ![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\