"markdown": "![Cellcom](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_Cellcom_tower_695a935fe1.jpg)\nCredit: Cellcom\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 21st, 2025\n# Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outages\nA large telecommunications firm serving Michigan and Wisconsin said on Tuesday a cyberattack was the cause of service outages that have persisted for the last week. \nIn a [video message](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=gnzKPQXuW6g) on Tuesday evening, Cellcom CEO Brighid Riordan said the company has been dealing with a \u201ccyber incident\u201d but admitted they \u201csimply don\u2019t have a lot of facts.\u201d \n\u201cThe cyber incident that we're experiencing is segmented to the voice and texting parts of your service \u2026 \u201cWe're prepared for these incidents, and we are rolling our protocol through this,\u201d Riordan said. \n\u201cWe live in a world where they are working on how to do damage just as hard as we are working to prevent it.\u201d \nRiordan [published](https:\/\/www.cellcom.com\/sites\/default\/files\/2025-05\/A%20Letter%20from%20Cellcom-Nsight%20CEO%202.pdf?fbclid=IwY2xjawKZ44dleHRuA2FlbQIxMABicmlkETEzVWdXZENLRnBualY5Z25MAR7CjK4PaaDIt5e2SpYtJmcU9J3XO3rKlK2jDKvT4AbTnoQYDg5rz2FlOstlBg_aem_qiHXnDmjrfgVV1RYvTHfQg) a letter alongside her video, noting that in addition to cybersecurity experts, the FBI and Wisconsin officials have been involved in the response. \nThousands of Cellcom customers have been without voice and SMS texting services since when the outages first began. \nThe company has not responded to requests for comment about whether they are dealing with a ransomware incident and did not cite a cyber incident as the cause of the outage until Tuesday. \nCalls between Cellcom customers and some SMS text services were restored on Monday, and the company said the incident was concentrated on a part of the network that is separate from where customer data is held. \nAs of Wednesday, Cellcom still could not provide a timeline for when services will be fully restored but said experts were being flown in to help with the recovery. \nCellcom, a subsidiary of Nsight, provides text and voice services as well as internet to people and businesses throughout Wisconsin and Upper Michigan. \nAmid the deluge of angry messages from customers, the company it was unable to provide people with the information needed to switch telecommunication services and port phone numbers to other companies like Verizon, further angering those struggling with the outages. \nCellcom acknowledged in Facebook messages that customers had missed job interviews, important family calls, and more. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outages)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outages )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\nTags\n  * [telecommunications](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/telecommunications)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [internet outages](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/internet-outages)\n  * [Michigan](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/michigan)\n  * [Wisconsin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/wisconsin)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outagesMay 21st, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/midwestern-cellcom-telcom-cyberattack)\n  * [Senators question Noem about CISA cuts, but get few detailsMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/noem-cisa-cuts-senate-hearing)\n  * [Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kettering-health-system-ohio-cyberattack)\n  * [Cyberthreat to Alabama state government \u2018neutralized\u2019May 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-cyberattack-neutralized)\n  * [Major Russian state services disrupted, reportedly due to cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/major-russian-state-services-disrupted-ddos)\n  * [Dutch government passes law to criminalize cyber-espionageMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/netherlands-law-criminalizes-cyber-espionage)\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n  * [OPM urged to continue identity protection contracts shielding people affected by 2015 hackMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/opm-federal-employee-data-protection-contracts-2015-hack-warner)\n  * [EU court rules that tracking-based online ads are illegalMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-court-rules-tracking-based-ads-illegal)\n\n\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n## [2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report![2024 Malicious Infrastructure Report](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/2024_malicious_infrastructure_report_95f6761bdf.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/2024-malicious-infrastructure-report)\n",,
