"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Webinar: Learn How to Build a Reasonable and Legally Defensible Cybersecurity Program](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html)\n_\ue802_ May 22, 2025 _\ue804_ The Hacker NewsSecurity Framework \/ Cyber Defense\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhhZouTPAstJIkNS-hZFtprh2xDQTzds9hCN7uO9PmAl7pNSf3rUL2_g9i7jNQoqSvyhdmaLAUB_aUm2rAuyzDyXum8hhthPZQ4IaJ6FWjgW7z4FFaBxpxADw-ysPcpxQd8WKTnepvIvbMa2tEuZkbZ6BwpNkwVpsTzYWljHlLEdRh44s_vVWMjp0t559g\/s728-rw-e365\/cyber-program.jpg)](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/cyber-defense-program?source=article)\nIt's not enough to be secure. In today's legal climate, you need to prove it.\nWhether you're protecting a small company or managing compliance across a global enterprise, one thing is clear: cybersecurity can no longer be left to guesswork, vague frameworks, or best-effort intentions.\nRegulators and courts are now holding organizations accountable for how \"reasonable\" their security programs are\u2014and that's not just a buzzword anymore.\n### But what does \"_reasonable\"_ even mean in cybersecurity?[#](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html#but-what-does-reasonable-even-mean-in-cybersecurity-)\nThat's exactly what [this free webinar](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/cyber-defense-program?source=article) we hosted with the experts from Center for Internet Security (CIS) will help you answer.\nNew privacy laws, ransomware lawsuits, and regulatory investigations are raising the bar for cybersecurity expectations. If your defense program can't show structure, strategy, and measurable maturity, you're not just at risk\u2014you're already falling behind.\n**This isn't about hype. It's about legal risk, operational readiness, and your reputation.**\nIn this live session, CIS experts will walk you through a practical, no-fluff approach to building a cybersecurity program that meets legal and industry standards\u2014and makes sense for your size, scope, and resources.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html)](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/cyber-defense-program?source=article)\n## What You'll Learn (That You Can Actually Use)[#](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html#what-you-ll-learn-that-you-can-actually-use-)\nThis isn't another generic security talk. You'll walk away with:\n  * A clear definition of \"reasonable\" cybersecurity and why it matters to courts, regulators, and insurers.\n  * A step-by-step breakdown of the CIS Critical Security Controls\u00ae, used by thousands of organizations to build real-world defenses.\n  * How to assess and track your program's maturity using CIS CSAT Pro, a free and powerful self-assessment tool.\n  * Why a CIS SecureSuite\u00ae Membership could save you time, reduce risk, and help you generate compliance reports in a few clicks.\n\n\nYou don't need a massive budget or a 50-person SOC to get started. The CIS model is built for scalability and clarity\u2014and it's already trusted by schools, hospitals, local governments, and major enterprises alike.\n[Watch this Webinar](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/cyber-defense-program?source=article)\nMost security breaches don't happen because of zero-days. They happen because the basics weren't in place. And the legal fallout usually focuses on what you didn't do\u2014or can't prove you did.\nThis webinar shows you how to build a defense program that's not only smart and scalable but also provably responsible.\n\ud83d\udcc5 [Reserve your spot now](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/cyber-defense-program?source=article). It's free, it's practical, and it could save your organization from major headaches later.\nFound this article interesting? This article is a contributed piece from one of our valued partners. Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fwebinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html&t=Webinar%3A%20Learn%20How%20to%20Build%20a%20Reasonable%20and%20Legally%20Defensible%20Cybersecurity%20Program) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Webinar%3A%20Learn%20How%20to%20Build%20a%20Reasonable%20and%20Legally%20Defensible%20Cybersecurity%20Program \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fwebinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/webinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fwebinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fwebinar-learn-how-to-build-reasonable.html&