"summary": "Chinese hackers, specifically the UNC5221 group, exploited a remote code execution flaw (CVE-2025-4428) in Ivanti Endpoint Manager Mobile (EPMM) to breach various governmental and corporate entities globally. The flaw, which affects Ivanti EPMM version 12.5.0.0 and earlier, allows remote code execution via crafted API requests. Patch for CVE-2025-4428 and an authentication bypass (CVE-2025-4427) was released on May 13, 2025. High-profile organizations across healthcare, telecommunications, and other sectors were impacted by breaches that included data exfiltration and persistent malware injections.",,
