"markdown": "![city hall](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_sheboygan_1b6da578af.jpg)\nImage: Mrschimpf via Wikimedia Commons (CC BY-SA 4.0)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 22nd, 2025\n# Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bug\nA vulnerability in a critical tool used by local governments across the U.S. is being exploited by Chinese-speaking hackers, according to incident responders. \nSince January, cybersecurity experts at Cisco Talos have seen Chinese hackers exploiting CVE-2025-0994 \u2014 a bug impacting Trimble Cityworks. The tool is used by local governments to manage critical infrastructure assets from one platform and organize inspections, work orders, permits, operations and more. \nBoth Trimble and the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) [warned in February](https:\/\/therecord.media\/hackers-exploiting-trimble-cityworks-bug-used-by-local-govs) that CVE-2025-0994 was being exploited, but Cisco Talos has confirmed that the hackers \u201cconducted reconnaissance and rapidly deployed a variety of web shells and custom-made malware to maintain long-term access.\u201d \n\u201cUpon gaining access, [the hackers] expressed a clear interest in pivoting to systems related to utilities management,\u201d Cisco Talos [explained](https:\/\/blog.talosintelligence.com\/uat-6382-exploits-cityworks-vulnerability\/) in a blog on Thursday. \nThe malware and other tools used during the attacks \u201ccontained messaging written in the Chinese language\u201d and one of them was built \u201cusing a malware-builder called \u2018MaLoader\u2019 that is also written in Simplified Chinese.\u201d While some of the tools can be configured to use limited English, most require some level of Chinese proficiency. \nBased on the tools used, the tactics and the victims, Cisco Talos said they assessed with \u201chigh confidence\u201d that the people behind the attacks were Chinese-speaking threat actors. \nOnce access to a government system was achieved, the hackers looked for directories and files of interest before preparing them for exfiltration. \nFederal agencies were ordered to patch CVE-2025-0994 by February 28. The asset management system is used by many local and federal government agencies to manage infrastructure assets for airports, utilities, municipalities and counties. \nIn a [letter](https:\/\/learn.assetlifecycle.trimble.com\/i\/1532182-cityworks-customer-communication-2025-02-06-docx\/0) to customers earlier this year, the company behind the software said notice of the vulnerability followed \u201cinvestigations of reports of unauthorized attempts to gain access to specific customers' Cityworks deployments.\" \nCISA said Trimble reported the vulnerability to them and Symantec\u2019s Threat Hunter team contributed to the [advisory](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/news-events\/ics-advisories\/icsa-25-037-04) they released about the bug. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bug)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bug )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [local government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/local-government)\n  * [US municipal government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/us-municipal-government)\n  * [China](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/china)\n  * [Cisco Talos](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cisco-talos)\n  * [CISA](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cisa)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bugMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-speaking-hackers-target-municipalities-cityworks)\n  * [Russia-aligned hackers target Tajikistan in new espionage campaignMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-hackers-target-tajikistan-espionage)\n  * [Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outagesMay 21st, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/midwestern-cellcom-telcom-cyberattack)\n  * [Senators question Noem about CISA cuts, but get few detailsMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/noem-cisa-cuts-senate-hearing)\n  * [Ohio\u2019s Kettering Health system facing widespread outages after cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kettering-health-system-ohio-cyberattack)\n  * [Cyberthreat to Alabama state government \u2018neutralized\u2019May 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alabama-cyberattack-neutralized)\n  * [Major Russian state services disrupted, reportedly due to cyberattackMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/major-russian-state-services-disrupted-ddos)\n  * [Dutch government passes law to criminalize cyber-espionageMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/netherlands-law-criminalizes-cyber-espionage)\n  * [Hack of SEC social media account earns 14-month prison sentence for Alabama manMay 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sec-social-media-hack-sentencing)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
