"title": "TikTok videos now push infostealer malware in ClickFix attacks",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/tiktok-videos-now-push-infostealer-malware-in-clickfix-attacks\/",,
"summary": "Cybercriminals are using TikTok videos to distribute Vidar and StealC information-stealing malware through ClickFix attacks. The attackers create AI-generated videos that mislead users into executing PowerShell commands disguised as software activation steps. These commands download malware from specified URLs, compromising users by stealing sensitive information like credentials and cryptocurrency wallet details. The attack exploits TikTok's algorithm to reach a wide audience, with videos amassing significant views and interactions. ClickFix involves using fake errors or verification systems to coax victims into running malicious scripts.",,
