"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Hacker steals $223 million in Cetus Protocol cryptocurrency heist\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/)\n\n\n# Hacker steals $223 million in Cetus Protocol cryptocurrency heist\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * May 23, 2025\n  * 11:46 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Hacker steals $223 million in Cetus Protocol cryptocurrency heist](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2023\/12\/01\/Hackers_crypto.jpg)\nThe decentralized exchange Cetus Protocol announced that hackers have stolen $223 million in cryptocurrency and is offering a deal to stop all legal action if the funds are returned.\nThe project also announced a $5 million bounty to anyone providing relevant information leading to the identification and arrest of the attacker.\nCetus Protocol is a decentralized exchange (DEX) and liquidity protocol operating on the Sui and Aptos blockchains.\nIt employs a Concentrated Liquidity Market Maker (CLMM) model, allowing liquidity providers to allocate assets within specific price ranges, enhancing capital efficiency and enabling advanced trading strategies.\nCetus Protocol boasts a total trading volume of $57 billion (as of May 2025), with over 15 million accounts executing 144 million trades on the platform.\nThe incident occurred yesterday, initially prompting Cetus Protocol to for investigations.\nA few hours later, the project confirmed the theft and that \"$162M of the compromised funds have been successfully paused.\"\nIn a later statement, Cetus Protocol announced that the hacker had exploited a vulnerable package but no details have been disclosed.\n\u201cWe identified the root cause of the exploit and, fixed the related package, and informed ecosystem builders as fast as we could with help from ecosystem members to prevent other teams being affected,\u201d .\nAdditionally, the platform noted that it has identified the attacker\u2019s Ethereum wallet address and accounts, and is working with third parties to trace and freeze funds. Law enforcement has also been informed.\nCetus Protocol also offered the hacker \"a time-sensitive whitehat settlement,\" promising not to pursue legal action if the funds are returned. To put more pressure on the attacker, the project announced a $5 million bounty for information leading to the identification and the arrest of the hacker.\nMeanwhile, a significant $162 million was paused on the Sui blockchain following an emergency vote by the validators.\nBlockchain analytics company Elliptic [published a report](https:\/\/www.elliptic.co\/blog\/cetus-protocol-hacked-for-more-than-200-million) based on its visibility of the incident, pointing to a flaw in the automated market maker (AMM) logic, possibly involving pool price manipulation enabling flash loan-style attacks.\nThe blockchain intelligence firm also offers an overview of the attacker\u2019s fund movement attempts, including swaps from USDT to USDC and cross-chain movement from Suit to Ethereum.\n![Elliptic's tracing of the Cetus Protocol hack](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/)**Overview of the Cetus Protocol hack transactions** _Source: Elliptic_\nElliptic is actively tracing the transactions from the initial exploit on Sui to the attacker\u2019s wallets on Ethereum, and the hacker\u2019s address is flagged on all major exchanges and virtual asset service providers, preventing laundering or transfer attempts.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/)](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Israel arrests new suspect behind Nomad Bridge $190M crypto hack](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/legal\/israel-arrests-new-suspect-behind-nomad-bridge-190m-crypto-hack\/)\n[US charges 12 more suspects linked to $230 million crypto theft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/us-charges-12-more-suspects-linked-to-230-million-crypto-theft\/)\n[Germany takes down eXch cryptocurrency exchange, seizes servers](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/germany-takes-down-exch-cryptocurrency-exchange-seizes-servers\/)\n[Grinex exchange suspected rebrand of sanctioned Garantex crypto firm](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/cryptocurrency\/grinex-exchange-suspected-rebrand-of-sanctioned-garantex-crypto-firm\/)\n[U.S. seized $8.2 million in crypto linked to 'Romance Baiting' scams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/cryptocurrency\/us-seized-82-million-in-crypto-linked-to-romance-baiting-scams\/)\n  * [Cetus Protocol](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/cetus-protocol\/)\n  * [Crypto Exchange](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/crypto-exchange\/)\n  * [CryptoCurrency](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/cryptocurrency\/)\n  * [Exchange](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/exchange\/)\n  * [Financial Theft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/financial-theft\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fbi-warns-of-luna-moth-extortion-attacks-targeting-law-firms\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/dozens-of-malicious-packages-on-npm-collect-host-and-network-data\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Hacker box](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) Trojanized RVTools push Bumblebee malware in SEO poisoning campaign ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/trojanized-rvtools-push-bumblebee-malware-in-seo-poisoning-campaign\/)\n  * [ ![Russian flag](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) Russia to enforce location tracking app on all foreigners in Moscow ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/government\/russia-to-enforce-location-tracking-app-on-all-foreigners-in-moscow\/)\n  * [ ![School Hacker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) PowerSchool hacker pleads guilty to student data extortion scheme ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/powerschool-hacker-pleads-guilty-to-student-data-extortion-scheme\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![Identity Cybersecurity Framework passwords authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-steals-223-million-in-cetus-protocol-cryptocurrency-heist\/) Majority of browser extensions pose critical security risk - learn how to control it ](https:\/\/go.layerxsecurity.com\/enterprise-browser-extension-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=browser_extension_08052025)\n  * [ ![Security overwhelm is real. Learn how exposure validation helps you focus on what\u2019s real.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/s