"title": "Hackers Use Fake VPN and Browser NSIS Installers to Deliver Winos 4.0 Malware",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/hackers-use-fake-vpn-and-browser-nsis.html",,
"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers have unearthed a malware campaign deploying fake software installers to deliver the Winos 4.0 framework, initially identified by Rapid7 in February 2025. The attack uses fake VPN and browser NSIS installers that mask popular software tools such as LetsVPN and QQ Browser. The campaign employs a multi-stage, memory-resident loader named Catena. The threat actor Silver Fox (Void Arachne) targets Chinese-speaking environments. Winos 4.0 evolves from the Gh0st RAT remote access trojan, offering capabilities like data harvesting and DDoS attacks. The malware installs through NSIS installers with reflective DLL injection tactics designed to evade traditional antivirus detection. The campaign has displayed tactical flexibility, modifying avoidance techniques to evade cybersecurity countermeasures.",,
