"summary": "Glitch is ending its app hosting and user profiles services on July 8 due to changing market dynamics and increased operational costs from abuse issues. The platform\u2019s CEO, Anil Dash, announced these changes, highlighting that Glitch's service is no longer uniquely valuable compared to modern alternatives like Fly.io, Deno, and GitHub Pages. Users can download their project code until the end of the year and use new features to set up redirects for project subdomains until the end of 2026. Refunds will be issued for any paid subscription. The decision focuses on acknowledging the evolving developer landscape and plans to explore new ways to serve its community. There is mention of misuse from bad actors leading to increased costs.",,
