"summary": "The article describes a malware campaign targeting IT staff via SEO poisoning and typosquatting to distribute the Bumblebee malware loader. Fake websites mimicking popular tools Zenmap and WinMTR were used to trick users into downloading infected software. The malware is delivered alongside legitimate applications, evading many antivirus engines. The campaign also targets other software like Hanwha's WisenetViewer and Milestone XProtect, with infestations from fake domains such as milestonesys.org. Dell's RVTools were falsely implicated in distributing malware, being targeted by DDoS to drive traffic to malicious sites. The attack aims at corporate network breaches and lateral spread from IT tools requiring admin privileges.",,
