"summary": "This article summarizes the recent cyber incidents involving several threat actors and malware. Key insights include the takedown of Lumma Stealer and DanaBot infrastructures, exploitation of TikTok to distribute malware, targeting by APT28 and Chinese group UNC5221, malicious Chrome extensions, threats to SaaS providers, GitLab AI flaws, and trending CVEs. The recap includes various cybersecurity incidents: The Mask APT attributed to the Spanish government, a sophisticated malware campaign using AI-generated media by the Russian Storm-1516 group, the targeting of Coinbase users through social engineering, the legal action by Delta against CrowdStrike due to an outage, and vulnerabilities in WooCommerce websites committed via CSS and JS plugins. Other highlights involve sanctions against Stark Industries for cyber activities, information on SIM swapping tactics, and exploits in DICOM medical imaging files. Additionally, a technique named Cookie-Bite was described for stealing session tokens. The article discusses recent cyber incidents including APT campaigns, browser hijacks, AI-driven malware, and breaches involving cloud services and critical vulnerabilities. The content highlights the importance of revoking old OAuth permissions to prevent data exposure from unused apps. Additionally, it covers the release of AI Red Teaming Playground Labs for training security professionals on AI vulnerabilities. High-profile incidents include the exploitation of SAP vulnerability CVE-2025-31324 by China-linked APTs affecting 581 critical systems worldwide and a malicious npm package using Unicode steganography.",,
