"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Artificial Intelligence](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/)\n  * OpenAI plans to ship an interesting ChatGPT product by 2026\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-plans-to-ship-an-interesting-chatgpt-product-by-2026\/)\n\n\n# OpenAI plans to ship an interesting ChatGPT product by 2026\nBy \n###### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n  * May 26, 2025\n  * 08:02 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-plans-to-ship-an-interesting-chatgpt-product-by-2026\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2023\/04\/11\/OpenAI.jpg)\nOpenAI is planning to ship a new ChatGPT-powered product by 2026, but we aren't looking at yet another model.\nIn the U.S. v. Google antitrust, a pointed out that OpenAI has plans to \u201cship a [redacted] by 2026.\"\nThe redacted line comes from the very first slide of their H1 2025 strategy, dated December 2, 2024.\nAccording to the document, \u201cToday, ChatGPT is in our lives through existing form factors \u2014 our website, phone, and desktop apps.\u201d\nOpenAI hopes that ChatGPT will help in your life, no matter where you are, which appears to suggest that ChatGPT could soon expand beyond website and apps.\n![OpenAI](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1097497\/AI\/OpenAI.jpg)\nChatGPT \u201cshould help answer questions, play music, and suggest recipes,\u201d while on the go, it \u201cshould help you get to places, find the best restaurants, or catch up with friends.\u201d\nIn the office, it would \u201chelp you take meeting notes, or prepare for the big presentation.\u201d\n\"We want ChatGPT to be [REDACTED]\u2026 The best AI is the one that\u2019s right there with you. To do this, we will [REDACTED] 3P Confidential [REDACTED] But the best path to delivering this is [REDACTED], which will remain internally confidential for now,\" OpenAI wrote.\n\"We won\u2019t [REDACTED] in 2025. Our aim is to [REDACTED] by 2026, but to get there, we need to start preparing now.\"\nIf you put it all together, it seems to suggest that OpenAI is working on hardware that runs ChatGPT natively and allows you to use AI in your life.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[OpenAI hints at a big upgrade for ChatGPT Operator Agent](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-hints-at-a-big-upgrade-for-chatgpt-operator-agent\/)\n[OpenAI plans to combine multiple models into GPT-5](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-plans-to-combine-multiple-models-into-gpt-5\/)\n[ChatGPT is finally adding Download as PDF for Deep Research](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/chatgpt-is-finally-adding-download-as-pdf-for-deep-research\/)\n[ChatGPT Deep Research can now pull data from Dropbox and Box](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/chatgpt-deep-research-can-now-pull-data-from-dropbox-and-box\/)\n[Researchers claim ChatGPT o3 bypassed shutdown in controlled test](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/researchers-claim-chatgpt-o3-bypassed-shutdown-in-controlled-test\/)\n  * [AI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/ai\/)\n  * [Chat-GPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/chat-gpt\/)\n  * [ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/chatgpt\/)\n  * [GPT-5](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/gpt-5\/)\n  * [OpenAI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/openai\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openai-plans-to-ship-an-interesting-chatgpt-product-by-2026\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n##### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\nMayank Parmar is an technology entrepreneur who is currently pursuing an MBA. At BleepingComputer, he covers technology news with a strong focus on Microsoft and Windows-related stories. He is always poking under the hood of Windows, looking for the latest secrets to reveal. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/vibe-coding-company-says-claude-4-reduced-syntax-errors-by-25-percent\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/this-75-refurbished-lenovo-chromebook-makes-for-a-great-extra-computer\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-