"title": "Dutch intelligence unmasks previously unknown Russian hacking group 'Laundry Bear'",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/laundry-bear-void-blizzard-russia-hackers-netherlands",,
"summary": "Dutch intelligence services have uncovered a previously unknown Russian hacking group, dubbed 'Laundry Bear', responsible for a series of cyber attacks in the Netherlands, including an incident involving the Dutch national police. This group primarily engages in non-destructive cyber espionage, particularly targeting email environments. It has been linked with Microsoft under the name 'Void Blizzard' and operates similarly to APT28 but hasn't been identified as the same actor. The group focuses on sectors directly related to the Russian war effort in Ukraine, including defense, aerospace, and high-end technology due to Western sanctions. The attackers employ automated methods, leveraging existing software on victims' systems for large-scale data theft. Their methods involve relatively simple techniques such as phishing and exploiting legitimate cloud APIs.",,
