"markdown": "![Apple logo](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_apple_logo_1_2bab37b66f.jpg)\nCredit: Amin Zarbadast \/ Unsplash\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 27th, 2025\n# Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last year\nApple\u2019s App Store protected users from about $2 billion in fraudulent transactions in 2024 and about $9 billion over the last five years, the company said Tuesday. \n\u201cThese threats range from deceptive apps designed to steal personal information, to fraudulent payment schemes that attempt to exploit users,\u201d Apple said in a [news release](https:\/\/www.apple.com\/newsroom\/2025\/05\/the-app-store-prevented-more-than-9-billion-usd-in-fraudulent-transactions\/) tallying the App Store\u2019s security efforts over the past year. The tech giant has [touted](https:\/\/www.theverge.com\/news\/667484\/apple-eu-ios-app-store-warning-payment-system) the store\u2019s reputation for security as it faces pressure from government regulators to loosen some of its policies. \nWith more than 800 million visitors a week globally, protecting the marketplace \u201crequires constant vigilance\u201d as fraudsters continue to evolve their tactics, the tech giant said. \nThe job includes terminating suspicious app-developer accounts; reviewing submitted apps for security, reliability and user experience; rejecting and deactivating problematic customer accounts; and blocking pirated apps from launching on Apple devices. \nThe company also keeps a close eye on payment methods: \u201cLast year, Apple identified nearly 4.7 million stolen credit cards and banned over 1.6 million accounts from transacting again,\u201d the news release said. \nAnother area requiring constant attention, Apple said, is manipulation of App Store rankings. \n\u201cApple takes swift action against apps that attempt to cheat the system and boost their ranking on the App Store, such as by using bots or paid services to artificially inflate download numbers or post fake five-star reviews,\u201d the company said. \nAs TechCrunch [noted](https:\/\/techcrunch.com\/2025\/05\/27\/ahead-of-wwdc-apple-says-app-store-blocked-2b-in-fraud-transactions-last-year-9b-in-past-5-years\/), the fraud statistics come as Apple is preparing for its Worldwide Developers Conference (WWDC) next month. The company also is adapting to European Union rules requiring it to allow Apple device users to access [third-party app stores](https:\/\/support.apple.com\/en-us\/118110). The EU has [imposed fines](https:\/\/therecord.media\/eu-fines-apple-steering-meta-data-privacy-dma) on the company over how it handles revenues generated by apps. \nLast year, Apple said it blocked [about $1.8 billion](https:\/\/www.apple.com\/newsroom\/2024\/05\/app-store-stopped-over-7-billion-usd-in-potentially-fraudulent-transactions\/) in fraudulent App Store activity during 2023. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last year)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last year )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cybercrime)\n  * [scam](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scam)\n  * [app store](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/app-store)\n  * [Apple](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/apple)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n  * [MATLAB developer bringing systems back online following ransomware attackMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/matlab-developer-bringing-systems-online-ransomware)\n  * [Vietnam orders ban on Telegram messaging app over security concernsMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/vietnam-orders-telegram-messaging-ban)\n  * [DOJ charges man allegedly behind Qakbot malwareMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/doj-charges-man-allegedly-behind-qakbot-malware)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bugMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-speaking-hackers-target-municipalities-cityworks)\n  * [Russia-aligned hackers target Tajikistan in new espionage campaignMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-hackers-target-tajikistan-espionage)\n  * [Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service outagesMay 21st, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/midwestern-cellcom-telcom-cyberattack)\n  * [Senators question Noem about CISA cuts, but get few detailsMay 20th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/noem-cisa-cuts-senate-hearing)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
