"markdown": "![Sheboygan](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_Sheboygan_sign_91946f3295.jpg)\nCredit: MrSchimpf \/ Wikimedia Commons\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 27th, 2025\n# Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, Wisconsin\nThe Wisconsin city of Sheboygan warned about 67,000 people that a [ransomware attack in October](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sheboygan-wisconsin-hackers-demand-ransom) gave hackers access to their personal information. \nThe city [filed](https:\/\/www.maine.gov\/agviewer\/content\/ag\/985235c7-cb95-4be2-8792-a1252b4f8318\/1f937a68-1811-49e4-afe6-f0d34edbb837.html) breach notification letters with regulators on Friday explaining that Social Security numbers, state IDs and license plate numbers were taken when hackers breached the city\u2019s systems on October 31, 2024. \nOfficials in Sheboygan hired a cybersecurity firm to conduct an investigation that concluded on May 14 and confirmed that data was stolen. \nSheboygan, which has about 50,000 residents, previously [acknowledged](https:\/\/www.sheboyganwi.gov\/city-of-sheboygan-issues-update-on-network-security-investigation\/) that a ransomware gang had taken credit for the attack but said there was no evidence the hackers stole sensitive data. The attack was claimed in November by a gang called Chort, which [shared](https:\/\/www.sheboyganwi.gov\/itupdate-2\/) screenshots of a list of file archives and demanded a ransom. \nThe city reported the incident to law enforcement and said they were \u201cincorporating their guidance\u201d in their response to the incident. Officials said emergency services were still available in but didn\u2019t share any further updates after November 22. \nOne year of identity protection services will be provided to those affected, the city said in its breach notification letters. \nSheboygan is [one of several](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-group-claims-attack-on-wisconsin-school-district) government bodies in Wisconsin to be [targeted](https:\/\/therecord.media\/wisconsin-county-dealing-with-ransomware-attack-healthcare) by [ransomware gangs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/wisconsin-county-dealing-with-software-failure) over the last two years. \nThe Chort ransomware gang [emerged](https:\/\/www.ransomware.live\/group\/chort) in November 2024, claiming attacks on multiple state institutions including Kuwait\u2019s Public Authority of Agriculture Affairs and Fish Resources, a public school in Georgia, and others. \nNew York\u2019s Hartwick College was also named on the gang\u2019s leak site. The school confirmed it was attacked last October in breach notification letters sent last month to [more than 4,800 victims](https:\/\/www.maine.gov\/agviewer\/content\/ag\/985235c7-cb95-4be2-8792-a1252b4f8318\/8f7c122f-d1b4-4e83-b6e7-69f531f1c722.html). \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, Wisconsin)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, Wisconsin )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Ransomware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ransomware)\n  * [Wisconsin](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/wisconsin)\n  * [municipalities](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/municipalities)\n  * [data breach](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-breach)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n  * [MATLAB developer bringing systems back online following ransomware attackMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/matlab-developer-bringing-systems-online-ransomware)\n  * [Vietnam orders ban on Telegram messaging app over security concernsMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/vietnam-orders-telegram-messaging-ban)\n  * [DOJ charges man allegedly behind Qakbot malwareMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/doj-charges-man-allegedly-behind-qakbot-malware)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bugMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-speaking-hackers-target-municipalities-cityworks)\n  * [Russia-aligned hackers target Tajikistan in new espionage campaignMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-hackers-target-tajikistan-espionage)\n  * [Midwestern telco Cellcom confirms cyber incident after days of service