"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj_qMszEYVjwFa9p_Krb5PlKHZJ_qBguBZqxrUfXlqHzxZp2oUt8yjE6vjlrLVTK0Y1GtUlNL0C05SY-iq5GFsNkYrpPSTbPj30XarU3aO5dCJ-JkolvzdnxuynVOr9iXHx-dxJxuf-Ie7jyStTAnUzs8echAPUUsWcrutKu-pumRQLp2UIDfddyBqzblfx\/s728-e300\/training-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/training-d)\n# [New Self-Spreading Malware Infects Docker Containers to Mine Dero Cryptocurrency](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)\n_\ue802_ May 27, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCloud Security \/ Threat Intelligence\n[![Self-Spreading Docker Malware](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhH8eO7vfKPxcTGvyI5kEPTEpwCrTiyW4xa9tO9zb0-v3YuKsbQZIFQ-VVwPPEJZxqudQUsxk6_7N2m5IcWf7DpKAQcccod2ByPUGHTpeVOH7uufFvTCJPLA6huQbavp9dWNLF92ILDRbSUmZkhJeJC4SIh9_pD3At3FUyLjbahlmvtNkqSdrxql7l3uyH-\/s728-rw-e365\/dockers.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhH8eO7vfKPxcTGvyI5kEPTEpwCrTiyW4xa9tO9zb0-v3YuKsbQZIFQ-VVwPPEJZxqudQUsxk6_7N2m5IcWf7DpKAQcccod2ByPUGHTpeVOH7uufFvTCJPLA6huQbavp9dWNLF92ILDRbSUmZkhJeJC4SIh9_pD3At3FUyLjbahlmvtNkqSdrxql7l3uyH-\/s728-rw-e365\/dockers.jpg)\nMisconfigured Docker API instances have become the target of a new malware campaign that transforms them into a cryptocurrency mining botnet.\nThe attacks, designed to mine for Dero currency, is notable for its worm-like capabilities to propagate the malware to other exposed Docker instances and rope them into an ever-growing horde of mining bots.\nKaspersky said it observed an unidentified threat actor gaining initial access to a running containerized infrastructure by exploiting an insecurely published Docker API, and then weaponizing that access to create the illicit cryptojacking network.\n\"This led to the running containers being compromised and new ones being created not only to hijack the victim's resources for cryptocurrency mining but also to launch external attacks to propagate to other networks,\" security researcher Amged Wageh [said](https:\/\/securelist.com\/dero-miner-infects-containers-through-docker-api\/116546\/).\nThe attack chain is realized through two components: A propagation malware \"nginx\" that scans the internet for exposed Docker APIs and the \"cloud\" Dero cryptocurrency miner. Both the payloads are developed using Golang. The use of \"nginx\" is a deliberate attempt to masquerade as the legitimate nginx web server and fly under the radar.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-1 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe propagation malware is designed to record the running activities of the malware, launch the miner, and enter into an infinite loop to generate random IPv4 network subnets for flagging more susceptible Docker instances that have the default API port 2375 open and compromising them.\nIt then proceeds to check whether the remote dockerd daemon on the host with a matching IPv4 is running and responsive. If it fails to execute the \"docker -H PS\" command, \"nginx\" simply moves to the next IP address from the list.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjMFbdvGbk4odvuoVkxaRT0uN1GzQAtc7UJdEQn1d1guPDYSmvmGNmFv-rFtcnRSCI3EXItOrrAVVfd6KTtCL9N0c1NVDpJzmBetxXz5e5Nybtzx0Vh9jkdmLe7FDiCSzC0afVqaZddgQKDvCtj0TSgaHj4fYvnGUfjzXvGf4jpb_oZYis2YFuZT77a5T1v\/s728-rw-e365\/kas.png)\n\"After confirming that the remote dockerd daemon is running and responsive, nginx generates a container name with 12 random characters and uses it to create a malicious container on the remote target,\" Wageh explained. \"Then nginx prepares the new container to install dependencies later by updating the packages via 'docker -H exec apt-get -yq update.'\"\nThe propagation tool then installs masscan and docker.io in the container so as to allow the malware to interact with the Docker daemon and to perform the external scan to infect other networks, effectively spreading the malware further. In the last stage, the two payloads \"nginx\" and \"cloud\" are transferred to the container using the command \"docker -H cp -L \/usr\/bin\/ :\/usr\/bin.\"\nAs a way of setting up persistence, the transferred \"nginx\" binary is added to the \"\/root\/.bash_aliases\" file to make sure that it automatically launches upon shell login. Another significant aspect of the malware is that it's also engineered to infect Ubuntu-based running containers on remote vulnerable hosts.\nThe ultimate goal of the campaign is to execute the Dero cryptocurrency miner, which is based on the open-source DeroHE CLI miner available on GitHub.\nKaspersky has assessed that the activity overlaps with a Dero mining campaign that was [previously documented](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/03\/new-cryptojacking-operation-targeting.html) by CrowdStrike in March 2023 targeting Kubernetes clusters based on the wallet address and derod node addresses used. A subsequent iteration of the same campaign was [flagged](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/06\/cryptojacking-campaign-targets.html) by Wiz in June 2024.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"Containerized environments were compromised through a combination of a previously known miner and a new sample that created malicious containers and infected existing ones,\" Wageh said. \"The two malicious implants spread without a C2 server, making any network that has a containerized infrastructure and insecurely published Docker API to the internet a potential target.\"\nThe development comes as the AhnLab Security Intelligence Center (ASEC) detailed a campaign that involves the deployment of the Monero coin miner along with a never-before-seen backdoor that uses the [PyBitmessage](https:\/\/github.com\/Bitmessage\/PyBitmessage) peer-to-peer (P2P) communication protocol to process incoming instructions and execute them as PowerShell scripts.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhBrFlbuzbodkD7yC-PrawFWGWWhi0LGSN6B7rymu0Wh4TPl2PdCBCp5Na3jolC318NdCQdv6PsXRKByUiz6DoDzX6UhzImLZl5Vr9l1Hlls3yPZNw8p4PJTsf2_1UVha0GX2uODDLcy80-BV2MUELrZtcUa1DGOpQFGTszb4Ej4BJHEL-eSY7ktS6JLim0\/s728-rw-e365\/ahn.png)\nThe exact distribution method used in the campaign is currently not known, but it's suspected to be disguised as cracked versions of popular software, making it essential that users avoid downloading files from unknown or untrusted sources and stick to legitimate distribution channels. \n\"The Bitmessage protocol is a messaging system designed with anonymity and decentralization in mind, and it features the prevention of interception by intermediaries and the anonymization of message senders and receivers,\" ASEC [said](https:\/\/asec.ahnlab.com\/en\/88109\/).\n\"Threat actors exploited the PyBitmessage module, which implements this protocol in the Python environment, to exchange encrypted packets in a format similar to regular web traffic. In particular, C2 commands and control messages are hidden within messages from real users in the Bitmessage network.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fnew-self-spreading-malware-infects.html&t=New%20Self-Spreading%20Malware%20Infects%20Docker%20Containers%20to%20Mine%20Dero%20Cryptocurrency) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=New%20Self-Spreading%20Malware%20Infects%20Docker%20Containers%20to%20Mine%20Dero%20Cryptocurrency \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fnew-self-spreading-malware-infects.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-self-spreading-malware-infects.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fnew-self-spreading-malware-infects.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fnew-self-spreading-malware-infects.html&text=New%20Self-Spreading%20Malware%20Infects%20Docker%20Containers%20to%20Mine%20Dero%20Cryptocurrency)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Cloud security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cloud%20security)[cryptocurrency mining](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cryptocurrency%20mining)[cryptojacking](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cryptojacking)[Docker Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Docker%20Security)[Kubernetes](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Kubernetes)[linux](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/linux)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29v