"summary": "The article discusses the evolution of the Zanubis banking Trojan for Android, which emerged in 2022 and primarily targeted financial institutions in Peru. Over time, Zanubis has expanded its capabilities to include data exfiltration, remote control, and obfuscation techniques, among others. Newer iterations have expanded the scope to include virtual card and crypto wallet targets. The article discusses the evolution of the Zanubis Android banking trojan, highlighting its sophisticated methods of stealing device credentials, targeting banking apps and financial institutions, and executing silent installations. The threat actors, possibly based in Peru, have shifted their focus to financial institutions, abandoning broader targets such as cryptocurrency wallets.",,
