"summary": "The Czech Republic has accused China of attempting to hack its Ministry of Foreign Affairs, specifically targeting an unclassified network deemed critical infrastructure, as part of a campaign by APT31, also known as Judgment Panda, Bronze Vinewood, and RedBravo. This group is linked to China's Ministry of State Security. The attack began in 2022 with possible impacts on the Czech critical infrastructure, although it is unclear if the network was breached. Czechia's action follows similar past accusations against other foreign states for cyber-espionage. The EU and NATO have supported the Czech Republic's stance, with NATO condemning the malicious activities attributed to China.",,
