"title": "How 'Browser-in-the-Middle' Attacks Steal Sessions in Seconds",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/how-browser-in-middle-attacks-steal.html",,
"summary": "The article discusses Browser-in-the-Middle (BitM) attacks, similar to Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) attacks, that hijack user sessions on the web. These attacks involve a user unknowingly interacting with a transparent remote browser controlled by an attacker, leading to credential and session token theft. Through phases of phishing, fake browser use, and targeting web applications, attackers can compromise multi-factor authentication by stealing session tokens. Recommended mitigations include token hardening, content security policies, behavioral monitoring, and browser isolation. The article also emphasizes the importance of maintaining strong passwords and MFA.",,
