"markdown": "![Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky news conference](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_53410523614_394c906bc7_o_6d1dce1e5d.jpg)\nUkrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky appears on a news camera's viewfinder during a press conference in December 2023. Image: President of Ukraine \/ Flickr\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)May 28th, 2025\n# Ukraine tallies up Russian cyberattacks on local media since start of war\nRussian hackers have carried out more than 200 successful cyberattacks on Ukrainian media outlets since the start of the war three years ago, targeting television channels, news agencies and state-run media, according to a new report. \nThe attacks were aimed at spreading pro-Russian propaganda, manipulating public opinion and sowing chaos, said [researchers](https:\/\/cip.gov.ua\/services\/cm\/api\/attachment\/download?id=69131) at the SSSCIP, the state agency responsible for protecting information and critical infrastructure. \nHackers employed a range of tactics in their operations against Ukrainian media, including publishing disinformation, wiping content and launching DDoS attacks to temporarily disrupt access to media platforms. Another common method involved compromising social media accounts belonging to journalists and news organizations to disseminate false information. \nRussia has also actively used deepfake technology in its information operations. In the early days of the war, hackers created a [fabricated](https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2022\/03\/16\/1087062648\/deepfake-video-zelenskyy-experts-war-manipulation-ukraine-russia) video that appeared to show Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urging troops to surrender. The clip circulated on social media and was briefly posted on a Ukrainian news website before being debunked and removed. \n\u201cRussia used deepfakes to discredit Ukrainian military commanders, volunteers, and international partners by imitating their speeches and statements,\u201d the researchers said. \nMoscow also relies heavily on bot networks, fake accounts and paid posts to amplify pro-Russian narratives both in Ukraine and abroad. One of Russia\u2019s most notorious propaganda operations, known as [Doppelg\u00e4nger](https:\/\/therecord.media\/search-results?term=Doppleganger), has created hundreds of thousands of fake social media profiles and cloned websites of major news outlets to spread disinformation in countries including Germany, France, the United States, Ukraine and Israel. \nWhile the latest SSSCIP report does not specify which hacker groups were behind the cyberattacks on Ukrainian media, the agency has previously [attributed](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukrainian-news-outlets-attacked-by-russian-hackers) such operations to state-controlled threat actors, including the notorious [Sandworm](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/sandworm) unit. \nIn February, hackers [targeted](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukrainian-news-outlets-attacked-by-russian-hackers) several major Ukrainian media outlets \u2014 including the prominent online newspaper Ukrainska Pravda \u2014 to spread fake news related to the war. In 2023, Russia [targeted](https:\/\/cip.gov.ua\/en\/news\/kiberataka-ne-zmogla-zupiniti-robotu-informaciinogo-agentstva-ukrinform) Ukraine\u2019s national news agency, Ukrinform, causing \u201ccertain destructive effects\u201d to its information infrastructure. \nIn July 2022, two radio stations [owned](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukrainian-radio-broadcaster-hacked-to-spread-fake-news-about-zelenskys-health) by one of Ukraine\u2019s largest broadcasters, TAVR Media, were hacked to broadcast false claims that Zelensky had been hospitalized in critical condition. \nIn Ukraine, Russian hackers and troops are targeting Ukraine\u2019s telecommunication infrastructure both in cyberspace and on the ground, destroying radio and television towers, as well as radio centers that broadcast to the occupied territories. \nRussian cyberattacks on media outlets have also extended beyond Ukraine. Earlier in May, Azerbaijani officials [accused](https:\/\/therecord.media\/azerbaijan-blames-media-cyberattacks-russia-apt29) the Russian state-sponsored hacking group APT29 of launching cyberattacks against several local media organizations. Last year, suspected Russian hackers [infiltrated](https:\/\/therecord.media\/poland-cyberattack-investigation-state-agency) the Polish Press Agency\u2019s website to publish fake news. And in September 2024, \u201cunknown attackers from Russia\u201d [hacked](https:\/\/therecord.media\/germany-cyberattack-radio-geretsried) a German radio station and encrypted all of its music files. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Ukraine tallies up Russian cyberattacks on local media since start of war)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Ukraine tallies up Russian cyberattacks on local media since start of war )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Nation-state](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/nation-state)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [media](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/media)\n  * [social media](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/social-media)\n  * [deepfakes](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/deepfake)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [Ukraine War](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ukraine-war)\n  * [Ukraine](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ukraine)\n  * [Volodymyr Zelensky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/volodymyr-zelensky)\n  * [disinformation](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/disinformation)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [SSSCIP](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ssscip)\n  * [news media](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/news-media)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Russian hospital programmer gets 14 years for leaking soldier data to UkraineMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-programmer-gets-14-years-for-leaking-info-to-ukraine)\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n  * [MATLAB developer bringing systems back online following ransomware attackMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/matlab-developer-bringing-systems-online-ransomware)\n  * [Vietnam orders ban on Telegram messaging app over security concernsMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/vietnam-orders-telegram-messaging-ban)\n  * [DOJ charges man allegedly behind Qakbot malwareMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/doj-charges-man-allegedly-behind-qakbot-malware)\n  * [Chinese-speaking hackers targeting US municipalities with Cityworks bugMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/chinese-speaking-hackers-target-municipalities-cityworks)\n  * [Russia-aligned hackers target Tajikistan in new espionage campaignMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russia-hackers-target-tajikistan-espionage)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/