"summary": "A cybersecurity incident involving the Mimo hacking group was reported, where they exploited a vulnerability identified as CVE-2025-32432 in Craft CMS. This vulnerability allowed the attackers to deploy malicious payloads such as a cryptocurrency miner, Mimo Loader, and IPRoyal proxyware. The attack involved the use of a web shell to gain and maintain access to compromised systems, ultimately aiming to exploit system resources for cryptojacking and proxyjacking activities. The group, active since 2022, previously leveraged other critical vulnerabilities in well-known software products.",,
