"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Mimo Hackers Exploit CVE-2025-32432 in Craft CMS to Deploy Cryptominer and Proxyware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html)\n_\ue802_ May 28, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCryptojacking \/ Vulnerability\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgZ-zcRNqaTR0JyG96gVXYk1j6Q-yybW8LugW2ND7UaClzQMKbeHlFSBylvlew36Y71ci5jc8hQFJ07MCT0B_AYuyyqJTReUWrGQpT1pZfBRZaCYYYMHHFZxv2xFv7GFm28NsSU8MW_VfbrwUGY0SadpmS-GEPSV3ClW_URmyhn-X8gd0_7uUFbkhukT01j\/s728-rw-e365\/miner.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgZ-zcRNqaTR0JyG96gVXYk1j6Q-yybW8LugW2ND7UaClzQMKbeHlFSBylvlew36Y71ci5jc8hQFJ07MCT0B_AYuyyqJTReUWrGQpT1pZfBRZaCYYYMHHFZxv2xFv7GFm28NsSU8MW_VfbrwUGY0SadpmS-GEPSV3ClW_URmyhn-X8gd0_7uUFbkhukT01j\/s728-rw-e365\/miner.jpg)\nA financially motivated threat actor has been observed exploiting a recently disclosed remote code execution flaw affecting the Craft Content Management System (CMS) to deploy multiple payloads, including a cryptocurrency miner, a loader dubbed Mimo Loader, and residential proxyware.\nThe vulnerability in question is [CVE-2025-32432](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/04\/hackers-exploit-critical-craft-cms.html), a maximum severity flaw in Craft CMS that was patched in versions 3.9.15, 4.14.15, and 5.6.17. The existence of the security defect was first disclosed in April 2025 by Orange Cyberdefense SensePost after it was observed in attacks earlier this February.\nAccording to a new report published by Sekoia, the threat actors behind the campaign weaponized CVE-2025-32432 to obtain unauthorized access to the target systems and then deploy a web shell to enable persistent remote access.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-2 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe web shell is then used to download and execute a shell script (\"4l4md4r.sh\") from a remote server using curl, wget, or the Python library urllib2.\n\"Regarding the use of Python, the attacker imports the urllib2 library under the alias fbi. This unusual naming choice may be an intentional reference \u2014 possibly a tongue-in-cheek nod to the American federal agency \u2014 and stands out as a distinctive coding choice,\" Sekoia researchers Jeremy Scion and Pierre Le Bourhis [said](https:\/\/blog.sekoia.io\/the-sharp-taste-of-mimolette-analyzing-mimos-latest-campaign-targeting-craft-cms\/).\n\"This naming convention could serve as a useful indicator for detection, especially in threat hunting or retroactive analysis of suspicious Python activity.\"\nThe shell script, for its part, first checks for indicators or prior infection, as well as uninstalls any version of a known cryptocurrency miner. It also terminates all active XMRig processes and other competing cryptomining tools, if any, before delivering next-stage payloads and launching an ELF binary named \"4l4md4r.\"\nThe executable, known as Mimo Loader, modifies \"\/etc\/ld.so.preload,\" a file read by the dynamic linker, to hide the presence of the malware process (\"alamdar.so\"). The ultimate goal of the loader is to deploy the IPRoyal proxyware and the XMRig miner on the compromised host.\nThis allows the threat actor to not only abuse the system resources for illicit cryptocurrency mining, but also monetize the victim's internet bandwidth for other malicious activities -- techniques commonly referred to as [cryptojacking and proxyjacking](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/09\/exposed-selenium-grid-servers-targeted.html), respectively.\nThe threat activity has been attributed to an intrusion set dubbed Mimo (aka Mimo), which is believed to be active since March 2022, previously relying on vulnerabilities in Apache Log4j (CVE-2021-44228), Atlassian Confluence (CVE-2022-26134), PaperCut (CVE-2023\u201327350), and Apache ActiveMQ (CVE-2023-46604) to deploy the miner.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe hacking group, per a report [published](https:\/\/asec.ahnlab.com\/en\/60440\/) by AhnLab in January 2024, has also been observed staging ransomware attacks in 2023 using a Go-based strain known as Mimus, which is a fork of the open-source MauriCrypt project.\nSekoia said the exploitation efforts originate from a Turkish IP address (\"85.106.113[.]168\") and that it uncovered open-source evidence that points to Mimo being a threat actor who is physically located in the country.\n\"Initially identified in early 2022, the Mimo intrusion set has been characterised by its consistent exploitation of vulnerabilities for the purpose of cryptominer deployment,\" the French cybersecurity company said. \"Ongoing investigation confirms that Mimo remains active and operational, continuing to exploit newly disclosed vulnerabilities.\"\n\"The short timeframe observed between the publication of CVE-2025-32432, the release of a corresponding proof-of-concept (PoC), and its subsequent adoption by the intrusion set, reflects a high level of responsiveness and technical agility.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html&t=Mimo%20Hackers%20Exploit%20CVE-2025-32432%20in%20Craft%20CMS%20to%20Deploy%20Cryptominer%20and%20Proxyware) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Mimo%20Hackers%20Exploit%20CVE-2025-32432%20in%20Craft%20CMS%20to%20Deploy%20Cryptominer%20and%20Proxyware \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fmimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html&text=Mimo%20Hackers%20Exploit%20CVE-2025-32432%20in%20Craft%20CMS%20to%20Deploy%20Cryptominer%20and%20Proxyware)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[CMS](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/CMS)[Craft CMS](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Craft%20CMS)[cryptojacking](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cryptojacking)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Proxyware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Proxyware)[Python](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Python)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)[Vulnerability](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Vulnerability)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEj5q7racGwMr5emA21v4uOtTjSF4X1U2UIB1VXdECJy_UlSerg-4nUz1sWoQPECXE52nExclTrzA8PSWUvGhM_NOY6KlHcLZHn61pnpthgtEfcAqeRnCVYq1timp_hDOibhzVIVe88exkuUO-W29dSFiS96BH2j2HD-_-aPf7X73C3l2V5FKCuy8t04tiTI\/s728-rw-e365\/cis-side-2.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/cis-controls-rsrcs)\nMost Read News\n[ ![Microsoft Fixes 78 Flaws, 5 Zero-Days Exploited; CVSS 10 Bug Impacts Azure DevOps Server](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html) Microsoft Fixes 78 Flaws, 5 Zero-Days Exploited; CVSS 10 Bug Impacts Azure DevOps Server ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/microsoft-fixes-78-flaws-5-zero-days.html)\n[ ![\u26a1 Weekly Recap: Zero-Day Exploits, Insider Threats, APT Targeting, Botnets and More](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html) \u26a1 Weekly Recap: Zero-Day Exploits, Insider Threats, APT Targeting, Botnets and More ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/weekly-recap-zero-day-exploits-insider.html)\n[ ![AWS Default IAM Roles Found to Enable Lateral Movement and Cross-Service Exploitation](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/mimo-hackers-exploit-cve-2025-32432-in.html) AWS Default IAM Roles Found to Enable Lateral Movement and Cross-Service Exploitation ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/aws-default-iam-roles-found-to-enable.html)\n[ ![Malicious PyPI Package Posing as Solana Tool Stole Source Code in 761 Downloads](https:\/\/thehac