"title": "New PumaBot Botnet Targets Linux IoT Devices to Steal SSH Credentials and Mine Crypto",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-pumabot-botnet-targets-linux-iot.html",,
"summary": "PumaBot is a new botnet targeting Linux IoT devices, specifically written in Go, to perform brute-force SSH attacks. It retrieves targets from a command-and-control server and attempts to brute-force SSH credentials. Once access is obtained, it establishes persistence using system service files and disguises itself as Redis legit binaries. The botnet is employed to mine cryptocurrency and has a worm-like capability due to its SSH brute-force approach.",,
