"markdown": "![Data breach](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_digital_hack_computer_data_breach_f97e2f823d.jpg)\nImage: Allison Saeng via Unsplash\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 28th, 2025\n# LexisNexis Risk Solutions says 364,000 impacted by breach involving GitHub data\nInformation belonging to more than 360,000 people was leaked in a data breach affecting an arm of the analytics giant LexisNexis, the company said Wednesday. \nA spokesperson for the company told Recorded Future News that on April 1, officials at LexisNexis Risk Solutions (LNRS) received a report from \u201can unknown third party\u201d saying they accessed information from the company. \nLNRS is a branch of LexisNexis that provides risk management services to business customers and is one of the largest data brokers in the U.S. \n\u201cOur Information Security team, in consultation with a forensic firm, immediately began investigating and confirmed that some data which was held in GitHub, a third-party platform used by LNRS for software development purposes was acquired by an unknown third party,\u201d the spokesperson said. \n\u201cSpecifically, we have determined that some software artifacts as well as some personal information was accessed. The personal information involved was limited to name, contact information (such as phone number, postal or email address), Social Security number, driver\u2019s license number or date of birth.\u201d \nThe spokesperson added that their systems and products were never compromised. Regulatory filings said more than 364,000 people were affected. \nLNRS has faced [significant backlash](https:\/\/therecord.media\/texas-probes-four-more-car-companies-data-collection-sharing) over the last three years for its data sharing relationship with [U.S. Customs and Border Patrol](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cbp-lexisnexis-ri***REMOVED***) and [car companies](https:\/\/therecord.media\/texas-warns-kia-about-sharing-driver-info-to-data-brokers). It has [faced lawsuits in multiple states](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-of-data-brokers-disclose-selling-info-on-kids-geolocation-data-reproductive-health) for its role as a data broker that collects and sells sensitive information on topics like [driver behavior](https:\/\/therecord.media\/data-broker-shuts-product-driver-patterns) and [reproductive health](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-of-data-brokers-disclose-selling-info-on-kids-geolocation-data-reproductive-health), as well as data belonging to children. \nIn breach notification letters filed in [Maine](https:\/\/www.maine.gov\/agviewer\/content\/ag\/985235c7-cb95-4be2-8792-a1252b4f8318\/782e2159-f2d4-4394-8d03-51bf08a6b3e5.html), [South Carolina](https:\/\/consumer.sc.gov\/sites\/consumer\/files\/Documents\/Security%20Breach%20Notices\/2025\/LexisNexisRiskSolutions.pdf) and [Vermont](https:\/\/ago.vermont.gov\/document\/2025-05-27-lexisnexis-ri***REMOVED***), the company said the breach occurred last Christmas and they were informed of it on April 1. The letters do not mention GitHub but say the data came from a \u201cthird-party platform used for software development.\u201d \nNo hacker has come forward to claim the attack. In the notification letters, LNRS said there is \u201cno evidence that your data has been further misused.\u201d \nLaw enforcement was notified of the issue and an investigation was launched with cybersecurity experts. Victims are being provided two years of identity protection services. \nThe Georgia-based company is best known for its data and technology services, analytics and predictive insights and has offices across Asia and Europe. It is a subsidiary of RELX, a British analytics company that [reported](https:\/\/www.relx.com\/media\/press-releases\/year-2025\/relx-2024-results) more than $12 billion in revenue last year. \nMore than 18,000 people associated with New Jersey law enforcement [filed a class action lawsuit](https:\/\/therecord.media\/new-jersey-law-enforcement-lawsuit-lexisnexis-data) against LexisNexis Risk Data Management last year alleging that after they asked for their information to remain private, the data broker retaliated against them by freezing their credit and falsely reporting them as identity theft victims. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=LexisNexis Risk Solutions says 364,000 impacted by breach involving GitHub data)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=LexisNexis Risk Solutions says 364,000 impacted by breach involving GitHub data )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Privacy](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/privacy)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [data broker](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-broker)\n  * [data breach](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-breach)\n  * [LexisNexis](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/lexisnexis)\n  * [GitHub](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/github)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Estonia issues arrest warrant for Moroccan wanted for major pharmacy data breachMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/estonia-arrest-warrant-pharmacy-data-breach)\n  * [Ukraine detains alleged Russian spies who used dash cams to guide missile strikesMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukraine-detains-russian-spies-using-dashcams-missile-strikes)\n  * [Russian hospital programmer gets 14 years for leaking soldier data to UkraineMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-programmer-gets-14-years-for-leaking-info-to-ukraine)\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n  * [MATLAB developer bringing systems back online following ransomware attackMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/matlab-developer-bringing-systems-online-ransomware)\n  * [Vietnam orders ban on Telegram messaging app over security concernsMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/vietnam-orders-telegram-messaging-ban)\n  * [DOJ charges man allegedly behind Qakbot malwareMay 22nd, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/doj-charges-man-allegedly-behind-qakbot-malware)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
