"markdown": "  * [Blog](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog)\n  * [Palo Alto Networks](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/corporate)\n  * [Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/)\n  * Cortex XDR Named 2025 Gar... \n\n\n# Cortex XDR Named 2025 Gartner Customers\u2019 Choice for Endpoint Security\n[ ](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/2025\/05\/cortex-xdr-named-gartner-customers-choice-endpoint-security\/)\nLink copied \nBy [Dan Flaherty](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/author\/dan-flaherty\/ \"Posts by Dan Flaherty\")\nMay 28, 2025\n4 minutes\n... views\n[Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/)\n[Must-Read Articles](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/must-read-articles\/)\n[News and Events](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/news-and-events\/)\n[2025 Gartner Peer Insights Customers\u2019 Choice](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/tag\/2025-gartner-peer-insights-customers-choice\/)\n[Analyst Report](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/tag\/analyst-report\/)\n[Cortex XDR](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/tag\/cortex-xdr\/)\n[endpoint security](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/tag\/endpoint-security\/)\n## **Highest Willingness to Recommend Score of All Gartner Customers\u2019 Choice Vendors**\nFor cybersecurity professionals evaluating new technologies, there's nothing more illuminating than the real-world experiences of peers who defend against threats every single day. The 2025 Gartner\u00ae Peer Insights\u2122 Voice of Customer Report captures this practical reality with insight spanning hundreds of companies worldwide.\nIn this year\u2019s report, the verdict is clear: Palo Alto Networks [Cortex XDR](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cortex\/cortex-xdr)\u00ae is a Gartner Customers\u2019 Choice for Endpoint Protection Platforms. An extraordinary 98% of reviewers are willing to recommend our industry-leading endpoint security to their peers, the highest of all Customers\u2019 Choice vendors. This isn't theoretical analysis, it's real-world validation from the users who depend on this technology to protect their organizations' most valuable assets.\nOperations Manager in the Banking Industry gives Cortex XDR 5\/5 Rating in [Gartner Peer Insights Endpoint Protection Platforms Market](https:\/\/gtnr.io\/H06ezfAML).\n## **What the Voice of Customer Report Reveals**\nThe Gartner Voice of Customer Report stands apart from typical analyst evaluations by putting customers at the center of the assessment. It aggregates verified reviews exclusively from organizations with annual revenue exceeding $50 million, transforming individual experiences into collective wisdom.\nFor security buyers evaluating [endpoint protection platforms (EPP)](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cyberpedia\/what-is-an-endpoint-protection-platform-epp), this represents the unfiltered voice of their peers \u2013 professionals who have implemented, managed and relied on these solutions in environments similar to their own.\nCortex XDR's performance in this report is exceptional across all dimensions:\n  * **98% Willingness to Recommend \u2013 the highest of all Customers\u2019 Choice vendors**\n  * **4.9 out of 5 stars for product capabilities**\n  * **4.7 out of 5 stars for both sales and deployment experience**\n  * **4.6 out of 5 stars for support experience**\n\n\nThese metrics earned Cortex XDR placement in the \"Customers' Choice\" quadrant, reserved for vendors who exceed market averages in Overall Experience and User Interest and Adoption, indicating strong ratings for product capabilities, service and support, as well as high willingness to recommend.\n## **Why This Matters**\nThe willingness-to-recommend metric is particularly important. When Gartner asks, \"How likely is it that you would recommend this product or service to a friend or colleague?\" on a scale of 0-10, only ratings of 8 or higher count as \"willing to recommend.\" **Achieving a 98% rating represents an unmatched level of customer satisfaction and confidence in Cortex XDR's capabilities.**\n## **What Sets Cortex XDR Apart**\nRecognition in Gartner Peer Insights underscores Cortex XDR's industry-leading security outcomes:\n  * **100%** technique detections in Round 6 of the MITRE ATT&CK Evals, with no delays or configuration changes \u2013 [an industry first](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cortex\/cortex-xdr\/mitre).\n  * **98%** reduction in alerts with advanced AI that groups all related alerts into unified incidents, allowing security teams to escape alert fatigue.\n  * **8x** faster investigations with automated root cause analysis driving rapid response times and minimizing breach impact.\n\n\n## **Pioneering the XDR Category with Continuous Innovation**\nSince first pioneering the XDR category, Palo Alto Networks has consistently innovated to transform endpoint security as a whole. The result is a comprehensive endpoint security solution that delivers superior protection for your organization.\nCortex XDR\u2019s key strengths:\n  * **AI-driven prevention** that stops malware, ransomware and fileless attacks before they can cause damage.\n  * **AI-driven detection proven by MITRE** that leverages behavioral analysis and machine learning to identify even the most evasive threats.\n  * **Automated root cause analysis** that dramatically accelerates investigation and remediation workflows.\n  * **Unified agent across enterprise and cloud** **environments** providing seamless protection, regardless of where your assets reside.\n\n\nOrganizations can expand XDR with industry-leading NG-SIEM, [SOAR](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cyberpedia\/what-is-soar), [ASM](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cyberpedia\/what-is-attack-surface-management) and other critical SOC capabilities, all in one unified backend, frontend and analyst experience with Cortex XSIAM\u00ae. This enables security teams to detect, investigate and respond to threats with unprecedented speed and accuracy across their entire attack surface.\nBy bringing together best-in-class endpoint protection with advanced detection and response capabilities, Cortex XDR continues to lead the industry in defending against evolving and accelerating cyberthreats.\nSystem Administrator Associate in the Manufacturing Industry gives Cortex XDR 5\/5 rating in [Gartner Peer Insights Endpoint Protection Platforms Market](https:\/\/gtnr.io\/6fyKSt14V).\n## **Beyond Customer Praise \u2014 Industry Recognition**\nCortex XDR's excellence isn't just recognized by customers. The major third-party analysts have consistently identified Palo Alto Networks as a leader in endpoint protection:\n  * Industry-best 100% detection with no delays or configuration changes in the [MITRE ATT&CK Round 6 Evaluation](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/resources\/guides\/the-essential-guide-mitre-attack-round-6)\n  * A Leader in the 2024 [Gartner Magic Quadrant\u2122 for EPP](https:\/\/start.paloaltonetworks.com\/gartner-epp-mq)\n  * A Leader in [The Forrester Wave\u2122: Extended Detection And Response Platforms, Q2 2024](https:\/\/start.paloaltonetworks.com\/2024-forrester-xdr-wave-leader)\n\n\n## **The Bottom Line**\nWith 98% of customers willing to recommend Cortex XDR, the verdict is clear: when it comes to endpoint protection that delivers both superior security and exceptional customer experience, Cortex XDR sets the standard.\n### Ready to experience Cortex XDR? Schedule a [personal demo today](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/cortex\/cortex-xdr-request-demo) and start improving your security to stay ahead of today\u2019s threats.\n## Related Blogs\n###  [Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/), [Products and Services](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/products-and-services\/)\n#### [Palo Alto Networks Excels in MITRE Managed Services Evaluation](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/2024\/06\/unit-42-mdr-in-mitre-managed-services-evaluation\/)\n###  [Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/), [Must-Read Articles](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/must-read-articles\/), [News and Events](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/news-and-events\/), [Product Features](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/product-features\/), [Products and Services](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/products-and-services\/)\n#### [Forrester Names Palo Alto Networks a Leader in XDR](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/2024\/06\/forrester-names-palo-alto-networks-a-leader-in-xdr\/)\n###  [Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/), [Company & Culture](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/company-culture\/), [Must-Read Articles](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/must-read-articles\/), [News and Events](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/news-and-events\/), [Product Features](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/product-features\/), [Products and Services](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/products-and-services\/)\n#### [2022 MITRE Engenuity ATT&CK Evaluations Results](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/2022\/03\/mitre-engenuity-evaluations-round-4-results\/)\n###  [Announcement](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/category\/announcement\/), [Must-Read Articles](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/must-read-articles\/), [News and Events](https:\/\/www.paloaltonetworks.com\/blog\/security-operations\/category\/news-and-events\/), [Products and Services](https:\/\/www.paloa