"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/czech-republic-blames-china-linked.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiKLqdTf2BnL4fIex_Fj-HhjsQU6HOZ_ao_WyUZ0ELrxsZ4ezufQqD8JfJabnIMeCtgdwKU-y948oMzHGFOP_Ox3vMW1Ymki-zmY4bSHWFP-m4zwD42-Huw3q9eM8VAY9_mL9yzihdsF1YygoUH-dDrY8EzKJb4dslf03xMaGFlYgAy0bA6p7gZ5vr5GHHb\/s728-e300\/team-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/team-d)\n# [Czech Republic Blames China-Linked APT31 Hackers for 2022 Cyberattack](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/czech-republic-blames-china-linked.html)\n_\ue802_ May 28, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCybersecurity \/ Cyber Espionage\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgs41mPz2y4BT36h4b7mTGCL3J7Yl3tyJjSCJkkh8mZtM0-6VQ9sJffhn-t76qjzcms_qw3lEoYCxaTbK81K6i_NH2dUUC7xyhklHsotPh8uM8qVd_zVZ88m37wQ_5Bq_oZQzYo6mO87A7Jjxt4lu2pUQsIrcp-DyFfJ5CxCT5YLRpV0TEh9x2dPlV8hz5H\/s728-rw-e365\/flag.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgs41mPz2y4BT36h4b7mTGCL3J7Yl3tyJjSCJkkh8mZtM0-6VQ9sJffhn-t76qjzcms_qw3lEoYCxaTbK81K6i_NH2dUUC7xyhklHsotPh8uM8qVd_zVZ88m37wQ_5Bq_oZQzYo6mO87A7Jjxt4lu2pUQsIrcp-DyFfJ5CxCT5YLRpV0TEh9x2dPlV8hz5H\/s728-rw-e365\/flag.jpg)\nThe Czech Republic on Wednesday formally accused a threat actor associated with the People's Republic of China (PRC) of targeting its Ministry of Foreign Affairs.\nIn a public statement, the government said it identified China as the culprit behind a malicious campaign targeting one of the unclassified networks of the Czech Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The extent of the breach is presently not known.\n\"The malicious activity [...] lasted from 2022 and affected an institution designated as Czech critical infrastructure,\" it [added](https:\/\/mzv.gov.cz\/jnp\/en\/issues_and_press\/press_releases\/statement_by_the_government_of_the_czech.html).\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEh6woLgqW8rZb7ncvV18oChEHw4feIrW6Uumk8HftuHVt_7SkSlHrRy9JRF2yo1RKxpD4umcPscEb2Y82vvLqai-VLjWpMx2jePfQteMWAe8Pn7fo2mdDP1mdJxESSOVDOS2XN5xlB0MuY8mirpygSNg0Jw3jbLXFQaWj7EKHwF_iOoNAGb9FIAAtv-UnVL\/s728-e100\/drata-d-3.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/drata-d-3 \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe attack has been attributed to a state-sponsored threat actor tracked as [APT31](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/08\/chinas-apt31-suspected-in-attacks-on.html), which also overlaps with threat clusters known as Altaire, Bronze Vinewood, Judgement Panda, PerplexedGoblin, RedBravo, Red Keres, and Violet Typhoon (formerly Zirconium).\nThe hacking group, publicly associated with the Ministry of State Security (MSS) and the Hubei State Security Department, is assessed to be active since at least 2010, per the U.S. Department of Justice (DoJ).\nBronze Vinewood is known to employ a variety of tools and techniques to gain access to target environments, while also relying on public code or file-sharing websites for its command and control (C2) domains to complicate network-based detection and intersperse C2 traffic amid legitimate web browsing activity.\nAccording to Sophos-owned Secureworks, the adversarial crew has a [particular focus](https:\/\/www.secureworks.com\/research\/threat-profiles\/bronze-vinewood) on organizations operating in government or defense supply chains, or providing services to those organizations.\nIn March 2024, the DoJ [indicted](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/03\/us-charges-7-chinese-nationals-in-major.html) seven hackers associated with APT31, accusing them of engaging in sweeping cyber espionage attacks aimed at U.S. and foreign critics, journalists, businesses, and political officials to advance MSS's foreign intelligence and economic espionage objectives.\nAround the same time, the Police of Finland [called out](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/03\/finland-blames-chinese-hacking-group.html) the threat actor for orchestrating a cyber attack targeting the country's Parliament in 2020.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/czech-republic-blames-china-linked.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nAs recently as this month, ESET [revealed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/chinese-hackers-deploy-marssnake.html) in its latest APT Activity Report that APT31 targeted a Central European government entity in December 2024 to deploy an espionage backdoor referred to as NanoSlate. While Czechia is a Central European nation, it's currently not clear if these attacks are related.\n[Strongly condemning](https:\/\/www.consilium.europa.eu\/en\/press\/press-releases\/2025\/05\/28\/cyber-statement-by-the-high-representative-on-behalf-of-the-european-union-on-malicious-behaviour-in-cyberspace-against-czechia\/) the malicious cyber campaign, the Government of the Czech Republic said \"such behavior undermines the credibility of the People's Republic of China and contradicts its public declarations.\"\nThe government further said the activities are in violation of responsible State behavior in cyberspace as endorsed by members of the United Nations. It called on China to adhere to these norms and refrain from staging such attacks in the future.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fczech-republic-blames-china-linked.html&t=Czech%20Republic%20Blames%20China-Linked%20APT31%20Hackers%20for%202022%20Cyberattack) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Czech%20Republic%20Blames%20China-Linked%20APT31%20Hackers%20for%202022%20Cyberattack \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fczech-republic-blames-china-linked.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/czech-republic-blames-china-linked.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fczech-republic-blames-china-linked.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fczech-republic-blames-china-linked.html&text=Czech%20Republic%20Blames%20China-Linked%20APT31%20Hackers%20for%202022%20Cyberattack)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[APT31](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/APT31)[Chinese Hackers](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Chinese%20Hackers)[critical infrastructure](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/critical%20infrastructure)[cyber espionage](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cyber%20espionage)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Czech Republic](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Czech%20Republic)[data breach](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/data%20breach)[network intrusion](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/network%20intrusion)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEipPJ-RDZPiSFyQaYgFV8WRuTbSKO9e6Y3LNezLfUhw-rhnR7wErUeM2AwrIEqjZKKDoZALBbfScKxiGBBXEqYul9nWZBKtfh11hbOq_3ZYS8GnFovgJ-OlOdvdDzYqX0AJwe_VYp3h5-uS_C7ycVtZTj_Xa3rwqaYuBDx4uiHlBjiR6tn4hKHycoenWb8j\/s728-rw-e365\/wiz-side-1.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-side-1)\n[![c](https:\/