"title": "APT41 malware abuses Google Calendar for stealthy C2 communication",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/apt41-malware-abuses-google-calendar-for-stealthy-c2-communication\/",,
"summary": "APT41, a Chinese hacking group, uses a new malware named ToughProgress to exploit Google Calendar for stealthy command-and-control (C2) operations. This campaign was identified by Google's Threat Intelligence Group. The attack begins with a malicious email leading to a ZIP archive, containing several files that mask their true purpose, which together facilitate the installation of the malware. APT41 adds commands in hidden Google Calendar events, which the malware reads to execute further actions stealthily.",,
