"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/devsecops-playbook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-devsecops?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q4_INB_FORM_DevSecOps-Getting-Started-Playbook&sfcid=701Py00000HwiF6IAJ&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=DevSecOpsPlaybook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft: Windows 11 might fail to start after installing KB5058405\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft: Windows 11 might fail to start after installing KB5058405\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 29, 2025\n  * 05:59 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/10\/02\/Windows_11_headpic.jpg)\nMicrosoft has confirmed that some Windows 11 systems might fail to start after installing the KB5058405 cumulative update released during this month's Patch Tuesday.\nOn affected devices, users see 0xc0000098 recovery errors in ACPI.sys, warning that the device has to be repaired because the operating system couldn't be loaded.\nACPI.sys is the Windows Advanced Configuration and Power Interface (ACPI) driver, a kernel-mode driver critical for power management and device configuration on Windows with an ACPI BIOS.\n\"We are investigating reports of the May 13, 2025 Windows security update (KB5058405) failing to install on some Windows 11, version 22H2 and 23H2 devices,\" the company [said](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/status-windows-11-23H2#kb5058405-might-fail-to-install-with-recovery-error-0xc0000098-in-acpi-sys) in a Wednesday update to the Windows release health dashboard.\n\"Your PC\/Device needs to be repaired. The operating system couldn't be loaded because a required file is missing or contains errors,\" the error warns.\nThis known issue impacts Windows 11 22H2\/23H2 systems in enterprise environments and mainly affects Azure Virtual Machines, Azure Virtual Desktop, and on-premises virtual machines hosted on Citrix or Hyper-V.\n![Recovery screen with 0xc0000098 ACPI.sys error](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2025\/0xc0000098_error_screen.jpg)_Recovery screen with 0xc0000098 ACPI.sys error ()_\n\u200bMicrosoft added that home users of Windows Home or Pro editions are unlikely to face these problems because the impacted virtual machines are mostly used in IT environments.\nRedmond is investigating this issue and said its engineers will provide more information when it's available.\nEarlier this month, the company fixed another known issue [blocking Windows 11 24H2 feature updates](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-24h2-updates-fail-with-0x80240069-errors\/) via Windows Server Update Services (WSUS) after installing the April 2025 security updates.\nPreviously, it shipped emergency out-of-band updates to [mitigate a Windows 10 bug](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/) that forced affected PCs into BitLocker recovery after installing the May 2025 security updates.\nIn April, Microsoft also addressed what it described as a \"latent code issue\" [causing some devices to be upgraded to Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-some-devices-offered-windows-11-upgrades-despite-intune-blocks\/) automatically despite Intune policies that should block Windows 11 upgrades.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Windows Server emergency update fixes Hyper-V VM freezes, restart issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-server-emergency-update-fixes-hyper-v-vm-freezes-restart-issues\/)\n[Microsoft adds hotpatching support to Windows 11 Enterprise](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-adds-hotpatching-support-to-windows-11-enterprise\/)\n[Microsoft fixes Linux boot issues on dual-boot Windows systems](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-linux-boot-issues-on-dual-boot-windows-systems\/)\n[Microsoft May 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes 5 exploited zero-days, 72 flaws](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-may-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-5-exploited-zero-days-72-flaws\/)\n[Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/)\n  * [0xc0000098](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/0xc0000098\/)\n  * [ACPI.sys](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/acpisys\/)\n  * [Azure](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/azure\/)\n  * [Boot Issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/boot-issues\/)\n  * [KB5058405](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kb5058405\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Security Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/security-update\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-update\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/data-broker-lexisnexis-discloses-data-breach-affecting-364-000-people\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/delivery-chains.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/advancements-in-delivery-scripting-with-nietzsche\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trun-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/) Microsoft wants Windows to update all software on your PC ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-wants-windows-to-update-all-software-on-your-pc\/)\n  * [ ![ASUS](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/) Botnet hacks 9,000+ ASUS routers to add persistent SSH backdoor ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/botnet-hacks-9-000-plus-asus-routers-to-add-persistent-ssh-backdoor\/)\n  * [ ![MathWorks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomput