"title": "Fake Bitdefender website used to spread infostealer malware",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/fake-bitdefender-website-venomrat-infostealer",,
"summary": "Cybercriminals are exploiting a fake Bitdefender antivirus website to spread the VenomRAT malware. This malicious campaign aims to steal financial credentials by mimicking Bitdefender\u2019s Windows download page. Victims are duped into downloading a seemingly legitimate application, which is actually a malware archive containing VenomRAT, SilentTrinity, and StormKitty. These tools enable remote access, keylogging, and data exfiltration. Bitdefender and DomainTools identified the threat, with Bitdefender products flagging the malware and URL as harmful. The fake website mimicked other trusted entities to widen its phishing reach. Bitdefender was aware of the campaign since early May and, in collaboration with Cloudflare and other partners, is working to remove the site. Tracking VenomRAT\u2019s use in criminal forums complicates attribution to specific groups.",,
