"title": "China-linked hackers exploit Google Calendar in cyberattacks on governments",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-linked-apt41-exploits-google-calendar-in-cyberattacks",,
"summary": "A China-based hacking group known as APT41, also referred to as Brass Typhoon, Wicked Panda, and RedGolf, has been exploiting Google Calendar in a cyber-espionage campaign targeting government entities. The campaign was attributed to APT41 by Google researchers and involved spearphishing emails directing victims to a malicious ZIP archive on a hijacked government website. Once the victim opens the archive, it deploys malware named ToughProgress, which uses Google Calendar for command-and-control operations, making detection challenging. The malware executes encrypted commands embedded in Google Calendar events and uploads stolen data back to the service. APT41 has a history of targeting various sectors like logistics, media, automobiles, and technology, and has been involved in notable intrusions, including those affecting Southeast Asian government agencies.",,
