"markdown": "![victoria's secret](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_victorias_secret_9212228a38.jpg)\nImage: Unsplash\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 29th, 2025\n# Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incident\nWomen\u2019s fashion brand Victoria\u2019s Secret said it is working to restore operations after experiencing a security incident. \nThe company did not respond to requests for comment but the victoriassecret.com domain now features a brief message to customers explaining that it has \u201cidentified and are taking steps to address a security incident.\u201d \n\u201cWe immediately enacted our response protocols, third-party experts are engaged, and we took down our website and some in store services as a precaution,\u201d the company said. \n\u201cWe are working to quickly and securely restore operations. We continue to serve customers in our Victoria\u2019s Secret and PINK stores.\u201d \n![secret.jpg](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/secret_45c0a86e66.jpg)\nCybersecurity experts the website has displayed the banner for at least three days. On its corporate website, the company published a similar message, noting that it is \u201cworking around the clock to fully restore operations.\u201d \nVictoria\u2019s Secret is a retailer of bras, panties, lingerie, apparel and more, with 1,380 retail stores across 70 countries and about 30,000 employees. The company [reported](https:\/\/www.victoriassecretandco.com\/news-releases\/news-release-details\/victorias-secret-co-reports-fourth-quarter-2024-results) net sales of $6.2 billion in 2024. \nVictoria\u2019s Secret is just the latest fashion brand to announce a cyberattack in the last month after multiple high-profile incidents. [Adidas](https:\/\/www.adidas-group.com\/en\/data-security-information), [Dior, and Tiffany](https:\/\/www.chosun.com\/english\/industry-en\/2025\/05\/26\/ORM5MULB7NEM7EBUFVXHVLSB4A\/) all announced data breaches or security incidents that exposed customer and employee data. \nThe incidents [prompted the FBI](https:\/\/www.cnn.com\/2025\/05\/16\/politics\/cybercriminal-group-targets-us-retailers) to deliver cyber-intelligence briefings to major retailers over the last month after reports that a well-known group of hackers called [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-challenge-for-FBI) had [shifted their focus](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert) from attacks on outlets in the U.K. to U.S.-based companies. \nThe notices came after multiple attacks on U.K. retailers [Marks & Spencer](https:\/\/therecord.media\/british-retailer-marks-spencer-insurance), the [Co-op](https:\/\/therecord.media\/co-op-cyberattack-uk-company-fears-hackers-still-in-system), and luxury retailer [Harrods](https:\/\/therecord.media\/harrods-cyberattack-uk-retailer). The group behind these attacks is reported to have attempted to monetize its access to the victims\u2019 networks using the DragonForce ransomware. \n\"The U.S. retail sector is currently being targeted in ransomware and extortion operations that we suspect are linked to UNC3944, also known as Scattered Spider,\u201d said John Hultquist, chief analyst at Google Threat Intelligence Group. \n\u201cThe actor, which has reportedly targeted retail in the U.K. following a long hiatus, has a history of focusing their efforts on a single sector at a time, and we anticipate they will continue to target the sector in the near term. U.S. retailers should take note.\u201d \nHultquist added that the group is \u201caggressive, creative, and particularly effective at circumventing mature security programs.\u201d \nThe group, which previously gained notoriety for its ransomware attacks on casino giants [MGM Resorts](https:\/\/therecord.media\/mgm-cyberattack-response) and [Caesars Entertainment](https:\/\/finance.yahoo.com\/news\/caesars-entertainment-paid-millions-ransom-185252473.html), has had significant success with social engineering and leveraging third parties to gain entry to their targets, Hultquist explained. \nCybersecurity experts believe Scattered Spider is an offshoot of a larger criminal organization calling itself \u201cthe Community,\u201d or \u201cthe Com,\u201d that claimed several major attacks on companies like [Coinbase](https:\/\/therecord.media\/coinbase-explains-how-0ktapus-hacker-accessed-corporate-directory), [Riot Games](https:\/\/therecord.media\/riot-games-to-pause-updates-after-social-engineering-attack) and [Reddit](https:\/\/therecord.media\/reddit-suffers-sophisticated-and-highly-targeted-phishing-attack-exposing-source-code). \nThere were multiple arrests of alleged members in the [U.S.](https:\/\/therecord.media\/five-scattered-spider-members-charged-breaches-11-million-theft), [U.K.](https:\/\/therecord.media\/mgm-hack-teenager-arrest-britain) and [Europe](https:\/\/therecord.media\/suspected-scattered-spider-cybercriminal-arrested-spain) over the last three years. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incident)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incident )\n\n\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [retail](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/retail)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incidentMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/victorias-secret-website-down-security-incident)\n  * [China-linked hackers exploit Google Calendar in cyberattacks on governmentsMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-linked-apt41-exploits-google-calendar-in-cyberattacks)\n  * [More than $12 million stolen from crypto platform Cork ProtocolMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cork-protocol-defi-12million-crypto-theft)\n  * [Estonia issues arrest warrant for Moroccan wanted for major pharmacy data breachMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/estonia-arrest-warrant-pharmacy-data-breach)\n  * [Ukraine detains alleged Russian spies who used dash cams to guide missile strikesMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukraine-detains-russian-spies-using-dashcams-missile-strikes)\n  * [Russian hospital programmer gets 14 years for leaking soldier data to UkraineMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-programmer-gets-14-years-for-leaking-info-to-ukraine)\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
