"markdown": "![phone](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_moshed_05_29_12_31_48_ceff8b473b.png)\nImage: Getty via Unsplash+\/Photomosh\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)May 29th, 2025\n# Southeast Asian provider of \u2018infrastructure laundering\u2019 for scams is sanctioned by US\nA Philippines-based web infrastructure provider is linked to the \u201cmajority of virtual currency investment scam websites reported to the FBI,\u201d the U.S. government said in imposing sanctions against the company on Thursday. \nFunnull Technology Inc. supports \u201chundreds of thousands of websites\u201d dedicated to the scams, otherwise known as pig butchering, according to the sanctions [announcement](https:\/\/home.treasury.gov\/news\/press-releases\/sb0149) by the Treasury Department\u2019s Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC). \nU.S.-based victims of websites connected to Funnull \u201chave reported over $200 million in losses, with average losses of over $150,000 per individual,\u201d OFAC said. \u201cThese figures likely underestimate the total losses, as many victims of scams do not report the crime.\u201d \nThe FBI also released a [technical advisory](https:\/\/www.ic3.gov\/CSA\/2025\/250529.pdf) with a long list of internet domains linked to Funnull, which cybersecurity researchers have labeled as a provider of \u201cinfrastructure laundering.\u201d \nThe company facilitates fraud \u201cby purchasing IP addresses and providing hosting services and other internet infrastructure to groups performing these frauds,\u201d the FBI said. \u201cFunnull acquires these facilities from legitimate providers in the United States and sells them to cyber criminals.\u201d \nInvestment fraud helps to fuel the Southeast Asian cybercrime ecosystem \u2014 a nexus of transnational organized crime, [shadowy companies](https:\/\/therecord.media\/us-fincen-cut-off-huione-group-southeast-asia-cyber-scam), [gambling operations](https:\/\/therecord.media\/southeast-asia-casino-industry-scams-money-laundering-un-report), [local militias](https:\/\/therecord.media\/myanmar-militia-leader-us-sanctions-cyber-scam-industry) and [scam compounds](https:\/\/therecord.media\/thousands-rescued-from-cyber-scam-compounds-stuck-at-thai-border). Victims often interact directly with a fraudster who pushes them to hand over cryptocurrency to fuel a fake romance or financial opportunity. \nThe illicit industry is continuing to expand worldwide, a United Nations report [warned last month](https:\/\/therecord.media\/southeast-asia-cyber-fraud-at-inflection-point). \nThe U.S. also sanctioned Liu Lizhi, a Chinese national that OFAC labeled as an \u201cadministrator\u201d of Funnull. \n\u201cLiu was involved in and possessed spreadsheets and other documents containing information about Funnull\u2019s employees, their performance, and their progress on tasks,\u201d OFAC said. \u201cThese tasks included assigning domain names to cybercriminals, including domains associated with virtual currency investment fraud, phishing scams, and online gambling sites.\u201d \nOFAC cites Liu as having an address in Ganzhou, China. Funnull\u2019s headquarters is [listed at an address in the Manila area](https:\/\/ofac.treasury.gov\/recent-actions\/20250529). Previous reports about the company had suggested it was based in China. \nEarlier this year, [researchers at cybersecurity company Silent Push](https:\/\/www.silentpush.com\/blog\/infrastructure-laundering\/) analyzed the company\u2019s illicit tactics for renting IP addresses from U.S. providers such as Amazon and Microsoft, which were said to be fighting an \u201cuphill battle\u201d against the operation. \nFunnull\u2019s name also surfaced last year after the company [acquired the web domain for polyfill](https:\/\/therecord.media\/polyfill-cloudflare-trade-barbs-supply-chain-attack), a service known for helping websites bridge compatibility gaps between modern code and older browsers. Afterward researchers found the site injecting malware onto the devices of visitors. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Southeast Asian provider of \u2018infrastructure laundering\u2019 for scams is sanctioned by US)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Southeast Asian provider of \u2018infrastructure laundering\u2019 for scams is sanctioned by US )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/technology)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Southeast Asia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/southeast-asia)\n  * [Phillipines](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/phillipines)\n  * [email scam](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/email-scam)\n  * [romance scams](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/romance-scams)\n  * [Scams](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scams)\n  * [pig butchering](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/pig-butchering)\n  * [OFAC](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/ofac)\n  * [Treasury Department](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/treasury-department)\n  * [sanctions](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/sanctions)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/warminsky2024_c08fb80bd8.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\n[Joe Warminsky](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/joe-warminsky)\nis the news editor for Recorded Future News. He has more than 25 years experience as an editor and writer in the Washington, D.C., area. He previously he helped lead CyberScoop for more than five years. Prior to that, he was a digital editor at WAMU 88.5, the NPR affiliate in Washington, and he spent more than a decade editing coverage of Congress for CQ Roll Call. \n[](https:\/\/bsky.app\/profile\/jwarminsky.bsky.social)\n## Briefs\n  * [Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incidentMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/victorias-secret-website-down-security-incident)\n  * [China-linked hackers exploit Google Calendar in cyberattacks on governmentsMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-linked-apt41-exploits-google-calendar-in-cyberattacks)\n  * [More than $12 million stolen from crypto platform Cork ProtocolMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cork-protocol-defi-12million-crypto-theft)\n  * [Estonia issues arrest warrant for Moroccan wanted for major pharmacy data breachMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/estonia-arrest-warrant-pharmacy-data-breach)\n  * [Ukraine detains alleged Russian spies who used dash cams to guide missile strikesMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukraine-detains-russian-spies-using-dashcams-missile-strikes)\n  * [Russian hospital programmer gets 14 years for leaking soldier data to UkraineMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-programmer-gets-14-years-for-leaking-info-to-ukraine)\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n  * [China accuses Taiwan-linked group of cyberattack on local tech companyMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-accuses-taiwan-linked-group-of-cyberattacks)\n  * [Apple says it blocked $2 billion in App Store fraud last yearMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/apple-billions-app-store-fraud)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
