"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/ai-security-risk-ebook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-ai-security-ai-risks-how-to-prevent-them-and-ai-for-defender?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q3_INB_FORM_Getting-Started-with-AI-Security-AI-Risks-How-to-Prevent-Them&sfcid=701Py00000DP3ZaIAL&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AISecurityeBook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Software](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/)\n  * Mozilla releases Firefox 139.0.1 update to fix artifacts on Nvidia GPUs\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/)\n\n\n# Mozilla releases Firefox 139.0.1 update to fix artifacts on Nvidia GPUs\nBy \n###### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n  * May 29, 2025\n  * 07:58 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Firefox](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/05\/29\/firefox-header.jpg)\nMozilla has rolled out an emergency Firefox 139.0.1 update after the Tuesday release caused graphical artifacts on PCs with NVIDIA GPUs.\nFirefox 139 shipped on May 27 with features like Full-Page Translations, but it also caused graphical artifacts when browsing the web in Firefox.\nIn a , several Firefox users complained that videos would flicker or flash. This issue also affects webpages, including sites like Instagram.\nMozilla has quickly identified the root cause and has shipped a hotfix with v139.0.1.\nIn a [post on Bugzilla](https:\/\/bugzilla.mozilla.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=1968876), Mozilla confirmed that Firefox 139 re-enabled a specific DirectComposition path behavior, which caused these issues.\nIn previous releases, Firefox kept a block list that stopped Firefox from using DirectComposition on mixed-refresh NVIDIA setup.\nUnfortunately, the block list was removed with Firefox 139, and it allowed the browser to use DirectComposition in a way that exposed a graphics driver bug on NVIDIA cards under Windows 10.\nWhen you play a 60 FPS video on the 60 Hz monitor and then scroll or hover over the content on the high-refresh monitor, parts of the video buffer leak into the other window.\nThat shows up as flashing artifacts or corruption wherever the page repaints. The issue doesn't happen with 30 FPS content because the frame timing lines up with both refresh rates.\nSingle-monitor or AMD\/Intel setups weren't affected by these issues.\nIt is also worth noting that DirectComposition isn't the problem, but Mozilla's implementation clashes with certain GPUs.\n\"Currently the only thing that makes Firefox special in this respect is that it uses Windows DirectComposition in a certain way (Surfaces rather than Swapchains) for the majority of web content...\" a Firefox developer noted in a [post on Bugzilla](http:\/\/bugzilla.mozilla.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=1968876).\n\"We have a new code path (the Layer Compositor as it is called) which should become available for testing in Firefox Nightly in the coming weeks if all goes well, we will have an interest in testing that on the same computers when it is ready, to verify if any of this flickering occurs with that approach which is much more similar to other browsers.\"\n## Mozilla fixed artifacts in Firefox 139\nAs per the [release notes](https:\/\/www.mozilla.org\/en-US\/firefox\/139.0\/releasenotes\/), a new update (139.0.1) is now rolling out, and it restores the blocklist, which means you should no longer run into artifacts.\n\"Fixed graphics corruption with certain NVIDIA graphics adapters and multiple monitors running at mixed refresh rates after updating to Firefox 139,\" Mozilla noted on the release notes page.\nTo install Firefox 139.0.1, open Settings and check for updates.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft introduces new Windows backup tool for businesses](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-introduces-new-windows-backup-tool-for-businesses\/)\n[Windows 10 emergency updates fix BitLocker recovery issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-emergency-updates-fix-bitlocker-recovery-issues\/)\n[Mozilla fixes Firefox zero-days exploited at hacking contest](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/mozilla-fixes-firefox-zero-days-exploited-at-hacking-contest\/)\n[Microsoft confirms May Windows 10 updates trigger BitLocker recovery](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-confirms-may-windows-10-updates-trigger-bitlocker-recovery\/)\n[Hackers exploit VMware ESXi, Microsoft SharePoint zero-days at Pwn2Own](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-exploit-vmware-esxi-microsoft-sharepoint-zero-days-at-pwn2own\/)\n  * [Firefox](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/firefox\/)\n  * [Mozilla](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/mozilla\/)\n  * [NVIDIA](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/nvidia\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 10](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-10\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\n##### [Mayank Parmar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/mayank-parmar\/)\nMayank Parmar is an technology entrepreneur who is currently pursuing an MBA. At BleepingComputer, he covers technology news with a strong focus on Microsoft and Windows-related stories. He is always poking under the hood of Windows, looking for the latest secrets to reveal. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-authenticator-now-warns-to-export-passwords-before-july-cutoff\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/skuld-stealer.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/tmpn-skuld-stealer-the-dark-side-of-open-source\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trus-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) Microsoft wants Windows to update all software on your PC ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-wants-windows-to-update-all-software-on-your-pc\/)\n  * [ ![ASUS](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) Botnet hacks 9,000+ ASUS routers to add persistent SSH backdoor ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/botnet-hacks-9-000-plus-asus-routers-to-add-persistent-ssh-backdoor\/)\n  * [ ![MathWorks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) MATLAB dev confirms ransomware attack behind service outage ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/mathworks-blames-ransomware-attack-for-ongoing-outages\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Tired of Patch Tuesday Surprises? Automate it All with ThreatLocker Today](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) Tired of Patch Tuesday Surprises? Automate it All with ThreatLocker Today ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/pages\/threatlocker-platform-patch-management?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=patch_management_q2_25&utm_content=patch_management&utm_term=display)\n  * [ ![Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers?](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) Do You Know Which AI Tools Are Running in Your Users\u2019 Browsers? ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/demo\/generative-ai-monitoring?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=article&utm_campaign=validated_phishing_may)\n  * [ ![What exploits are lurking in your attack surface? Find out at no cost with Sprocket ASM](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) What exploits are lurking in your attack surface? Find out at no cost with Sprocket ASM ](https:\/\/www.sprocketsecurity.com\/solutions\/attack-surface-management?utm_campaign=Attack%20Surface%20Management%20Launch%203%2F24&utm_source=Bleeping%20Computer)\n  * [ ![CVSS 9.8? It might be harmless. Find out what's truly risky.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/) CVSS 9.8? It might be harmless. Find out what's truly risky. ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q03nKGps0)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/software\/mozilla-releases-firefox-13901-update-to-fix-artifacts-on-nvidia-gpus\/ \"Submit\")\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.8485609372550098)![](https:\/\/sync.intentiq.com\/profiles_engine\/ProfilesEngineServlet?at=20&mi=10&secure=1&dpi=456059511&iiqidtype=2&iiqpcid=a526861c-3315-4d2b-aa9e-2b145d556acd&iiqpciddate=1748566811927&tsrnd=863_1748566811927&vrref=&jsver=5.082)\n",,
