"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/connectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Zenith Live 2025](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEi4bDwl8OzN93dfWqW26S8nXvZrUacPG5o9-Aaz8NqskX3Wl7MbCeWyQ-AhG-fE4bZu4EKf1EFEYeFNDspe76IE2wglgB5_izZ9dQ9FV4qcwZgTldXXcL7TriQaXoqMwekq_seWN4k87GV6G8bG2bfV04U8ikHa5PLOdqb_6DsjJj3xHIC1gaweDsRfe7lu\/s728-e300\/Zenith-d.jpg)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/zenithlive-ams25-d)\n# [ConnectWise Hit by Cyberattack; Nation-State Actor Suspected in Targeted Breach](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/connectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html)\n_\ue802_ May 30, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Data Breach\n[![ConnectWise Investigates ScreenConnect Breach](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgzdBsek7uschAYcoDTA3uS5w5hma3iTiRlOpZfwkGKJtrnpKgbDLTKrIsLkjPZmzKVTzasHKDNLCjghH-iIRmSduke_xS3H41AjxUc3APmO_xJh_Zni2lpoPCLV4O__Ljuq9pnqkpXtoOiPGELckuBsAeyg7-nCrLPC9RskriaRyVosSJQiSenWepzv8Dv\/s728-rw-e365\/screen.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgzdBsek7uschAYcoDTA3uS5w5hma3iTiRlOpZfwkGKJtrnpKgbDLTKrIsLkjPZmzKVTzasHKDNLCjghH-iIRmSduke_xS3H41AjxUc3APmO_xJh_Zni2lpoPCLV4O__Ljuq9pnqkpXtoOiPGELckuBsAeyg7-nCrLPC9RskriaRyVosSJQiSenWepzv8Dv\/s728-rw-e365\/screen.jpg)\nConnectWise, the developer of remote access and support software ScreenConnect, has disclosed that it was the victim of a cyber attack that it said was likely perpetrated by a nation-state threat actor.\n\"ConnectWise recently learned of suspicious activity within our environment that we believe was tied to a sophisticated nation-state actor, which affected a very small number of ScreenConnect customers,\" the company [said](https:\/\/www.connectwise.com\/company\/trust\/advisories) in a brief advisory on May 28, 2025.\nThe company said it has engaged the services of Google Mandiant to conduct a forensic probe into the incident and that it has notified all affected customers. The incident was first reported by CRN.\nHowever, it did not reveal the exact number of customers who were impacted by the hack, when it happened, or the identity of the threat actor behind it.\nIt's worth noting that the company, in late April 2025, patched [CVE-2025-3935](https:\/\/www.connectwise.com\/company\/trust\/security-bulletins\/screenconnect-security-patch-2025.4) (CVSS score: 8.1), a high-severity vulnerability in ScreenConnect versions 25.2.3 and earlier that could be exploited for ViewState code injection attacks using publicly disclosed ASP.NET machine keys \u2013 a technique Microsoft [disclosed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/02\/microsoft-identifies-3000-publicly.html) earlier this February.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/connectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/tines-incident-response-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe issue was addressed in ScreenConnect version 25.2.4. That said, it's currently not known if the cyber attack is linked to the exploitation of the vulnerability.\nConnectWise said it has implemented enhanced monitoring and hardening measures across its environment to prevent such attacks from happening again in the future.\n\"We have not observed any further suspicious activity in any customer instances,\" it added, stating it's closely monitoring the situation.\nIn early 2024, [security flaws](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/02\/critical-flaws-found-in-connectwise.html) in ConnectWise ScreenConnect software (CVE-2024-1708 and CVE-2024-1709) were exploited by both cybercrime and nation-state threat actors, including those from [China](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/03\/china-linked-group-breaches-networks.html), [North Korea](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/03\/hackers-exploit-connectwise.html), and [Russia](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/02\/microsoft-uncovers-sandworm-subgroups.html), to deliver a variety of malicious payloads.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fconnectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html&t=ConnectWise%20Hit%20by%20Cyberattack%3B%20Nation-State%20Actor%20Suspected%20in%20Targeted%20Breach) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=ConnectWise%20Hit%20by%20Cyberattack%3B%20Nation-State%20Actor%20Suspected%20in%20Targeted%20Breach \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fconnectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/connectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fconnectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F05%2Fconnectwise-hit-by-cyberattack-nation.html&text=ConnectWise%20Hit%20by%20Cyberattack%3B%20Nation-State%20Actor%20Suspected%20in%20Targeted%20Breach)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[ConnectWise](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/ConnectWise)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[data breach](https:\/\/thehackernews.