"summary": "The U.S. Department of Treasury's Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC) has sanctioned Funnull Technology Inc., a Philippines-based company, and its administrator Liu Lizhi. Funnull was providing infrastructure for romance baiting scams tied to cryptocurrency fraud, leading to over $200 million in U.S. victim-reported losses. The company facilitated virtual currency investment scams by acquiring IP addresses from major cloud providers and selling them to cybercriminals. These infrastructures were used to promote scams, gambling sites, and redirect legitimate traffic to fraudulent sites using Domain Generation Algorithms (DGA). The FBI identified significant activities associated with Funnull domains, including infrastructure laundering. Victims have primarily been found in the U.S., Singapore, and other South-east Asian nations.",,
