"title": "Exploits and vulnerabilities in Q1 2025",,
"url": "https:\/\/securelist.com\/vulnerabilities-and-exploits-in-q1-2025\/116624\/",,
"summary": "The report focuses on vulnerabilities, exploits, and malware threats in Q1 2025, detailing specifics such as the ZDI-CAN-25373 vulnerability in Windows LNK files, the CVE-2025-21333 heap buffer overflow issue in the vkrnlintvsp.sys driver, and the CVE-2025-24071 NetNTLM hash leakage vulnerability in the file system indexer. These vulnerabilities have been actively exploited in the wild, with some affecting sectors in ASEAN countries, including Singapore. In the first quarter of 2025, significant vulnerabilities were reported across multiple platforms, with a focus on Windows and Linux. Common vulnerabilities include CVE-2025-21333 and CVE-2025-24071. Active exploitation was observed in both operating systems with older known vulnerabilities still being targeted. Notable vulnerabilities include manipulation of LNK files in Windows and several identified in the Linux kernel, such as Dirty Pipe. Microsoft Office products remain widely targeted. The threat landscape emphasizes the need for prompt updates and includes trends of attacks using exploits in cloud and local apps alike.",,
