"title": "New EDDIESTEALER Malware Bypasses Chrome's App-Bound Encryption to Steal Browser Data",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/eddiestealer-malware-uses-clickfix.html",,
"summary": "EDDIESTEALER is a new malware campaign leveraging ClickFix CAPTCHA social engineering to deploy a Rust-based information stealer. Compromised legitimate websites have malicious JavaScript that masquerades as CAPTCHAs to trick users into executing a PowerShell script, deploying the infostealer. This malware harvests system information, accesses browser data, and extracts credentials, particularly from Chromium browsers by bypassing app-bound encryption. The malware also adapts to avoid detection in sandbox environments and uses encrypted communications to a command-and-control server.",,
