"summary": "The German Federal Criminal Police (BKA) identified Vitaly Nikolaevich Kovalev, a Russian national, as the leader of the infamous TrickBot and Conti ransomware gangs. Known by aliases such as 'Stern', Kovalev was implicated in several ransomware operations, including Ryuk, and is subject to an Interpol Red Notice. The Trickbot group, linked to several malware strains, has been involved in infecting systems worldwide, affecting various sectors and amassing significant illegal gains. The group has been linked to activities that exposed their internal communications and structure, leading to the eventual shutdown of Conti operations.",,
