"summary": "Several Senate Democrats are urging the Trump administration to reinstate the Cyber Safety Review Board (CSRB), which was disbanded during an ongoing investigation into the Salt Typhoon hacks. These hacks, attributed to Chinese-linked attackers, breached at least nine U.S. telecommunications companies. The senators argue that the CSRB's dismissal hampers the public's understanding of the incident and the ability to prevent future compromises. The CSRB was responsible for reviewing significant cybersecurity incidents, including the Salt Typhoon, which remains a concern as it is linked to Chinese espionage efforts.",,
