"markdown": "![senate](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_harold_mendoza_6xaf_Y_AE_1_LM_unsplash_0e22d607b0.jpg)\nImage: Harold Mendoza via Unsplash\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)May 30th, 2025\n# Senators call on Trump admin to reinstate cyber review board for Salt Typhoon investigation\nSeveral Senate Democrats [penned](https:\/\/www.warner.senate.gov\/public\/_cache\/files\/b\/b\/bbf743ed-a62b-4ddd-acbd-9efbb1b57e59\/8F69B96E6BE00A94BA8DBDD3B9443CF17A885D52A40748B7A5000FDFFD217870.quill---letter-l27283---250521.warner-noem-csrb-reappointment---version-3---05-29-2025-02-29-pm.pdf) a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem on Thursday asking her to reestablish the Cyber Safety Review Board (CSRB) after the Trump administration dismissed its members earlier this year. \nWhen the CSRB was disbanded, it was in the middle of an investigation into the [Salt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/nine-us-companies-hacked-salt-typhoon-china-espionage) hacks involving Chinese-linked attackers penetrating the networks of at least nine major U.S. telecommunications companies. \nThe senators \u2014 Mark Warner (D-VA), Ron Wyden (D-OR), Richard Blumenthal (D-CT) and Elissa Slotkin (D-MI) \u2014 said the board\u2019s dismissal is \u201cdepriving the public of a fuller accounting of the origin, scope, scale, and severity of\u201d the Salt Typhoon compromises. \n\u201cIt is essential that the U.S. develop a complete and thorough understanding of the factors that contributed to the success of these intrusions \u2013 including clear root-cause analyses of each successful penetration \u2013 and present key recommendations for the telecommunications sector to better protect itself against similarly complex and large-scale compromises by future threat actors,\u201d the senators said. \nThe CSRB, loosely modeled after the National Transportation Safety Board, was created in 2021 and convened cybersecurity experts alongside senior government officials for investigations into important cyber incidents. The board, composed of 20 members, conducted three deep investigations on the [Log4j vulnerability](https:\/\/therecord.media\/first-cyber-safety-review-board-report-finds-log4j-has-become-an-endemic-vulnerability), the [Lapsus$ hacker group](https:\/\/therecord.media\/sim-swapping-lapsus-cyber-safety-review-board-report) and a [2023 attack on Microsoft products](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dhs-cascade-of-security-failures-microsoft-china-hack) used by the U.S. government perpetrated by Chinese hackers. \nIn December, the CSRB [announced](https:\/\/therecord.media\/salt-typhoon-csrb-review) that it planned to next examine China\u2019s Salt Typhoon campaign \u2014 which has caused alarm across the U.S. government after officials from CISA and the FBI [acknowledged the China-linked spies are still inside U.S. telecom networks](https:\/\/therecord.media\/fbi-cisa-china-lurking-in-telecom-systems) roughly six months after the government began investigating the breach. \nBut members of all DHS advisory committees, including the Cyber Safety Review Board (CSRB), were [removed from their posts](https:\/\/therecord.media\/trump-dhs-removal-private-sector-members-advisory-boards) days after President Donald Trump\u2019s inauguration in January. \nDespite disbanding the CSRB during its Salt Typhoon investigation, Noem [has repeatedly questioned](https:\/\/therecord.media\/noem-house-hearing-proposed-cisa-funding-cuts) why the U.S. government does not know more about the campaign in speeches and in testimony before Congress. \nThe letter on Thursday said the CSRB \u201cplayed a vital role in U.S. national security carrying out post-incident reviews and providing information and making recommendations to improve public and private sector cyber security.\u201d \nThe senators called disbanding the CSRB \u201cparticularly confounding\u201d in light of the Trump administration\u2019s \u201crepeated insistence\u2026 on the need to leverage private sector and external expertise in government.\u201d They noted that the CSRB\u2019s findings from the 2023 Microsoft incident were recently [cited](https:\/\/www.dni.gov\/index.php\/newsroom\/congressional-testimonies\/congressional-testimonies-2025\/4059-ata-opening-statement-as-prepared) in a threat assessment by Director of National Intelligence Tulsi Gabbard. \n\u201cThe January dismissal of CSRB members, and continued uncertainty about the future role of the Board, has undermined cyber defense preparations for public and private entities across the United States,\u201d the senators said. \nThe Department of Homeland Security and the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency did not respond to requests for comment about the letter. \nIn January, acting Secretary of Homeland Security Benjamine Huffman [said](https:\/\/www.documentcloud.org\/documents\/25500093-dhs-advisory-boards-termination-letter\/) the decision to disband the CSRB reflected the Trump administration\u2019s \u201ccommitment to eliminating the misuse of resources and ensuring that DHS activities prioritize our national security.\u201d \nIn April, Rep. Mark Green \u2014 chair of the House Homeland Security Committee \u2014 [floated the idea](https:\/\/therecord.media\/mark-green-interview-cisa-cuts-china-hacking) that a Congressional oversight committee needed to take over the work the CSRB was doing. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Senators call on Trump admin to reinstate cyber review board for Salt Typhoon investigation)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Senators call on Trump admin to reinstate cyber review board for Salt Typhoon investigation )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/technology)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Cyber Safety Review Board (CSRB)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyber-safety-review-board)\n  * [US Senate](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/senate)\n  * [Salt Typhoon](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/salt-typhoon)\n  * [China](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/china)\n  * [Trump administration](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/trump-administration)\n  * [Department of Homeland Security (DHS)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/department-of-homeland-security)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Meta says it disrupted influence operations linked to China, Iran, RomaniaMay 30th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/meta-influence-operations-takedown-china-iran-romania)\n  * [DDoS incident disrupts internet for thousands in MoscowMay 30th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/moscow-internet-provider-asvt-ddos-attack)\n  * [Victoria\u2019s Secret website down as company investigates security incidentMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/victorias-secret-website-down-security-incident)\n  * [China-linked hackers exploit Google Calendar in cyberattacks on governmentsMay 29th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/china-linked-apt41-exploits-google-calendar-in-cyberattacks)\n  * [More than $12 million stolen from crypto platform Cork ProtocolMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cork-protocol-defi-12million-crypto-theft)\n  * [Estonia issues arrest warrant for Moroccan wanted for major pharmacy data breachMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/estonia-arrest-warrant-pharmacy-data-breach)\n  * [Ukraine detains alleged Russian spies who used dash cams to guide missile strikesMay 28th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukraine-detains-russian-spies-using-dashcams-missile-strikes)\n  * [Russian hospital programmer gets 14 years for leaking soldier data to UkraineMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-programmer-gets-14-years-for-leaking-info-to-ukraine)\n  * [Nearly 70,000 impacted by ransomware attack on Sheboygan, WisconsinMay 27th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-sheboygan-breach-notice)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
