"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/w\/wiz\/ai-security-risk-ebook.png)](https:\/\/www.wiz.io\/lp\/getting-started-with-ai-security-ai-risks-how-to-prevent-them-and-ai-for-defender?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=FY25Q3_INB_FORM_Getting-Started-with-AI-Security-AI-Risks-How-to-Prevent-Them&sfcid=701Py00000DP3ZaIAL&utm_term=FY26Q2-bleepingcomputer-970x250&utm_content=AISecurityeBook)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft now testing Notepad text formatting in Windows 11\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-now-testing-notepad-text-formatting-in-windows-11\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft now testing Notepad text formatting in Windows 11\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * May 30, 2025\n  * 02:41 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-now-testing-notepad-text-formatting-in-windows-11\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Notepad text formatting](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/posts\/2025\/05\/30\/Windows_11_Notepad_Markdown.jpg)\nMicrosoft announced today that the Windows 11 Notepad application is getting a text formatting feature supporting Markdown-style input.\nThe feature is being introduced one year after Microsoft [removed the WordPad basic word processing app](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-24h2-will-remove-cortana-and-wordpad-apps\/) that had text formatting capabilities, with the rollout of Windows 11 24H2 to Insiders in the Release Preview Channel.\n\"With this update, we are introducing lightweight formatting in Notepad, providing additional flexibility in how you structure content across your files,\" [said](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/05\/30\/text-formatting-in-notepad-begin-rolling-out-to-windows-insiders\/) Dave Grochocki, a Principal Product Manager Lead at Microsoft.\n\"The experience supports Markdown style input and files for users who prefer to work directly with the lightweight markup language. To get started, use the new formatting toolbar to apply formatting as you type or to selected text, including bold and italic styling, hyperlinks, and support for simple lists and headings.\"\nTo switch to plain text in the currently opened document, you can quickly remove formatting using the toolbar or the edit menu. You can also toggle between formatted Markdown and Markdown syntax views from the view menu or the status bar.\nAdditionally, those who don't need text formatting support when editing or viewing their documents in Notepad can disable it in the app settings.\nThis new Notepad capability is rolling out to all Windows Insiders in the Canary and Dev Channels who have updated the app to version 11.2504.50.0.\n## Stream of new Notepad features\nHowever, the update is also part of a larger effort to modernize the Notepad app, which began in December 2021 with the [launch of a fully redesigned Notepad app](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-starts-rolling-out-redesigned-notepad-for-windows-11\/) for Windows 11, 38 years after Microsoft introduced the original program in 1983.\nTwo years later, Redmond started testing [support for multiple tabs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-starts-testing-notepad-tabs-in-windows-11\/) and added a [built-in character counter](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-notepad-gets-a-built-in-character-counter-finally\/) (this missing feature forced many Notepad users to use third-party alternatives such as Notepad++ or Notepad2).\nIn July 2024, the company also [added spell check and autocorrect features](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/notepad-finally-gets-spellcheck-autocorrect-for-all-windows-11-users\/) in Notepad for all Windows 11 users that can fix spelling mistakes automatically as you type them.\nMore recently, since the start of 2025, Microsoft has also rolled out AI-powered [text summarization](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-notepad-to-get-ai-text-summarization-in-windows-11\/) and [text generation](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-notepad-gets-ai-powered-text-writing-capabilities\/)features for Windows 11 Insiders in the Canary and Dev Channels, which require Microsoft 365 Personal, Family, and Copilot Pro subscriptions.\nHowever, those who don't want the new AI options can disable them from the app's settings or uninstall the Windows Notepad app to use the Windows built-in notepad.exe program.\n[ ![Red Report 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/picus\/red-report-in-article.jpg) ](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n## [Top 10 MITRE ATT&CK\u00a9 Techniques Behind 93% of Attacks](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\nBased on an analysis of 14M malicious actions, discover the top 10 MITRE ATT&CK techniques behind 93% of attacks and how to defend against them.\n[Read the Red Report 2025](https:\/\/hubs.li\/Q039Tm490)\n### Related Articles:\n[Windows 11 Notepad gets AI-powered text writing capabilities](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-notepad-gets-ai-powered-text-writing-capabilities\/)\n[Microsoft testing Windows 11 support for third-party passkeys](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-testing-windows-11-support-for-third-party-passkeys\/)\n[Microsoft starts testing Windows 11 taskbar icon scaling](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-starts-testing-windows-11-taskbar-icon-scaling\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows 11 might fail to start after installing KB5058405](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/)\n[Windows Server emergency update fixes Hyper-V VM freezes, restart issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-server-emergency-update-fixes-hyper-v-vm-freezes-restart-issues\/)\n  * [Markdown](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/markdown\/)\n  * [Notepad](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/notepad\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows Insider](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-insider\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-now-testing-notepad-text-formatting-in-windows-11\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/police-takes-down-avcheck-antivirus-site-used-by-cybercriminals\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-are-exploiting-critical-flaw-in-vbulletin-forum-software\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Sharp Rhino story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/a\/acronis\/sharp-rhino.jpg)](https:\/\/www.acronis.com\/en-us\/cyber-protection-center\/posts\/sharprhino-an-old-new-threat\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer-fy25-q2-mixed-amer-en-ba-q2brand-trur-bleeping-d)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![ASUS](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-now-testing-notepad-text-formatting-in-windows-11\/) Botnet hacks 9,000+ ASUS routers to add persi