"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-are-exploiting-critical-flaw-in-vbulletin-forum-software\/",,
"summary": "Two critical vulnerabilities in vBulletin forum software (CVE-2025-48827 and CVE-2025-48828) are being actively exploited. These vulnerabilities allow remote code execution through misuse of PHP's Reflection API, impacting versions 5.0.0 through 5.7.5 and 6.0.0 through 6.0.3 on PHP 8.1 or later. Exploitation is ongoing, with observed attempts to deploy PHP backdoors. Forum administrators are advised to apply the latest security patches or upgrade to non-affected versions.",,
