"summary": "Two information disclosure vulnerabilities, CVE-2025-5054 and CVE-2025-4598, have been discovered in Linux systems, affecting Ubuntu, RHEL, and Fedora. These vulnerabilities are related to the core dump handlers in apport and systemd-coredump. They are race condition bugs that allow local attackers to access sensitive information such as password hashes. Specific mitigations include disabling core dumps for SUID binaries. The vulnerabilities have moderate severity due to high exploitation complexity. Active exploitation is supported by the availability of proof-of-concept code.",,
