"markdown": "This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. [Learn more](https:\/\/www.cookiesandyou.com)\nGot it!\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/news\/)\n  * [The Management & Operations Channel](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/the-management-operations-channel\/)\n\n\n# Equinix's SG1 data center in Singapore hit by outage during maintenance\nImpacting Singtel, StarHub, ViewQwest, and others\nJune 01, 2025 \n\nBy\n     [ Sebastian Moss ](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/profile\/sebastian-moss\/) [Comment](https:\/\/news.google.com\/rss\/articles\/CBMitAFBVV95cUxOSnpQemwtSTNtcEVhLUJFRC11ell4ZmgtV3lfZW1jVU5mM3hGbXktbzRQVGlFcGlRM2V5dkt5VWlZaVRTRTZ6aDF4Mk5nUTNuWlJEakdQbjgyOFdLdlFCZ0prbDdNRlNrWTJVQzQxaExJZWdxNnVzUjRFZkYyZjVCM3E2eDdpeURPeDBYMHZ4WmxCNFJkWnZQOE9sQ0gzc0EyMkEwX1FqaGhwQUdJaXhSeGJ2bFk?oc=5#disqus_thread)\n[](https:\/\/www.addtoany.com\/share)\nEquinix's SG1 data center in Singapore saw two data halls go offline in a major outage.\nThe 31 May incident lasted more than an hour, and caused widespread service issues across the country.\n[ ](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/equinix-inaugura-quinto-data-center-brasileiro-.original_vxBkfXL.jpg) ![equinix-inaugura-quinto-data-center-brasileiro-.original](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/equinix-inaugura-quinto-data-center-brasileiro.width-358_9LMweIe.jpg)\n\u2013 Equinix\n\"During scheduled maintenance at SG1 that required a reduction in power redundancy, we experienced equipment failure resulting in a power outage to two data halls in the data center,\" Equinix said in a statement. \n\"The issue has been resolved.\"\nThe facility at 20 Ayer Rajah Crescent has 13MW of capacity and spans more than 100,000 sq ft.\nMultiple Internet Service Providers were impacted by the outage, including Singtel, StarHub, and ViewQwest.\n\u201cWe would like to stress that this incident is entirely unrelated to any previous service issue,\" ViewQwest said. \"It was triggered by an external infrastructure failure beyond our direct control.\" \nThe company said it will work with Equinix to discover the root cause.\nSG1 last suffered an outage in October 2023, when [an issue with the chilled water system](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/news\/equinix-data-center-outage-causes-banking-issues-across-singapore\/) brought down banking apps, WhatsApp, and _Call of Duty_.\nThe facility also saw service disruptions in 2013, [during scheduled power maintenance](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/news\/equinix-singapore-suffers-limited-power-outage\/).\n## More in Outages\n  * ![AA-modius-4topissues-pg1](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/AA-modius-4topissues-pg1.height-150.png)\n#  [Navigating the top four risks of data center infrastructure](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/whitepapers\/navigating-the-top-four-risks-of-data-center-infrastructure\/)\n  * ![Alaska United Southeast](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/Screenshot_2025-03-21_143724.2e16d0ba.fill-280x185.png)\n21 Mar 2025\n#  [Subsea cable repaired after outage in Sitka, Alaska](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/news\/subsea-cable-repaired-after-outage-in-sitka-alaska\/)\n  * ![IMG_5856](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/IMG_5856.2e16d0ba.fill-280x185.jpg)\n11 Dec 2024\n#  Sponsored [Standby generators for the data center market](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/product-news\/standby-generators-for-the-data-center-market\/)\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.addtoany.com\/share)\n### Tags\n  * [Equinix](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/equinix\/)\n  * [SG1](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/sg1\/)\n  * [Singapore](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/singapore\/)\n  * [Singtel](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/singtel\/)\n  * [StarHub](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/starhub\/)\n  * [ViewQwest](https:\/\/news.google.com\/en\/tags\/viewqwest\/)\n\n\n## Whitepapers [ More](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/)\n  * ![AA-eaton-Consulting](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/AA-eaton-Consulting.height-150.png)\n#  [UPS refreshes: Opex vs. capex considerations](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/ups-refreshes-opex-vs-capex-considerations\/)\n29 May 2025\n  * #  [Strategic imperatives: Prioritizing your AI transformation for banking and financial services](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/strategic-imperatives-prioritizing-your-ai-transformation-for-banking-and-financial-services\/)\n28 May 2025\n  * #  [Retrofitting existing power systems for AI clusters](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/retrofitting-existing-power-systems-for-ai-clusters\/)\n27 May 2025\n  * #  [DCD Survey Report: The advent of AI](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/dcd-survey-report-the-advent-of-ai\/)\n23 May 2025\n  * [More](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/whitepapers\/)\n\n\n![Data Center Cooling SITE THUMBNAIL](https:\/\/media.datacenterdynamics.com\/media\/images\/Data_Center_Cooling__SITE_THUMBNAI.2e16d0ba.fill-280x185.png)\n# [Stream Now: Balancing legacy infrastructure with next-generation innovation](https:\/\/www.datacenterdynamics.com\/en\/broadcasts\/kitc-liquid\/2025\/balancing-legacy-infrastructure-with-next-generation-innovation\/)\nThank you! You will receive a confirmation email shortly. \n",,
