"summary": "A new variant of the Mirai malware botnet is exploiting a command injection vulnerability in TBK DVR-4104 and DVR-4216 digital video recording devices, tracked as CVE-2024-3721. This vulnerability allows attackers to hijack these devices, most likely to conduct DDoS attacks and proxy malicious traffic. Approximately 50,000 internet-exposed devices are known to be vulnerable. The attack primarily impacts regions such as China, India, Egypt, Ukraine, Russia, Turkey, and Brazil. The vulnerability is actively being exploited by threat actors to spread the new Mirai variant.",,
