"title": "New Supply Chain Malware Operation Hits npm and PyPI Ecosystems, Targeting Millions Globally",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-supply-chain-malware-operation-hits.html",,
"summary": "A new supply chain malware operation has impacted the npm and PyPI ecosystems, posing a threat to millions globally. The operation targets developers and end users by injecting malicious code into open-source packages. This incident highlights vulnerabilities in software supply chains, demanding enhanced security measures. A supply chain attack has targeted numerous npm and PyPI packages, introducing malware that executes shell commands, captures screenshots, and uploads files from infected systems. The malware has been detected in several packages associated with GlueStack, collectively accounting for nearly 1 million weekly downloads. Similarities were noted with prior attacks involving the npm package 'rand-user-agent.' Attackers potentially aim for cryptocurrency mining, data theft, and service disruption. Additionally, two rogue npm packages, 'express-api-sync' and 'system-health-sync-api,' unleash destructive operations, including file deletion. On PyPI, a credential harvester, 'imad213,' poses as an Instagram growth tool, collecting user credentials.",,
