"summary": "India's Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI), with the assistance of Microsoft and the National Police Agency of Japan, dismantled two illegal call centers in India that were involved in a sophisticated tech support scam targeting Japanese citizens. The scam involved tricking victims into believing their devices were compromised and coercing them into transferring funds. The operation, part of Operation Chakra V, also led to the arrest of six individuals and the seizure of various electronic evidence. Microsoft, through cross-sector collaboration, has taken down 66,000 malicious domains and has been actively working with international partners to combat the broader network responsible for these scams.",,
