"summary": "The Librarian Ghouls, also known as Rezet or Rare Werewolf, is an APT group that targets entities, mainly in Russia and the CIS, using legitimate third-party software to execute their operations. They deploy tools like command files and PowerShell scripts to gain remote access, steal credentials, and mine cryptocurrency using XMRig. Initial attacks are facilitated via phishing emails containing password-protected archives. The Librarian Ghouls APT is actively targeting Russian entities, focusing on industrial enterprises and engineering schools. The campaign, which began in December 2024, uses phishing emails composed in Russian with archives and decoy documents to compromise credentials primarily for Russian-speaking victims. Attackers leverage legitimate third-party utilities rather than custom-built malware, utilizing tools like RAR and PowerShell scripts for data exfiltration, remote access tools deployment, and even crypto-mining activities. Hundreds of users in Russia, Belarus, and Kazakhstan have been impacted.",,
