"title": "NHS calls for 1 million blood donors as UK stocks remain low following cyberattack",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/uk-nhs-calls-for-blood-donations-after-cyberattack",,
"summary": "The UK's National Health Service (NHS) is urgently calling for one million people to donate blood due to critically low blood stocks caused by a previous cyberattack. The attack involved the ransomware group Qilin, which disrupted pathology services and resulted in increased use of O-type blood. As the NHS attempts to avoid a Red Alert status, it is also addressing a significant data breach that exposed sensitive patient information, including pathology and medical details. The data breach affected over 900,000 individuals, and those affected have not yet been fully informed. The breach compromised patient safety and privacy, aligning with cybercrime threats primarily targeting the healthcare sector, specifically NHS services.",,
