"title": "Trump cyber executive order drops Biden-era provisions",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/trump-cybersecurity-executive-order-june-2025",,
"summary": "President Donald Trump's new executive order revises cybersecurity policies by removing Biden-era software security rules and focusing on quantum and AI-related cybersecurity measures. The order mandates government agencies to update their cybersecurity strategies, including quantum-resistant encryption and AI vulnerability management. Notably, cybersecurity enforcement is restricted to foreign actors, excluding domestic applications. The Trump administration views previous sanctions as politically charged and redesigns them to avoid misuse against domestic political operators. Additionally, the order influences regulations on IoT products, cryptography, and secure communications.",,
