"summary": "A critical vulnerability in the Wazuh Server, designated CVE-2025-24016, is being actively exploited by threat actors to deploy Mirai botnet variants. The exploitation allows for remote code execution due to an unsafe deserialization vulnerability in the server's API. Notably, the attackers have used this flaw to unleash two distinct botnets to conduct DDoS attacks. Akamai discovered the campaign targeting this vulnerability, and it has been observed that the botnets involved employ shell scripts to download and spread the malware across various architectures. The campaigns have been linked to multiple exploits targeting products such as Huawei routers and Realtek SDK, among others.",,
