"title": "Spyware maker cuts ties with Italy after government refused audit into hack of journalist\u2019s phone",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/paragon-spyware-maker-cuts-ties-italy-government",,
"summary": "Paragon, a spyware manufacturer, ended its contract with the Italian government after the latter declined an audit into the alleged hacking of a journalist's phone using Paragon's spyware, Graphite. Paragon's decision follows Italy's Parliamentary Committee for the Security of the Republic (COPASIR) report denying the misuse of its spyware against Francesco Cancellato, a journalist known for investigative reporting. Paragon stated the termination was due to the Italian authorities not allowing an independent verification to confirm that the spyware was not misused. This move is unprecedented for a spyware manufacturer to acknowledge terminating a government contract over such matters.",,
