"markdown": "X\n[![Wiz](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/b\/bleepingcomputer\/Webcast-20250709_970x250.jpg)](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/go\/65\/)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Over 84,000 Roundcube instances vulnerable to actively exploited flaw\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/)\n\n\n# Over 84,000 Roundcube instances vulnerable to actively exploited flaw\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * June 9, 2025\n  * 04:14 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Vulnerable](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2023\/12\/18\/warning.jpg)\nOver 84,000 Roundcube webmail installations are vulnerable to CVE-2025-49113, a critical remote code execution (RCE) flaw with a public exploit.\nThe flaw, which impacts Roundcube versions 1.1.0 through 1.6.10, spanning over a decade, was [patched on June 1, 2025](https:\/\/roundcube.net\/news\/2025\/06\/01\/security-updates-1.6.11-and-1.5.10), following its discovery and reporting by security researcher Kirill Firsov.\nThe bug stems from unsanitized $_GET['_from'] input, enabling PHP object deserialization and session corruption when session keys begin with an exclamation mark.\nShortly after the patch was released, hackers reverse-engineered it to develop a working exploit, which they [sold on underground forums](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-selling-critical-roundcube-webmail-exploit-as-tech-info-disclosed\/).\nThough the exploitation of [CVE-2025-49113](https:\/\/nvd.nist.gov\/vuln\/detail\/CVE-2025-49113) requires authentication, attackers claim that valid credentials can be obtained via CSRF, log scraping, or brute-forced.\nFirsov shared technical details about the flaw [on his blog](https:\/\/fearsoff.org\/research\/roundcube) to help defend against active exploitation attempts that are very likely to occur.\n## Massive exposure\nRoundcube is widely used in shared hosting (GoDaddy, Hostinger, OVH) and government, education, and tech sectors, with over 1,200,000 instances visible online.\nThreat monitoring platform that its internet scans return [84,925 Roundcube instances](https:\/\/dashboard.shadowserver.org\/statistics\/combined\/time-series\/?date_range=7&source=http_vulnerable&source=http_vulnerable6&tag=cve-2025-49113%2B&dataset=unique_ips&limit=100&group_by=geo&stacking=stacked&auto_update=on) vulnerable to CVE-2025-49113 as of June 8, 2025.\nMost of these instances are in the United States (19,500), India (15,500), Germany (13,600), France (3,600), Canada (3,500), and the United Kingdom (2,400).\n![Heatmap of exposure to CVE-2025-49113](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1220909\/2025\/June\/map.jpg)**Heatmap of exposure to CVE-2025-49113** _Source: The Shadowserver Foundation_\nConsidering the high risk of exploitation and the potential for data theft, the exposure of those instances is a significant cybersecurity risk.\nSystem administrators are recommended to update to version 1.6.11 and 1.5.10, which address CVE-2025-49113, as soon as possible.\nIt is unclear if the flaw is being leveraged in actual attacks and at what scale, but immediate action is advised nonetheless.\nIf upgrading is impossible, it is recommended to restrict access to webmail, turn off file uploads, add CSRF protection, block risky PHP functions, and monitor for exploit indicators.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Hacker selling critical Roundcube webmail exploit as tech info disclosed](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hacker-selling-critical-roundcube-webmail-exploit-as-tech-info-disclosed\/)\n[Exploit details for max severity Cisco IOS XE flaw now public](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/exploit-details-for-max-severity-cisco-ios-xe-flaw-now-public\/)\n[Hackers are exploiting critical flaw in vBulletin forum software](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/hackers-are-exploiting-critical-flaw-in-vbulletin-forum-software\/)\n[Ivanti fixes EPMM zero-days chained in code execution attacks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/ivanti-fixes-epmm-zero-days-chained-in-code-execution-attacks\/)\n[Fortinet fixes critical zero-day exploited in FortiVoice attacks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fortinet-fixes-critical-zero-day-exploited-in-fortivoice-attacks\/)\n  * [Actively Exploited](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/actively-exploited\/)\n  * [Exploit](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/exploit\/)\n  * [RCE](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/rce\/)\n  * [Remote Code Execution](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/remote-code-execution\/)\n  * [Roundcube](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/roundcube\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/google-patched-bug-leaking-phone-numbers-tied-to-accounts\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/Avast_v2_dog.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_b&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_b:banner)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Microsoft shares script to restore inetpub folder you shouldn\u2019t delete ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-shares-script-to-restore-inetpub-folder-you-shouldnt-delete\/)\n  * [ ![NPM supply chain](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Malware found in NPM packages with 1 million weekly downloads ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/supply-chain-attack-hits-gluestack-npm-packages-with-960k-weekly-downloads\/)\n  * [ ![Qilin ransomware](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Critical Fortinet flaws now exploited in Qilin ransomware attacks ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/critical-fortinet-flaws-now-exploited-in-qilin-ransomware-attacks\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Register to attend Xposure, the Exposure Management vSummit, to learn more about Exposure Management ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Register to attend Xposure, the Exposure Management vSummit, to learn more about Exposure Management  ](https:\/\/events.pentera.io\/xposure2025?utm_source=Article%20&source=Article%20&utm_medium=Bleeping%20Computer%20&medium=Bleeping%20Computer%20&utm_campaign=Xposure&campaign=Xposure)\n  * [ ![Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12883224-FY25Q2_Scattered-Spider&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=sponsored-ad)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now!](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/) Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now! ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=build_robust_windows_service_farid_q2_25&utm_content=build_robust_windows_service_farid&utm_term=display)\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-84-000-roundcube-instances-vulnerable-to-actively-exploited-flaw\/ \"Submit\")\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.3232165085899191)\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n",,
