"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/researcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Maximizing Efficiency and Security in Government Cloud Environments](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjmy-PEKftk11FkFxOmdctMAQvuNZs31RGGDpxe66f8A72_iHu6NGjK0aDPU80YpR1m3Yo1zLbr-jR6RpBlz7xcjBXRasIVB2ELtOxV39r54fCWfLtySFA6x5eeDix9sZtk4aXcEBSQaEqR-y1EY_wtaQI34gSbWHYLpRqj9oUOE12EE2S3xGVTsoU9TIZ8\/s728-e100\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d)\n# [Researcher Found Flaw to Discover Phone Numbers Linked to Any Google Account](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/researcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 10, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ API Security\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjm_b9X2yeRdAZJbwW1Dej6WpVj3miNiiGgpjN0lZ9DmQvEFZX49hkGJlHCac6nd8OZTCxJMvc3LzkPEZJ4V9z53Nfz4tQMkXlHddVoEYJvck2uO29OGhd1k-EM7lv5jwIC0GmrGRIIiflps6HhChuY6sXhLhfO20gQ_Chuzo-AlRXFyWXqqyelBJK1arhyphenhyphen\/s728-rw-e365\/google.gif)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjm_b9X2yeRdAZJbwW1Dej6WpVj3miNiiGgpjN0lZ9DmQvEFZX49hkGJlHCac6nd8OZTCxJMvc3LzkPEZJ4V9z53Nfz4tQMkXlHddVoEYJvck2uO29OGhd1k-EM7lv5jwIC0GmrGRIIiflps6HhChuY6sXhLhfO20gQ_Chuzo-AlRXFyWXqqyelBJK1arhyphenhyphen\/s728-rw-e365\/google.gif)\nGoogle has stepped in to address a security flaw that could have made it possible to brute-force an account's recovery phone number, potentially exposing them to privacy and security risks.\nThe issue, [according](https:\/\/brutecat.com\/articles\/leaking-google-phones) to Singaporean security researcher \"brutecat,\" leverages an issue in the company's account recovery feature.\nThat said, exploiting the vulnerability hinges on several moving parts, specifically targeting a now-deprecated JavaScript-disabled version of the Google username recovery form (\"accounts.google[.]com\/signin\/usernamerecovery\") that lacked anti-abuse protections designed to prevent spammy requests.\nThe page in question is designed to help users check if a recovery email or phone number is associated with a specific display name (e.g., \"John Smith\").\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/researcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/grc-now-2025-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nBut circumventing the CAPTCHA-based rate limit ultimately made it possible to try out all permutations of a Google account's phone number in a short space of time and arrive at the correct digits in seconds or minutes, depending on the length of the phone number (which varies from country to country).\nAn attacker could also take advantage of Google's Forgot Password flow to figure out the country code associated with a victim's phone number, as well as obtain their display name by creating a [Looker Studio](https:\/\/cloud.google.com\/looker\/docs\/studio) document and transferring ownership to the victim, effectively causing their full name to be leaked on the home page.\nIn all, the exploit requires performing the following steps -\n  * Leak the Google account display name via Looker Studio\n  * Run the forgot password flow for a target email address to get the masked phone number with the last 2 digits displayed to the attacker (e.g., \u2022\u2022 \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u202203)\n  * Brute-force the phone number against the username recovery endpoint to brute-force the phone number\n\n\nBrutecat said a Singapore-based number could be leaked using the aforementioned technique in a span of 5 seconds, while a U.S. number could be unmasked in about 20 minutes.\nArmed with the knowledge of a phone number associated with a Google account, a bad actor could take control of it through a [SIM-swapping attack](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/11\/fcc-enforces-stronger-rules-to-protect.html) and ultimately reset the password of any account associated with that phone number.\nFollowing responsible disclosure on April 14, 2025, Google awarded the researcher a $5,000 bug bounty and plugged the vulnerability by completely getting rid of the non-JavaScript username recovery form as of June 6, 2025.\nThe findings come months after the same researcher [detailed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/02\/thn-weekly-recap-google-secrets-stolen.html#:~:text=Google%20Addresses%20High%20Impact%20Flaws) another $10,000 exploit that an attacker could have weaponized to expose the email address of any YouTube channel owner by chaining a flaw in the YouTube API and an outdated web API associated with Pixel Recorder.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/researcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nThen in March, brutecat also [revealed](https:\/\/brutecat.com\/articles\/youtube-creator-emails) that it's possible to glean email addresses belonging to creators who are part of the YouTube Partner Program ([YPP](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/creators\/partner-program\/)) by leveraging an access control issue in the \"\/get_creator_channels\" endpoint, earning them a reward of $20,000.\n\"[An] access control issue in \/get_creator_channels leaks channel contentOwnerAssociation, which leads to channel email address disclosure via Content ID API,\" Google [said](https:\/\/bughunters.google.com\/reports\/vrp\/PLviDoABs).\n\"An attacker with access to a Google account that had a channel that joined the YouTube Partner Program (over 3 million channels) can obtain the email address as well as monetization details of any other channel in the YouTube Partner Program. The attacker can use this to de-anonymize a YouTuber (as there is an expectation of pseudo-anonymity in YouTube), or phish them.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fresearcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html&t=Researcher%20Found%20Flaw%20to%20Discover%20Phone%20Numbers%20Linked%20to%20Any%20Google%20Account) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Researcher%20Found%20Flaw%20to%20Discover%20Phone%20Numbers%20Linked%20to%20Any%20Google%20Account \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fresearcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/researcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fresearcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fresearcher-found-flaw-to-discover-phone.html&text=Researcher%20Found%20Flaw%20to%20Discover%20Phone%20Numbers%20Linked%20to%20Any%20Google%20Account)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[API Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/API%20Security)[bug bounty](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/bug%20bounty)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Google](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Google)[JavaScript](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/JavaScript)[Privacy]