"title": "ConnectWise rotating code signing certificates over security concerns",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/connectwise-rotating-code-signing-certificates-over-security-concerns\/",,
"summary": "ConnectWise is changing its digital code signing certificates used for signing ScreenConnect, ConnectWise Automate, and ConnectWise RMM executables due to security concerns. The issue was raised by a security researcher highlighting a configuration handling vulnerability in ScreenConnect that could be exploited if system-level access is achieved. The certificates were originally set to be revoked on June 10, 2025, but an extension to June 13 was granted. This action affects both on-premises and cloud users, who must update to avoid disruptions. The change is not linked to a recent nation-state cyberattack incident.",,
