"title": "CISA, Microsoft warn of Windows zero-day used in attack on \u2018major\u2019 Turkish defense org",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/microsoft-cisa-zero-day-turkish-defense-org",,
"summary": "Microsoft and CISA have warned about a zero-day vulnerability, CVE-2025-33053, in the Windows Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) tool, which has been used in cyberattacks by the hacking group Stealth Falcon. The vulnerability, which requires a user to click on a specially crafted URL, was first discovered by Check Point during an investigation into a failed cyberattack on a major Turkish defense organization. The attack involved a .url file disguised as a PDF document, used for espionage and delivered via phishing emails. Microsoft has released a fix, and the vulnerability is included in CISA's catalog of exploited bugs with a severity score of 8.8. Stealth Falcon is known for its sophisticated cyber espionage operations targeting governments and defense sectors, particularly in the Middle East and Africa.",,
