"summary": "A new Secure Boot bypass vulnerability, tracked as CVE-2025-3052, has been discovered by Binarly researcher Alex Matrosov. This vulnerability affects PCs and servers that trust the Microsoft 'UEFI CA 2011' certificate, allowing attackers with admin rights to install bootkit malware by exploiting a flaw in a BIOS-flashing utility. Microsoft has released a patch to mitigate this issue along with 13 other affected modules. This flaw allows arbitrary data to be written during the UEFI boot process, effectively disabling Secure Boot security measures.",,
