"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Maximizing Efficiency and Security in Government Cloud Environments](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjmy-PEKftk11FkFxOmdctMAQvuNZs31RGGDpxe66f8A72_iHu6NGjK0aDPU80YpR1m3Yo1zLbr-jR6RpBlz7xcjBXRasIVB2ELtOxV39r54fCWfLtySFA6x5eeDix9sZtk4aXcEBSQaEqR-y1EY_wtaQI34gSbWHYLpRqj9oUOE12EE2S3xGVTsoU9TIZ8\/s728-e100\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d)\n# [Adobe Releases Patch Fixing 254 Vulnerabilities, Closing High-Severity Security Gaps](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 10, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Cloud Security\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhQ0KmTHFU0m6sxsmDu_7AAeEatV_zSK-123uo0vgshHtbgHshVGSnjxHhbUAe_r-fZ6JFumINHIU3WawDEDlsCxjEH_dm-6PcAbMdkVFhY86YG72JC2V8NrUbJnz-i8N2Kc61XIs28907vXAT2v91_mPfJCymEZWH_r-3D3AN0FjVni87oaIAkF2QhtawV\/s728-rw-e365\/adobe.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhQ0KmTHFU0m6sxsmDu_7AAeEatV_zSK-123uo0vgshHtbgHshVGSnjxHhbUAe_r-fZ6JFumINHIU3WawDEDlsCxjEH_dm-6PcAbMdkVFhY86YG72JC2V8NrUbJnz-i8N2Kc61XIs28907vXAT2v91_mPfJCymEZWH_r-3D3AN0FjVni87oaIAkF2QhtawV\/s728-rw-e365\/adobe.jpg)\nAdobe on Tuesday pushed [security updates](https:\/\/helpx.adobe.com\/security.html) to address a total of 254 security flaws impacting its software products, a majority of which affect Experience Manager (AEM).\nOf the 254 flaws, 225 reside in AEM, impacting AEM Cloud Service (CS) as well as all versions prior to and including 6.5.22. The issues have been resolved in AEM Cloud Service Release 2025.5 and version 6.5.23.\n\"Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could result in arbitrary code execution, privilege escalation, and security feature bypass,\" Adobe [said](https:\/\/helpx.adobe.com\/security\/products\/experience-manager\/apsb25-48.html) in an advisory.\nAlmost all the 225 vulnerabilities have been classified as cross-site scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities, specifically a mix of stored XSS and DOM-based XSS, that could be exploited to achieve arbitrary code execution.\nAdobe has credited security researchers Jim Green (green-jam), Akshay Sharma (anonymous_blackzero), and lpi for discovering and reporting the XSS flaws.\nThe most severe of the flaws patched by the company as part of this month's update concerns a code execution flaw in Adobe Commerce and Magento Open Source.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe critical-rated vulnerability, CVE-2025-47110 (CVSS score: 9.1) is a reflected XSS vulnerability that could result in arbitrary code execution. Also addressed is an improper authorization flaw (CVE-2025-43585, CVSS score: 8.2) that could lead to a security feature bypass.\nThe [following versions](https:\/\/helpx.adobe.com\/security\/products\/magento\/apsb25-50.html) are impacted -\n  * Adobe Commerce (2.4.8, 2.4.7-p5 and earlier, 2.4.6-p10 and earlier, 2.4.5-p12 and earlier, and 2.4.4-p13 and earlier)\n  * Adobe Commerce B2B (1.5.2 and earlier, 1.4.2-p5 and earlier, 1.3.5-p10 and earlier, 1.3.4-p12 and earlier, and 1.3.3-p13 and earlier)\n  * Magento Open Source (2.4.8, 2.4.7-p5 and earlier, 2.4.6-p10 and earlier, 2.4.5-p12 and earlier)\n\n\nOf the remaining updates, four relate to code execution flaws in [Adobe InCopy](https:\/\/helpx.adobe.com\/security\/products\/incopy\/apsb25-41.html) (CVE-2025-30327, CVE-2025-47107, CVSS scores: 7.8) and [Substance 3D Sampler](https:\/\/helpx.adobe.com\/security\/products\/substance3d-sampler\/apsb25-55.html) (CVE-2025-43581, CVE-2025-43588, CVSS scores: 7.8).\nWhile none of the bugs have been listed as publicly known or exploited in the wild, users are advised to update their instances to the latest version to safeguard against potential threats.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fadobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html&t=Adobe%20Releases%20Patch%20Fixing%20254%20Vulnerabilities%2C%20Closing%20High-Severity%20Security%20Gaps) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Adobe%20Releases%20Patch%20Fixing%20254%20Vulnerabilities%2C%20Closing%20High-Severity%20Security%20Gaps \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fadobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fadobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fadobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html&text=Adobe%20Releases%20Patch%20Fixing%20254%20Vulnerabilities%2C%20Closing%20High-Severity%20Security%20Gaps)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Adobe](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Adobe)[Adobe Commerce](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Adobe%20Commerce)[arbitrary code execution](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/arbitrary%20code%20execution)[Cloud security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cloud%20security)[Cross-site Scripting](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cross-site%20Scripting)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Magento Open Source](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Magento%20Open%20Source)[privilege escalation](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/privilege%20escalation)[Software Patching](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Software%20Patching)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgxPMKDLOYLRl__e78OahbBFWWhXUWR8tguoT5Fnr-mwr-igCnlMdpxWH97szR92LqmuQMzY2_aMRzEW_rjQ5gxcqs-rF6V0xjqEn5yS4bMyEZZtAtl9sAfQ2ZnsRrcrlOxh5TUJUzp3xoqGoEG2JpWrMvS739Lnk1_5lanEdPBOAgaK-zi2GTKxeoGoRlW\/s300-rw-e100\/animated.gif)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/xmcyber-em-course-anim)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgf3htno2k3FtYs6xQqRvYIOqrmqOFoTyPa6DkEV_Ep9gaj9Jk4LG66X10Z6104CmB-S1pCY0hnpwwe3JvBMRuZeTlRZbnoDgEpJnY111NJurNHeqUlJ8XSTcvr2Lvy0lGPsN1nU-4msWTfy_Qyn7v5MxxExQXugkSTz5T90lzcmdC0xfVO9WwB2ax8VU0C\/w300-e100\/chain.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/true-cost-cves)\nMost Read News\n[ ![New Linux Flaws Allow Password Hash Theft via Core Dumps in Ubuntu, RHEL, Fedora](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html) New Linux Flaws Allow Password Hash Theft via Core Dumps in Ubuntu, RHEL, Fedora ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/new-linux-flaws-allow-password-hash.html)\n[ ![FBI and Europol Disrupt Lumma Stealer Malware Network Linked to 10 Million Infections](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/adobe-releases-patch-fixing-254.html) FBI and Europol Disrupt Lumma Stealer Malware Network Linked to 10 Million Infections ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fbi-and-europol-disrupt-lumma-stealer.html)\n[ ![From Infection to Access: A 24-Ho