"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/ncsc-pushes-uk-government-create-strategic-cyber-policy-agenda",,
"summary": "The UK National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC) has urged the government to adopt a strategic policy agenda to address escalating cybersecurity risks. The NCSC, while not a policymaking body, criticizes the lack of political focus on cybersecurity and the slow progress in implementing necessary legislation. Ollie Whitehouse, NCSC's CTO, emphasized the shortcomings in regulation and the technology market's failure to prioritize resilient systems. The article highlights comparisons with US and EU cybersecurity approaches and underscores the need for incentives to adopt secure technologies. Joe Jarnecki from RUSI emphasizes the UK's historically low regulatory burden on vendors as a barrier to improved cybersecurity.",,
