"title": "5 plead guilty to laundering nearly $37 million stolen through Cambodian cyber scam centers",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/guilty-pleas-cambodia-cyber-scams",,
"summary": "Five individuals pleaded guilty to laundering $36.9 million obtained from investment scams in Cambodia. The fraud involved a network convincing U.S. citizens to invest in fake cryptocurrency schemes, stealing their funds, which were then laundered through shell companies and cryptocurrency avenues. The organized crime operation, referred to as pig butchering, saw funds transferred to accounts in the Bahamas and converted to stablecoin USDT. Several players were based in Los Angeles and China, and coordination of the operation occurred between the U.S. and Cambodia. This is part of a broader effort to dismantle Cambodian scam operations with ties to money laundering and international crime syndicates.",,
