"summary": "Ivanti released security updates to address three high-severity vulnerabilities in Workspace Control that involve hardcoded cryptographic keys. These vulnerabilities, identified as CVE-2025-5353, CVE-2025-22455, and CVE-2025-22463, allow local attackers to decrypt SQL credentials and environment passwords, potentially leading to privilege escalation and system compromise. Ivanti confirmed no active exploitation in the wild but advised patching to prevent future risks.",,
