"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Maximizing Efficiency and Security in Government Cloud Environments](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjmy-PEKftk11FkFxOmdctMAQvuNZs31RGGDpxe66f8A72_iHu6NGjK0aDPU80YpR1m3Yo1zLbr-jR6RpBlz7xcjBXRasIVB2ELtOxV39r54fCWfLtySFA6x5eeDix9sZtk4aXcEBSQaEqR-y1EY_wtaQI34gSbWHYLpRqj9oUOE12EE2S3xGVTsoU9TIZ8\/s728-e100\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d)\n# [SinoTrack GPS Devices Vulnerable to Remote Vehicle Control via Default Passwords](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 11, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananIoT Security \/ Vulnerability\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgJxLk8qZyEML8cI6rxFLnJSFHBJWvTnXfx2_K2XscOelaL9r5L6sKuhw3wUnOYTZ9LLATc3NYUP-Dw0bsZC1BdcIANbHqOr96cxO851THhyVGdOC6Pog8vTplONpP_SdsQ7j_z2Oc2iPOFfvK7aX_jGRekqk5wBdcq0CoQKjG4x4hY5IHY2NKIPZ-wxFQJ\/s728-rw-e365\/gps.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgJxLk8qZyEML8cI6rxFLnJSFHBJWvTnXfx2_K2XscOelaL9r5L6sKuhw3wUnOYTZ9LLATc3NYUP-Dw0bsZC1BdcIANbHqOr96cxO851THhyVGdOC6Pog8vTplONpP_SdsQ7j_z2Oc2iPOFfvK7aX_jGRekqk5wBdcq0CoQKjG4x4hY5IHY2NKIPZ-wxFQJ\/s728-rw-e365\/gps.jpg)\nTwo security vulnerabilities have been disclosed in SinoTrack GPS devices that could be exploited to control certain remote functions on connected vehicles and even track their locations.\n\"Successful exploitation of these vulnerabilities could allow an attacker to access device profiles without authorization through the common web management interface,\" the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) [said](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/news-events\/ics-advisories\/icsa-25-160-01) in an advisory.\n\"Access to the device profile may allow an attacker to perform some remote functions on connected vehicles such as tracking the vehicle location and disconnecting power to the fuel pump where supported.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/grc-now-2025-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe vulnerabilities, per the agency, affect all versions of the SinoTrack IoT PC Platform. A brief description of the flaws is below -\n  * **CVE-2025-5484** (CVSS score: 8.3) - Weak authentication to the central SinoTrack device management interface stems from the use of a default password and a username that's an identifier printed on the receiver.\n  * **CVE-2025-5485** (CVSS score: 8.6) - The username used to authenticate to the web management interface, i.e., the identifier, is a numerical value of no more than 10 digits.\n\n\nAn attacker could retrieve device identifiers with either physical access or by capturing identifiers from pictures of the devices posted on publicly accessible websites such as eBay. Furthermore, the adversary could enumerate potential targets by incrementing or decrementing from known identifiers or through enumerating random digit sequences.\n\"Due to its lack of security, this device allows remote execution and control of the vehicles to which it is connected and also steals sensitive information about you and your vehicles,\" security researcher Ra\u00fal Ignacio Cruz Jim\u00e9nez, who reported the flaws to CISA, told The Hacker News in a statement.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nThere are currently no fixes that address the vulnerabilities. The Hacker News has reached out to SinoTrack for comment, and we will update the story if we hear back.\nIn the absence of a patch, users are advised to change the default password as soon as possible and take steps to conceal the identifier. \"If the sticker is visible on publicly accessible photographs, consider deleting or replacing the pictures to protect the identifier,\" CISA said.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html&t=SinoTrack%20GPS%20Devices%20Vulnerable%20to%20Remote%20Vehicle%20Control%20via%20Default%20Passwords) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=SinoTrack%20GPS%20Devices%20Vulnerable%20to%20Remote%20Vehicle%20Control%20via%20Default%20Passwords \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html&text=SinoTrack%20GPS%20Devices%20Vulnerable%20to%20Remote%20Vehicle%20Control%20via%20Default%20Passwords)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[CISA](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/CISA)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[Information theft](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Information%20theft)[iot security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/iot%20security)[Patch Management](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Patch%20Management)[Vulnerability](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Vulnerability)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhXtybRvdTPePyrr9VDzCT_1cw9oNHYpbVxfHYoWprN1eVgaF0NRWEdTBCCTKQXkiO1MUHuaiHlPAfzw9RNttuGLNTLdR3p2zpAMb3D7N2GaZs8c-OG272mx8bXYh4QmHX1cbtC16Mg3htaVWMigvda79TfF4qVHvsuMmJX5EML2p-Adcgyuw7ctWq8w47m\/s300-e100\/em-course-person.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/em-course-person)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgf3htno2k3FtYs6xQqRvYIOqrmqOFoTyPa6DkEV_Ep9gaj9Jk4LG66X10Z6104CmB-S1pCY0hnpwwe3JvBMRuZeTlRZbnoDgEpJnY111NJurNHeqUlJ8XSTcvr2Lvy0lGPsN1nU-4msWTfy_Qyn7v5MxxExQXugkSTz5T90lzcmdC0xfVO9WwB2ax8VU0C\/w300-e100\/chain.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/true-cost-cves)\nMost Read News\n[ ![The Secret Defense Strategy of Four Critical Industries Combating Advanced Cyber Threats](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html) The Secret Defense Strategy of Four Critical Industries Combating Advanced Cyber Threats ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/the-secret-defense-strategy-of-four.html)\n[ ![New Atomic macOS Stealer Campaign Exploits ClickFix to Target Apple Users](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html) New Atomic macOS Stealer Campaign Exploits ClickFix to Target Apple Users ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-atomic-macos-stealer-campaign.html)\n[ ![Chinese APT41 Exploits Google Calendar for Malware Command-and-Control Operations](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/sinotrack-gps-devices-vulnerable-to.html) Chinese APT41 Exploits Google Calendar for Malware Command-and-Control Operations ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/chinese-apt41-exploits