"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![Maximizing Efficiency and Security in Government Cloud Environments](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjmy-PEKftk11FkFxOmdctMAQvuNZs31RGGDpxe66f8A72_iHu6NGjK0aDPU80YpR1m3Yo1zLbr-jR6RpBlz7xcjBXRasIVB2ELtOxV39r54fCWfLtySFA6x5eeDix9sZtk4aXcEBSQaEqR-y1EY_wtaQI34gSbWHYLpRqj9oUOE12EE2S3xGVTsoU9TIZ8\/s728-e100\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/gov-cloud-efficiency-d)\n# [INTERPOL Dismantles 20,000+ Malicious IPs Linked to 69 Malware Variants in Operation Secure](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 11, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananCybercrime \/ Malware\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhW9QONGnvcgpxpW_jzjW9GIDgz9c4y55v9p3DLrAj_Hz1YMJzdn0DP6vqqkHcSGC94kwIXOAshR7XI_OkKWLCTI58XRiaH2KmttNzX02zdab2vmvy3IPL1MUr4wDZlrQCU09bOdnBOPQxyi4vrvpUZz98d81noxPxbhVhXeqKCujjFWxb8_TXL0c9lnGiG\/s728-rw-e365\/police.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhW9QONGnvcgpxpW_jzjW9GIDgz9c4y55v9p3DLrAj_Hz1YMJzdn0DP6vqqkHcSGC94kwIXOAshR7XI_OkKWLCTI58XRiaH2KmttNzX02zdab2vmvy3IPL1MUr4wDZlrQCU09bOdnBOPQxyi4vrvpUZz98d81noxPxbhVhXeqKCujjFWxb8_TXL0c9lnGiG\/s728-rw-e365\/police.jpg)\nINTERPOL on Wednesday announced the dismantling of more than 20,000 malicious IP addresses or domains that have been linked to 69 information-stealing malware variants.\nThe joint action, codenamed , took place between January and April 2025, and involved [law enforcement agencies](https:\/\/www.coe.int\/en\/web\/cybercrime\/-\/operation-secure-strengthening-cybersecurity-in-asia-and-the-south-pacific) from 26 countries to identify servers, map physical networks, and execute targeted takedowns.\n\"These coordinated efforts resulted in the takedown of 79 percent of identified suspicious IP addresses,\" INTERPOL [said](https:\/\/www.interpol.int\/News-and-Events\/News\/2025\/20-000-malicious-IPs-and-domains-taken-down-in-INTERPOL-infostealer-crackdown) in a statement. \"Participating countries reported the seizure of 41 servers and over 100 GB of data, as well as the arrest of 32 suspects linked to illegal cyber activities.\"\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/grc-now-2025-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nVietnamese authorities arrested 18 suspects, and confiscated devices, SIM cards, business registration documents, and money worth $11,500. Further house raids have led to the arrest of another 12 people in Sri Lanka and two individuals in Nauru.\nThe Hong Kong Police, per INTERPOL, identified 117 command-and-control servers hosted across 89 internet service providers. These servers were designed to act as a hub to launch and manage malicious campaigns, such as phishing, online fraud, and social media scams.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgJvEDRRYpa06Y6YfMvafJ8f9eF-NjXKJ9kabPSU29W4TA4RTT6Sa9oL1_-8Kdbcd-M4na6cxRbzmCIP_vvYaDPKsLdA03tnn5qiJgegwT0rVX7N_RFdUZb4XfBga0jrmjvGrZCq0qr4do_xxwgdu6X2C7yfxECOxiNWR0JiAXS8Wk014-wyi5PW0uaHK2w\/s728-rw-e365\/secure.jpg)\nCountries involved in Operation Secure include Brunei, Cambodia, Fiji, Hong Kong (China), India, Indonesia, Japan, Kazakhstan, Kiribati, Laos, Macau (China), Malaysia, Maldives, Nauru, Nepal, Papua New Guinea, Philippines, Samoa, Singapore, Solomon Islands, South Korea, Sri Lanka, Thailand, Timor-Leste, Tonga, Vanuatu, and Vietnam.\nThe development comes weeks after a global operation led to the [seizure of 2,300 domains](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/fbi-and-europol-disrupt-lumma-stealer.html) associated with the Lumma Stealer malware.\nInformation stealers, often sold on the cybercrime underground on a subscription basis, are seen as a stepping stone for threat actors to gain unauthorized access to target networks. These malicious programs make it possible to siphon browser credentials, passwords, cookies, credit card details, and cryptocurrency wallet data from infected machines.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe stolen information is then monetized in the form of logs on various forums, enabling other actors to conduct follow-on attacks, including ransomware, data breaches, and business email compromise (BEC).\nSingapore-headquartered Group-IB, which was one of the private sector companies that participated in the operation, said it provided mission-critical intelligence related to user accounts compromised by stealer malware like Lumma, RisePro, and Meta Stealer.\n\"The compromised credentials and sensitive data acquired by cybercriminals through infostealer malware often serve as initial vectors for financial fraud and ransomware attacks,\" said Dmitry Volkov, CEO of Group-IB.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Finterpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html&t=INTERPOL%20Dismantles%2020%2C000%2B%20Malicious%20IPs%20Linked%20to%2069%20Malware%20Variants%20in%20Operation%20Secure) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=INTERPOL%20Dismantles%2020%2C000%2B%20Malicious%20IPs%20Linked%20to%2069%20Malware%20Variants%20in%20Operation%20Secure \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Finterpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/interpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Finterpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Finterpol-dismantles-20000-malicious-ips.html&text=INTERPOL%20Dismantles%2020%2C000%2B%20Malicious%20IPs%20Linked%20to%2069%20Malware%20Variants%20in%20Operation%20Secure)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Cybercrime](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cybercrime)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[data breach](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/data%20breach)[Group-IB](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Group-IB)[Interpol](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Interpol)[law enforcement](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/law%20enforcement)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[online fraud](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/online%20fraud)[Phishing](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Phishing)[ransomware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/ransomware)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhXtybRvdTPePyrr9VDzCT_1cw9oNHYpbVxfHYoWprN1eVgaF0NRWEdTBCCTKQXkiO1MUHuaiHlPAfzw9RNttuGLNTLdR3p2zpAMb3D7N2GaZs8c-OG272mx8bXY