"title": "FIN6 cybercriminals pose as job seekers on LinkedIn to hack recruiters",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/fin6-recruitment-scam-malware-campaign",,
"summary": "Cybercriminals from the FIN6 group are posing as job seekers on LinkedIn to infect recruiters with malware delivered through fake resumes. Researchers at DomainTools report that FIN6, traditionally known for targeting payment card data and PoS systems, is now using phishing emails to distribute a backdoor called MoreEggs. This tactic includes sending well-crafted emails that require manual URL typing to bypass security filters, leading recruiters to landing pages hosted on AWS. These landing pages deliver a malicious ZIP file with the MoreEggs backdoor, allowing FIN6 to access systems, steal credentials, and potentially deploy ransomware.",,
