"markdown": "X\n[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft fixes Windows Server auth issues caused by April updates\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft fixes Windows Server auth issues caused by April updates\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * June 11, 2025\n  * 08:34 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/05\/14\/Windows-Server.jpg)\nMicrosoft has fixed a known issue causing authentication problems on Windows Server domain controllers after installing the April 2025 security updates.\nPlatforms affected by these problems include Windows Server 2016, Windows Server 2019, Windows Server 2022, and the latest version, Windows Server 2025.\nHowever, as Microsoft further explained when it acknowledged this known issue [in early May](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/), home users are unlikely to be impacted since domain controllers are typically used in enterprise authentication scenarios.\n\"After installing the April Windows monthly security update released April 8, 2025 (KB5055523) or later, Active Directory Domain Controllers (DC) might experience issues when processing Kerberos logons or delegations using certificate-based credentials that rely on key trust via the Active Directory msds-KeyCredentialLink field,\" Microsoft said.\n\"This can result in authentication issues in Windows Hello for Business (WHfB) Key Trust environments or environments that have deployed Device Public Key Authentication (also known as Machine PKINIT).\"\nThese issues could also affect software using these two features for authentication, including but not limited to identity management systems, third-party single sign-on (SSO) solutions, and smart card authentication products.\nThis week, the company [released](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/) the following cumulative updates that resolve the auth issues on all impacted Windows releases:\n  * [KB5060842](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-10-2025-kb5060842-os-build-26100-4349-47ff300b-2a04-440c-9476-2860d04fce8d) (Windows Server 2025)\n  * [KB5060526](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-10-2025-kb5060526-os-build-20348-3807-4e9453c4-6602-48ea-b349-689cd66dfdb9) (Windows Server 2022)\n  * [KB5060531](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-10-2025-kb5060531-os-build-17763-7434-32fce7e7-305d-4d32-913f-3fdc0709a763) (Windows Server 2019)\n  * [KB5061010](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-10-2025-kb5061010-os-build-14393-8148-6766ca26-dc1e-4592-b959-d0c92d6deb6f) (Windows Server 2016)\n\n\n\"We recommend you install the latest security update for your device as it contains important improvements and issue resolutions, including this one,\" Redmond [explains](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/status-windows-server-2025#logon-might-fail-with-windows-hello-in-key-trust-mode-and-log-kerberos-events) in a Tuesday Windows release health update.\n\"If you are using an update released before this date and have this issue, you should temporarily delay setting a value of '2' to registry key AllowNtAuthPolicyBypass on updated DCs servicing self-signed certificate-based authentication,\" it added, referring admins to the Registry Settings section of the [KB5057784](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/help\/5057784) support document.\nAs Microsoft explained last month, these authentication issues are [linked to security measures](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/protections-for-cve-2025-26647-kerberos-authentication-5f5d753b-4023-4dd3-b7b7-c8b104933d53) that mitigate a high-severity vulnerability ([CVE-2025-26647](https:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/vulnerability\/CVE-2025-26647)) that can let authenticated attackers escalate privileges remotely by exploiting an improper input validation weakness in Windows Kerberos (which [replaced NTLM](http:\/\/answers.microsoft.com\/en-us\/msoffice\/forum\/all\/ntlm-vs-kerberos\/d8b139bf-6b5a-4a53-9a00-bb75d4e219eb) as the new default authentication protocol for domain-connected devices on Windows versions released since Windows 2000.\nIn April, Microsoft [fixed another known issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-auth-issues-on-windows-server-windows-11-24h2\/) causing auth problems on Windows 11 and Windows Server 2025 systems using the Kerberos PKINIT security protocol when Credential Guard is enabled.\nThe company also had to release emergency out-of-band (OOB) updates in November 2022 to [resolve a bug causing Kerberos sign-in failures](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-kerberos-auth-issues-in-emergency-updates\/) and other auth issues affecting Windows domain controllers.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft: April updates cause Windows Server auth issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-april-updates-cause-windows-server-auth-issues\/)\n[Microsoft fixes auth issues on Windows Server, Windows 11 24H2](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-auth-issues-on-windows-server-windows-11-24h2\/)\n[New Windows Server emergency updates fix container launch issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/new-windows-server-emergency-updates-fix-container-launch-issue\/)\n[Microsoft: New Windows updates fix Active Directory policy issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-new-emergency-windows-updates-fix-ad-policy-issues\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows Server 2025 restarts break connectivity on some DCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-server-2025-restarts-break-services-on-domain-controllers\/)\n  * [Active Directory](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/active-directory\/)\n  * [Authentication](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/authentication\/)\n  * [Domain Controller](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/domain-controller\/)\n  * [KB5055523](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kb5055523\/)\n  * [Kerberos](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kerberos\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows Hello](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-hello\/)\n  * [Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server\/)\n  * [Windows Server 2019](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server-2019\/)\n  * [Windows Server 2022](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server-2022\/)\n  * [Windows Server 2025](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-server-2025\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/block-ads-forever-with-this-16-adguard-family-deal\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Delivery Chains](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/Avast_v3_tablet.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_c&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_c:banner)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![United Natural Foods UNFI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) Grocery wholesale giant United Natural Foods hit by cyberattack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/grocery-wholesale-giant-united-natural-foods-hit-by-cyberattack\/)\n  * [ ![Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) Microsoft June 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes exploited zero-day, 66 flaws ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/)\n  * [ ![Chinese Hacker China](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) SentinelOne shares new details on China-linked breach attempt ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/sentinelone-shares-new-details-on-china-linked-breach-attempt\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-windows-server-auth-issues-caused-by-april-updates\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_