"title": "Operation Secure disrupts global infostealer malware operations",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/operation-secure-disrupts-global-infostealer-malware-operations\/",,
"summary": "Operation Secure was a large-scale international law enforcement operation led by Interpol, conducted from January to April 2025, targeting infostealer malware operations. The operation led to 32 arrests, takedown of over 20,000 malicious IPs\/domains, seizure of 41 servers, and notification of 216,000 victims globally. The operation impacted malware infrastructure related to Lumma, RisePro, and META Stealer. Companies like Kaspersky, Group-IB, and Trend Micro assisted with intelligence. Significant arrests occurred in Vietnam, with 18 suspects apprehended. The operation disrupts groups that compromised financial and personal data leading to breaches in several high-profile companies.",,
