"summary": "Singapore led a multinational anti-scam operation involving seven Asian nations, resulting in the shutdown of numerous scam centers and over 1,800 arrests. The effort, named 'Operation Frontier+', focused on schemes involving fraudulent investments, dating apps, government impersonations, job websites, and more. The operation froze 32,000 bank accounts and seized $20 million, with the scams totaling $225 million in thefts. Singapore alone arrested 106 individuals responsible for $30 million in scams and seized nearly $8 million from 714 bank accounts.",,
