"markdown": "![photos from April-May 2025 anti-scam operation](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_operation_frontier_plus_photos_singapore_police_e61f03447a.jpg)\nA handout photo from Singapore police featuring images from the seven nations participating in an anti-scam operation in April and May 2025.\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)June 11th, 2025\n# Singapore leads multinational operation to shutter scam centers tied to $225 million in thefts\nSeven law enforcement agencies in Asia coordinated on an operation to shut down dozens of scam centers and arrested more than 1,800 people involved. \nLed by officials from the Singapore Police Force, authorities In Hong Kong, South Korea, Malaysia, the Maldives, Thailand and Macao executed a month-long operation in April and May \u2014 investigating 33,900 suspects believed to be involved in at least 9,200 scam cases ranging from fraudulent investments to schemes involving dating apps, government impersonations, job websites and more. \nIn total, officials believe victims had about $225 million stolen from them. About 32,000 bank accounts linked to the scams \u2014 sometimes known as pig butchering \u2014 were frozen and $20 million was seized as part of the operation. \nSingapore said it arrested 106 people locally who were responsible for 1,300 scams that netted them about $30 million. Police in the island nation were able to seize nearly $8 million worth of stolen funds taken from 714 bank accounts. \nThose arrested are facing a range of charges related to hacking, stolen government ID use and more. \nDavid Chew, a senior Singaporean police official, said they needed to work with international law enforcement agencies because scam syndicates now operate \u201cwithout geographical constraints, employing increasingly sophisticated methods across multiple jurisdictions to defraud victims and launder their illicit proceeds.\u201d \n\u201cA transnational threat requires a transnational response. No single jurisdiction has an adequate answer to this scourge, but we are collectively stronger together,\u201d he [said](https:\/\/www.police.gov.sg\/media-room\/news\/20250504_seven_law_enforcement_agencies_collaborate_in_major_anti-scam_operations), noting that the effort was called \u201cOperation Frontier+.\u201d \nThe effort began, according to Singapore\u2019s police force, at the end of April when two separate victims transferred thousands to a bank account provided by scammers. Police officials were able to trace the funds to bank accounts in Malaysia and coordination between the two governments allowed a portion of the money to be frozen almost immediately. \nSingapore said it plans to continue Operation Frontier+, exchanging \u201creal-time intelligence and analysis\u201d with the other countries to quickly retrieve money obtained through cyber scams. \nHong Kong police [said](https:\/\/www.ecns.cn\/m\/news\/society\/2025-06-04\/detail-ihesawyz5552464.shtml) the operation began last year and involves at least 10 countries, including Australia, Canada and Indonesia. \nThe operation comes as multiple countries have taken a more aggressive posture toward shutting down scam syndicates. This week, the U.S. Justice Department [secured plea deals from six men](https:\/\/therecord.media\/guilty-pleas-cambodia-cyber-scams) accused of scamming more than $35 million from people through illicit cyber scheme centers in Cambodia. \nLast week, Microsoft [partnered](https:\/\/blogs.microsoft.com\/on-the-issues\/2025\/06\/05\/microsoft-dismantle-transnational-scam\/) with Japanese and Indian officials to shut down a tech support fraud syndicate that was scamming the elderly in Japan. \nIndia\u2019s Central Bureau of Investigation 19 locations and arrested six men, taking down two illegal call centers and seizing troves of digital infrastructure. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Singapore leads multinational operation to shutter scam centers tied to $225 million in thefts)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Singapore leads multinational operation to shutter scam centers tied to $225 million in thefts )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Singapore](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/singapore)\n  * [malaysia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/malaysia)\n  * [pig butchering](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/pig-butchering)\n  * [recruitment scam](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/recruitment-scam)\n  * [Southeast Asia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/southeast-asia)\n  * [romance scams](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/romance-scams)\n  * [Scams](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scams)\n  * [fraud](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/fraud)\n  * [Scam call centers](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scam-call-centers)\n  * [Impersonation scams](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/impersonation-scams)\n  * [dating apps](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/dating-apps)\n  * [financial](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/financial)\n  * [Thailand](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/thailand)\n  * [Hong Kong](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/hong-kong)\n  * [South Korea](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/south-korea)\n  * [Police](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/police)\n  * [takedown](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/takedown)\n  * [seizure](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/seizure)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Dozens arrested across Asia in global infostealer malware crackdownJune 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-arrested-infostealer-interpol-crackdown)\n  * [FIN6 cybercriminals pose as job seekers on LinkedIn to hack recruiters June 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/fin6-recruitment-scam-malware-campaign)\n  * [Hundreds of Russian devices hit by Rare Werewolf cryptomining attacksJune 10th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-devices-hit-by-rare-werewolf-crypto-mining)\n  * [Nearly 300,000 crash records stolen from Texas transportation departmentJune 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/car-crash-records-stolen-texas-transportation-department)\n  * [Major food wholesaler says cyberattack impacting distribution systemsJune 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/major-food-wholesaler-cyberattack-impacting-distribution)\n  * [New hacker group uses LockBit ransomware variant to target Russian companiesJune 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/new-hacker-group-lockbit-target-russia)\n  * [Kazakhstan detains over 140 for allegedly selling citizens\u2019 data via Telegram channelsJune 9th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/kazakhstan-arrests-suspects-stolen-data-network)\n  * [Off-brand IoT devices are still vulnerable to BadBox botnet, FBI saysJune 6th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/iot-devices-vulnerable-to-badbox-botnet-fbi)\n  * [Ukrainian police arrest hacker who used hosting firm's servers to mine cryptocurrencyJune 5th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ukrainian-police-arrest-hacker-cryptomining)\n\n\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n## [TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered![TerraStealerV2 and TerraLogger: Golden Chickens' New Malware Families Discovered](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/cta_2025_0501_Blog_Main_Feature_55a0e64897.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/terrastealerv2-and-terralogger)\n## [Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting![Uncovering MintsLoader With Recorded Future Malware Intelligence Hunting](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_cta_2025_0429_Main_Feature_e924c36cbd.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/uncovering-mintsloader-with-recorded-future-malware-intelligence-hunting)\n## [Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives![Iran\u2019s AI Ambitions: Balancing Economic Isolation with National Security Imperatives](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/irans_ai_ambitions_balancing_economic_isolation_national_security_imperatives_151fba814d.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/irans-ai-ambitions-balancing-economic-isolation-national-security-imperatives)\n",,
