"title": "Hackers exploited Windows WebDav zero-day to drop malware",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/stealth-falcon-hackers-exploited-windows-webdav-zero-day-to-drop-malware\/",,
"summary": "The APT group 'Stealth Falcon' exploited a Windows WebDav remote code execution vulnerability, CVE-2025-33053, in zero-day attacks targeting defense and government organizations in Turkey, Qatar, Egypt, and Yemen. The exploit involves manipulating the working directory of legitimate Windows tools to execute malicious executables remotely from WebDAV servers. This technique allows for stealthy operations by avoiding dropping files locally. The attacks were detected by Check Point Research. Microsoft has patched this vulnerability in the latest Patch Tuesday update, and critical organizations are advised to update immediately or monitor WebDAV traffic.",,
