"markdown": "X\n[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft creates separate Windows 11 24H2 update for incompatible PCs\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft creates separate Windows 11 24H2 update for incompatible PCs\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * June 11, 2025\n  * 11:35 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/04\/02\/Windows-11.jpg)\nMicrosoft confirmed on Tuesday that it's pushing a revised security update targeting some Windows 11 24H2 systems incompatible with the initial update released during this month's Patch Tuesday.\n\"This update is being gradually rolled out to devices running Windows 11, version 24H2. We've identified a compatibility issue affecting a limited set of these devices,\" the company in a Twitter thread.\n\"If your device is affected, you'll receive a revised update with all the June 2025 security improvements in the near term.\"\nIn a message center update on Tuesday, Redmond [added](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/windows-message-center#3570) that \"the June 2025 security update is fully available for all other supported versions of Windows.\"\nMicrosoft has yet to disclose the hardware or software configurations affected by the compatibility issue that prompted the release of a revised security update and how the affected PCs were impacted after installing this month's Patch Tuesday cumulative updates.\nAlso, the company didn't share if this was the first time it released a revised Patch Tuesday update to address compatibility issues and if this is something customers can expect from Microsoft in the future.\nA Microsoft spokesperson was not immediately available for comment when contacted by BleepingComputer earlier today.\n![Windows 24H2 revised update](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2025\/Windows-Update-revised-update.png)\n\u200bOn Tuesday, Microsoft [released](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/) security updates ([KB5060842 and KB5060999](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-kb5060842-and-kb5060999-cumulative-updates-released\/)) for 66 vulnerabilities in Windows 11 24H2 and 23H2, including one actively exploited Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) zero-day ([CVE-2025-33053](http:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2025-33053)) and a publicly disclosed Windows SMB privilege escalation flaw.\nThis month's Patch Tuesday Windows updates addressed ten critical vulnerabilities, eight allowing attackers to gain remote code execution on unpatched devices and two enabling them to escalate privileges.\nKB5060842 also resolves a Windows Hello issue preventing users from signing in with self-signed certificates and extends system restore points availability up to 60 days on Windows 11 24H2 devices, while KB5060999 fixes a graphics support issue blocking Remote Desktop connections with \"session has ended\" and \"remote desktop connection cannot be established\" errors.\nThe same day, Microsoft released the [KB5060533](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5060533-cumulative-update-released-with-7-changes-fixes\/) Windows 10 22H2 cumulative update, which brings seconds back to the time shown in the Calendar flyout and fixes an issue causing Hyper-V virtual machines with Windows 10, Windows 11, and Windows Server [to freeze or restart unexpectedly](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-server-emergency-update-fixes-hyper-v-vm-freezes-restart-issues\/).\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft: Windows 11 might fail to start after installing KB5058405](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-might-fail-to-start-after-installing-kb5058405\/)\n[Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows 11 24H2 now ready to rollout to everyone](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-24h2-now-ready-to-rollout-to-everyone\/)\n[Microsoft pushes fix for Windows 11 24H2 update failures](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-pushes-fix-for-windows-11-update-0x80240069-errors\/)\n[Microsoft: Windows 11 24H2 updates fail with 0x80240069 errors](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-windows-11-24h2-updates-fail-with-0x80240069-errors\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows 11 24H2](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11-24h2\/)\n  * [Windows Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-update\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/brute-force-attacks-target-apache-tomcat-management-panels\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/stealth-falcon-hackers-exploited-windows-webdav-zero-day-to-drop-malware\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Skuld Stealer story](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/Avast_v2_dog.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_b&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_b:banner)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![United Natural Foods UNFI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Grocery wholesale giant United Natural Foods hit by cyberattack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/grocery-wholesale-giant-united-natural-foods-hit-by-cyberattack\/)\n  * [ ![Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Microsoft June 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes exploited zero-day, 66 flaws ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/)\n  * [ ![Chinese Hacker China](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) SentinelOne shares new details on China-linked breach attempt ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/sentinelone-shares-new-details-on-china-linked-breach-attempt\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12883224-FY25Q2_Scattered-Spider&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=sponsored-ad)\n  * [ ![Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now!](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now! ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=build_robust_windows_service_farid_q2_25&utm_content=build_robust_windows_service_farid&utm_term=display)\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n\n\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/ \"Submit\")\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_