"summary": "A critical vulnerability, named 'EchoLeak', was discovered in Microsoft 365 Copilot, allowing attackers to exfiltrate sensitive data without user interaction. This zero-click AI flaw could automate silent data exfiltration from AI-integrated systems. It was identified by Aim Labs and assigned CVE-2025-32711 by Microsoft. Though the flaw was patched and not exploited maliciously in the wild, it highlights the emerging risks associated with 'LLM Scope Violation'. The vulnerability could allow attackers to manipulate Microsoft 365 Copilot to leak internal data.",,
