"summary": "A new method dubbed 'SmartAttack' leverages smartwatches equipped to receive ultrasonic signals as a means to exfiltrate data from air-gapped systems. These systems are typically used in secure environments like government facilities and nuclear plants to prevent external threats. The attack was developed by Israeli researchers and involves malware that modulates computer speakers to emit high-frequency sounds that convey data to a nearby smartwatch. Though challenging due to tiny smartwatch microphones, this method can transmit sensitive information over short distances.",,
