"title": "ConnectWise to Rotate ScreenConnect Code Signing Certificates Due to Security Risks",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/connectwise-to-rotate-screenconnect.html",,
"summary": "ConnectWise is set to rotate its digital code signing certificates for ScreenConnect, ConnectWise Automate, and ConnectWise remote monitoring and management (RMM) executables due to a security vulnerability. A third-party researcher raised concerns about how ScreenConnect handled configuration data in earlier versions, allowing certain data to be stored in a non-signed area of the installer, potentially creating an insecure design. The revocation of digital certificates will be executed by June 13, 2025, with new certificates and updates planned to handle the configuration data more securely. The situation was brought into focus after a cyberattack suspected to be by a nation-state actor exploited CVE-2025-3935 for ViewState code injection attacks. ConnectWise emphasized that their systems or certificates were not compromised, but systems using on-premise versions need to be updated to avoid service disruption. This incident highlights the use of remote monitoring tools like ScreenConnect in sophisticated attacks known as living-off-the-land (LotL).",,
