"title": "Windows 11 24H2 emergency update fixes Easy Anti-Cheat BSOD issue",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft released an emergency update for Windows 11 24H2 (KB5063060) to fix a compatibility issue that causes BSODs on systems running Easy Anti-Cheat. The problem resulted in restarts with 'IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL' errors tied to ntoskrnl.exe or EasyAntiCheat_EOS.exe crashes while running multiplayer games. The update is automatically available via Windows Update and Microsoft Update on affected devices. Microsoft also implemented a compatibility hold for certain Intel systems. Additionally, security updates were released for other vulnerabilities in June 2025, but unrelated to this specific issue.",,
