"markdown": "X\n[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Windows 11 24H2 emergency update fixes Easy Anti-Cheat BSOD issue\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/)\n\n\n# Windows 11 24H2 emergency update fixes Easy Anti-Cheat BSOD issue\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * June 12, 2025\n  * 06:43 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/02\/07\/Windows_11.jpg)\nMicrosoft has released an emergency Windows 11 24H2 update to address an incompatibility issue triggering restarts with blue screen of death (BSOD) errors on systems with Easy Anti-Cheat.\nThe out-of-band update (**[KB5063060](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-11-2025-kb5063060-os-build-26100-4351-out-of-band-b1746442-8c6c-425d-ac5a-3a8f51e372f3)**) is a revised version of the Windows 11 KB5060842 cumulative update released during this month's Patch Tuesday after many customers experiencing system reboots and IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL BSODs tied to ntoskrnl.exe or EasyAntiCheat_EOS.exe crashing on computers running various games, .\nMicrosoft [said on Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/) that the emergency update addressed a compatibility issue and rolled out to \"a limited set of these devices\" running Windows 11, version 24H2.\nHowever, the company didn't initially share what hardware or software configurations were affected and what impact KB5060842 had after being installed on incompatible PCs.\nOne day later, Redmond revealed that the issues only impacted devices running [Easy Anti-Cheat](https:\/\/steamdb.info\/tech\/AntiCheat\/EasyAntiCheat\/), a massively popular anti-cheating service installed with hundreds of multiplayer games (including Apex Legends, War Thunder, Dead by Daylight, ELDEN RING, Rust, Squad, NBA 2K25, and many others) to prevent cheating while playing online.\n\"This update addresses an incompatibility issue where Windows might restart unexpectedly when opening games that use the Easy Anti-Cheat service,\" Microsoft [said](https:\/\/learn.microsoft.com\/en-us\/windows\/release-health\/windows-message-center#3570).\n\"This update downloads and installs automatically from Windows Update and Microsoft Update on devices with Easy Anti-Cheat installed and on devices that have not installed KB506842 yet,\" it .\nIf you can't install the KB5063060 out-of-band cumulative update via Windows Update, you can install it manually on x64 and arm64 systems after downloading it from the [Microsoft Update Catalog](https:\/\/www.catalog.update.microsoft.com\/Search.aspx?q=KB5063060).\nMicrosoft [also placed a compatibility hold](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-warns-of-windows-11-24h2-gaming-performance-issues\/) in October to block Windows 24H2 upgrades on Intel Alder Lake+ and vPro systems because of known issues causing Easy Anti-Cheat blue screens with \"MEMORY_MANAGEMENT\" errors.\n\u200bOn Tuesday, Redmond [released](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/) security updates ([KB5060842 and KB5060999](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-kb5060842-and-kb5060999-cumulative-updates-released\/)) for 66 vulnerabilities in Windows 11, including a publicly disclosed Windows SMB privilege escalation flaw ([CVE-2025-33073](http:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2025-33073)) and an actively exploited Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning (WebDAV) zero-day ([CVE-2025-33053](http:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2025-33053)).\nThe July 2025 Patch Tuesday Windows updates addressed ten critical vulnerabilities, eight allowing attackers to gain remote code execution on unpatched devices, and the other two enabling them to escalate privileges.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft warns of blue screen crashes caused by April updates](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-warns-of-blue-screen-crashes-caused-by-april-updates\/)\n[Windows Server emergency update fixes Hyper-V VM freezes, restart issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-server-emergency-update-fixes-hyper-v-vm-freezes-restart-issues\/)\n[Windows 11 24H2 blocked on PCs with code-obfuscation driver BSODs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/windows-11-24h2-blocked-on-pcs-with-code-obfuscation-driver-bsods\/)\n[Microsoft creates separate Windows 11 24H2 update for incompatible PCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-creates-separate-windows-11-24h2-update-for-incompatible-pcs\/)\n[Windows 11 upgrade block lifted after Safe Exam Browser fix](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-upgrade-block-lifted-after-safe-exam-browser-fix\/)\n  * [Blue Screen of Death](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/blue-screen-of-death\/)\n  * [BSOD](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/bsod\/)\n  * [Crash](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/crash\/)\n  * [Easy Anti-Cheat](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/easy-anti-cheat\/)\n  * [Emergency Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/emergency-update\/)\n  * [KB5063060](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kb5063060\/)\n  * [Known Issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/known-issue\/)\n  * [Out-of-Band](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/out-of-band\/)\n  * [Reboot](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/reboot\/)\n  * [Restart](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/restart\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows 11 24H2](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11-24h2\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fog-ransomware-attack-uses-unusual-mix-of-legitimate-and-open-source-tools\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/b\/bleepingcomputer\/Webcast-20250709_400x500.jpg)](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)\n[![Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/b\/bleepingcomputer\/Webcast-20250709_400x500.jpg)](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![United Natural Foods UNFI](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Grocery wholesale giant United Natural Foods hit by cyberattack ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/grocery-wholesale-giant-united-natural-foods-hit-by-cyberattack\/)\n  * [ ![Patch Tuesday](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Microsoft June 2025 Patch Tuesday fixes exploited zero-day, 66 flaws ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/)\n  * [ ![CPU Motherboard BIOS](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) New Secure Boot flaw lets attackers install bootkit malware, patch now ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-secure-boot-flaw-lets-attackers-install-bootkit-malware-patch-now\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Learn about Scattered Spider\u2019s evolving TTPs and how to defend your organization ](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12883224-FY25Q2_Scattered-Spider&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_content=sponsored-ad)\n  * [ ![Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now!](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now! ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=build_robust_windows_service_farid_q2_25&utm_content=build_robust_windows_service_farid&utm_term=display)\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n\n\n[![Picus](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/GD-300-600-Laptop-v1.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_d&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_d:sidebar)\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/ \"Submit\")\n[Freestar.com](https:\/\/ads.freestar.com\/?utm_campaign=branding&utm_medium=stickyFooter&utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_content=bleepingcomputer_970x90_728x90_320x50_sticky)\n![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=2)![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/ad-delivery.net\/px.gif?ch=1&e=0.40008973344595267)\n",,
