"summary": "GitLab has released security updates to address vulnerabilities in its DevSecOps platform, including account takeover and missing authorization issues. The updates include GitLab Community and Enterprise editions versions 18.0.2, 17.11.4, and 17.10.8. CVE-2025-4278 is an HTML injection issue allowing account takeovers, and CVE-2025-5121 is a missing authorization issue impacting GitLab Ultimate EE that allows unauthorized CI\/CD job injections. CVE-2025-2254 is a cross-site scripting flaw, and CVE-2025-0673 is a denial of service vulnerability. Admins are urged to upgrade immediately.",,
