"title": "Fog ransomware attack on Asia financial org draws attention over use of employee monitoring software",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/fog-ransomware-incident-asia-financial-org-employee-monitoring",,
"summary": "The recent cyberattack targeting a financial institution in Asia employed the Fog ransomware, attracting attention due to the use of unusual tools and tactics, including legitimate employee monitoring software, Syteca, and open-source pentesting tools. This has raised suspicion that the attack may have espionage intentions. Symantec researchers have not linked the attack to a specific nation-state, although persistent access after ransomware deployment and tool usage suggest possible espionage motives. Syteca's role remains unclear, while the attack methodically deleted evidence of illicit activities.",,
