"title": "23andMe privacy ombudsman recommends company obtains consent for sale of customer data",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/23andme-privacy-ombudsman-recommends-consent-sale",,
"summary": "The consumer privacy ombudsman for genomics company 23andMe, which is undergoing bankruptcy proceedings, recommended that the company obtain 'separate and affirmative' customer consent before selling their genetic data. The recommendation responded to concerns from 23andMe customers about their genetic data being sold without consent, potentially in conflict with the company's privacy policy. A Congressional hearing highlighted the issue after a hack in 2023 led to many data deletion requests. The ombudsman suggested that, if the court doesn't mandate consent, the potential buyers of 23andMe should obtain consent before using the data.",,
