"summary": "The article focuses on the importance of regulatory harmonization in cybersecurity, arguing that economic prosperity and national security cannot be achieved without it. The collaboration of independent regulators is sought to leverage expertise and lower business costs while increasing national security. Recommendations are made to prioritize cybersecurity, clarify roles in the cyber domain, and foster interagency cooperation. Harry Coker Jr., the former National Cyber Director, emphasized the critical role of cybersecurity in ensuring economic and national security. His tenure focused on harmonizing cyber regulations, enhancing interagency collaboration, and addressing longstanding internet vulnerabilities, such as the Border Gateway Protocol (BGP). Coker advocated for actionable cybersecurity strategies with proper implementation plans, highlighting the convergence of economic prosperity with national security. Challenges remain, including defining roles within cyber governance and the protection of state and local entities from nation-state cyber threats.",,
