"summary": "The article discusses a malicious PyPI package that disguises itself as a legitimate Python module called Chimera to steal sensitive data. It targets AWS credentials, CI\/CD systems, and macOS information. This poses a security risk to developers and organizations using Python packages. The content discusses a malicious PyPI package named chimera-sandbox-extensions that was discovered to be stealing sensitive developer information, such as AWS tokens, CI\/CD environment variables, and macOS data. The package masquerades as a module for Chimera Sandbox, a service by Singaporean tech company Grab, targeting corporate and cloud infrastructures. The malware uses a domain generation algorithm to download further payloads and has the ability to exploit OSX environments by extracting JAMF receipts. Further, several malware-laced npm packages were found to execute remote code. The findings indicate a sophisticated cyber threat aimed at compromising software supply chains.",,
