"title": "Microsoft: June Windows Server security updates cause DHCP issues",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-windows-server-security-updates-cause-dhcp-issues\/",,
"summary": "Microsoft has acknowledged an issue with the June 2025 security updates, which causes the DHCP service to freeze on some Windows Server systems. This issue impacts IP renewal for clients, affecting the Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol (DHCP) service responsible for automating IP address assignments. The affected Windows Server versions include Windows Server 2016, 2019, 2022, and 2025. Microsoft plans to release a resolution shortly. Additionally, this update follows previous issues with authentication and domain controller connectivity in Windows Server systems.",,
