"title": "Whole Foods supplier making progress on restoration after cyberattack left shelves empty",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/unfi-groceries-supplier-cyberattack-update",,
"summary": "United Natural Foods (UNFI), the main supplier for Whole Foods, experienced a cyberattack that limited its operations, causing empty shelves in grocery stores. The company has been working to restore its electronic ordering systems while using alternative processes to ensure product delivery. No specific vulnerabilities, malware, or threat groups were mentioned in the content. UNFI reported disruption in its operations but is gradually increasing its operational capacity. The attack did not mention any direct harm or exploitation details in Singapore or other ASEAN members.",,
