"summary": "The U.S. State Department is offering a reward of up to $10 million for information on Iranian hackers associated with the CyberAv3ngers group, known for using the IOControl malware to target Industrial Control Systems (ICS) and Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) devices in U.S. critical infrastructure sectors. These attacks are linked to Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps Cyber-Electronic Command. The IOControl malware has been used to compromise technology from vendors including Unitronics, D-Link, Hikvision, and Baicells. The State Department's notice comes amid heightened military tensions between Israel and Iran.",,
