"summary": "A high-severity security flaw, CVE-2023-33538, affecting TP-Link wireless routers, has been added to CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog due to active exploitation. This command injection vulnerability could result in the execution of arbitrary commands when processing malformed HTTP GET requests. Affected models include TP-Link TL-WR940N and TL-WR841N, among others. CISA warns that these products could be end-of-life, urging users to discontinue use if no mitigations are available. There is no confirmed information on exploitation in the wild with the FrostyGoop malware incident. Exploitation activities targeting similar vulnerabilities like CVE-2023-28771 in Zyxel firewalls have been observed.",,
