"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEg8huJBVEvXupx8-XvBHKiOtZyICMh8wyW8VgfSaZUBvMGFFSrkPoFUpsjZfKnTjzwYBGDtM-ey2i7MA6aNhTFrJiZq55ISkJeKR19Qvwfonlc4YMbyfFbY0W83WtvkcMLRm3N5Z6IJdqtBQtgHjjRAPrlgCYSumFtdWLLk8mogc0Vyo3jjOpVTu5p4lApA\/s728-e100\/header.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-eks-security-cheat-d)\n# [New Flodrix Botnet Variant Exploits Langflow AI Server RCE Bug to Launch DDoS Attacks](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 17, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananBotnet \/ Vulnerability\n[![New Flodrix Botnet Variant](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhFZVmzcURB7mnjZ-xuTUrHVdYczMEBFSNw3b-PXGY0C57BX-c4ApOoudwQyEvnzH1BXtHwT3UPiKLzMvDJvKPOdvUSHEpObkex0BJIHmCBxYW_fygHd1FelmqWlg_3CeuxPQDIyL3LeaHfHWU7cQ8Fx69cipwpwszsdFSSDPemhJwwEhdnSzyy6TV2MJYn\/s728-rw-e365\/Langflow-AI.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhFZVmzcURB7mnjZ-xuTUrHVdYczMEBFSNw3b-PXGY0C57BX-c4ApOoudwQyEvnzH1BXtHwT3UPiKLzMvDJvKPOdvUSHEpObkex0BJIHmCBxYW_fygHd1FelmqWlg_3CeuxPQDIyL3LeaHfHWU7cQ8Fx69cipwpwszsdFSSDPemhJwwEhdnSzyy6TV2MJYn\/s728-rw-e365\/Langflow-AI.jpg)\nCybersecurity researchers have called attention to a new campaign that's actively exploiting a recently disclosed critical security flaw in Langflow to deliver the **Flodrix** botnet malware.\n\"Attackers use the vulnerability to execute downloader scripts on compromised Langflow servers, which in turn fetch and install the Flodrix malware,\" Trend Micro researchers Aliakbar Zahravi, Ahmed Mohamed Ibrahim, Sunil Bharti, and Shubham Singh [said](https:\/\/www.trendmicro.com\/en_us\/research\/25\/f\/langflow-vulnerability-flodric-botnet.html) in a technical report published today.\nThe activity entails the exploitation of **CVE-2025-3248** (CVSS score: 9.8), a missing authentication vulnerability in [Langflow](https:\/\/docs.langflow.org), a Python-based \"visual framework\" for building artificial intelligence (AI) applications.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/sygnia-mdr-guide-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nSuccessful exploitation of the flaw could enable unauthenticated attackers to execute arbitrary code via crafted HTTP requests. It was patched by Langflow in March 2025 with version 1.3.0.\nLast month, the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) [flagged](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/critical-langflow-flaw-added-to-cisa.html) the active exploitation of CVE-2025-3248 in the wild, with the SANS Technology Institute revealing that it detected exploit attempts against its honeypot servers.\nThe latest findings from Trend Micro show that threat actors are targeting unpatched internet-exposed Langflow instances leveraging a [publicly-available](https:\/\/github.com\/verylazytech\/CVE-2025-3248) proof-of-concept (PoC) code to conduct reconnaissance and drop a shell script downloader responsible for retrieving and executing the Flodrix botnet malware from \"80.66.75[.]121:25565.\"\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjt4MLtOrkBxSG-sEP7J0rIcuuy4EZIS3UMVSEf2sKoTce5W6Kw5xEe2v4kpBC4HiKD0oQFqN9veWATd8FYr8LSwIMzmoducRSypGAoFdY1-GYoJJaKtv_6JoKzX0vE3fifYDUtiKHtcZAtQ7muOr2g0knGEL1VNForqc0nMywPgZUvpOCVtKRZewNLzyiH\/s728-rw-e365\/Langflow.png)\nOnce installed, Flodrix sets up communications with a remote server to receive commands over TCP in order to launch distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks against target IP addresses of interest. The botnet also supports connections over the TOR anonymity network.\n\"Since Langflow does not enforce input validation or sandboxing, these payloads are compiled and executed within the server's context, leading to [remote code execution],\" the researchers said. \"Based on these steps, the attacker is likely profiling all vulnerable servers and uses the collected data to identify high-value targets for future infections.\"\nTrend Micro said it identified the unknown threat actors to be hosting different downloader scripts on the same host used to fetch Flodrix, suggesting that the campaign is undergoing active development.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nFlodrix is assessed to be an evolution of another botnet called [LeetHozer](https:\/\/blog.netlab.360.com\/the-leethozer-botnet-en\/) that's linked to the [Moobot group](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2021\/02\/beware-new-matryosh-ddos-botnet.html). The improved variant incorporates the ability to discreetly remove itself, minimize forensic traces, and complicate analysis efforts by obfuscating command-and-control (C2) server addresses and other important indicators.\n\"Another significant change is the introduction of new DDoS attack types, which are now also encrypted, adding a further layer of obfuscation,\" Trend Micro said. \"The new sample also notably enumerates the running processes by opening \/proc directory to access all running processes.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fnew-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html&t=New%20Flodrix%20Botnet%20Variant%20Exploits%20Langflow%20AI%20Server%20RCE%20Bug%20to%20Launch%20DDoS%20Attacks) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=New%20Flodrix%20Botnet%20Variant%20Exploits%20Langflow%20AI%20Server%20RCE%20Bug%20to%20Launch%20DDoS%20Attacks \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fnew-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fnew-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fnew-flodrix-botnet-variant-exploits.html&text=New%20Flodrix%20Botnet%20Variant%20Exploits%20Langflow%20AI%20Server%20RCE%20Bug%20to%20Launch%20DDoS%20Attacks)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[AI Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/AI%20Security)[Botnets](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Botnets)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[ddos](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/ddos)[Langflow](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Langflow)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[network security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/network%20security)[Python](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Python)[remote code execution](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/remote%20code%20execution)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)[Tor network](https:\/