"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers have identified three vulnerabilities in Sitecore Experience Platform (XP) that can be exploited in a chain to achieve pre-authenticated remote code execution. The vulnerabilities include a hard-coded password ('b') in a default user account, path traversal, and an unrestricted file upload flaw. The hard-coded password is embedded in the Sitecore installer version 10.1 and above. If exploited, these vulnerabilities could allow attackers to upload malicious files like web shells, resulting in significant risks for enterprises using Sitecore.",,
