"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/google-warns-of-scattered-spider.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEg8huJBVEvXupx8-XvBHKiOtZyICMh8wyW8VgfSaZUBvMGFFSrkPoFUpsjZfKnTjzwYBGDtM-ey2i7MA6aNhTFrJiZq55ISkJeKR19Qvwfonlc4YMbyfFbY0W83WtvkcMLRm3N5Z6IJdqtBQtgHjjRAPrlgCYSumFtdWLLk8mogc0Vyo3jjOpVTu5p4lApA\/s728-e100\/header.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-eks-security-cheat-d)\n# [Google Warns of Scattered Spider Attacks Targeting IT Support Teams at U.S. Insurance Firms](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/google-warns-of-scattered-spider.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 17, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananThreat Intelligence \/ Identity Security\n[![Scattered Spider Attacks Targeting IT Support Teams](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhqip-_RWEO6KOhE3MGgXX7Q2R6R5xURtI6ZPEWsAwfw0SAQJ3xyzpBFUpyHwz5t5sZ8YFrfn3Nzn0Ba9azKlT_KqVr2o8jpsErETUO2c0WAMTX1X97IGxN44258CfsAZsXdIBodQp7Cif49GwTjqbY5C_mXmqkDhRV_MVgkjCuzuyUg5HZe4B0bORmMHEE\/s728-rw-e365\/hackers.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhqip-_RWEO6KOhE3MGgXX7Q2R6R5xURtI6ZPEWsAwfw0SAQJ3xyzpBFUpyHwz5t5sZ8YFrfn3Nzn0Ba9azKlT_KqVr2o8jpsErETUO2c0WAMTX1X97IGxN44258CfsAZsXdIBodQp7Cif49GwTjqbY5C_mXmqkDhRV_MVgkjCuzuyUg5HZe4B0bORmMHEE\/s728-rw-e365\/hackers.jpg)\nThe notorious cybercrime group known as Scattered Spider (aka UNC3944) that recently targeted [various U.K. and U.S. retailers](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/dragonforce-exploits-simplehelp-flaws.html) has begun to target major insurance companies, according to Google Threat Intelligence Group (GTIG).\n\"Google Threat Intelligence Group is now aware of multiple intrusions in the U.S. which bear all the hallmarks of Scattered Spider activity,\" John Hultquist, chief analyst at GTIG, said in an email Monday.\n\"We are now seeing incidents in the insurance industry. Given this actor's history of focusing on a sector at a time, the insurance industry should be on high alert, especially for social engineering schemes which target their help desks and call centers.\"\nScattered Spider is the name assigned to an amorphous collective that's known for its use of advanced social engineering tactics to breach organizations. In recent months, the threat actors are believed to have forged an alliance with the DragonForce ransomware cartel in the wake of the latter's supposed takeover of [RansomHub](https:\/\/www.esentire.com\/blog\/socket-puppet-how-ransomhub-affiliates-pull-the-strings)'s infrastructure.\n\"The group has repeatedly demonstrated its ability to impersonate employees, deceive IT support teams, and bypass multi-factor authentication (MFA) through cunning psychological tactics,\" SOS Intelligence [said](https:\/\/sosintel.co.uk\/understanding-scattered-spider-tactics-targets-and-defence-strategies\/).\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/google-warns-of-scattered-spider.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/2025-threat-report-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"Often described as 'native English speakers,' they are suspected to operate in or have ties to Western countries, bringing a cultural fluency that makes their phishing and phone-based attacks alarmingly effective.\"\nEarlier this month, ReliaQuest [revealed](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/former-black-basta-members-use.html) that Scattered Spider and DragonForce are increasingly targeting managed service providers (MSPs) and IT contractors to obtain access to several downstream customers through a single compromise.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/google-warns-of-scattered-spider.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjsFtZP1bDfNNzzuzKd1PqKjBcrhV89p8gFzVo7xuy-Xj4Vy88okqMxJ7VLECCUtjyMU9BdjFQ58gqy8LHWdp6kQcgVFXYT5AjrPUKnfJyXtNkUoaXgcOtdm7jO7lMyAQYcLNDIf0yUMw2-Q3id_Msjq4TH8jonzclbU4Kz6PhT-RduVb4nfc541F6YPt-t\/s728-rw-e365\/google.png)\nGoogle-owned Mandiant [said](https:\/\/cloud.google.com\/blog\/topics\/threat-intelligence\/unc3944-proactive-hardening-recommendations?e=48754805) the threat actors often single out large enterprise organizations, likely hoping to land a bigger payday.\nParticularly targeted are enterprises with large help desks and outsourced IT functions that are susceptible to social engineering attacks.\nTo mitigate against tactics utilized by the e-crime group, it's recommended to enhance authentication, enforce rigorous identity controls, implement access restrictions and boundaries to prevent privilege escalation and lateral movement, and train help desk personnel to positively identify employees before resetting their accounts.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fgoogle-warns-of-scattered-spider.html&t=Google%20Warns%20of%20Scattered%20Spider%20Attacks%20Targeting%20IT%20Support%20Teams%20at%20U.S.%20Insurance%20Firms) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Google%20Warns%20of%20Scattered%20Spider%20Attacks%20Targeting%20IT%20Support%20Teams%20at%20U.S.%20Insurance%20Firms \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fgoogle-warns-of-scattered-spider.html) [![Facebook 