"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEg8huJBVEvXupx8-XvBHKiOtZyICMh8wyW8VgfSaZUBvMGFFSrkPoFUpsjZfKnTjzwYBGDtM-ey2i7MA6aNhTFrJiZq55ISkJeKR19Qvwfonlc4YMbyfFbY0W83WtvkcMLRm3N5Z6IJdqtBQtgHjjRAPrlgCYSumFtdWLLk8mogc0Vyo3jjOpVTu5p4lApA\/s728-e100\/header.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-eks-security-cheat-d)\n# [Silver Fox APT Targets Taiwan with Complex Gh0stCringe and HoldingHands RAT Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 17, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananMalware \/ Email Security\n[![Gh0stCringe and HoldingHands RAT Malware](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEisoFBGBznrofikjYaQSHCuffEHsm-LU-IqI92GeHQY9CVX3X29jqKwjyBkzSIG5SytIRjwVe-9lfjx5ZVlGJiCdA6ndQg6N4HUbqDz_tvkPol5EHmWB4NtWyyEA914VPYHlpexL_6Hg5cCRkl3VjhSliAmKICyQ_-apU3YQiH_sAPF9PQylgQJAnb4aqNh\/s728-rw-e365\/Taiwan-cyberattack.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEisoFBGBznrofikjYaQSHCuffEHsm-LU-IqI92GeHQY9CVX3X29jqKwjyBkzSIG5SytIRjwVe-9lfjx5ZVlGJiCdA6ndQg6N4HUbqDz_tvkPol5EHmWB4NtWyyEA914VPYHlpexL_6Hg5cCRkl3VjhSliAmKICyQ_-apU3YQiH_sAPF9PQylgQJAnb4aqNh\/s728-rw-e365\/Taiwan-cyberattack.jpg)\nCybersecurity researchers are warning of a new phishing campaign that's targeting users in Taiwan with malware families such as HoldingHands RAT and Gh0stCringe.\nThe activity is part of a broader campaign that delivered the [Winos 4.0](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/05\/hackers-use-fake-vpn-and-browser-nsis.html) malware framework earlier this January by [sending phishing messages](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/02\/silver-fox-apt-uses-winos-40-malware-in.html) impersonating Taiwan's National Taxation Bureau, Fortinet FortiGuard Labs [said](https:\/\/www.fortinet.com\/blog\/threat-research\/threat-group-targets-companies-in-taiwan) in a report shared with The Hacker News.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjjzOTzX8fxPo8m-J1-TYLW6y3bXQ79rkNpHzeXVW14qRSDgSxqdTyGiqKuKoymvuv9Q06UT-JXtbv94OSdFnvi9sq-AA4xsrgeTiKPVp4od1Gu6KYfA_7xBWv4i0NvZzseYqf9XeeRfDdnqSviavrXtyCK6i_eFo5TjcdiyX046qOIdilTagPqcoIZIWQ0\/s728-e100\/report-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/2025-threat-report-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe cybersecurity company said it identified additional malware samples through continuous monitoring and that it observed the same threat actor, referred to as Silver Fox APT, using malware-laced PDF documents or ZIP files distributed via phishing emails to deliver Gh0stCringe and a malware strain based on HoldingHands RAT.\nIt's worth noting that both [HoldingHands RAT](https:\/\/any.run\/cybersecurity-blog\/gh0stbins-chinese-rat-malware-analysis\/) (aka Gh0stBins) and [Gh0stCringe](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/09\/new-report-uncovers-three-distinct.html) are variants of a known remote access trojan called Gh0st RAT, which is widely used by Chinese hacking groups.\n[![Silver Fox APT Targets Taiwan](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgD9cSmCYhSbU1H_UnVaXY_C2-RuJ8zBBJu_3MR2dspeoEiZfh5GFIVv1OEAJGG1kfn9A0i0bKctExUh1wOtp9HFVU_-WxOxNtiVtTyldGqHJM1w6k76mV7EuVKxLHkVe-uHqnc1JK3v8yP2fJG2TGP1BCa5E_VGs2Dk6hVEwTO5cUgdmLGPEqb-nO_vbs0\/s728-rw-e365\/zip.jpg)\nThe starting point of the attack is a phishing email that masquerades as messages from the government or business partners, employing lures related to taxes, invoices, and pensions to persuade recipients into opening the attachment. Alternate attack chains have been found to leverage an embedded image that, when clicked, downloads the malware.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhlYEDkAs7BIqeKz4Xu5tAJYxtw8U6bGRLX02dbaWUHpQf2ZpsAahdAHn7Xqdfp3TbH9_KHmiRWOvndcuuyoWFX-UktKpwHOYHT_-NNu_iKUCl9yQ65faIy3s_qiNsom0Ml9XyLBC0_-oPnEq-4KB7Hu8Q__tmQ-3KZRUiLF1CX2JeyS_N1wfjR6zo4HM2L\/s728-rw-e365\/download.jpeg)\nThe PDF files, in turn, contain a link that redirects prospective targets to a download page hosting a ZIP archive. Present within the file are several legitimate executables, shellcode loaders, and encrypted shellcode.\nThe multi-stage infection sequence entails the use of the shellcode loader to decrypt and execute the shellcode, which is nothing but DLL files sideloaded by the legitimate binaries using DLL side-loading techniques. Intermediate payloads deployed as part of the attack incorporate anti-VM and privilege escalation so as to ensure that the malware runs unimpeded on the compromised host.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/security-zscaler \"Cybersecurity\")\nThe attack culminates with the execution of \"msgDb.dat,\" which implements command-and-control (C2) functions to collect user information and download additional modules to facilitate file management and remote desktop capabilities.\nFortinet said it also discovered the threat actor propagating Gh0stCringe via PDF attachments in phishing emails that take users to document download HTM pages.\n\"The attack chain comprises numerous snippets of shellcode and loaders, making the attack flow complex,\" the company said. \"Across winos, HoldingHands, and Gh0stCringe, this threat group continuously evolves its malware and distribution strategies.\"\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsilver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html&t=Silver%20Fox%20APT%20Targets%20Taiwan%20with%20Complex%20Gh0stCringe%20and%20HoldingHands%20RAT%20Malware) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Silver%20Fox%20APT%20Targets%20Taiwan%20with%20Complex%20Gh0stCringe%20and%20HoldingHands%20RAT%20Malware \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsilver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/silver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsilver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fsilver-fox-apt-targets-taiwan-with.html&text=Silver%20Fox%20APT%20Targets%20Taiwan%20with%20Complex%20Gh0stCringe%20and%20HoldingHands%20RAT%20Malware)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[DLL side-loading](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/DLL%20side-loading)[email security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/email%20security)[Fortinet](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Fortinet)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Phishing](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Phishing)[privilege escalation](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/privilege%20escalati