"markdown": "X\n[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Microsoft fixes Surface Hub boot issues with emergency update\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/)\n\n\n# Microsoft fixes Surface Hub boot issues with emergency update\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * June 17, 2025\n  * 10:06 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/03\/26\/Windows.jpg)\nMicrosoft has released an emergency update to fix a known issue causing startup failures for some Surface Hub v1 devices running Windows 10.\nAs the company explained when it [acknowledged](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-kb5060533-update-triggers-boot-errors-on-surface-hub-v1-devices\/) this issue last week, users see Secure Boot Violation errors on affected devices, prompting them to check the Secure Boot Policy in setup.\nThese boot problems only impact Surface Hub v1 systems running Windows 10, version 22H2, after installing the June 2025 Windows security update ([KB5060533](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/help\/5060533)). Microsoft also noted that these boot problems do not affect Surface Hub 2S and Surface Hub 3 devices.\nWhile the company released a mitigation one day after discovering it to ensure that other systems would not be impacted after installing the buggy update, it also rolled out an emergency out-of-band update (KB5063159) to address this issue on Monday.\n\"This update prevents Surface Hub v1 devices from encountering a start failure issue. The start failure issue was observed when some Surface Hub v1 devices installed the update KB5060533,\" [Microsoft said](https:\/\/support.microsoft.com\/en-us\/topic\/june-16-2025-kb5063159-os-build-19045-5968-out-of-band-14c3bec4-7d9f-4626-b099-63a0c73b8c88).\n\"On June 11, 2025, we paused the update KB5060533 offering for Surface Hub v1 to prevent new devices from experiencing the failure. If you installed earlier updates, only the new updates contained in this package will be downloaded and installed on your device.\"\n![Secure Boot Violation error](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2025\/Secure-Boot-Violation.jpg)_Secure Boot Violation error ()_\n\u200b\u200bThe KB5060533 Windows update behind this issue [fixes another bug](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-server-emergency-update-fixes-hyper-v-vm-freezes-restart-issues\/) that triggers unexpected restarts or freezes on some Hyper-V virtual machines with Windows 10, Windows 11, and Windows Server.\nLast week, Microsoft [issued another emergency update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/) (KB5063060) to address an Easy Anti-Cheat incompatibility issue, causing some Windows 11 24H2 systems to reboot with blue screen of death errors.\nRedmond also [released](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-2025-patch-tuesday-fixes-exploited-zero-day-66-flaws\/) security updates for 66 security flaws last Tuesday, including a publicly disclosed Windows SMB privilege escalation vulnerability ([CVE-2025-33073](http:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2025-33073)) and an actively exploited WebDAV (Web Distributed Authoring and Versioning) zero-day ([CVE-2025-33053](http:\/\/msrc.microsoft.com\/update-guide\/en-US\/advisory\/CVE-2025-33053)).\nThe June 2025 Patch Tuesday Windows updates addressed ten critical vulnerabilities, eight allowing attackers to gain remote code execution on unpatched devices, while the other two can let them escalate privileges.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft: KB5060533 update triggers boot errors on Surface Hub v1 devices](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-kb5060533-update-triggers-boot-errors-on-surface-hub-v1-devices\/)\n[Windows 11 24H2 emergency update fixes Easy Anti-Cheat BSOD issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/)\n[New Secure Boot flaw lets attackers install bootkit malware, patch now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-secure-boot-flaw-lets-attackers-install-bootkit-malware-patch-now\/)\n[Windows 10 KB5060533 cumulative update released with 7 changes, fixes](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-10-kb5060533-cumulative-update-released-with-7-changes-fixes\/)\n[Microsoft shares script to restore inetpub folder you shouldn\u2019t delete](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-shares-script-to-restore-inetpub-folder-you-shouldnt-delete\/)\n  * [Boot Issues](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/boot-issues\/)\n  * [Emergency Update](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/emergency-update\/)\n  * [KB5060533](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/kb5060533\/)\n  * [Out-of-Band](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/out-of-band\/)\n  * [Secure Boot](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/secure-boot\/)\n  * [Surface Hub](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/surface-hub\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 10](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-10\/)\n  * [Windows 10 22H2](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-10-22h2\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/how-to-automate-it-ticket-handling-with-ai-and-tines\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/b\/bleepingcomputer\/Webcast-20250709-V02_400x500.jpg)](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)\n[![Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/b\/bleepingcomputer\/Webcast-20250709-V02_400x500.jpg)](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=display&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Microsoft: June Windows Server security updates cause DHCP issues ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-windows-server-security-updates-cause-dhcp-issues\/)\n  * [ ![ChatGPT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) ChatGPT Search gets an upgrade as OpenAI takes aim at Google ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/chatgpt-search-gets-an-upgrade-as-openai-takes-aim-at-google\/)\n  * [ ![Grafana](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Over 46,000 Grafana instances exposed to account takeover bug ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/over-46-000-grafana-instances-exposed-to-account-takeover-bug\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Overdue a password health-check? Audit your Active Directory for free ](https:\/\/specopssoft.com\/product\/specops-password-auditor\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/tines-vs-python-understanding-alternative-approaches-to-automation\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=article-sidebar)\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now!](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now! ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=build_robust_windows_service_farid_q2_25&utm_content=build_robust_windows_service_farid&utm_term=display)\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-fixes-surface-hub-boot-issues-with-emergency-update\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n\n\n[![Picus](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/GD-300-600-Laptop-v2.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_e&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_e:sidebar)\n![](https:\/\/ad.doub