"markdown": "![near field communication, payment card, phone](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_pexels_anete_lusina_6353663_84f284bc93.jpg)\nImage: Anete Lusina via Pexels\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)June 17th, 2025\n# Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFC\nRussian cybersecurity researchers have identified the first domestic data-stealing attacks involving a modified version of legitimate near field communication (NFC) software, in what appears to be a test run for a broader campaign. \nThe report involves SuperCard, a previously identified malicious variant of the legitimate [NFCGate program](https:\/\/therecord.media\/android-malware-atm-stealing-czech-banks), originally designed to relay NFC data between two devices in close proximity. Cybercriminals have long abused NFC technology in schemes to siphon funds from victims\u2019 bank accounts. \nIn previous SuperCard attacks targeting European banks, hackers used compromised Android smartphones to relay data from victims\u2019 physical payment cards to attacker-controlled devices. The stolen data was then used to carry out ATM transactions. If this method failed, the hackers resorted to transferring funds directly from the victims\u2019 bank accounts to other accounts. \nMoscow-based cybersecurity firm F6 said in its [report](https:\/\/habr.com\/ru\/companies\/F6\/news\/918840\/) on Tuesday that SuperCard was first deployed against Android users in Russia in May, after the malware was initially [spotted](https:\/\/therecord.media\/new-payment-card-scam-involves-malware-tap) in Italy in April. Italian security company Cleafy reported that the tool is distributed as malware-as-a-service (MaaS) and is offered by \u201cChinese-speaking\u201d actors. \nAttackers used social engineering techniques to trick victims into downloading SuperCard, disguising it as a legitimate app, F6 said. Once installed, the malware identifies which payment system \u2014 Visa, Mastercard, American Express, UnionPay or JCB \u2014 is used by the victim, allowing criminals to exploit the data for fraudulent transactions. \nWhat sets SuperCard apart from previous NFCGate-based malware, according to researchers, is its commercial distribution strategy. For the first time, the malware has been openly marketed through Telegram channels \u2014 including Chinese-language ones \u2014 and sold via subscription plans with customer support. F6 says it was advertised as capable of targeting customers of major banks in the U.S., Australia and Europe. \nF6 first [observed](https:\/\/www.f6.ru\/blog\/nfcgate\/) NFCGate-based attacks \u2014 prior to SuperCard\u2019s spread \u2014 in Russia in January. Since then, attackers have expanded their toolset with multiple modifications. In the first quarter of 2025, total losses from NFCGate variants in Russia amounted to 432 million rubles (approximately $5.5 million), with over 175,000 Android devices infected, according to F6. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFC)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFC )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Malware](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/malware)\n  * [Technology](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/technology)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [NFC](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/nfc)\n  * [mobile](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/mobile)\n  * [banking](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/banking)\n  * [Android](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/android)\n  * [Russia](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/russia)\n  * [MaaS](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/maas)\n  * [payment cards](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/payment-card)\n  * [credit cards](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/credit-card)\n  * [fraud](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/fraud)\n  * [scam](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scam)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/d887de47708acda42945a172d61c0ca2_38f4568326.png)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\n[Daryna Antoniuk](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/daryna-antoniuk)\nis a reporter for Recorded Future News based in Ukraine. She writes about cybersecurity startups, cyberattacks in Eastern Europe and the state of the cyberwar between Ukraine and Russia. She previously was a tech reporter for Forbes Ukraine. Her work has also been published at Sifted, The Kyiv Independent and The Kyiv Post.\n## Briefs\n  * [Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFCJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/supercard-nfc-banking-malware-russia)\n  * [8.4 million people affected by data breach at Indian car share company ZoomcarJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/8-million-affected-zoomcar-data-breach)\n  * [Police dismantle Archetyp dark web drug market, arrest administratorJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/archetyp-market-dark-web-takedown-europol)\n  * [Hackers impersonating US government compromise email account of prominent Russia researcherJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/keir-giles-russia-researcher-email-hacked)\n  * [CISA warns of SimpleHelp ransomware compromises after string of retail attacksJune 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cisa-warns-of-simplehelp-ransomware-compromises)\n  * [Predator spotted in Mozambique for first time, another sign of spyware\u2019s availabilityJune 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/predator-spyware-mozambique)\n  * [Dozens arrested across Asia in global infostealer malware crackdownJune 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-arrested-infostealer-interpol-crackdown)\n  * [FIN6 cybercriminals pose as job seekers on LinkedIn to hack recruiters June 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/fin6-recruitment-scam-malware-campaign)\n  * [Hundreds of Russian devices hit by Rare Werewolf cryptomining attacksJune 10th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-devices-hit-by-rare-werewolf-crypto-mining)\n\n\n## [Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence![Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/artificial_eyes_generative_ai_chinas_military_intelligence_a374052c6a.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/artificial-eyes-generative-ai-chinas-military-intelligence)\n## [GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT![GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_gray_alpha_1600x600_e9dc818048.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/grayalpha-uses-diverse-infection-vectors-deploy-powernet-loader-netsupport-rat)\n## [Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified![Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_predator_1600x600_2acdebaf2c.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/predator-still-active-new-links-identified)\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n",,
