"title": "Sitecore CMS exploit chain starts with hardcoded 'b' password",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/sitecore-cms-exploit-chain-starts-with-hardcoded-b-password\/",,
"summary": "A series of vulnerabilities in Sitecore Experience Platform (XP) allows attackers to remotely execute code without authentication. The exploit chain involves three key vulnerabilities: a hardcoded password, a Zip Slip flaw, and an issue with the Sitecore PowerShell Extensions (SPE) module. Patches addressing these vulnerabilities were released in May 2025, and the risks of exploitation remain high due to detailed technical disclosure.",,
