"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/uk-fines-23andme-for-profoundly-damaging-breach-exposing-genetics-data\/",,
"summary": "The UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) fined genetic testing provider 23andMe \u00a32.31 million ($3.12 million) following a security breach due to credential stuffing attacks. This attack exposed sensitive personal data, including genotype and health information, of 4.1 million users in the UK and Germany, and 1 million Ashkenazi Jews. The breach went undetected from April to September 2023, and resulted in multiple class-action lawsuits. Following the breach, 23andMe enabled two-factor authentication and required password resets to prevent future incidents.",,
