"title": "New Veeam RCE flaw lets domain users hack backup servers",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-veeam-rce-flaw-lets-domain-users-hack-backup-servers\/",,
"summary": "Veeam has released security updates to address several vulnerabilities in Veeam Backup & Replication (VBR), including a critical remote code execution (RCE) flaw CVE-2025-23121. This vulnerability affects domain-joined installations of VBR and can be exploited by authenticated domain users, allowing remote code execution on the backup server. The flaw is particularly concerning as many organizations have their backup servers joined to a Windows domain, contrary to best practices. Ransomware gangs and other threat actors have exploited similar vulnerabilities in the past, highlighting the critical nature of this security issue. Patches have been made available in version 12.3.2.3617.",,
