"markdown": "![spiders](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_spiders_34f0a0fb73.jpg)\nImage: Hans Isacson via Unsplash\/Photomosh\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)June 17th, 2025\n# Scattered Spider hackers targeting insurance industry following retail hits, Google warns\nA group of hackers behind a recent string of attacks on retail stores in the U.K. and U.S. has shifted its focus to insurance firms in recent days, according to cybersecurity researchers. \nSecurity analysts at Google\u2019s Threat Intelligence Group published a warning this week to insurance companies, writing that it is \u201cnow aware of multiple intrusions in the US which bear all the hallmarks of Scattered Spider activity.\u201d \n\u201cGiven this actor's history of focusing on a sector at a time, the insurance industry should be on high alert, especially for social engineering schemes which target their help desks and call centers,\u201d said John Hultquist, chief analyst at the company. \nCharles Carmakal, the chief technology officer of Manidant, which is also owned by Google, added in comments to Recorded Future News that there is more than one U.S.-based insurance company that has been attacked and noted that the targeting of the insurance industry began around a week and a half ago. \nGoogle declined to offer specifics about the victims but several insurance companies have reported attacks over the last week. Erie Insurance [released](https:\/\/www.erieinsurance.com\/newsroom\/press-releases\/2025\/erie-insurance-network-outage) a statement Tuesday about a recent cybersecurity issue that it [reported](https:\/\/www.sec.gov\/Archives\/edgar\/data\/922621\/000092262125000023\/erie-20250607.htm) to regulators at the Securities Exchange Commission (SEC) last week. \nAlthough the company did not attribute the hack to a specific group, it told Recorded Future News in a statement on Tuesday that it is still dealing with network outages caused by \u201cproactive measures\u201d Erie Insurance officials had to take. The company, which is a major provider of homeowner, automobile and commercial insurance, said it now has control of its system and has seen \u201cno evidence of ransomware.\u201d \nPhiladelphia Insurance Companies [was also hit](https:\/\/www.phly.com\/) with a cyber incident that began on June 9. The company is now facing a network outage that has affected its phone and email systems, as well as its online applications. The company replaced its website with a notice that said they are working with law enforcement to recover from the cyberattack. \nLike Erie, Philadelphia Insurance Companies did not provide details about the hackers behind the incident. \nA major Swedish insurance firm was also by cybercriminals this week who took down the company\u2019s website. \nBeyondTrust\u2019s Fletcher Davis said insurance companies are attractive targets for Scattered Spider because they typically handle [vast amounts of sensitive customer data](https:\/\/therecord.media\/globe-life-updated-sec-filing-hackers-extortion-data-breach), including personal information, financial records and health data, which can be [targeted for data theft](https:\/\/therecord.media\/landmark-admin-data-breach-insurance-industry) and extortion. \n## Scattered Spider moves from retail\nGoogle officials attributed the insurance company campaign to a threat actor they call UNC3944, which they said overlaps with Scattered Spider but has \u201cmore narrowly defined\u201d boundaries. \nThe [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scattered-spider) cybercriminal operation has caused angst across the cybersecurity industry over the past month for its alleged attacks on the [retail industry in the U.S. and U.K](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert). \nThe group, an offshoot of the larger cybercrime community known as The Com, is best known for leveraging its English-speaking members to conduct attacks where they impersonate members of a company\u2019s IT department. \nBeyondTrust\u2019s Davis noted that Insurance companies often have large help desk and outsourced IT functions that are susceptible to social engineering attacks, which align directly with Scattered Spider\u2019s competencies and playbooks. \n\u201cThe global and complex structure of many of these insurance firms makes comprehensive security and detection of malicious activity significantly difficult as well,\u201d he said. \nScattered Spider has used the tactic in high-profile attacks on casino giants [MGM Resorts](https:\/\/therecord.media\/mgm-cyberattack-response) and [Caesars Entertainment](https:\/\/finance.yahoo.com\/news\/caesars-entertainment-paid-millions-ransom-185252473.html) \u2014 eventually using their access to steal data or deploy ransomware. Despite a [series](https:\/\/therecord.media\/five-scattered-spider-members-charged-breaches-11-million-theft) of [arrests](https:\/\/therecord.media\/another-hacker-scattered-spider-charged) and [convictions](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-member-noah-urban-guilty-plea), the group resurfaced with the attacks on the retail industry. \nThe incidents [prompted the FBI](https:\/\/www.cnn.com\/2025\/05\/16\/politics\/cybercriminal-group-targets-us-retailers) to deliver cyber-intelligence briefings to major retailers over the last month after reports that [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-challenge-for-FBI) had [shifted their focus](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert) from attacks on outlets in the U.K. to U.S.-based companies. U.K. retailers like [Marks & Spencer](https:\/\/therecord.media\/british-retailer-marks-spencer-insurance), the [Co-op](https:\/\/therecord.media\/co-op-cyberattack-uk-company-fears-hackers-still-in-system) and luxury retailer [Harrods](https:\/\/therecord.media\/harrods-cyberattack-uk-retailer) were attacked as well as stores like [Victoria\u2019s Secret](https:\/\/therecord.media\/victorias-secret-website-down-security-incident), [North Face](https:\/\/therecord.media\/north-face-customer-accounts-data-breach-notification), , [Adidas](https:\/\/www.adidas-group.com\/en\/data-security-information), [Dior, and Tiffany](https:\/\/www.chosun.com\/english\/industry-en\/2025\/05\/26\/ORM5MULB7NEM7EBUFVXHVLSB4A\/). \nLast week, Google [published a report](https:\/\/therecord.media\/google-warns-cybercriminals-targeting-salesforce-apps) about the same group tricking companies into giving them widespread access to a popular Salesforce tool, allowing them to steal sensitive data and move through other parts of the organizations. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Scattered Spider hackers targeting insurance industry following retail hits, Google warns)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Scattered Spider hackers targeting insurance industry following retail hits, Google warns )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [Government](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/government)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [retail](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/retail)\n  * [insurance](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/insurance)\n  * [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scattered-spider)\n  * [Google](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/google)\n  * [Mandiant](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/mandiant)\n  * [the Com](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/the-com)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFCJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/supercard-nfc-banking-malware-russia)\n  * [8.4 million people affected by data breach at Indian car share company ZoomcarJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/8-million-affected-zoomcar-data-breach)\n  * [Police dismantle Archetyp dark web drug market, arrest administratorJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/archetyp-market-dark-web-takedown-europol)\n  * [Hackers impersonating US government compromise email account of prominent Russia researcherJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/keir-giles-russia-researcher-email-hacked)\n  * [CISA warns of SimpleHelp ransomware compromises after string of retail attacksJune 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cisa-warns-of-simplehelp-ransomware-compromises)\n  * [Predator spotted in Mozambique for first time, another sign of spyware\u2019s availabilityJune 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/predator-spyware-mozambique)\n  * [Dozens arrested across Asia in global infostealer malware crackdownJune 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-arrested-infostealer-interpol-crackdown)\n  * [FIN6 cybercriminals pose as job seekers on LinkedIn to hack recruiters June 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/fin6-recruitment-scam-malware-campaign)\n  * [Hundreds of Russian devices hit by Rare Werewolf cryptomining attacksJune 10th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/russian-devices-hit-by-rare-werewolf-crypto-mining)\n\n\n## [Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence![Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/artificial_eyes_generative_ai_chinas_military_intelligence_a374052c6a.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/artificial-eyes-generative-ai-chinas-military-intelligence)\n## [GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT![GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_gray_alpha_1600x600_e9dc818048.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/grayalpha-uses-diverse-infection-vectors-deploy-powernet-loader-netsupport-rat)\n## [Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified![Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_predator_1600x600_2acdebaf2c.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/predator-still-active-new-links-identified)\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n## [Measuring the US-China AI Gap![Measuring the US-China AI Gap](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/BLOG_ta_2025_0508_Main_Feature_0873ea3526.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/measuring-the-us-china-ai-gap)\n",,
