"summary": "A zero-day vulnerability in Google Chrome, identified as CVE-2025-2783, was exploited by the threat actor TaxOff to deploy the Trinper backdoor. The vulnerability allowed a sandbox escape leading to infection through phishing emails targeting Russian organizations. The Trinper backdoor, written in C++, was used to gather information, record keystrokes, and establish a foothold for further command execution. The campaign was part of Operation ForumTroll, and shares similarities with activities by the group Team46.",,
