"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/veeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEg8huJBVEvXupx8-XvBHKiOtZyICMh8wyW8VgfSaZUBvMGFFSrkPoFUpsjZfKnTjzwYBGDtM-ey2i7MA6aNhTFrJiZq55ISkJeKR19Qvwfonlc4YMbyfFbY0W83WtvkcMLRm3N5Z6IJdqtBQtgHjjRAPrlgCYSumFtdWLLk8mogc0Vyo3jjOpVTu5p4lApA\/s728-e100\/header.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/wiz-eks-security-cheat-d)\n# [Veeam Patches CVE-2025-23121: Critical RCE Bug Rated 9.9 CVSS in Backup & Replication](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/veeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 18, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananVulnerability \/ Data Protection\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhCw3K17yq0vOkBrMgi9DYNFpQE1kuS62UeEKK71qfi_-rOgg6i7gJ9pRh13lxx3rbY4x0xOsXDOsEHWnnri1DTHf7JJeXhJICEEGe9c91tTGJPSlBw9XTAQG7c5p4ZZncHObK4Duly-gwD9pi1iDph_44GbZFcoCoksm0jv14rcUQ_ll6oNHsJd0WxwWHS\/s728-rw-e365\/veeam.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEhCw3K17yq0vOkBrMgi9DYNFpQE1kuS62UeEKK71qfi_-rOgg6i7gJ9pRh13lxx3rbY4x0xOsXDOsEHWnnri1DTHf7JJeXhJICEEGe9c91tTGJPSlBw9XTAQG7c5p4ZZncHObK4Duly-gwD9pi1iDph_44GbZFcoCoksm0jv14rcUQ_ll6oNHsJd0WxwWHS\/s728-rw-e365\/veeam.jpg)\nVeeam has rolled out patches to contain a critical security flaw impacting its Backup & Replication software that could result in remote code execution under certain conditions.\nThe security defect, tracked as CVE-2025-23121, carries a CVSS score of 9.9 out of a maximum of 10.0.\n\"A vulnerability allowing remote code execution (RCE) on the Backup Server by an authenticated domain user,\" the company [said](https:\/\/www.veeam.com\/kb4743) in an advisory.\nCVE-2025-23121 impacts all earlier version 12 builds, including 12.3.1.1139. It has been addressed in version 12.3.2 (build 12.3.2.3617). Security researchers at CODE WHITE GmbH and watchTowr have been credited with discovering and reporting the vulnerability.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/veeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/2025-threat-report-d \"Cybersecurity\")\nCybersecurity company Rapid7 [noted](https:\/\/www.rapid7.com\/blog\/post\/etr-critical-veeam-backup-replication-cve-2025-23121\/) that the update likely addresses [concerns](https:\/\/infosec.exchange\/@codewhitesec\/114241026482611250) shared by CODE WHITE in late March 2025 that the patch put in place to plug a similar hole ([CVE-2025-23120](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/03\/veeam-and-ibm-release-patches-for-high.html), CVSS score: 9.9) could be bypassed.\nAlso addressed by Veeam is another flaw in the same product (CVE-2025-24286, CVSS score: 7.2) that allows an authenticated user with the Backup Operator role to modify backup jobs, which could result in arbitrary code execution.\nThe American company separately patched a vulnerability that affected Veeam Agent for Microsoft Windows (CVE-2025-24287, CVSS score: 6.1) that permits local system users to modify directory contents, leading to code execution with elevated permissions. The issue has been patched in version 6.3.2 (build 6.3.2.1205).\nAccording to Rapid7, [more than 20% of its incident response cases](https:\/\/www.rapid7.com\/blog\/post\/2024\/09\/09\/etr-multiple-vulnerabilities-in-veeam-backup-and-replication\/) in 2024 involved either the access or exploitation of Veeam, once a threat actor has already established a foothold in the target environment.\nWith security flaws in Veeam backup software [becoming a prime target for attackers](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2024\/11\/cisa-alert-active-exploitation-of.html) in recent years, it's crucial that customers update to the latest version of the software with immediate effect.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fveeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html&t=Veeam%20Patches%20CVE-2025-23121%3A%20Critical%20RCE%20Bug%20Rated%209.9%20CVSS%20in%20Backup%20%26%20Replication) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Veeam%20Patches%20CVE-2025-23121%3A%20Critical%20RCE%20Bug%20Rated%209.9%20CVSS%20in%20Backup%20%26%20Replication \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fveeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/veeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fveeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fveeam-patches-cve-2025-23121-critical.html&text=Veeam%20Patches%20CVE-2025-23121%3A%20Critical%20RCE%20Bug%20Rated%209.9%20CVSS%20in%20Backup%20%26%20Replication)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Backup Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Backup%20Security)[critical infrastructure](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/critical%20infrastructure)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[data protection](https:\/\/thehackernew