"summary": "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) has added a Linux kernel vulnerability, CVE-2023-0386, to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) catalog. This vulnerability, caused by an improper ownership management in the OverlayFS subsystem, allows unauthorized users to escalate their privileges. Although it was patched in early 2023, it is actively exploited in the wild. The vulnerability can be exploited by creating a SUID binary owned by root and executing it, mostly affecting systems using OverlayFS.",,
