"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiZLvfEiF0mIN5JYAVIj4efKgKKH8SaMBLIYVSTIfHTfaA8mpwqvAxp8wWSq73qsUYWQus2_tM5Kzw9weRVdQ0RYavu30YG1Xr0ol0renB6HmhjtI9IvxO1-MCUJ4TnLqnePPgBEe4CqDKmPQvfOXX6nOpNDkewgEAHURtd7YhX1SbyTBVMIVC6GBXwkAOa\/s728-e100\/ai-security-readiness-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/ai-security-readiness-d)\n# [CISA Warns of Active Exploitation of Linux Kernel Privilege Escalation Vulnerability](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 18, 2025 _\ue804_ Ravie LakshmananLinux \/ Vulnerability\n[![Linux Kernel Privilege Escalation Vulnerability](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgLeHx1PBqUOOY6yZdqU5k5NOXyVL3tBd5pfVa7wZnok4nWRgDKyMxDO3xwMCLTh7sVoLCjOZ8h2KyIyejwjMZ1iUCY38DVrzPdW_YeG5wwm2Y_vixQHtzZmj0vCQx4pxdrXBiu_DSMTamRU4jDV_zXwaHZdSPiQ6GBZwBchacgT-v53YdtiWHrguu_BhCH\/s728-rw-e365\/linux.jpg)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgLeHx1PBqUOOY6yZdqU5k5NOXyVL3tBd5pfVa7wZnok4nWRgDKyMxDO3xwMCLTh7sVoLCjOZ8h2KyIyejwjMZ1iUCY38DVrzPdW_YeG5wwm2Y_vixQHtzZmj0vCQx4pxdrXBiu_DSMTamRU4jDV_zXwaHZdSPiQ6GBZwBchacgT-v53YdtiWHrguu_BhCH\/s728-rw-e365\/linux.jpg)\nThe U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) on Tuesday [placed](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/news-events\/alerts\/2025\/06\/17\/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog) a security flaw impacting the Linux kernel in its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities ([KEV](https:\/\/www.cisa.gov\/known-exploited-vulnerabilities-catalog)) catalog, stating it has been actively exploited in the wild.\nThe vulnerability, [CVE-2023-0386](https:\/\/nvd.nist.gov\/vuln\/detail\/CVE-2023-0386) (CVSS score: 7.8), is an improper ownership bug in the Linux kernel that could be exploited to escalate privileges on susceptible systems. It was patched in early 2023.\n\"Linux kernel contains an improper ownership management vulnerability, where unauthorized access to the execution of the setuid file with capabilities was found in the Linux kernel's OverlayFS subsystem in how a user copies a capable file from a nosuid mount into another mount,\" the agency said.\n[![Cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/2025-threat-report-d \"Cybersecurity\")\n\"This uid mapping bug allows a local user to escalate their privileges on the system.\"\nIt's currently not known how the security flaw is being exploited in the wild. In a report published in May 2023, Datadog said the vulnerability is trivial to exploit and that it works by tricking the kernel into creating a SUID binary owned by root in a folder like \"\/tmp\" and executing it.\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html)](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEjz9pHBXqTHWnI7jgN1ZQamYRWgzCsfRXnajGqiOicrvZrHicwozZvNrtm5xwLTLadkvrQttpQkji0XkuUCZPauK4_DAuk-re9vtcRb_xtxpAvEvCcSqB82Un4FZvjXj46bxTa1wqhscKQsH1sha5CAumlEvd4jLT7QuE_CNMl3UNMlUHDypjGfqMvK-083\/s728-rw-e365\/linux.png)\n\"CVE-2023-0386 lies in the fact that when the kernel copied a file from the overlay file system to the 'upper' directory, it did not check if the user\/group owning this file was mapped in the current user namespace,\" the company [said](https:\/\/securitylabs.datadoghq.com\/articles\/overlayfs-cve-2023-0386\/).\n\"This allows an unprivileged user to smuggle an SUID binary from a 'lower' directory to the 'upper' directory, by using OverlayFS as an intermediary.\"\nLater that year, cloud security firm Wiz detailed two security vulnerabilities dubbed [GameOver(lay)](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2023\/07\/gameoverlay-two-severe-linux.html) (CVE-2023-32629 and CVE-2023-2640) affecting Unix systems that led to similar consequences as CVE-2023-0386.\n\"These flaws allow the creation of specialized executables, which, upon execution, grant the ability to escalate privileges to root on the affected machine,\" Wiz researchers said.\nFederal Civilian Executive Branch (FCEB) agencies are required to apply the necessary patches by July 8, 2025, to secure their networks against active threats.\nFound this article interesting? Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fcisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html&t=CISA%20Warns%20of%20Active%20Exploitation%20of%20Linux%20Kernel%20Privilege%20Escalation%20Vulnerability) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=CISA%20Warns%20of%20Active%20Exploitation%20of%20Linux%20Kernel%20Privilege%20Escalation%20Vulnerability \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fcisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/cisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Fcisa-warns-of-active-exploitation-of.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2