"title": "New Linux udisks flaw lets attackers get root on major Linux distros",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/linux\/new-linux-udisks-flaw-lets-attackers-get-root-on-major-linux-distros\/",,
"summary": "Attackers can exploit two local privilege escalation vulnerabilities (CVE-2025-6018 and CVE-2025-6019) to gain root privileges on major Linux distributions. These flaws impact openSUSE Leap 15, SUSE Linux Enterprise 15, and potentially other systems where udisks is installed by default. The Qualys Threat Research Unit has developed proof-of-concept exploits and strongly advises immediate patching to prevent root access compromises.",,
