"summary": "CISA has alerted U.S. federal agencies about attackers exploiting a vulnerability in the Linux kernel's OverlayFS subsystem (CVE-2023-0386), which allows attackers to gain root privileges. This local privilege escalation flaw is due to improper ownership management in the Linux kernel and affects a wide range of Linux distributions using kernel versions lower than 6.2. Proof-of-concept exploits for this vulnerability have been published, prompting its inclusion in CISA's Known Exploited Vulnerabilities catalog. Agencies have been given a deadline to patch their systems to mitigate this threat.",,
