"title": "1,500+ Minecraft Players Infected by Java Malware Masquerading as Game Mods on GitHub",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/1500-minecraft-players-infected-by-java.html",,
"summary": "A sophisticated malware campaign has targeted over 1,500 Minecraft players with a multi-stage Java-based malware disguised as game mods on GitHub. The malware campaign uses a distribution-as-service model called Stargazers Ghost Network, which involves fake repositories set up to appear like cracked software and game cheats. These repositories host malicious Java loader files that execute a second-stage .NET stealer, affecting devices with Minecraft installed. The malware steals user data, including credentials and tokens, while remaining undetected by antivirus software. The attack was traced back to a Russian-speaking threat actor, potentially linking to financial motivations.",,
