"title": "More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm Episource",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/5-million-affected-episource-data-breach",,
"summary": "A healthcare tech firm, Episource, experienced a data breach where hackers stole sensitive information of over 5 million people. Personal and medical data was accessed, including Social Security numbers, health insurance IDs, and medical records. The breach involved turning off some systems for security, with law enforcement engaged in the investigation. More than 5.4 million people were affected, including those receiving services from doctors or health plans using Episource. Previously, Episource had a similar data breach incident in 2023. The company was acquired by Optum in 2023, which has had its own cybersecurity issues.",,
