"markdown": "![hospital ](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_hospital_3_520fe1cddc.jpg)\nImage: Getty via Unsplash+\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)June 18th, 2025\n# More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm Episource\nA tech firm providing services to the healthcare industry said hackers stole information on millions of people in an incident discovered in early February. \nDocuments filed with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services Department show that 5,418,866 people had information taken from Episource. \nCalifornia-based Episource disclosed in filings with the U.S. Department of Health and Human Services that more than 5.4 million people had their information taken, and said in a [notice](https:\/\/response.idx.us\/episource\/) on its website that hackers had copied files from their system between January 27 and February 6. \nThe data stolen includes: \n  * Social Security numbers\n  * Health insurance ID numbers\n  * Medicaid-Medicare ID numbers\n  * Medical records covering doctor, diagnoses, test results, images, care and treatment\n\n\nLaw enforcement was involved in the investigation and the company said it was forced to turn off its computer system in order to protect customers and their patients. The company did not respond to requests for comment. \nEpisource says it provides medical coding and risk adjustment services to doctors, health plans and health companies. \nVictims of the data breach either received services from one of the doctors or were members of a health plan that uses Episource\u2019s tools. \nThe company said it is working with its customers to help them coordinate providing the notice to everyone affected. \nEpisource urged victims to watch their benefit statements in case they are ever charged for services they did not receive. The company set up a call line for victims with questions. \nSome customers of Episource published their own breach notices, including [Sharp Healthcare](https:\/\/www.sharp.com\/episource-data-breach). \nEpisource [previously dealt with](https:\/\/oag.ca.gov\/system\/files\/EpiSource%20Notice%20Letter%20%285.27.23%29.pdf) a data breach in 2023 that leaked much of the same information for an unknown number of people. \nEpisource was founded in 2006 and [acquired](https:\/\/lawire.com\/episources-role-in-shaping-healthcare-technology-and-its-synergy-with-optum\/) in 2023 by [Optum](https:\/\/klasresearch.com\/vendor-ratings\/episource-an-optum-company\/73467) \u2014 a healthcare giant owned by UnitedHealth that was itself at the [center of a large cybersecurity incident](https:\/\/therecord.media\/ransomware-unitedhealth-costs-billions-still-climbing) last year. Optum itself was forced to take some of its systems offline last February after a [ransomware attack on its subsidiary Change Healthcare](https:\/\/therecord.media\/change-healthcare-blackcat-alphv-incident-drags-on). \nThat attack ended up leaking the sensitive healthcare information of [190 million people](https:\/\/therecord.media\/unitedhealth-updates-change-healthcare-data-breach-190-million). \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm Episource)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm Episource )\n\n\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [News Briefs](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [healthcare](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/healthcare)\n  * [data breach](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-breach)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm EpisourceJune 18th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/5-million-affected-episource-data-breach)\n  * [Pro-Cambodian hacktivists launch attacks on Thai government sites amid border disputeJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/pro-cambodian-hacktivists-target-thai-websites-amid-border-dispute)\n  * [Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFCJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/supercard-nfc-banking-malware-russia)\n  * [8.4 million people affected by data breach at Indian car share company ZoomcarJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/8-million-affected-zoomcar-data-breach)\n  * [Police dismantle Archetyp dark web drug market, arrest administratorJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/archetyp-market-dark-web-takedown-europol)\n  * [Hackers impersonating US government compromise email account of prominent Russia researcherJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/keir-giles-russia-researcher-email-hacked)\n  * [CISA warns of SimpleHelp ransomware compromises after string of retail attacksJune 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cisa-warns-of-simplehelp-ransomware-compromises)\n  * [Predator spotted in Mozambique for first time, another sign of spyware\u2019s availabilityJune 12th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/predator-spyware-mozambique)\n  * [Dozens arrested across Asia in global infostealer malware crackdownJune 11th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/dozens-arrested-infostealer-interpol-crackdown)\n\n\n## [Threats to the 2025 NATO Summit![Threats to the 2025 NATO Summit](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/threats_2025_nato_summit_745b9b78b0.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/threats-2025-nato-summit)\n## [Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence![Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/artificial_eyes_generative_ai_chinas_military_intelligence_a374052c6a.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/artificial-eyes-generative-ai-chinas-military-intelligence)\n## [GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT![GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_gray_alpha_1600x600_e9dc818048.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/grayalpha-uses-diverse-infection-vectors-deploy-powernet-loader-netsupport-rat)\n## [Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified![Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_predator_1600x600_2acdebaf2c.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/predator-still-active-new-links-identified)\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n",,
