"title": "North Korea targeting Indian crypto job applicants with malware",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/north-korea-india-crypto-applicants",,
"summary": "North Korean hackers, identified as the group 'Famous Chollima,' are targeting job applicants in India's cryptocurrency and blockchain industry. They create fake employers to lure individuals into phishing schemes, eventually installing malware labeled 'PylangGhost' onto victims' devices. The hackers exploit skill-testing sites, impersonating genuine companies like Coinbase and Robinhood, to eventually induce applicants into copying and pasting code that downloads malware. This malware can steal browser credentials and session cookies from MacOS and Windows devices.",,
