"summary": "The content describes how Keir Giles, a British expert on Russia, was targeted by a sophisticated phishing attack that used app-specific passwords (ASPs) to bypass multi-factor authentication (MFA). The attack was reportedly executed by a Russian state-sponsored group and was identified by Google's Threat Intelligence Group. The attackers used social engineering tactics to trick Giles into creating and sharing ASPs, providing full access to his email accounts. The incident highlights a vulnerability in Google's services, specifically around the use of less secure apps. This attack method, masquerading as communication from the State Department, may be the first of its kind and indicates potential new phishing tactics.",,
