"title": "New Linux Flaws Enable Full Root Access via PAM and Udisks Across Major Distributions",,
"url": "https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/new-linux-flaws-enable-full-root-access.html",,
"summary": "Cybersecurity researchers have discovered two local privilege escalation (LPE) vulnerabilities in Linux systems, CVE-2025-6018 and CVE-2025-6019. These flaws impact major Linux distributions, including openSUSE Leap 15, SUSE Linux Enterprise 15, Ubuntu, Debian, and Fedora. CVE-2025-6018 allows an attacker to escalate privileges to 'allow_active' via PAM, while CVE-2025-6019 enables escalation to root through libblockdev via the udisks daemon. Both vulnerabilities can be chained for a full system takeover, allowing attackers with any active GUI or SSH session to gain root access. A related path traversal flaw, CVE-2025-6020, was also disclosed in Linux PAM and patched in version 1.7.1.",,
