"summary": "The article details how the Russian state-sponsored hacking group APT29 leverages Google app-specific passwords to bypass two-factor authentication (2FA) in targeted phishing campaigns. The threat actors impersonate the U.S. Department of State to deceive high-profile academics and critics of Russia into setting up app-specific passwords, granting persistent access to their Gmail accounts. Google and Citizen Lab identified and reported on this sophisticated campaign. The attackers also employ Ukrainian themes and use residential proxies to evade detection, highlighting a geopolitical dimension to these cyber threats.",,
