"markdown": "[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\nContact\/Tip Us\n[ _\uf0e0_ Reach out to get featured\u2014contact us to send your exclusive story idea, research, hacks, or ask us a question or leave a comment\/feedback! ](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/p\/submit-news.html)\nFollow Us On Social Media\n[_\uf167_](https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/c\/thehackernews?sub_confirmation=1)\n[_\uf09e_ RSS Feeds](https:\/\/feeds.feedburner.com\/TheHackersNews) [_\uf0f3_ Email Alerts](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html#email-outer) [_\uf2c6_ Telegram Channel](https:\/\/t.me\/+wKrQxniFO1Q1OTRk)\n[![AWS EKS Security Best Practices](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEiZLvfEiF0mIN5JYAVIj4efKgKKH8SaMBLIYVSTIfHTfaA8mpwqvAxp8wWSq73qsUYWQus2_tM5Kzw9weRVdQ0RYavu30YG1Xr0ol0renB6HmhjtI9IvxO1-MCUJ4TnLqnePPgBEe4CqDKmPQvfOXX6nOpNDkewgEAHURtd7YhX1SbyTBVMIVC6GBXwkAOa\/s728-e100\/ai-security-readiness-d.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/ai-security-readiness-d)\n# [Uncover LOTS Attacks Hiding in Trusted Tools \u2014 Learn How in This Free Expert Session](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html)\n_\ue802_ Jun 19, 2025 _\ue804_ The Hacker NewsCybersecurity \/ Threat Hunting\n[![](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEg0VPtMwQsrwEF3r5YndhUUFRWoBF2bU2_8hoZ4p1iCyA1Hxjrk09MCTEtLLce9ttRz63LQxeKK3xktIa4PRnnsFkH14z0J7MBkVz1-2B1LOjiviEy7VahqoMEAKhX3BqDoo7TdHZ_76tL7ium_H2AAcFauh7aETMcmjA8RzCcWU1X45g5BkyVMhTBf5d4\/s728-rw-e365\/webinars.gif)](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article)\nMost cyberattacks today don't start with loud alarms or broken firewalls. They start quietly\u2014inside tools and websites your business already trusts.\nIt's called \"[Living Off Trusted Sites](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article)\" (LOTS)\u2014and it's the new favorite strategy of modern attackers. Instead of breaking in, they blend in.\nHackers are using well-known platforms like Google, Microsoft, Dropbox, and Slack as launchpads. They hide malicious code inside routine traffic, making it incredibly difficult for traditional defenses to detect them.\nAnd here's the scary part: many security teams don't even realize it's happening\u2014until it's too late.\n## Why You're Not Seeing These Attacks[#](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html#why-you-re-not-seeing-these-attacks)\nLOTS tactics don't look suspicious at first glance. There's no malware signature to flag, and no unusual IP address to trace. It's legitimate traffic\u2014until it's not.\nAttackers are exploiting:\n  * **Common business tools** like Teams, Zoom, and GitHub\n  * **Shortened or vanity URLs** to redirect users\n  * **Trusted cloud services** to host malicious payloads\n\n\nIn short, they're using your trust against you.\n## What You'll Learn in This Free Webinar[#](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html#what-you-ll-learn-in-this-free-webinar)\nJoin Zscaler's top threat hunters for \"**[Threat Hunting Insights from the World's Largest Security Cloud](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article)** \"\u2014a must-attend webinar revealing how stealthy LOTS attacks are detected and stopped in real time. Get frontline tactics to outsmart threats hiding in trusted tools.\nYou'll discover:\n  * \ud83d\udd0d The latest LOTS attack techniques seen in real environments\n  * \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f How threat hunters caught stealthy attackers hiding inside \"normal\" traffic\n  * \ud83d\udea8 What trusted tools are being misused right now by threat actors\n  * \ud83d\udd10 Simple, proven ways to improve LOTS detection and reduce risk\n  * \ud83d\udd2d What's coming next: trends shaping the future of stealth-based attacks\n\n\n[![](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html)](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article)\nThis session is for anyone responsible for defending their organization\u2014whether you're a security leader trying to stay ahead of evolving threats, a threat hunter sharpening your detection skills, or part of an IT or SOC team overwhelmed by false positives and stealthy attacks. If your company relies on SaaS apps, cloud platforms, or collaborative tools, you're already a target\u2014and LOTS tactics are designed to slip past unnoticed.\n[Watch this Webinar](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article)\nAttackers today aren't trying to break in\u2014they're blending in. By hiding inside trusted tools and platforms, they bypass traditional defenses and operate in plain sight. This webinar gives you rare access to real-world detection stories and techniques from experts who analyze trillions of security signals every day inside the world's largest inline security cloud.\n[Reserve your seat now](https:\/\/thehacker.news\/threat-hunting-insights?source=article) to gain exclusive frontline insights, proven tactics, and smarter strategies that could save your team hours\u2014and stop attacks before they succeed.\nFound this article interesting? This article is a contributed piece from one of our valued partners. Follow us on and to read more exclusive content we post.\nSHARE [_\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n_\uf1e0_ Share\n[_\ue80a_](javascript:void\\(0\\)) [_\uf1d4_ Share on Hacker News](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Funcover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html&t=Uncover%20LOTS%20Attacks%20Hiding%20in%20Trusted%20Tools%20%E2%80%94%20Learn%20How%20in%20This%20Free%20Expert%20Session) _\uf0e0_ Share on Email [_\uf232_ Share on WhatsApp](https:\/\/api.whatsapp.com\/send?text=Uncover%20LOTS%20Attacks%20Hiding%20in%20Trusted%20Tools%20%E2%80%94%20Learn%20How%20in%20This%20Free%20Expert%20Session \u2014 https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Funcover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html) [![Facebook Messenger](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/2025\/06\/uncover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html)Share on Facebook Messenger](fb-messenger:\/\/share\/?link=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Funcover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html&app_id=280117418781535) [_\uf2c6_ Share on Telegram](https:\/\/telegram.me\/share\/url?url=https%3A%2F%2Fthehackernews.com%2F2025%2F06%2Funcover-lots-attacks-hiding-in-trusted.html&text=Uncover%20LOTS%20Attacks%20Hiding%20in%20Trusted%20Tools%20%E2%80%94%20Learn%20How%20in%20This%20Free%20Expert%20Session)\n[SHARE _\uf1e0_](javascript:void\\(0\\))\n[Cloud security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Cloud%20security)[cybersecurity](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity)[cybersecurity webinar](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/cybersecurity%20webinar)[Malware](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Malware)[Microsoft](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Microsoft)[SaaS Security](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/SaaS%20Security)[Threat Hunting](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Hunting)[Threat Intelligence](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Threat%20Intelligence)[Zscaler](https:\/\/thehackernews.com\/search\/label\/Zscaler)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgJOseRkjmPrTbm87L4lYW_5Gqo6lXoBbN7tWbCa6tDc4bK8uzxlRQoz6uwVFf8x1x21dzStYp_Az64eL6T_jF3pB0z4Pjnb717hN4KDZz1tehoBrK8Zn-Vjv6p8cWMGlHBfFCc-Qrfm7kGrgTTuv5BP2GGeiAtOY3Hg6NVjCNvejGVpBRahyphenhyphenQyQOXLZ8DI\/s728-rw-e365\/find-saas-account.png)](https:\/\/thehackernews.uk\/find-saas-account)\n[![c](https:\/\/blogger.googleusercontent.com\/img\/b\/R29vZ2xl\/AVvXsEgf3htno2k3FtYs6xQqRvYIOqrmqOFoTyPa6DkEV_Ep9gaj9Jk4LG66X10Z6104CmB-S1pCY0hnpwwe3JvBMRuZeTlRZbnoDgEpJnY111NJurNHeqUlJ8XSTcvr2Lvy0lGPsN1nU-4msWTfy_Qyn7v5MxxExQXugkSTz5T90lzcmdC0xfVO9WwB2ax8VU0C\/w300-e100\/chain.png)](https:\/\/thehackerne