"markdown": "X\n[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * DuckDuckGo beefs up scam defense to block fake stores, crypto sites\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/)\n\n\n# DuckDuckGo beefs up scam defense to block fake stores, crypto sites\nBy \n###### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n  * June 19, 2025\n  * 08:00 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![DuckDuckGo](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2022\/08\/26\/duckduckgo-mobile.jpg)\nThe DuckDuckGo web browser has expanded its built-in Scam Blocker tool to protect against a broader range of online scams, including fake e-commerce, cryptocurrency exchanges, and \"scareware\" sites.\nDuckDuckGo is a privacy-focused web browser and search engine that doesn't track users' searchers or browsing history.\nThe browser, which became available as a public beta for [macOS](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-for-mac-enters-public-beta-now-available-to-everyone\/) and [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-browser-for-windows-available-for-everyone-as-public-beta\/) in October 2022 and June 2023, respectively, blocks all trackers by default, does not engage in personalized search profiling, and offers powerful anonymity tools.\nScam Blocker has been a component of the browser's privacy toolkit since its launch in 2018, protecting users attempting to visit known malware distribution and phishing URLs.\nAs part of the [latest update](https:\/\/spreadprivacy.com\/p\/b00d6763-b789-4e21-a0d6-fb35eed7acaf\/), in addition to blocking phishing sites and malware, Scam Blocker now also detect and block the following:\n  * Fake e-commerce stores\n  * [Scam investment](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/cryptocurrency\/us-seized-82-million-in-crypto-linked-to-romance-baiting-scams\/) and crypto trading sites\n  * Survey scams with false cash rewards\n  * Scareware (fake virus alerts prompting [bogus tech support](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/ftc-will-send-255-million-to-victims-of-tech-support-scams\/))\n  * [Malvertising](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-says-malvertising-campaign-impacted-1-million-pcs\/) (malicious tracker-powered ads)\n\n\nWhen the user attempts to load a webpage, the tool scans the URLs locally against a continually updated (every 20 minutes) threat list supplied by cybersecurity firm Netcraft.\nRare or unknown threats are checked against DuckDuckGo servers using an [anonymous cryptographic process](https:\/\/duckduckgo.com\/duckduckgo-help-pages\/threat-protection\/scam-blocker#:~:text=How%20does%20Scam%20Blocker%20work%20anonymously%20in%20DuckDuckGo%20browsers%3F), ensuring that this process doesn't compromise user privacy.\nWhen a scam site is detected, users are served a prominent warning message giving them the option to leave or ignore it and proceed to the risky site.\n![DuckDuckGo's Scam Blocker warning on the desktop and on mobile](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1220909\/2025\/June\/warning\\(1\\).jpg)**DuckDuckGo's Scam Blocker warning on the desktop (left) and on mobile (right)**_Source: DuckDuckGo_\nDuckDuckGo notes that, unlike Chrome, Safari, or Firefox, which rely on Google Safe Browsing and hence share data with Google, Scam Blocker offers privacy-first protection with no external data sharing.\nScam Blocker is activated in the browser by default and requires no account to work effectively.\nPrivacy Pro subscribers get a significant perk, as Scam Blocker will work across any internet apps on their devices when the [DuckDuckGo VPN](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-launches-a-premium-privacy-pro-vpn-service\/) is active, covering other browsers as well.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Instagram ads mimicking BMO, EQ Bank are finance scams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/instagram-ads-mimicking-bmo-eq-bank-are-finance-scams\/)\n[Five plead guilty to laundering $36 million stolen in investment scams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/five-plead-guilty-to-laundering-36-million-stolen-in-investment-scams\/)\n[FBI warns of NFT airdrop scams targeting Hedera Hashgraph wallets](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/fbi-warns-of-nft-airdrop-scams-targeting-hedera-hashgraph-wallets\/)\n[Apple Safari exposes users to fullscreen browser-in-the-middle attacks](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/apple-safari-exposes-users-to-fullscreen-browser-in-the-middle-attacks\/)\n[Google Chrome to use on-device AI to detect tech support scams](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/google-chrome-to-use-on-device-ai-to-detect-tech-support-scams\/)\n  * [Browser](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/browser\/)\n  * [DuckDuckGo](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/duckduckgo\/)\n  * [Scam](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/scam\/)\n  * [Scam Blocker](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/scam-blocker\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\n##### [Bill Toulas](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/bill-toulas\/)\nBill Toulas is a tech writer and infosec news reporter with over a decade of experience working on various online publications, covering open-source, Linux, malware, data breach incidents, and hacks. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/telecom-giant-viasat-breached-by-chinas-salt-typhoon-hackers\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Avast](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/Avast_400x500_v1.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_a&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_a:banner )\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) Microsoft: June Windows Server security updates cause DHCP issues ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-windows-server-security-updates-cause-dhcp-issues\/)\n  * [ ![Ghost Spider](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) Hackers switch to targeting U.S. insurance companies ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/google-warns-scattered-spider-hackers-now-target-us-insurance-companies\/)\n  * [ ![Veeam](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) New Veeam RCE flaw lets domain users hack backup servers ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-veeam-rce-flaw-lets-domain-users-hack-backup-servers\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![ChainLink Phishing: Designed to Bypass Traditional Defenses. Watch the Webinar. ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) ChainLink Phishing: Designed to Bypass Traditional Defenses. Watch the Webinar.  ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/resources\/webinars\/chainlink-phishing-the-chained-sequences-of-modern-phishing?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=banner&utm_campaign=chainlink_phishing_june)\n  * [ ![Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/tines-vs-python-understanding-alternative-approaches-to-automation\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=article-sidebar)\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now!](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/) Learn to build a strong Windows service\u2014protect your systems from malware. Start now! ](https:\/\/www.threatlocker.com\/?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=sponsor&utm_campaign=build_robust_windows_service_farid_q2_25&utm_content=build_robust_windows_service_farid&utm_term=display)\n\n\n[![Picus](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/300-600-Laptopv1.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_d&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_d:sidebar)\n![](https:\/\/ad.doubleclick.net\/favicon.ico?ad=300x250&ad_box_=1&adnet=1&showad=1&size=250x250)![](https:\/\/widgets.outbrain.com\/images\/widgetIcons\/achoice.svg)\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto-sites\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/duckduckgo-beefs-up-scam-defense-to-block-fake-stores-crypto