"summary": "Microsoft announced new security defaults for Windows 365 Cloud PCs. These defaults, starting in the second half of 2025, will disable clipboard, drive, USB, and printer redirections by default to reduce data theft and malware risks. USB redirections affecting only low-level device access exclude devices like USB mice, keyboards, and webcams. Additionally, at the kernel level, virtualization-based security, Credential Guard, and hypervisor-protected code integrity (HVCI) are enabled by default. The changes will also affect Azure Virtual Desktop, with alerts for IT admins visible in the Intune Admin Center.",,
