"markdown": "  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Security](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/)\n  * Webinar: Stolen credentials are the new front door to your network\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/)\n\n\n# Webinar: Stolen credentials are the new front door to your network\nBy \n###### [BleepingComputer](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * June 19, 2025\n  * 12:33 PM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Hand stealing data](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/06\/18\/hand.jpg)\nCybercriminals no longer need zero-day exploits or other vulnerabilities to breach your systems\u2014these days, they just log in.\nOn July 9th at 2:00 PM ET, BleepingComputer and SC Media will co-host a live webinar with identity security expert Darren Siegel of Specops Software (part of Outpost24), exploring how threat actors are increasingly breaching networks by simply logging in with stolen credentials.\nThe webinar \"_[Stolen credentials: The New Front Door to Your Network](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=bc_article&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)_ \" will unpack the real-world mechanics behind credential-based attacks and how to stop them before damage is done.\nSpecops Software, part of Outpost24, brings expertise in password security and authentication controls, helping organizations defend against modern identity threats and credential-based intrusions.\nIn this must-watch webinar, you will learn how attackers are shifting from exploiting vulnerabilities to simply logging in using large-scale credential abuse, with insights into the infostealer economy and how enterprises can defend against these increasingly effective threats.\u200b\n[![Webinar promotion](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/security\/w\/webinars\/stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door\/Webcast-20250709-V02_1200x628.jpg)](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=bc_article&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)\nInfostealer malware campaigns have [exploded in recent years](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/info-stealer\/), stealing billions of credentials from infected systems and feeding a booming cybercrime marketplace.\nThese types of attacks are becoming the norm, with threat actors regularly buying stolen credentials for as little as a few dollars on Telegram and [dark web marketplaces](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/russian-market-emerges-as-a-go-to-shop-for-stolen-credentials\/).\nIn other approaches, credentials are gathered using [password-spray attacks against Microsoft 365](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/botnet-targets-basic-auth-in-microsoft-365-password-spray-attacks\/), weak MFA implementations using [adversary-in-the-middle phishing kits](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/new-rockstar-2fa-phishing-service-targets-microsoft-365-accounts\/), and [brute-force VPN portals](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/black-basta-ransomware-creates-automated-tool-to-brute-force-vpns\/) for initial access.\n**The upcoming webinar will cover:**\n  * How infostealers harvest and distribute login credentials\n  * Methods used to bypass MFA and hijack sessions\n  * Techniques to detect compromised accounts and recover from breaches\n  * Strategies to harden identity surfaces and prevent lateral movement\n\n\nThe event will be hosted by Lawrence Abrams (BleepingComputer), Adrian Sanabria (SC Media), and Darren Siegel from Outpost24, the parent company of Specops Software.\n**Don't miss this opportunity to gain real-world insights and defense strategies directly from cybersecurity practitioners.**\n**[Register now to secure your spot!](https:\/\/www.scworld.com\/cybercast\/stolen-credentials-the-new-front-door-to-your-network?utm_source=partner-campaign&utm_medium=bc_article&utm_campaign=sc-cybercast-bleepingcomputer-2025-july)**\n  * [Credentials](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/credentials\/)\n  * [Cybersecurity](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/cybersecurity\/)\n  * [Infostealer](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/infostealer\/)\n  * [Password Spray](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/password-spray\/)\n  * [Specops](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/specops\/)\n  * [Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/webinar\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/artificial-intelligence\/openais-sam-altman-discusses-gpt-5-release-date\/)\n\n\n###### Comments have been disabled for this article.\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Windows Server](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/05\/16\/thumb\/292x176_Windows-Server.jpg) Microsoft: June Windows Server security updates cause DHCP issues ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-june-windows-server-security-updates-cause-dhcp-issues\/)\n  * [ ![Ghost Spider](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2024\/11\/25\/thumb\/292x176_ghost-spider-center.jpg) Hackers switch to targeting U.S. insurance companies ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/google-warns-scattered-spider-hackers-now-target-us-insurance-companies\/)\n  * [ ![Linux](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) New Linux udisks flaw lets attackers get root on major Linux distros ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/linux\/new-linux-udisks-flaw-lets-attackers-get-root-on-major-linux-distros\/)\n\n\nSponsor Posts\n  * [ ![Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh.](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) Elevate your cyber defense: Learn to design powerful Blue Team playbooks with Wazuh. ](https:\/\/wazuh.com\/?utm_source=bleepingcomputer.com&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=wazuh_bleepingcomputer)\n  * [ ![Inside the 2025 Verizon DBIR - Register for the Webinar](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) Inside the 2025 Verizon DBIR - Register for the Webinar ](https:\/\/layerx.easywebinar.live\/layerx-verizon-dbir?utm_source=bleeping&utm_campaign=DBIRwebinar26062025)\n  * [ ![ChainLink Phishing: Designed to Bypass Traditional Defenses. Watch the Webinar. ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) ChainLink Phishing: Designed to Bypass Traditional Defenses. Watch the Webinar.  ](https:\/\/keepaware.com\/resources\/webinars\/chainlink-phishing-the-chained-sequences-of-modern-phishing?utm_source=bleeping_computer&utm_medium=banner&utm_campaign=chainlink_phishing_june)\n  * [ ![AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) AI is a data-breach time bomb: Read the new report ](https:\/\/info.varonis.com\/en\/state-of-data-security-report-2025?utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=bleepingcomputer_referral&utm_content=article)\n  * [ ![Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/) Still writing scripts in Python? Tines has a better way -- no custom code required ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/tines-vs-python-understanding-alternative-approaches-to-automation\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=article-sidebar)\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/ \"Back to Top\")\n[](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Login\n[ ](javascript:; \"Close\")\n#### Reporter\n###### Help us understand the problem. What is going on with this comment?\nSubmitting...\n[SUBMIT](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/webinar-stolen-credentials-are-the-new-front-door-to-your-network\/ \"Submit\")\n",,
