"title": "Aflac says it stopped ransomware attack launched by \u2018sophisticated cybercrime group\u2019",,
"url": "https:\/\/therecord.media\/aflac-cyberattack-potential-data-breach",,
"summary": "Aflac, a Georgia-based insurance company, experienced a cybersecurity incident caused by a sophisticated cybercrime group known for using social engineering tactics. The attack attempted to deploy ransomware but was halted within hours, though some data was stolen. The stolen data includes claims, health information, Social Security numbers, and other personal details of Aflac's stakeholders like customers and employees. The threat actors involved may be linked to a group called Scattered Spider, previously known for attacking large retail and now targeting the insurance sector. Aflac continues to operate without disruption to its services. They have established a helpline for those concerned about data breaches and are providing identity theft protection.",,
