"markdown": "![Aflac Tower](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/large_AFLAC_Tower_Columbus_Georgia_ffb593d7ae.jpg)\nThe Aflac Tower in Columbus, Georgia. Image: Wikimedia Commons \/ CC BY-SA 3.0\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)June 20th, 2025\n# Aflac says it stopped ransomware attack launched by \u2018sophisticated cybercrime group\u2019\nInsurance company Aflac said a \u201csophisticated cybercrime group\u201d breached its systems and may have stolen data during an attempted ransomware attack. \nThe Georgia-based company [published](https:\/\/www.prnewswire.com\/news-releases\/aflac-incorporated-discloses-cybersecurity-incident-302487036.html?tc=eml_cleartime) a statement and [notified](https:\/\/www.sec.gov\/ix?doc=\/Archives\/edgar\/data\/0000004977\/000000497725000128\/afl-20250620.htm) the Securities Exchange Commission (SEC) on Friday, explaining that the incident was initially identified on June 12. \nThe intrusion was stopped \u201cwithin hours\u201d and no business functions were affected by ransomware, Aflac said. But the company admitted that there were files stolen during the incident and said officials are determining the total number of affected individuals. \nThe potentially impacted files contain information on claims, health information, Social Security numbers and other personal data of \u201ccustomers, beneficiaries, employees, agents, and other individuals in its U.S. business.\u201d The company said it can still \u201cunderwrite policies, review claims, and otherwise service our customers as usual.\u201d \nAflac did not respond to requests for comment but explained in a press release that the attack is something \u201cmany insurance companies are currently experiencing.\u201d \n\u201cThis was part of a cybercrime campaign against the insurance industry,\u201d the company said, adding that the hackers \u201cused social engineering tactics to gain access to our network.\u201d \nA source working with Aflac on the incident explained explained that the threat actors did not identify themselves but the characteristics of the attack bear the hallmarks of [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scattered-spider), a loosely affiliated group of English-speaking cybercriminals known for gaining access to major companies by posing as IT workers. \nGoogle warned earlier this week that Scattered Spider had recently [shifted from attacking](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-suspected-retail-hackers-google-alert) large retail companies [to targeting the insurance industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/scattered-spider-targeting-insurance-sector-following-retail-attacks). \nErie Insurance and the Philadelphia Insurance Companies each published notices this week about cyberattacks. A major Swedish insurance firm also was by cybercriminals this week who took down the company\u2019s website. \nCharles Carmakal, the chief technology officer of Mandiant, previously told Recorded Future News that there is more than one U.S.-based insurance company that has been attacked and noted that the targeting of the insurance industry began around a week and a half ago. \n\u201cGiven this actor's history of focusing on a sector at a time, the insurance industry should be on high alert, especially for social engineering schemes which target their help desks and call centers,\u201d said John Hultquist, chief analyst at Google. \nLast week, Google [published a report](https:\/\/therecord.media\/google-warns-cybercriminals-targeting-salesforce-apps) about Scattered Spider tricking companies into giving them widespread access to a popular Salesforce tool, allowing them to steal sensitive data and move through other parts of the organizations. \nAflac created a phone line for those concerned that their data may have been accessed and is providing two years of identity theft protection to anyone who calls. \nIn 2023, Aflac [reported a data breach in Japan](https:\/\/therecord.media\/millions-of-aflac-zurich-insurance-customers-in-japan-have-data-leaked-after-breach) that affected 1.3 million customers holding cancer-related insurance policies. \nAflac is one of the largest insurance companies in the U.S. and Japan, [reporting](https:\/\/s24.q4cdn.com\/367535798\/files\/doc_financials\/2024\/q4\/4Q24-final-Press-Release.pdf) a total 2024 revenue of $18.9 billion. In the SEC filing, the company said the \u201cfull scope and potential ultimate impact\u201d on their finances is unknown. \n  * [](https:\/\/news.ycombinator.com\/submitlink?u=&t=Aflac says it stopped ransomware attack launched by \u2018sophisticated cybercrime group\u2019)\n  * [](https:\/\/bsky.app\/intent\/compose?text=Aflac says it stopped ransomware attack launched by \u2018sophisticated cybercrime group\u2019 )\n\n\n  * [Industry](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n  * [Cybercrime](https:\/\/therecord.media\/news\/cybercrime)\n  * [News](https:\/\/therecord.media\/)\n\n\nGet more insights with the \nRecorded Future\nIntelligence Cloud.\n[Learn more.](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/platform?mtm_campaign=ad-unit-record)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_300x1050_1_0f2f11757e.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\n[![Recorded Future](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/2025_0514_Record_Ads_970x250_1_d144dbf901.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/?utm_source=therecord&utm_medium=ad)\nTags\n  * [Aflac](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/aflac)\n  * [insurance](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/insurance)\n  * [Cyberattack](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/cyberattack)\n  * [Scattered Spider](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/scattered-spider)\n  * [data breach](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/data-breach)\n  * [financial](https:\/\/therecord.media\/tag\/financial)\n\n\nNo previous article\nNo new articles\n[![Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/cms.therecord.media\/uploads\/format_webp\/DSC_0283_1_a6f4e4e315.jpg)](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\n[Jonathan Greig](https:\/\/therecord.media\/author\/jonathan-greig)\nis a Breaking News Reporter at Recorded Future News. Jonathan has worked across the globe as a journalist since 2014. Before moving back to New York City, he worked for news outlets in South Africa, Jordan and Cambodia. He previously covered cybersecurity at ZDNet and TechRepublic.\n## Briefs\n  * [Alleged Ryuk ransomware gang member arrested in Ukraine and extradited to US June 19th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/alleged-ryuk-member-arrest-ukraine-extradited-us)\n  * [Argentina uncovers suspected Russian spy ring behind disinformation campaignsJune 19th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/argentina-russia-spies-disinformation-project-lakhta)\n  * [More than 5 million affected by data breach at healthcare tech firm EpisourceJune 18th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/5-million-affected-episource-data-breach)\n  * [Pro-Cambodian hacktivists launch attacks on Thai government sites amid border disputeJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/pro-cambodian-hacktivists-target-thai-websites-amid-border-dispute)\n  * [Russia detects first SuperCard malware attacks skimming bank data via NFCJune 17th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/supercard-nfc-banking-malware-russia)\n  * [8.4 million people affected by data breach at Indian car share company ZoomcarJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/8-million-affected-zoomcar-data-breach)\n  * [Police dismantle Archetyp dark web drug market, arrest administratorJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/archetyp-market-dark-web-takedown-europol)\n  * [Hackers impersonating US government compromise email account of prominent Russia researcherJune 16th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/keir-giles-russia-researcher-email-hacked)\n  * [CISA warns of SimpleHelp ransomware compromises after string of retail attacksJune 13th, 2025](https:\/\/therecord.media\/cisa-warns-of-simplehelp-ransomware-compromises)\n\n\n## [Threats to the 2025 NATO Summit![Threats to the 2025 NATO Summit](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/threats_2025_nato_summit_745b9b78b0.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/threats-2025-nato-summit)\n## [Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence![Artificial Eyes: Generative AI in China\u2019s Military Intelligence](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/artificial_eyes_generative_ai_chinas_military_intelligence_a374052c6a.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/artificial-eyes-generative-ai-chinas-military-intelligence)\n## [GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT![GrayAlpha Uses Diverse Infection Vectors to Deploy PowerNet Loader and NetSupport RAT](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_gray_alpha_1600x600_e9dc818048.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/grayalpha-uses-diverse-infection-vectors-deploy-powernet-loader-netsupport-rat)\n## [Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified![Predator Still Active, with New Client and Corporate Links Identified](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_cover_predator_1600x600_2acdebaf2c.jpg)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/predator-still-active-new-links-identified)\n## [Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents![Russia-Aligned TAG-110 Targets Tajikistan with Macro-Enabled Word Documents](https:\/\/cms.recordedfuture.com\/uploads\/format_webp\/recordedfuture_insikt_Main_Featured_Banner_1600x600_2a9d7e6d39.png)](https:\/\/www.recordedfuture.com\/research\/russia-aligned-tag-110-targets-tajikistan-with-macro-enabled)\n",,
