"title": "Cloudflare blocks record 7.3 Tbps DDoS attack against hosting provider",,
"url": "https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/cloudflare-blocks-record-73-tbps-ddos-attack-against-hosting-provider\/",,
"summary": "Cloudflare mitigated a record-breaking distributed denial of service (DDoS) attack in May 2025 targeting a hosting provider. The attack peaked at 7.3 Tbps, delivering 37.4 TB of data within 45 seconds. The attack utilized 122,145 source IP addresses across 161 countries and involved multiple vectored attacks such as UDP floods and NTP amplification. Cloudflare's Magic Transit service was used for mitigation, dispersing attack traffic across 477 data centers. Indicators of Compromise (IoCs) were shared through Cloudflare's DDoS Botnet Threat Feed to help other organizations preemptively block similar threats.",,
