"markdown": "[![push](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/p\/push\/Push-Security-Display-Ad-Scattered-Spider.png)](https:\/\/pushsecurity.com\/webinar\/scatteredspider?utm_campaign=12905815-FY25_Bleeping+Computer&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_medium=sponsored-content)\n  * [Home](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/)\n  * [News](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/)\n  * Windows Snipping Tool now lets you create animated GIF recordings\n\n\n  * [ ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-snipping-tool-now-lets-you-create-animated-gif-recordings\/)\n\n\n# Windows Snipping Tool now lets you create animated GIF recordings\nBy \n###### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n  * June 22, 2025\n  * 10:11 AM\n  * [0](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-snipping-tool-now-lets-you-create-animated-gif-recordings\/#comment_form)\n\n\n![Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/content\/hl-images\/2025\/04\/02\/Windows-11.jpg)\n\u200bMicrosoft announced that the Windows screenshot and screencast Snipping Tool utility is getting support for exporting animated GIF recordings.\nThis new capability is rolling out to Windows 11 Insiders in the Canary and Dev Channels, who have updated the app to version 11.2505.21.0.\n\"In this update, we are adding GIF export for screen recordings \u2013 designed to boost your productivity and turn quick captures into shareable moments,\" [said](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/06\/19\/gif-export-in-snipping-tool-begins-rolling-out-to-windows-insiders\/) Dave Grochocki, a Principal Product Manager Lead at Microsoft.\n\"Please note: GIF export is limited to videos that are 30 seconds or less. If your video is longer than 30 seconds, Snipping Tool will offer to export the first 30 seconds of your video instead.\"\nTo begin recording a new GIF, open the Snipping Tool's screen recorder by pressing Win + Shift + R or launching the app and switching to screen recording mode. Start recording your screen, and once the preview opens, click the 'Export GIF' button at the top of the toolbar.\nNext, choose low GIF quality for a smaller size or high quality for a clearer recording, and then copy it directly to your clipboard or save it to your hard drive.\n![Snipping Tool GIF dialog](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/images\/news\/u\/1109292\/2025\/GIF-popup.png)_Snipping Tool GIF dialog (Microsoft)_\n\u200bLast month, Microsoft [also started testing](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/05\/22\/paint-snipping-tool-and-notepad-updates-with-new-features-begin-rolling-out-to-windows-insiders\/) a new AI-powered 'perfect screenshot' tool that helps precisely capture screen content to avoid cropping and a color picker utility that allows picking color codes using HEX, RGB, or HSL values.\n\"Once activated, perfect screenshot will intelligently resize based on the content in your selection,\" Grochocki said at the time. \"You can also quickly enable perfect screenshot by holding the Ctrl keyboard shortcut after invoking Snipping Tool while selecting a region of your screen.\"\nIn April, Snipping Tool was also updated to [include a Text Extractor feature](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/04\/15\/text-extractor-in-snipping-tool-begins-rolling-out-to-windows-insiders\/) that copies text to the clipboard without actually having to take a screenshot.\nEarlier this year, the company also [added a draw & hold feature](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/03\/13\/snipping-tool-and-notepad-app-updates-begin-rolling-out-to-windows-insiders\/) that helps users draw straight lines and shapes more easily, and [a trim capability](https:\/\/blogs.windows.com\/windows-insider\/2025\/02\/28\/announcing-windows-11-insider-preview-build-22635-5015-beta-channel\/) that helps adjust the start and end times of screen recordings to cut out any unnecessary video snippets from their video.\n[ ![Tines Needle](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/t\/tines\/tines-needle.jpg) ](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n## [Why IT teams are ditching manual patch management](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\nPatching used to mean complex scripts, long hours, and endless fire drills. Not anymore.\nIn this new guide, Tines breaks down how modern IT orgs are leveling up with automation. Patch faster, reduce overhead, and focus on strategic work -- no complex scripts required.\n[Get the free guide](https:\/\/www.tines.com\/access\/guide\/unlocking-it-agility-with-automation-patch-management\/?utm_source=BleepingComputer&utm_medium=paid_media&utm_content=june-in-article-banner)\n### Related Articles:\n[Microsoft adds quick machine recovery to Windows 11 settings](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/microsoft-adds-quick-machine-recovery-to-windows-11-settings\/)\n[Windows 11 Notepad gets AI-powered text writing capabilities](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-notepad-gets-ai-powered-text-writing-capabilities\/)\n[Microsoft testing Windows 11 support for third-party passkeys](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-testing-windows-11-support-for-third-party-passkeys\/)\n[Microsoft unveils new security defaults for Windows 365 Cloud PCs](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/microsoft-unveils-new-security-defaults-for-windows-365-cloud-pcs\/)\n[Windows 11 24H2 emergency update fixes Easy Anti-Cheat BSOD issue](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-11-24h2-emergency-update-fixes-easy-anti-cheat-bsod-issue\/)\n  * [GIF](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/gif\/)\n  * [Microsoft](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/microsoft\/)\n  * [Screen Recording](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/screen-recording\/)\n  * [Snipping Tool](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/snipping-tool\/)\n  * [Video](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/video\/)\n  * [Windows](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows\/)\n  * [Windows 11](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-11\/)\n  * [Windows Insider](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/tag\/windows-insider\/)\n\n\n  * [](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-snipping-tool-now-lets-you-create-animated-gif-recordings\/ \"Print article\")\n\n\n[](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\n##### [Sergiu Gatlan](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/author\/sergiu-gatlan\/)\nSergiu is a news reporter who has covered the latest cybersecurity and technology developments for over a decade. Email or Twitter DMs for tips. \n  * [ Previous Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/offer\/deals\/unlock-lifelong-learning-with-1-000-plus-courses-for-under-20-today-in-this-deal\/)\n  * [Next Article ](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/security\/oxford-city-council-suffers-breach-exposing-two-decades-of-data\/)\n\n\n##### Post a Comment [Community Rules](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/posting-guidelines\/)\n###### You need to login in order to post a comment\nNot a member yet? [Register Now](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/forums\/index.php?app=core&module=global&section=register)\n### You may also like:\n[![Avast](https:\/\/www.bleepstatic.com\/c\/g\/gendigital\/Avast_400x500_v1.png)](https:\/\/www.avast.com\/lp-free-av?full_trSrc=mmm_blp_dlp_008_407_a&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=bleepingcomputer&utm_campaign=blp_dlp_008_407_a:banner )\nPopular Stories\n  * [ ![Angry Cat](https:\/\/www.bleepingcomputer.com\/news\/microsoft\/windows-snipping-tool-now-lets-you-crea